</div> </div> </div>Yes. In fact Demon the Descent was the first 2E game (before 2E was fully a thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:25:03-07:00","id":947999,"title":"","content":"In fact, they aren't 'updated' to 2e. It was only ever in the 2e rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:17:41-07:00","id":948056,"title":"","content":"I've got one, though it isn't a simple question, nor answer, I suspect.<br /> <br /> Is there any reason a fresh Demon <i>can't</i> make a bunch of Rank 5 Cryptid monstrosities to throw at their enemies with the Hellounds Exploit and the local kennel? RAW, that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:32:53-07:00","id":948072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948056#post948056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got one, though it isn't a simple question, nor answer, I suspect.<br /> <br /> Is there any reason a fresh Demon <i>can't</i> make a bunch of Rank 5 Cryptid monstrosities to throw at their enemies with the Hellounds Exploit and the local kennel? RAW, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>can't</i>, no, nothing stops them, it seems like a terrible idea though. Its really expensive and Cover erroding. There's also no guarantee they would be rank five, you'd probably have to use willpower and/or roll really well for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Willpower isnt strictly needed, exploding 10s could do it. 08-10-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:59:31-07:00","id":948084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948072#post948072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <i>can't</i>, no, nothing stops them, it seems like a terrible idea though. Its really expensive and Cover erroding. There's also no guarantee they would be rank five, you'd probably have to use willpower and/or roll really well for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gadgets don't risk Compromise. And you don't actually need to track Primum or Successes for creating Cryptids - it merely gives Primum + Successes to Attributes as an <i>option</i>. Sure, the ST would have to be okay with your broken antics, but the rules don't really give any indication why you <i>can't</i>, do they?<br /> <br /> (This is actually one of the cases where I wish they added <i>more</i> restrictions to a power.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:23:24-07:00","id":948111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948084#post948084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gadgets don't risk Compromise. And you don't actually need to track Primum or Successes for creating Cryptids - it merely gives Primum + Successes to Attributes as an <i>option</i>. Sure, the ST would have to be okay with your broken antics, but the rules don't really give any indication why you <i>can't</i>, do they?<br /> <br /> (This is actually one of the cases where I wish they added <i>more</i> restrictions to a power.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suppose your right? I took the Cryptid creation part to be included in the success version, and that the only base one is a dog. But I can see it going either way.<br /> <br /> As for a Gadget, I didnt think about that since you hadnt mentioned it before. You'd still pump Aether out while making it, buts its defiently less of a risk. What would be the restriction though? I suppose it could be that it only makes the one kind of hellhound, but it might be more balanced to make it a collar that only goes on one creature at a time? kind of hard to adjucate RAW here when it is up to ST fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:13:49-07:00","id":948160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948111#post948111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose your right? I took the Cryptid creation part to be included in the success version, and that the only base one is a dog. But I can see it going either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to the Or part, where it says if you take the time beforehand, you can work out a Cryptid to create with your Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948111#post948111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a Gadget, I didnt think about that since you hadnt mentioned it before. You'd still pump Aether out while making it, buts its defiently less of a risk. What would be the restriction though? I suppose it could be that it only makes the one kind of hellhound, but it might be more balanced to make it a collar that only goes on one creature at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. I'd personally be more amenable to the collar as a One Shot. Though I guess the collar is technically reusable.<br /> <br /> I was thinking something like a cattle brand. Stick animal with it, get loyal monster. (If going literal, head down to the cattle farm and re-enact the Running of the Bulls with your legion of cybernetic minotaurs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948111#post948111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">kind of hard to adjucate RAW here when it is up to ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:21:40-07:00","id":948164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948160#post948160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was referring to the Or part, where it says if you take the time beforehand, you can work out a Cryptid to create with your Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I got it now. I just grouped it in two parts in my head:<br /> <br /> <i>The traits of such a creature vary depending on its base animal, but the dog traits on p. 203 of the World of Darkness Rulebook work nicely to simulate such creatures with little to no alteration.</i><br /> <br /> and <br /> <br /> <i>For other animals, use the traits of the animal (or a similar animal; the raven\u2019s traits work for most birds, for example) and add the demon\u2019s Primum + successes on the Exploit roll in dots at the player\u2019s discretion. Or, if the player has some time to think ahead, use the cryptid creation rules on p. 228 to come up with a Hell-beast that the Storyteller and the player agree upon.</i><br /> <br /> So I just assumed when using the cryptid rules you were still bound by the die roll. I can see know that that is not the only way to read it (and may be the wrong way).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T20:07:12-07:00","id":948299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948056#post948056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got one, though it isn't a simple question, nor answer, I suspect.<br /> <br /> Is there any reason a fresh Demon <i>can't</i> make a bunch of Rank 5 Cryptid monstrosities to throw at their enemies with the Hellounds Exploit and the local kennel? RAW, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sort of Aetheric radiance that would cause would get you a dozen hunter-killer angels bearing down on you at the turn of the clock.<br /> <br /> So, you could. It's just not very smart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T21:10:41-07:00","id":948335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948299#post948299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sort of Aetheric radiance that would cause would get you a dozen hunter-killer angels bearing down on you at the turn of the clock.<br /> <br /> So, you could. It's just not very smart.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So bail afterwards and let them deal with monsters you created. Decent enough distraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:56:11-07:00","id":948636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948335#post948335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So bail afterwards and let them deal with monsters you created. Decent enough distraction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another thought on this, when you say fresh Demon, do you mean freshly Fallen or a freshly made character? As a storyteller, I wouldn't allow a freshly fallen demon to have any exploits, they don't know them as angels and learn them by pushing the boundries of the embeds they have. That would take some time, same with making Gadgets, is that innate knowledge or learned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:16:52-07:00","id":948642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948636#post948636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Another thought on this, when you say fresh Demon, do you mean freshly Fallen or a freshly made character? As a storyteller, I wouldn't allow a freshly fallen demon to have any exploits, they don't know them as angels and learn them by pushing the boundries of the embeds they have. That would take some time, same with making Gadgets, is that innate knowledge or learned?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant a freshly rolled character, since just what a freshly Fallen Demon has or doesn't is more Storyteller purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:35:01-07:00","id":948647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948642#post948642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant a freshly rolled character, since just what a freshly Fallen Demon has or doesn't is more Storyteller purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OK, then yeah, back where we were with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:49:25-07:00","id":948653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948647#post948647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> OK, then yeah, back where we were with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I mean, I houserule Hellhounds to only be able to create a maximum of 1/2 Primum (round up) Rank Cryptid (at about 3 Adaptations or Attributes over 5 per Rank, it is still nice), and modify the Aether requirements to (usually) be by Rank (so stronger Cryptids consume more), but that's excessive houseruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:53:52-07:00","id":948656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948653#post948653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I mean, I houserule Hellhounds to only be able to create a maximum of 1/2 Primum (round up) Rank Cryptid (at about 3 Adaptations or Attributes over 5 per Rank, it is still nice), and modify the Aether requirements to (usually) be by Rank (so stronger Cryptids consume more), but that's excessive houseruling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I'll stick with my previous interpertation: The roll determines how many points can be used to build the cryptid, same as just making an enhanced animal. Solve the time issue by working with a player that has the exploit to build some prototype hellhounds ahead of time at various levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:59:46-07:00","id":948660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948656#post948656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think I'll stick with my previous interpertation: The roll determines how many points can be used to build the cryptid, same as just making an enhanced animal. Solve the time issue by working with a player that has the exploit to build some prototype hellhounds ahead of time at various levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you price Adaptations in that case, then? Worth 1 Attribute dot? 2? If assuming 1 Success per Adaptation, that would require 13-15 Successes to reach Rank 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:32:36-07:00","id":948673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948660#post948660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you price Adaptations in that case, then? Worth 1 Attribute dot? 2? If assuming 1 Success per Adaptation, that would require 13-15 Successes to reach Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say 1 yeah. So it would be possible for a starting demon to make a Rank 5 Hellhound but not likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:03:16-07:00","id":950010,"title":"","content":"A bit late, but some thoughts<br /> <br /> ~ Restrictions on building an army of Hellhounds - it costs a lot in terms of aether. How do you have enough saved up? Sure, technically using a gadget won't cost aether, but then we've got them living for a single scene, and transporting from a kennel is going to be a scene shift. That means we're talking investing aether in keeping the hounds alive. These cryptids are also obvious unnatural, so the situations they can be used are limited without the hoard of angels.<br /> <br /> ~ Exploited Gadgets reek of aether. It might not be a compromise, but its still a huge flag. They're also obviously unnatural, so any observer will possibly trigger some Compromises due to exposure. <br /> <br /> ~ Making a bunch of hellhounds and running away, leaving angels to clean up the mess is likely to not work. Their Mission is to capture the rogue, not kill hellhounds. Someone else can clean that up. Or, worse. The hunter angel has some kind of animal-control power that can turn your hellhounds against you. God can clean up any surviving witnesses later.<br /> <br /> ~ I'd say that long term hellhounds probably should be bought as Retainers. That's how Vampire handles ghouls, including animal ghouls. <br /> <br /> ~ I can't think of any reason I'd ever allow a player to have a Rank 5 cryptid. They need to work with the ST, which means veto power is in play, and I can't think of any reason why I'd allow that many attributes and skills above 5 or supernatural merits/Adaptations. <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, there's not a lot of rules, but I think its clear that the intent is that you're going to end up with something just slightly stronger than an average animal. That's not enough to make it to Rank 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:20:13-07:00","id":950621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950010#post950010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit late, but some thoughts<br /> <br /> ~ Restrictions on building an army of Hellhounds - it costs a lot in terms of aether. How do you have enough saved up? Sure, technically using a gadget won't cost aether, but then we've got them living for a single scene, and transporting from a kennel is going to be a scene shift. That means we're talking investing aether in keeping the hounds alive. These cryptids are also obvious unnatural, so the situations they can be used are limited without the hoard of angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>So create them on-site.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950010#post950010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~ Exploited Gadgets reek of aether. It might not be a compromise, but its still a huge flag. They're also obviously unnatural, so any observer will possibly trigger some Compromises due to exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Load up a Animal Control van with critters. Have a small device Exploited to make Hellhounds. Roll up to target, go wild, let target deal with it. Ideally while you were never there (via 4 Minutes Ago).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950010#post950010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~ Making a bunch of hellhounds and running away, leaving angels to clean up the mess is likely to not work. Their Mission is to capture the rogue, not kill hellhounds. Someone else can clean that up. Or, worse. The hunter angel has some kind of animal-control power that can turn your hellhounds against you. God can clean up any surviving witnesses later.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books state that the Machine works to stop Cryptids from growing too numerous and causing a scene, and even puts for the suggestion of using them as a distraction. And Hellhounds are stated in the rules to be Creator-loyal, so any animal control power would at least call for a clash of wills. And hypothetical Rank 5 Cryptids gnawing on an Angel's face, even in Twilight might lead to a priority shift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950010#post950010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~ I'd say that long term hellhounds probably should be bought as Retainers. That's how Vampire handles ghouls, including animal ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950010#post950010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~ I can't think of any reason I'd ever allow a player to have a Rank 5 cryptid. They need to work with the ST, which means veto power is in play, and I can't think of any reason why I'd allow that many attributes and skills above 5 or supernatural merits/Adaptations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I covered the caveat that the ST would need to be okay with it. I was looking for a rules answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950010#post950010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, there's not a lot of rules, but I think its clear that the intent is that you're going to end up with something just slightly stronger than an average animal. That's not enough to make it to Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd contest that: there's no point to a &quot;make a Cryptid&quot; power if you aren't actually using the Cryptid rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:50:34-07:00","id":950697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950621#post950621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So create them on-site.</div> </div> </div> </div> On-site? Okay then. How are you going to bring in a kennel of dogs into God Machine's infrastructure without shredding Cover or attracting attention for having a ton of dogs show up? You're a spy. Under what situation is this going to be worth drawing the attention? At best, we're looking at a end-of-Matrix situation where you're charging into a building with guns blazing and killing everything that gets in your way to some goal as sirens are blazing, Covers shreded beyond repair, and hunter angels hounding you the entire time. <br /> <br /> Personally, I find that even Going Loud isn't a match for hunter angels. Not long term anyways. Certainly, even Rank 5 cryptids won't be a match either, especially when we're talking about striking the demons from Twilight and just ignoring the hellhounds. Chances are, we're talking about a Defense high enough that the hound's can't even hit the angels.<br /> <br /> The main reason that you can't just do this is the sheer improbablity of arranging the logistics to make it worthwhile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Load up a Animal Control van with critters. Have a small device Exploited to make Hellhounds. Roll up to target, go wild, let target deal with it. Ideally while you were never there (via 4 Minutes Ago). </div> </div> </div>&quot;Small device&quot; is kind of a misnomer there. Size doesn't really matter if you got a van, and in any case, its still going to reek of aether, and the local security measures will quite possibly notice it. Its still a giant red flag. Exposure always has been the greatest check on a demon's abilty to go crazy. This situation is no different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The books state that the Machine works to stop Cryptids from growing too numerous and causing a scene, </div> </div> </div>Immaterial. That's not the Mission of the hunter angels. Some other angels, who has a job to maintain secrecy, will care. But that's a different kind of angel with a different Mission, and likely come in as clean up after the fact. They will be non-combatant angels in the first place, most likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and even puts for the suggestion of using them as a distraction. And Hellhounds are stated in the rules to be Creator-loyal, so any animal control power would at least call for a clash of wills. And hypothetical Rank 5 Cryptids gnawing on an Angel's face, even in Twilight might lead to a priority shift. </div> </div> </div> Distractions are great for mortals and enhanced cultists. But guardian angels aren't stupid, and have a tendacy to have sensory powers to watch over their Infrastructure. <br /> <br /> High Rank angels will generally win a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> Cryptids can't attack into Twilight naturally. Nor are there abilities or powers that make sense for the cryptid to be given to allow this. Even demons can't see into Twilight to see angels eitehr to attack, so making a cryptid that suddenly can is also a bit strange. Angels also have the benefit of being hidden within their Infrastructure, so having cryptids that can suddenly see angels in Twilight to attack is against the rules. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I covered the caveat that the ST would need to be okay with it. I was looking for a rules answer. </div> </div> </div> ST oversight is a rule. Its right there in the text to work with the ST. If the ST ever wants to grant someone lots of powerful things, you'll never find any kind of rule to stop it in the first place.<br /> <br /> What you are suggesting is that a player should have access to make whatever creature they want, with any power and ability they want, and any skill / attribute levels you want. The rules don't specifically say &quot;No!&quot; but that's kind of against all common sense here. That's what the suggestions and ST oversight is for. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd contest that: there's no point to a &quot;make a Cryptid&quot; power if you aren't actually using the Cryptid rules. </div> </div> </div> Three things. One, there's a ton of points to &quot;make a cryptid&quot; powers that use different rules. Just because you don't agree doesn't make it untrue. Two, setting a power level for the ability does not in any way invalidate the Cryptid rules. For that matter, I didn't suggest not using cryptid rules, since the cryptid rules use animal bases anyways. Three, you can't really contest that the power intends on having a relatively weaker Cryptid because the power even says to start with a base animal from core book. Well, you can contest, but its in the writing, so its very hard to put a lot of credibilty behind it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In short - in a white room, this sounds like a valid tactic, but actual play means that there's far too many restrictions to make it worth the while. And that's before we get to the fact that you'd have to be pretty callous and blase about both human and animal life to do it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:55:27-07:00","id":950821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950697#post950697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On-site? Okay then. How are you going to bring in a kennel of dogs into God Machine's infrastructure without shredding Cover or attracting attention for having a ton of dogs show up? You're a spy. Under what situation is this going to be worth drawing the attention? At best, we're looking at a end-of-Matrix situation where you're charging into a building with guns blazing and killing everything that gets in your way to some goal as sirens are blazing, Covers shreded beyond repair, and hunter angels hounding you the entire time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angel's can't even detect Aether without Cryptid - that's why they sometimes use them as hunting dogs. So &quot;reaks&quot; Aether is only a factor regarding other Demons, or those cases (which obviously aren't all) where Cryptid detectors are used.<br /> <br /> The Cryptids will cause a scene, but that's their point in this scenario. You can create them, and leave before they tear things up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950697#post950697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I find that even Going Loud isn't a match for hunter angels. Not long term anyways. Certainly, even Rank 5 cryptids won't be a match either, especially when we're talking about striking the demons from Twilight and just ignoring the hellhounds. Chances are, we're talking about a Defense high enough that the hound's can't even hit the angels.<br /> <br /> The main reason that you can't just do this is the sheer improbablity of arranging the logistics to make it worthwhile.<br /> <br /> &quot;Small device&quot; is kind of a misnomer there. Size doesn't really matter if you got a van, and in any case, its still going to reek of aether, and the local security measures will quite possibly notice it. Its still a giant red flag. Exposure always has been the greatest check on a demon's abilty to go crazy. This situation is no different.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't that hard to drive a van around. By the time the fun happens, it's too late to really stop it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950697#post950697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immaterial. That's not the Mission of the hunter angels. Some other angels, who has a job to maintain secrecy, will care. But that's a different kind of angel with a different Mission, and likely come in as clean up after the fact. They will be non-combatant angels in the first place, most likely.<br /> <br /> Distractions are great for mortals and enhanced cultists. But guardian angels aren't stupid, and have a tendacy to have sensory powers to watch over their Infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>The surveillance web isn't as total as implied here. &quot;Getting a van near&quot; is the difficulty that has to be worked with. Not even that if you want to use Deep Pocket shenanigans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950697#post950697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Rank angels will generally win a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says you are going to be confronted by high Rank Angels? They don't grow on trees, you know, and a crisis is already in motion to make summoning or reallocation unfeasible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950697#post950697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cryptids can't attack into Twilight naturally. Nor are there abilities or powers that make sense for the cryptid to be given to allow this. Even demons can't see into Twilight to see angels eitehr to attack, so making a cryptid that suddenly can is also a bit strange. Angels also have the benefit of being hidden within their Infrastructure, so having cryptids that can suddenly see angels in Twilight to attack is against the rules.<br /> ST oversight is a rule. Its right there in the text to work with the ST. If the ST ever wants to grant someone lots of powerful things, you'll never find any kind of rule to stop it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight Form Adaptation. It's in Core. Sure Angels can hide in their Infrastructure. But then they aren't responding to the threat anyways, so are irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950697#post950697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you are suggesting is that a player should have access to make whatever creature they want, with any power and ability they want, and any skill / attribute levels you want. The rules don't specifically say &quot;No!&quot; but that's kind of against all common sense here. That's what the suggestions and ST oversight is for.<br /> <br /> Three things. One, there's a ton of points to &quot;make a cryptid&quot; powers that use different rules. Just because you don't agree doesn't make it untrue. Two, setting a power level for the ability does not in any way invalidate the Cryptid rules. For that matter, I didn't suggest not using cryptid rules, since the cryptid rules use animal bases anyways. Three, you can't really contest that the power intends on having a relatively weaker Cryptid because the power even says to start with a base animal from core book. Well, you can contest, but its in the writing, so its very hard to put a lot of credibilty behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't against common sense. It doesn't even require an odd reading of the rules. There really <i>aren't</i> very many rules on it, which is my point. Quick and Dirty is 1) Pick Animal 2) Add Successes to Attributes. The other option is Cryptid creation - no alternate rules listed, so use the default Cryptid creation rules, which are Rank is Adaptations or Attributes over 5, divide by 3. Starting with a base animal is irrelevant. The sample Cryptid in the book starts out as a cat, and is a lethal monster by the end at only Rank 3. It's in the book - that's plenty of support.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950697#post950697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short - in a white room, this sounds like a valid tactic, but actual play means that there's far too many restrictions to make it worth the while. And that's before we get to the fact that you'd have to be pretty callous and blase about both human and animal life to do it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>We <i>are</i> talking about Demons here. They aren't all heartless assholes. but it <i>is</i> a character theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T18:19:56-07:00","id":950829,"title":"","content":"Apparently, we play the game very differently, because I'm just seeing you push a white room scenario that is going to fall apart the minute you try something. Its not going to work the way you're suggesting in anything approaching any game I've ever played in or seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-14-2016, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:11:52-07:00","id":950854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=950829#post950829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, we play the game very differently, because I'm just seeing you push a white room scenario that is going to fall apart the minute you try something. Its not going to work the way you're suggesting in anything approaching any game I've ever played in or seen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not at all white room, because it is taking in context into account. Perhaps you play with opposition forces with near omniscience more. Personally, I just houseruled structured limitations on it. I just found it odd how very open ended it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T04:41:46-07:00","id":951045,"title":"","content":"I think you are mistaken on what the difference between white room and actual context is. There's no discussion of current plot, of what the demon's goals are beyond &quot;have puppies eat angelic faces,&quot; what said angels Missions are, what the current defensive Infrastructure is, there presence nor absense of angel-side cryptids and stigmatics and cultists, where the location you are attacking specifically is, etc. I mean, are you trying to just raze any Infrastructure to the ground? Subvert it? Just sneak in, get information and aether and escape? Rescue mission? Kill or corrupt an angel?<br /> <br /> Without any of those above details, there is no context. That makes it a white room exercise. If we actually had a plot, a mission, a goal, a location described, and a living world, then yeah, that'd be context. The totality (or at least a brief summary) of an actual event that you encounter over the course of a story with actual PCs and NPCs. This? Its assuming that you have the perfect set up and the enemies are complacent without any stated goal for a group of spies to achieve. You are giving your side all the powers they could possibly want, while denying the enemy the same courtesy. <br /> <br /> None of this is realistic enough to apply to actual game play. <br /> <br /> Now, Demon is a very flexible game. There are a <i>ton</i> of things that are extremely open ended and, frankly, very open to abuse if the ST simply allows anything and everything. I could ask for an Interlock that gives me the ability to force an angel to Fall with a glance for no cost and as a Reflexive action. And Gadgets / Lambdas can, in theory, do pretty much anything as well as long as its narrower in scope for each individual gadget than the parent Embed/Exploit. And there's nothing in the &quot;rules&quot; that says no other than the fact it has to be ST approved. There are lots of things in DtD specifically that are like that. Its actually a <i>design goal, </i>one that relies heavily on ST oversight. Pretty much everything is open ended, with only the ST as a check. <br /> <br /> Its actually a stated theme of the game is that your characters have the potential ability to do anything, but you'll always been less powerful and less flexible than the God-Machine. The creation of powerful things that stand out will send up flags in the God-Machine's probabilty and aetheric scanning routines - its been stated several times in the book over several places. So, yeah, if you can con your ST into allowing it, then yes, you can have super-hounds with every imaginable stat and magical power to answer any threat. But the game is designed in such a way that the G-M will know, and does have the resources to exceed anything you throw at it. Those are the rules that stop you. Exposure and superior power. Not only can the ST pull out stronger monsters for you to fight, they're expected to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T07:15:52-07:00","id":951094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=951045#post951045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are mistaken on what the difference between white room and actual context is. There's no discussion of current plot, of what the demon's goals are beyond &quot;have puppies eat angelic faces,&quot; what said angels Missions are, what the current defensive Infrastructure is, there presence nor absense of angel-side cryptids and stigmatics and cultists, where the location you are attacking specifically is, etc. I mean, are you trying to just raze any Infrastructure to the ground? Subvert it? Just sneak in, get information and aether and escape? Rescue mission? Kill or corrupt an angel?<br /> <br /> Without any of those above details, there is no context. That makes it a white room exercise. If we actually had a plot, a mission, a goal, a location described, and a living world, then yeah, that'd be context. The totality (or at least a brief summary) of an actual event that you encounter over the course of a story with actual PCs and NPCs. This? Its assuming that you have the perfect set up and the enemies are complacent without any stated goal for a group of spies to achieve. You are giving your side all the powers they could possibly want, while denying the enemy the same courtesy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goal: Use Cryptids to create a distraction. Since this is about a game rule as opposed to a specific case example, exact details are simply not available - generalities have to be dealt with. Given that, I'm not really slanting things one sided - I've listed where problems can arise, what's reasonable given setting/rules information, and where things can go wrong. If you are playing your local God-Machine forces as so observant that a van or anything with Aether Resonance cannot approach, then yeah, the plan will have difficulties. But any Unchained in the area will have other problems due to those criteria. Your counter position seems to assume that rather the <i>God-Machine</i> has all assets and preparations in Its favor (High Rank Hunter Angels with an overriding focus on capturing Demons nearby, Aetheric detection already set up, all areas under constant surveillance).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=951045#post951045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of this is realistic enough to apply to actual game play.<br /> <br /> Now, Demon is a very flexible game. There are a <i>ton</i> of things that are extremely open ended and, frankly, very open to abuse if the ST simply allows anything and everything. I could ask for an Interlock that gives me the ability to force an angel to Fall with a glance for no cost and as a Reflexive action. And Gadgets / Lambdas can, in theory, do pretty much anything as well as long as its narrower in scope for each individual gadget than the parent Embed/Exploit. And there's nothing in the &quot;rules&quot; that says no other than the fact it has to be ST approved. There are lots of things in DtD specifically that are like that. Its actually a <i>design goal, </i>one that relies heavily on ST oversight. Pretty much everything is open ended, with only the ST as a check.<br /> <br /> Its actually a stated theme of the game is that your characters have the potential ability to do anything, but you'll always been less powerful and less flexible than the God-Machine. The creation of powerful things that stand out will send up flags in the God-Machine's probabilty and aetheric scanning routines - its been stated several times in the book over several places. So, yeah, if you can con your ST into allowing it, then yes, you can have super-hounds with every imaginable stat and magical power to answer any threat. But the game is designed in such a way that the G-M will know, and does have the resources to exceed anything you throw at it. Those are the rules that stop you. Exposure and superior power. Not only can the ST pull out stronger monsters for you to fight, they're expected to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are dramatically distorting my statements. I never said, nor implied &quot;super-hounds with every imaginable stat and magical power to answer any threat&quot;, nor talking about unaccountable powers developed at individual games, but a power <u>in the Core book</u>, that simply lets you create a Cryptid <u>using the Core Cryptid creation rules</u>, which can include things like <u>sample Adaptations that are in Core</u>. I'm not reaching into anything that isn't listed in the text. &quot;But the game is designed in such a way that the G-M will know, and does have the resources to exceed anything you throw at it&quot; Yeah, <i>eventually</i>. It has also been stated that the Machine isn't perfect, and can't be everywhere at once. In the above example, I'm talking about a distraction, which is by nature a transitory event. Given how Hellhounds works, unless you &quot;fed&quot; the Cryptids, they'll collapse at the end of the Scene anyways, so longer term solutions are moot.<br /> <br /> Now, if a Demon makes a habit of such a tactic, that's another issue. As is if any resources pulled to deal with the distraction get reassigned to deal with the Demons. But those are narrative consequences.<br /> <br /> My issue is that the text offers no help nor reasoning why this (creating a Rank 5 Cryptid, even temporarily) isn't fully possible. Is it intentional that Demons can simply do this? Is it oversight? Is it simple to conserve word count? Why should a Storyteller just say no arbitrarily?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-15-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T16:09:58-07:00","id":951360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=951094#post951094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue is that the text offers no help nor reasoning why this (creating a Rank 5 Cryptid, even temporarily) isn't fully possible. Is it intentional that Demons can simply do this? Is it oversight? Is it simple to conserve word count? Why should a Storyteller just say no arbitrarily?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does this matter? Any given story/storyteller will have it work or not, and to varying effectivness. It doesn't matter why it was written the way it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:07:23-07:00","id":951412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=951094#post951094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this is about a game rule as opposed to a specific case example, exact details are simply not available - generalities have to be dealt with.</div> </div> </div> </div> And THAT is why its a white room scenario. Details make all the difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My issue is that the text offers no help nor reasoning why this (creating a Rank 5 Cryptid, even temporarily) isn't fully possible. Is it intentional that Demons can simply do this? Is it oversight? Is it simple to conserve word count? Why should a Storyteller just say no arbitrarily? </div> </div> </div> Because that's kind of their job? I said it above, I'll say it again. Demon: the Descent is a game built on flexiblity with powers, with only the ST to adjust them. You can make a Gadget that can do pretty much anything you want - in one game, I personally had a character that made a 2nd degree Lambda that could create entire <i>worlds </i>with simple words. That character could literally speak &quot;Be!&quot; and have new Creation spring up around them. Granted, this was the end point of the game for the character, since this was the Hell that they worked for over the entire chronicle, but that's not the point.<br /> <br /> This is the point - cryptids, cults, gadgets, interlocks, pacts, all of them can be just as powerful as the player and ST agree on. The only limit on any of this is that same agreement between players and ST. And this is a deliberate design decision for the game as a whole. Much like Mage, this is a game about having the power to reshape reality at your finger tips. The difference is that, in Mage, paradox is what limits your potential, while in Demon, its the God Machine keeping you down. There's even a side bar in the core book that mentions this on page 47. &quot;Achievable Goals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Being able to theoretically make anything with ST approval is the game working as intended. That's how it was designed. You might think it strange, or not like it, but that is how the game is designed. The individual STs are the ones with the burden to keep the game working, not the rules. You seem to be thinking that the ST shouldn't say no to that kind of thing, but that's exactly what the game is expecting the ST to do. Its like you're objecting to one of the design goals of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-15-2016, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:42:21-07:00","id":973900,"title":"","content":"So, Heirs of Hell-ish question. If a Demon is using a Sleeve Integrator as a Cover, and a child is conceived, would the child be Demon-Blooded? If the Cover was female, would the pregnancy stick with the Demon, or the Stigmatic (I'd assume the answer to this one is &quot;depends&quot;, since pregnancy is variably tied to Cover anyways).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T20:50:11-07:00","id":974851,"title":"","content":"are pacts taught? or innate (meaning the fallen angel just knows).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:15:50-07:00","id":998042,"title":"","content":"Finally reading through the core book.<br /> <br /> I have a question. I get the soul pact. The demon doesn't really take the soul, but annihilates it. Still, the soul is required, perhaps as a sort of anchor for the annihilation or something, and a Soul Pact cannot be made with someone with the Soulless Condition.<br /> <br /> I'm sure it's answered somewhere but it doesn't seem to be in this book. What happens if someone is afflicted with the Soulless Condition after they have made a Soul Pact? I'd guess that it would just nullify the Soul Pact, alerting the Demon. But I suppose it's possible, if the soul is placed somewhere else, such as in a different person, the contract is merely sort of edited? The Demon would be notified in that case, I'm sure. But what if the soul was just reaped and kept outside of a body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:40:22-07:00","id":998054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=998042#post998042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally reading through the core book.<br /> I'm sure it's answered somewhere but it doesn't seem to be in this book. What happens if someone is afflicted with the Soulless Condition after they have made a Soul Pact? I'd guess that it would just nullify the Soul Pact, alerting the Demon. But I suppose it's possible, if the soul is placed somewhere else, such as in a different person, the contract is merely sort of edited? The Demon would be notified in that case, I'm sure. But what if the soul was just reaped and kept outside of a body?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably say simply that, whether the demon intuits it or has to find out on his own, the soul pact remains valid and binding, but simply can't be cashed in for any benefit while the victim is without a soul (making it effectively worthless for the demon, unless there are relevant conditions the pact binds the signatories to). Shove a soul back into the signatory and the pact ought to function properly again, or at least sort-of properly, with some gameable interesting side effects, like odd quirks to the nature of the resulting Cover.<br /> <br /> This is an uncommon enough edge case for most games, though, that I'm comfortable with Storytellers coming up with answers case by case, to suit what's going on in their game. I like the pact being intact but uncashable because it keeps the story elements of having signatories lose their soul be a problem, and of trying to hunt down a soul somehow being an option, without just arbitrarily stripping a player's character of something that can be hard to haggle for and expensive to sign.<br /> <br /> All of this, of course, is contingent on the soul being taken before the pact is cashed in. After that, the signatory <i>is</i> the demon, and demons don't have souls to take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:32:38-07:00","id":998297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=998054#post998054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably say simply that, whether the demon intuits it or has to find out on his own, the soul pact remains valid and binding, but simply can't be cashed in for any benefit while the victim is without a soul (making it effectively worthless for the demon, unless there are relevant conditions the pact binds the signatories to).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is an uncommon enough edge case for most games, though, that I'm comfortable with Storytellers coming up with answers case by case, to suit what's going on in their game. </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised it hasn't popped up, I'm sure it would have been in some book or another. I was going to use that as the hook, with souls going missing and wanting to find out why without potentially bumping into psychopomps or drawing the attention of the GM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of this, of course, is contingent on the soul being taken before the pact is cashed in. After that, the signatory <i>is</i> the demon, and demons don't have souls to take. </div> </div> </div>Yeah I've got that much down. Thanks a ton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:26:27-07:00","id":998831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=948299#post948299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sort of Aetheric radiance that would cause would get you a dozen hunter-killer angels bearing down on you at the turn of the clock.<br /> <br /> So, you could. It's just not very smart.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Angels can't sense Aetheric resonance. What you could do as GM is have more powerful Cryptids take notice or other demons who would let angels know even normal groups such as the FBI could take notice and go after them. I personally would have something like the DMS (Department of military Science) Go after that demon by sending hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:52:02-08:00","id":999198,"title":"","content":"Can you use Urban Legend Exploit to create angel banes ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:48:44-08:00","id":999270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=998831#post998831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels can't sense Aetheric resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, but while angels can't sense aether like demons, an abundance of it leads to side-effects that can be easily tracked by savvy angels. It's the main risk of producing gadgets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:45:54-08:00","id":1007812,"title":"","content":"According to the core book, page 183: &quot;In addition, all of the Unchained are fluent<br /> in every native human language currently in use. This includes<br /> local dialects as well as slang and innuendo \u2014 the demon can<br /> <b>speak</b> any language like a native speaker&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that only apply to speaking or can demons also read and write and if not what do you have to do to not be illiterate in your covers native language?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11209-blackfyre","name":"Blackfyre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11209_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:56:56-08:00","id":1007817,"title":"","content":"It covers literacy too. English, Spanish, Portuguese, Mandarin, Roman lettering, the Hebrew alphabet, hangul: as long as it's not a dead language, as a demon, you've got it covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:52:31-08:00","id":1012148,"title":"","content":"What happens if a Demon collects a soul pact on a pregnant woman?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:40:59-08:00","id":1012217,"title":"","content":"The demon might become pregnant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T16:48:58-08:00","id":1012259,"title":"","content":"Looking for advice on Fractals having demon form abilities. I was thinking about running a demon the decent game using fractals and I thought it would be interesting if fractals could have one or two demon forms their parents have but a little bit more refined. Do you think turning on demon forms using will power would be better then aether due to the fact that most demon forms gobble up aether like crazy ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:26:12-08:00","id":1012511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1012259#post1012259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking for advice on Fractals having demon form abilities. I was thinking about running a demon the decent game using fractals and I thought it would be interesting if fractals could have one or two demon forms their parents have but a little bit more refined. Do you think turning on demon forms using will power would be better then aether due to the fact that most demon forms gobble up aether like crazy ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heh. I was actually working on allowing Fractals (and potentially Offspring) to get Demonic Form powers and other abilities (and become a kind of Demon-lite). Nephilim (from the Demon Storytellers Guide) are a good place to looks for such material. Though they have Primum, and thus, Aether reliably.<br /> <br /> I'd allow Willpower or Aether to be used, or just require them to have access to Aether (either storing it via Aether Pool, or grabbing as necessary with Ambient Aether), and to run it as a Partial Transformation. Nephilim also take a point of Lethal Damage when transforming, I think.<br /> <br /> I'm currently looking at the implications of a Merit that just lets a Fractal be treated as a Demon for the purposes of other Merits - They could then talk Terrible Form (which grants extra Form Abilities) to get Form Abilities, Resonance Aware for improved detection, etc.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Added my ideas <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=1012643#post1012643\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-05-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T00:33:22-08:00","id":1013622,"title":"","content":"Compromise scene: from the core book, seem that only human (mage too?) discovery can cause compromise, but not from other &quot;deniezen of the darkness&quot;.<br /> At pp 114, talk about human discovery... Demon can talk about itself real nature with vampire, mage ,hangeling etc, without the risk of compromisie roll?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T00:54:02-08:00","id":1013627,"title":"","content":"Supernatural beings don't cause compromises when they discover key facts about your demonic nature, no. This doesn't do anything about compromises caused by adopting demonic form, using Exploits, or performing gross breaks of your Cover's character: those can be made worse by human witnesses, but they still happen even without witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:00:17-08:00","id":1013628,"title":"","content":"My bad, thanks you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:25:51-08:00","id":1013638,"title":"","content":"How about mages? Mages are technically humans. The text talks about &quot;humans&quot;, not &quot;mortals&quot;. Is a demon going to cause compromise if a mage learns about its nature and believes it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T02:12:25-08:00","id":1013654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1013638#post1013638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about mages? Mages are technically humans. The text talks about &amp;quot;humans&amp;quot;, not &amp;quot;mortals&amp;quot;. Is a demon going to cause compromise if a mage learns about its nature and believes it?</div> </div> </div> </div>For this I think we can look at mage for an answer, supernatural beings don't cause their magic to go array.<br /> In this same sense mortals are apart of the machine. Supernatural beings are outside it's natural network. So in that sense it fits with other supernatural beings not triggering comprimise and such.<br /> Edit: Or rather they won't make things worse like a mortal does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 12-07-2016, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T03:20:08-08:00","id":1014231,"title":"","content":"I have a few simple but related questions that I don't feel are worth an independent post.<br /> <br /> <b>Q1:</b> Does a ghost cover generated through the 'ephemeral cover' exploit have an anchor?<br /> <br /> I believe the answer is no but because of how that interacts with some manifestations (like image) as well as being in a sense an 'easy' to identify that you are not a real ghost I find myself wondering. It is a integral part of a ghosts identity but the exploit doesn't go one way or another explicitly from my reading.<br /> <br /> <b>Q2:</b> Are you able to repair / improve an existing cover created via 'ephemeral cover'?<br /> <br /> I understand not being able to use contacts with ghosts (though that would be cool) to improve the cover could you use say, 'ephemeral cover' to improve it or once active can you only improve a ghostly / spiritual cover by living the cover (DtD pg.116)? <br /> <br /> <b>Q3:</b> How do you determine &quot;of comparable rank&quot; for ephemeral cover?<br /> <br /> I find myself unsure if Primum = Rank or if it is better to go by the attribute total (pow, fin and res) determining rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:16:46-08:00","id":1016235,"title":"","content":"Question: Is it true that Matt is outlining a new <b>Demon</b> book?<br /> <br /> Answer: WHATHASFALLENMAYRISEAGAIN","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/m