re book, but I was wondering if a Demon is able to use a fresh corpse as a new Cover? I know in one of the stories in the core book (slowly reading through it again) an angel was able to take over the body of its Cover's granddaughter after she died, was wondering if a Demon could do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11491-thehallow1","name":"thehallow1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:24:11-08:00","id":1016734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thehallow1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1016713#post1016713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was probably in the core book, but I was wondering if a Demon is able to use a fresh corpse as a new Cover? I know in one of the stories in the core book (slowly reading through it again) an angel was able to take over the body of its Cover's granddaughter after she died, was wondering if a Demon could do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can only forge a pact with a living person but there is an embed 'the voting dead' that kinda functions like you want. However that is more a temporary disguise to your cover than a cover in its own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:22:05-08:00","id":1016797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1016734#post1016734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can only forge a pact with a living person but there is an embed 'the voting dead' that kinda functions like you want. However that is more a temporary disguise to your cover than a cover in its own right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks - I should have figured that was more Angel territory than something a Demon could pull off as a permanent measure. I probably will look into that embed, however - might see what I can do with that for the game I'm a part of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11491-thehallow1","name":"thehallow1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T01:28:41-08:00","id":1016942,"title":"","content":"The section on Pacts in the book says that non-personal Merits can still be grants, but they take time to transfer and can't be given in large amounts in one go. It doesn't mention supernatural merits, though.<br /> <br /> If a Demon was to give a cultist or an other stigmatic contact Suborned Infrastructure, how would you handle it? They acquire something from another Demon (who isn't very happy)? A GM installation goes offline nearby? I'm guessing it would involve someone not being very happy with the change, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2149-isvan","name":"Isvan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T02:02:02-08:00","id":1016953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isvan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1016942#post1016942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The section on Pacts in the book says that non-personal Merits can still be grants, but they take time to transfer and can't be given in large amounts in one go. It doesn't mention supernatural merits, though.<br /> <br /> If a Demon was to give a cultist or an other stigmatic contact Suborned Infrastructure, how would you handle it? They acquire something from another Demon (who isn't very happy)? A GM installation goes offline nearby? I'm guessing it would involve someone not being very happy with the change, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the merit Suborned infrastructure I do not believe it is a valid merit for a pact for a few reasons. First off it is intended for demons and is demon specific as far as I am aware. It may not say the restriction in its description but the location of the merit is proof enough. Next the merit represents infrastructure the demon has disconnected from the machine for their own use so I don't feel pacts should have the power to directly affect the machine. Then finally this benefit has no benefit to the one signing the pact so in that way I do not feel it should be valid from an OOC standpoint as it is obvious what the intent is.<br /> <br /> However, if you were to allow it I do not feel it would be taken from another demon as that is outside the machine's influence, since the infrastructure has been disconnected. Possibly you could do it with the deed of a random bit of infrastructure now belonging to this mortal. If this was able to work however you would no doubt draw attention from the machine as it tries to identify the cause in this sudden shifting of variables. Now, because it is not protected by the sanctity of merits if this was allowed to occur by an st I'd expect fallout as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:24:27-08:00","id":1017941,"title":"","content":"Q1: Is a gadget made with the tattooed gadget merit available in all covers or just the one it was made in and tattooed upon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T06:37:14-08:00","id":1018048,"title":"","content":"Based on the wording, it sounds like you are using your Demonic Form as the hardware. I'm not at all sure. Similar with Subsumed Gadgets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T12:18:26-08:00","id":1022419,"title":"","content":"Analysts create their Ciphers with Exploits, right? Or do they use Embeds, and only have access to Exploit-Interlocks when Going Loud?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T19:52:59-08:00","id":1022593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_