","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1022644#post1022644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Demon goes Loud their Aether pool is refilled, but their Primum also goes up to 10. Does that mean they get 50 points of Aether?</div> </div> </div> </div>They get 100 points of Aether, but yes. It's clearer in the description on page 113.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:03:21-08:00","id":1023182,"title":"","content":"Which demon book goes in depth into occult matrixes ?<br /> <br /> If not I would love to deep an in depth book about occult matrixes and infrastructures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:19:07-08:00","id":1023187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1023182#post1023182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which demon book goes in depth into occult matrixes ?<br /> <br /> If not I would love to deep an in depth book about occult matrixes and infrastructures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Define &quot;In Depth&quot;. I don't think any do, but Occult Matrices are more &quot;odd coincidences that combine to form a Plot Device&quot;.<br /> <br /> What's an Occult Matrix? Anything you need to happen - just flavor liberally with weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:31:25-08:00","id":1024906,"title":"","content":"When a Demon goes Loud their Primum goes up to 10. Do they get the extra Demonic Form that comes with Primum 10? and should players already have all bits of demonic form written down because of this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T04:11:40-08:00","id":1026443,"title":"","content":"I have a Question about the Possession exploit<br /> <br /> I currently have a player who used it on a werewolf and was able to take Possession of that werewolf. I wanted to know if the player could use any of the werewolf's powers?<br /> <br /> So far I've made it so they could do the whole werewolf transformation thing becoming the Gauru form and things like that.<br /> <br /> This also made me wonder could demon create a Russian nesting doll using Possession<br /> <br /> Example a demon takes Possession of a vampire who has Possession then makes the vampire use Possession to take possession of a mage who then takes Possession of another demon ?<br /> <br /> If so I think we could call this a double or triple agent lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 01-04-2017, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T05:38:35-08:00","id":1026460,"title":"","content":"As a general rule you can't use your own or the host's supernatural powers while possessing them. I'm not sure if this holds true for unchained demons, but neither vampires nor mages (except for a few spells targetting the host) mqy use their own or the host's supernatural abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T06:42:08-08:00","id":1026473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1026460#post1026460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general rule you can't use your own or the host's supernatural powers while possessing them. I'm not sure if this holds true for unchained demons, but neither vampires nor mages (except for a few spells targetting the host) mqy use their own or the host's supernatural abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Work-around: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Create a Possession or Show Of Power Gadget.</li> <li>Place Gadget on surface.</li> <li>Possess target.</li> <li>Retrieve Gadget.</li> <li>...?</li> <li>Profit!</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:58:53-08:00","id":1026520,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4046\" data-vbnamecard=\"4046\">xenoterracide</a> Yes. The rules saying that going loud brings you up to 10 Primum, &quot;with everything that comes with it&quot; that includes form abilities and glitches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T16:12:39-08:00","id":1029817,"title":"","content":"Should &quot;The Word&quot; be contested (by more than resolve)? one of my Demon Players used it on a Mage, and that feels like it should be contested/and or wondering if the mage can do anything to ward himself against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T20:48:06-08:00","id":1029899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1029817#post1029817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should &amp;quot;The Word&amp;quot; be contested (by more than resolve)? one of my Demon Players used it on a Mage, and that feels like it should be contested/and or wondering if the mage can do anything to ward himself against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most powers intended to be resisted already mention the supernatural tolerance trait in the description however, since it is the point of the supernatural tolerance of power stats I feel you wouldn't be in left field if you choose to. A lot of the powers after all are written with the assumption that they will be performed again mortals. The few I've seem the ST resisting are often with ones that seem to expect angel or other supernatural targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T21:04:24-08:00","id":1029903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1029899#post1029899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most powers intended to be resisted already mention the supernatural tolerance trait in the description however, since it is the point of the supernatural tolerance of power stats I feel you wouldn't be in left field if you choose to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural Tolerance applies to contested powers. The Word is a resisted power because its effects scale with successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T21:05:47-08:00","id":1029904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1029903#post1029903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural Tolerance applies to contested powers. The Word is a resisted power because its effects scale with successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the correction, I had not noticed that was why some did and others didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T21:14:59-08:00","id":1029906,"title":"","content":"That said some Demon Exploits and Embeds are apparently not meant to work on supernatural creatures at all (though it's up to the ST which ones, since that isn't specified anywhere). For example, the devs have said they didn't intend Knockout Punch to be allowed to work on Angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T06:57:02-08:00","id":1030033,"title":"","content":"Additionally, what is the Demon trying to force the Mage to do? Active spells and Fate oaths might run counter to the command.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T18:53:20-08:00","id":1030934,"title":"","content":"Question about memory Theft<br /> <br /> It says only an hours worth of memory does this mean you can only see the last our or you can go back how far you want but only an an hour of memory at a time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T22:14:24-08:00","id":1031009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1030033#post1030033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, what is the Demon trying to force the Mage to do? Active spells and Fate oaths might run counter to the command.</div> </div> </div> </div>the command in this case was &quot;Flee&quot; I didn't contest it... the PC Demon realized very quickly that what he was up against wasn't a normal human because he had used a different power to force the mage to give him a bauble... and of course a mage would have quickly realized he was being controlled. Of course if I was prepared I would have had him put up a mental shield of some sort then, but no plan survives contact with the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:52:42-08:00","id":1031830,"title":"","content":"Hunted condition. Are there any mechanics I should use for the hunting (as a GM?) is there any further descriptions of this I should read in any of the demon books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T00:40:44-08:00","id":1032032,"title":"","content":"Also does going loud require a cover to burn? meaning if you've gone loud, and you're on the run can you go loud again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T00:49:13-08:00","id":1032035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1032032#post1032032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also does going loud require a cover to burn? meaning if you've gone loud, and you're on the run can you go loud again?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need a cover to burn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T00:50:50-08:00","id":1032036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1031830#post1031830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunted condition. Are there any mechanics I should use for the hunting (as a GM?) is there any further descriptions of this I should read in any of the demon books?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want mechanics to dictate all, it's an extended, contested roll. It's probably more interesting to tell the story of the exposed demon doing what it can to hide, and the hunter angel trying to discover its location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:54:48-08:00","id":1032210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1032036#post1032036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want mechanics to dictate all, it's an extended, contested roll. It's probably more interesting to tell the story of the exposed demon doing what it can to hide, and the hunter angel trying to discover its location.</div> </div> </div> </div>chase mechanics might be some kind of appropriate.. but yeah I'm intending it to be more or less of a story, at the same time it's nice to have.... mechanics as so not to be unfair, or overly gentle to the player. Also was asking in case there was any extended advice as in how to portray the storytelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 01-15-2017, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T11:18:05-08:00","id":1032231,"title":"","content":"I like using the new Brief Nightmare mechanics for stats, however I'm wondering if it's worth having anything less than a lone terror for anything that should be a threat given Demon PCs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T15:18:08-08:00","id":1032345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1032231#post1032231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like using the new Brief Nightmare mechanics for stats, however I'm wondering if it's worth having anything less than a lone terror for anything that should be a threat given Demon PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, numbers can do wonders and a demon can also be attacked in non physical ways. What if a horror is attacking the cover itself with the propagation of doubt or information? Those are two ways I can see lower tiered horrors still being some form of a threat for demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:55:03-08:00","id":1033331,"title":"","content":"Question about memory Theft<br /> <br /> It says only an hours worth of memory does this mean you can only see the last our or you can go back how far you want but you can only alter an hour of memory at a time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:35:33-08:00","id":1033384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1033331#post1033331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about memory Theft<br /> <br /> It says only an hours worth of memory does this mean you can only see the last our or you can go back how far you want but you can only alter an hour of memory at a time</div> </div> </div> </div>The only restriction is an hours worth if time. There is no reference to when this hour must have taken place. No mention of &quot;the lady hour&quot; for example. So, I feel it'd be fair to say you can manipulate any 1 hr chunk of their memory with the memory theft form.<br /> <br /> Also, by default the downloaded memories would just be copies. It takes twice the time to do subtle changes and there is a penalty to grand changes. The default allows you to copy data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:00:44-08:00","id":1035776,"title":"","content":"Can you use Deep Cover to disguise yourself as a Beast? Likewise, can Show Of Power mimic their Atavisms, Nightmares and so on? Can you acquire a Beast as a Cover via Soul Pact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:07:13-08:00","id":1035780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1035776#post1035776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Deep Cover to disguise yourself as a Beast? Likewise, can Show Of Power mimic their Atavisms, Nightmares and so on? Can you acquire a Beast as a Cover via Soul Pact?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you can but like all other supernatruals you would not get there powers but who they seem to be as a human. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:25:59-08:00","id":1035786,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not - Demons are great liars. It doesn't say you can't in either Demon or Beast. The crossover chronicle might say more.<br /> <br /> Show of Power can replicate any non-Demon/Angel powers that aren't extended actions, at limited success.<br /> <br /> I actually had unfinished notes on an anti-Beast Demon that would fake their way into a Hive, then use Summon to call down every Hero they know on the Brood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-21-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:32:53-08:00","id":1035815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1035786#post1035786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not - Demons are great liars. It doesn't say you can't in either Demon or Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast does specify on one of these. I'd say yes on Deep Cover and Show of Power, but Beasts are an exception to pacting: they're completely invalid signatories. Can't even get their human identity or a relationship here or there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:30:18-08:00","id":1035838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1035815#post1035815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast does specify on one of these. I'd say yes on Deep Cover and Show of Power, but Beasts are an exception to pacting: they're completely invalid signatories. Can't even get their human identity or a relationship here or there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right - Begotten lack souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:07:05-08:00","id":1036072,"title":"","content":"I wanted to know when would the urban legend exploit be useful?<br /> Could you use it to create a rare item needed to hurt an angel ?<br /> <br /> Also how real are the people that are created by urban legend ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:41:09-08:00","id":1036361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1036072#post1036072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to know when would the urban legend exploit be useful?<br /> Could you use it to create a rare item needed to hurt an angel ?<br /> <br /> Also how real are the people that are created by urban legend ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Useful: When you want to establish the pretext for conducting some behavior. Example: You want to investigate there area for Infrastructure. Just showing up and poking around would raise flags, so you use Urban Legend to generate some &quot;genuine&quot; paranormal activity. Then you can roll into town, claim you are investigating the &quot;monster sightings&quot;, and use that as a cover (for your Cover, heh) for your actual Infrastructure hunting. Or, a Ring-mate killed someone, so you use Urban Legend to generate a Slasher myth to throw investigators off the trail. You can also co-opt the &quot;Legend&quot; as a flimsy Cover, should that be advantageous.<br /> <br /> Item to hurt an Angel: Maybe? But I doubt it - stuff created by Urban Legend is only quasi-&quot;real&quot;. I doubt that would have enough metaphysical authenticity to trigger as a Bane.<br /> <br /> Reality: They really aren't, much. For instance, taking one of the &quot;Legends&quot; as a Cover only gives you a Facade - an effectively 1 Dot Cover with limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T18:56:27-08:00","id":1039739,"title":"","content":"Two questions <br /> <br /> When in full demon form a demon gets aether back equal to their primum. How long are the intervals between rolling to get more aether when staying in that form ?<br /> <br /> Second question<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Resonance Sensitivity lets you see demons on sight and I Wanted to know can you spoof this ?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T02:13:06-08:00","id":1040501,"title":"","content":"Do angels have armor ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T02:24:18-08:00","id":1040504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1040501#post1040501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do angels have armor ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by default, but there are Numina that give them armor.<br /> Like all Ephemeral Beings, they downgrade Lethal to Bashing under most circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:15:36-08:00","id":1040548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1040504#post1040504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not by default, but there are Numina that give them armor.<br /> Like all Ephemeral Beings, they downgrade Lethal to Bashing under most circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Were does it say that ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:32:21-08:00","id":1040558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1040548#post1040548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Were does it say that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>ChroD page 129<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Physical attacks on a Manifested entity that would nor-mally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane. Despite appearing to the naked eye and being solid, a Manifested spirit, ghost, or angel doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure. </div> </div> </div>Demon page 343<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Physical attacks on a manifest entity that normally cause<br /> lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack<br /> utilizes the entity\u2019s bane. Despite appearing to the naked eye<br /> and being solid, a manifest spirit, ghost, or angel doesn\u2019t have<br /> any internal organs to injure. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:27:27-08:00","id":1040813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1039739#post1039739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions<br /> When in full demon form a demon gets aether back equal to their primum. How long are the intervals between rolling to get more aether when staying in that form ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't roll unless you run out.<br /> You roll every time you run out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T01:36:30-08:00","id":1046212,"title":"","content":"Do Demons gain willpower by sleeping like other splats do? It isn't mentioned in any of the books, as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T03:17:47-08:00","id":1046228,"title":"","content":"It's not mentioned in VtR 2E either. Since many people just assumed that vampires did regain Willpower by sleeping the devs clarified that the omission is deliberate. If it's not in DtD then it's most likely also deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T03:25:47-08:00","id":1046231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1046212#post1046212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Demons gain willpower by sleeping like other splats do? It isn't mentioned in any of the books, as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume yes - when in Cover, Demons are human unless otherwise stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T08:51:06-08:00","id":1046335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1046231#post1046231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd assume yes - when in Cover, Demons are human unless otherwise stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that the Demon mind is different from the human one, which has my group confused. Still, fair point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T10:05:25-08:00","id":1046364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1046335#post1046335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue is that the Demon mind is different from the human one, which has my group confused. Still, fair point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it has been established that Demons do sleep. I'd think they dream, too. Though how they interact with the various dream realms and the Astral is unknown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T15:49:02-08:00","id":1046959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1046228#post1046228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not mentioned in VtR 2E either. Since many people just assumed that vampires did regain Willpower by sleeping the devs clarified that the omission is deliberate. If it's not in DtD then it's most likely also deliberate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Difference there is that VtR is self contained and therefore the omission as deliberate makes sense. DtD requires the core book and assumes its rules are true unless it says otherwise. So Demons do while Vampires don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T20:01:25-08:00","id":1047032,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Reality Enforcement<br /> <br /> I had a player go loud when fighting an angel and used Reality Enforcement. <br /> <br /> Reading it we got a little confused. When a demon uses it is the demon also effected by the exploit ?<br /> <br /> Can a player who uses this not use exploits, embeds and demon form stuff while in the reality enforcement area ?<br /> <br /> Also Being this thing knocks out Numina and stuff like that does this also knock out an Angels Influence and intercepts ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T02:19:43-08:00","id":1047133,"title":"","content":"I have a player currently playing a succubus style demon in my demon the decent game I'm looking to make them an interlock based on the Majesty vampire power Green Eyes. I was looking for advice on what I should change to make this power work for a demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T02:51:45-08:00","id":1047139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1047032#post1047032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading it we got a little confused. When a demon uses it is the demon also effected by the exploit ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The demon also disempowers itself. &quot;This forces the demon to rely only on the Skills that his Cover gives him, but it also confuses and disempowers angels for a short time.&quot; - p.173.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1047032#post1047032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a player who uses this not use exploits, embeds and demon form stuff while in the reality enforcement area ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No exploits or embeds. They can use aspects of their demonic form that don't require Aether. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1047032#post1047032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Being this thing knocks out Numina and stuff like that does this also knock out an Angels Influence and intercepts ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. By literal reading of the Exploit, an angel's ability to use Essence isn't blocked, which means Influences could be used. However, dramatic failure amplifying both Aether and Essence use into feedback implies that the Exploit is intended to affect both Aether and Essence. <br /> <br /> My opinion is that angels in the area can't spend Essence, therefore can't use Influences. I'd suggest that Incepts are also covered by this and can't be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T03:02:11-08:00","id":1047141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1046364#post1046364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but it has been established that Demons do sleep. I'd think they dream, too. Though how they interact with the various dream realms and the Astral is unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want this covered in a book now, there should be at least 2 paragraphs on what demons can and can't do in the astral, especially if something like a Beast should invade their dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T00:37:18-08:00","id":1049177,"title":"","content":"Well I hope it will be covered in the crossover book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 02-15-2017, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T01:00:39-08:00","id":1049184,"title":"","content":"Can angels use gadgets ?<br /> <br /> Such as an Angel Using A Sword Made of light to kill demons or a special weapon but they are better then normal demonic gadgets ?<br /> <br /> If this is the case upon an angels death would the angel leave this behind along with any forms it has for a demon to take ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:34:56-08:00","id":1049222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1049184#post1049184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can angels use gadgets ?<br /> <br /> Such as an Angel Using A Sword Made of light to kill demons or a special weapon but they are better then normal demonic gadgets ?<br /> <br /> If this is the case upon an angels death would the angel leave this behind along with any forms it has for a demon to take ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea on the official ruling, but I'd say that an angel willing to use the tools of the enemy, created by power stolen and subverted to fulfil their blasphemous needs, is pretty close to Falling itself.<br /> <br /> If the angel is destroyed, then I guess it'd leave the gadget since it isn't the standard equipment issued by Control. If the angel Falls, then there's a nice in-universe justification for a beginning demon to have a gadget in hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T13:11:20-08:00","id":1049442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1047141#post1047141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want this covered in a book now, there should be at least 2 paragraphs on what demons can and can't do in the astral, especially if something like a Beast should invade their dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>You, uh, may wanna check out the Storyteller's Guide. The rules aren't where you're expecting them, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T13:59:46-08:00","id":1049462,"title":"","content":"Do Demons need to pay XP to learn an Embed or Exploit from a gadget they've taken apart? On the one hand it makes sense if you do, as it serves as a method of learning it; on the other hand, Gadgets practically require XP in order to make because you need to pay a dot of Willpower to solidify them, so paying two more XP on top of that when you could just as easily make up another reason seems arbitrary. The rules don't mention it either way in Flowers Of Hell, where this mechanic is mentioned, so I don't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1049442#post1049442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You, uh, may wanna check out the Storyteller's Guide. The rules aren't where you're expecting them, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean on page 65, where it mentions &quot;Demons appear fundamentally human. They sleep, eat, and work (usually in Cover) as humans do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or on page 109, where it states &quot;Demons face the physical struggle of fleeing through cramped crawlspaces as well as mental tortures that can prove just as dangerous. Those who fail to overcome their challenges are killed, waking in a cold sweat and receiving the Harrowed Condition. Survivors do not regain a point of Willpower for a night\u2019s restful sleep but are otherwise unaffected.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or in the Spiral World scenario on page 164, which is basically all about a Demon dreaming?<br /> <br /> Or even Lady Thorn's second interlock Poisoned Dreams, on page 45?<br /> <br /> ....there are a lot of instances of dreaming/sleeping in that book I'd not realized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 02-15-2017, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:19:58-08:00","id":1049483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1049462#post1049462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on the other hand, Gadgets practically require XP in order to make because you need to pay a dot of Willpower to solidify them, so paying two more XP on top of that when you could just as easily make up another reason seems arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea why the Willpower dot cost is relevant here, seeing as if you're trying to learn an Embed from a Gadget you de facto cannot spend Willpower dots to make Gadgets that contain it in the first place.<br /> <br /> The side benefits of learning an Embed by deconstructing a Gadget include:<br /> \u2022 You've removed an access to a resource by other demons in addition to gaining a new ability, thus building a potential bargaining chip into the acquisition.<br /> \u2022 You don't have deal with unknown quantities among the Unchained that can lie like your choice of magic carpet, thus cutting off avenues of potential betrayal.<br /> \u2022 You don't have to poke around Infrastructure and risk immediate detection, thus allowing you to save time otherwise spent managing your Covers to infiltrate a secure location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:30:37-08:00","id":1049495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1049483#post1049483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea why the Willpower dot cost is relevant here, seeing as if you're trying to learn an Embed from a Gadget you de facto cannot spend Willpower dots to make Gadgets that contain it in the first place.<br /> <br /> The side benefits of learning an Embed by deconstructing a Gadget include:<br /> \u2022 You've removed an access to a resource by other demons in addition to gaining a new ability, thus building a potential bargaining chip into the acquisition.<br /> \u2022 You don't have deal with unknown quantities among the Unchained that can lie like your choice of magic carpet, thus cutting off avenues of potential betrayal.<br /> \u2022 You don't have to poke around Infrastructure and risk immediate detection, thus allowing you to save time otherwise spent managing your Covers to infiltrate a secure location.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is, if you receive a gadget from another player or give them one. I'm in a gadget trade at the moment, where I've made a google glasses gadget with Special Someone that finds gang members (one of his cultists was killed in a very targeted manner by said gang, which lead to a whole lot of other red flags), and he's going to give me a gadget in the future (we're thinking Show Of Power) and, in addition, I'm going to precision engineer the gadget later on (I would have at the time but our schedule really didn't allow it). The willpower cost issue is that we're both planning on deconstructing the gadgets we received to learn the Embeds/Exploit that went into them (the player I'm referring to is effectively getting the same gadget twice, just the second one is going to be better).<br /> <br /> I'm confused about the third point, however, in regards to how learning an Embed/Exploit from a gadget doesn't require you to poke around infrastructure, unless the gadget itself was made from a piece of infrastructure or crafted there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:45:48-08:00","id":1049508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1049495#post1049495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused about the third point, however, in regards to how learning an Embed/Exploit from a gadget doesn't require you to poke around infrastructure, unless the gadget itself was made from a piece of infrastructure or crafted there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons &quot;learn&quot; Embeds by remembering or being reminded of the occult framework they occupied in service to the God-Machine. Esoteric effects from outside your Incarnation's area of specialty are necessarily going to be a little harder to find precedents for that aren't actual parts of the Machine or Gadgets on loan from other demons.<br /> <br /> The simple solution to your problem is to apply Sanctity of Merits to Willpower dot investment, but the mechanic doesn't give you a cost break normally because the vast majority of Gadgets in any given typical setting are not going to be lenders from your ringmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T01:04:02-08:00","id":1049740,"title":"","content":"Another gadget question here; if you make multiple One-Shot gadgets with the same effect, do you need to pay a willpower dot for each one, or just one for the whole batch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T05:56:27-08:00","id":1049811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1049740#post1049740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another gadget question here; if you make multiple One-Shot gadgets with the same effect, do you need to pay a willpower dot for each one, or just one for the whole batch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certain it is by batch - that's the whole point of One-Shots, quantity over quality. Built in Self-Destruct is just a fringe bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:18:28-08:00","id":1050056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1049462#post1049462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Demons need to pay XP to learn an Embed or Exploit from a gadget they've taken apart? On the one hand it makes sense if you do, as it serves as a method of learning it; on the other hand, Gadgets practically require XP in order to make because you need to pay a dot of Willpower to solidify them, so paying two more XP on top of that when you could just as easily make up another reason seems arbitrary. The rules don't mention it either way in Flowers Of Hell, where this mechanic is mentioned, so I don't know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You mean on page 65, where it mentions &quot;Demons appear fundamentally human. They sleep, eat, and work (usually in Cover) as humans do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or on page 109, where it states &quot;Demons face the physical struggle of fleeing through cramped crawlspaces as well as mental tortures that can prove just as dangerous. Those who fail to overcome their challenges are killed, waking in a cold sweat and receiving the Harrowed Condition. Survivors do not regain a point of Willpower for a night\u2019s restful sleep but are otherwise unaffected.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or in the Spiral World scenario on page 164, which is basically all about a Demon dreaming?<br /> <br /> Or even Lady Thorn's second interlock Poisoned Dreams, on page 45?<br /> <br /> ....there are a lot of instances of dreaming/sleeping in that book I'd not realized.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Specifically, I was referencing the 'Mechanics' section of the Nightmare Labyrinth, which includes rule for demons in the Astral, just above the Harrowed Condition. Any similarities between this Condition and any Conditions caused by Beasts, or the rules for entering dreams there and in BtP, or the nature of whatever is behind/<i>inside </i>the Nightmare Labyrinth are all surely coincidental...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:04:25-08:00","id":1050504,"title":"","content":"Demons in the Hedge. Any canon on how that works out for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:01:27-08:00","id":1050530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1050504#post1050504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons in the Hedge. Any canon on how that works out for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Soft formlock \u2014 full transformation costs an Aether or requires going loud, the Cover you go into the Hedge with is the only one you can switch to, and every hour in the Thorns requires that you roll Wits + Manipulation to avoid losing Cover (it doesn't say whether this is distinct from a compromise roll, but the context suggests it is). Also, no Aether collection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:42:24-08:00","id":1050550,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Is anything changed if they're in a Hollow or other such more defined area like a Hob Town?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T11:53:14-08:00","id":1050629,"title":"","content":"When you are using the possession exploit.<br /> <br /> How does damage work ?<br /> <br /> Lets say while your in someones body what happens when someone kill them ?<br /> <br /> Any idea ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 03-01-2017, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T13:21:12-08:00","id":1050681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1050550#post1050550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Is anything changed if they're in a Hollow or other such more defined area like a Hob Town?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say there's no difference - it's another realm with strange, esoteric rules, and one that plays off of a far weirder logic than the already strange normal world. Humanity generally can't stay in the Hedge without getting changed in some way, be it from the thorns, the fruit or just the atmosphere in general. The Wyrd and glamour just likes settling in, and the human body can't cope with that without change. As your Cover is supposed to remain as normal as possible to avoid getting attention from the God-Machine or its Angels, being in that kind of realm is liable to corrode it by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T14:02:07-08:00","id":1050703,"title":"","content":"cool. That also answers my &quot;humans in a hollow&quot; question I was going to ask elsewhere. i was just wondering if the Cover loss was from the Thorns, but your version makes sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T15:33:46-08:00","id":1050765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1016235#post1016235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Is it true that Matt is outlining a new <b>Demon</b> book?<br /> <br /> Answer: WHATHASFALLENMAYRISEAGAIN</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I periodically search what Matt, Dave, and David have posted by user name. I miss shit like this otherwise. <br /> <br /> Glad to hear there is more Demon on the way. I'm assuming since this is the first I've heard of it, it is still outlining and writers haven't been hired yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:37:08-08:00","id":1051240,"title":"","content":"Can a Demon apply patchwork to a mortal? Say if the demon wanted to be a &quot;Rock Star&quot; (or something) and Rick Springfield really wanted Jesse's Girl and the Demon got Jesse's boyfriend to trade his girl for something else (sorry couldn't help my analogy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:52:54-08:00","id":1051248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1051240#post1051240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Demon apply patchwork to a mortal? Say if the demon wanted to be a &quot;Rock Star&quot; (or something) and Rick Springfield really wanted Jesse's Girl and the Demon got Jesse's boyfriend to trade his girl for something else (sorry couldn't help my analogy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not directly, through pacting. Humans don't have Covers to patch, and demons can extract relationships to convert into Cover elements, but they can't retrofit them back. (Might be grounds for an interesting homebrew Exploit or Interlock, though...)<br /> <br /> Indirectly, a demon could make a conditional pact where her end of the bargain involved hooking Rick up with Jesse's Girl through either conventional meddling and interference, or through other supernatural trickery (Embeds or Exploits or, say, why don't you buy the soul off Jesse's Girl behind Rick's back and then hook up with him yourself? Demonically awful thing to do to somebody).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T18:12:38-08:00","id":1051257,"title":"","content":"There is one method; if the mortal is a Stigmatic with Sleeve Integrator, a Demon could wear them as a temporary cover and then apply pacts to it as a patch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T18:31:57-08:00","id":1051796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1051257#post1051257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one method; if the mortal is a Stigmatic with Sleeve Integrator, a Demon could wear them as a temporary cover and then apply pacts to it as a patch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a homebrew merit based on/from Sleeve Integrator that lets a character &quot;trade&quot; their life for a Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:01:16-08:00","id":1056669,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a some photos they can show me of the <b>Demon: The Descent</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Hardcover Color Book (Premium Heavyweight)</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I bought it and got it but the book is still black and white and I don't know how it should look. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:34:17-08:00","id":1056705,"title":"","content":"I don't have an image on hand, but Demon's illustrations aren't full-spectrum color like the Vampire 2e core. They're single-tone purplish, like grayscale but with a color tint. Is that what you're seeing, or is it gray without a hint of purple?<br /> <br /> (The paper should also be somewhat thicker than you get if you order a grayscale book, as I recall. The grayscale paper is thin and rough, or at least, it was the last time I ordered one grayscale.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:51:36-08:00","id":1056748,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> says, its pretty close to gray even in full color. I'd check the headers for the Incarnations and Agendas. They have a pretty obvious purple-ish glow effect around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:59:05-08:00","id":1056897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1056705#post1056705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have an image on hand, but Demon's illustrations aren't full-spectrum color like the Vampire 2e core. They're single-tone purplish, like grayscale but with a color tint. Is that what you're seeing, or is it gray without a hint of purple?<br /> <br /> (The paper should also be somewhat thicker than you get if you order a grayscale book, as I recall. The grayscale paper is thin and rough, or at least, it was the last time I ordered one grayscale.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire has been the best, I get that not everyone likes the full color, but I like a healthy mix and I wish that the other books had it. IIRC it's the only one like that, the rest are all basically a monochrome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T01:35:28-08:00","id":1057493,"title":"","content":"Does an Implanted gadget need to look crude, or can you make it look relatively...well, for a lack of a better term? That is, have a metallic prosthetic arm that would have an unusually glossy finish and complex looking joints if it were installed with something like Halo? Or would the installing render the implant looking crude? I appreciate Implants are supposed to stand out, and that Exploited gadgets do so on their own. However, I am considering precision engineering one for a character down the line, and I would prefer they had something akin to a functioning (if advanced) prosthetic than a crude hand made of bars of metal and such.<br /> <br /> ...I really shouldn't be asking questions at 1:30 am. It makes my questions so much less comprehensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 03-03-2017, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T03:49:45-08:00","id":1057521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1057493#post1057493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does an Implanted gadget need to look crude, or can you make it look relatively...well, for a lack of a better term? That is, have a metallic prosthetic arm that would have an unusually glossy finish and complex looking joints if it were installed with something like Halo? Or would the installing render the implant looking crude? I appreciate Implants are supposed to stand out, and that Exploited gadgets do so on their own. However, I am considering precision engineering one for a character down the line, and I would prefer they had something akin to a functioning (if advanced) prosthetic than a crude hand made of bars of metal and such.<br /> <br /> ...I really shouldn't be asking questions at 1:30 am. It makes my questions so much less comprehensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it would have to be &quot;crude&quot;, per say, as long as it is obvious you have a cyber-arm there. Since such things don't (publically, commonly) exist, it will call out attention as something wrong/off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T01:06:02-08:00","id":1057966,"title":"","content":"Another few gadget questions here;<br /> <br /> Can you precision engineer a Lambda, be it first or second-order? If so, do the components need to be precision engineered themselves, or does that simply help the process along (since precision engineering grants 8-again in disassembling gadgets for such a purpose)? There's a Lambda I'd like to make that is precision engineered, and I'd prefer to know this coming in so I can get it done right.<br /> <br /> Finally, if you make a second-order Lambda, do you have the option of allowing it to use all three of the original gadgets' effects, as you could with the first order, or just the single combined effect? I can appreciate just a single effect being the end result, given how potent a second-order Lambda is by default. It's just the book doesn't specify if this is the case or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 03-04-2017, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T05:39:55-08:00","id":1058006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1057966#post1057966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another few gadget questions here;<br /> <br /> Can you precision engineer a Lambda, be it first or second-order? If so, do the components need to be precision engineered themselves, or does that simply help the process along (since precision engineering grants 8-again in disassembling gadgets for such a purpose)? There's a Lambda I'd like to make that is precision engineered, and I'd prefer to know this coming in so I can get it done right.<br /> <br /> Finally, if you make a second-order Lambda, do you have the option of allowing it to use all three of the original gadgets' effects, as you could with the first order, or just the single combined effect? I can appreciate just a single effect being the end result, given how potent a second-order Lambda is by default. It's just the book doesn't specify if this is the case or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precision Engineering a Lambda: I don't think either of the source Gadgets need to be Precision Engineered, as long as you go through the process for making the Lambda (but you are right - it helps if they are). It doesn't say anything about you can't, and I can't see a good reason why you shouldn't be able to.<br /> <br /> As for Lambda use 3 power, I'd say stick with a single combined effect, or at least cascading the effect, for clarity. If you want 3 Gadget's powers, just use 3 Gadgets. Unless you mean combo power + original power. That's more of an ST call, power wise. And I think it would depend on what the combo power does - if it synergizes well with the original effects, go for it, if the combined effect is too different or make the originals redundant, I'd say no.<br /> <br /> An example of the Embeds/Exploits and desired effect would help further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T11:41:06-08:00","id":1058104,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm a fan of Doctor Who, and after discussing it with the GM of the Demon game I'm in over how a TARDIS (or a reasonable fascimile of one) could be reached in-game, we decided that a Bolthole with a Lambda (and a lot of occult matrix knowledge) installed with Rip The Gates and Four Minutes Ago could do it.<br /> <br /> However, I'm wanting to make something less...potentially screw-everything-up-timewise, so I'm going to instead make it a Lambda of Rip The Gates and Quick Change, to allow the bolthole's exterior (the portal to the normal world) be removed and reconstructed elsewhere, while Quick Change would allow said portal to be reshaped into a new form provided that it doesn't change the mass of the existing portal (a cupboard cannot become a tanker truck, and vice versa). Their combined effect would be that the exterior can be moved from the inside, and it becomes something that fits in with the new area it is in, though the Lambda would be constructed so it would retain the two base effects (so I could move the portal without changing its exterior, or change the exterior without moving it). Should I make it a Second-Order Lambda, I'd include the Four Minutes Ago aspect, granting some time travel to it. I was wondering if this meant that the moving-without-changing and change-without-moving aspects could be retained. If not...well I have a time travelling shapeshifting bolthole. I can live with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry, that was a lot of nerding out there in a thread about asking questions and getting answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T12:34:54-08:00","id":1058114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1058104#post1058104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm a fan of Doctor Who, and after discussing it with the GM of the Demon game I'm in over how a TARDIS (or a reasonable fascimile of one) could be reached in-game, we decided that a Bolthole with a Lambda (and a lot of occult matrix knowledge) installed with Rip The Gates and Four Minutes Ago could do it.<br /> <br /> However, I'm wanting to make something less...potentially screw-everything-up-timewise, so I'm going to instead make it a Lambda of Rip The Gates and Quick Change, to allow the bolthole's exterior (the portal to the normal world) be removed and reconstructed elsewhere, while Quick Change would allow said portal to be reshaped into a new form provided that it doesn't change the mass of the existing portal (a cupboard cannot become a tanker truck, and vice versa). Their combined effect would be that the exterior can be moved from the inside, and it becomes something that fits in with the new area it is in, though the Lambda would be constructed so it would retain the two base effects (so I could move the portal without changing its exterior, or change the exterior without moving it). Should I make it a Second-Order Lambda, I'd include the Four Minutes Ago aspect, granting some time travel to it. I was wondering if this meant that the moving-without-changing and change-without-moving aspects could be retained. If not...well I have a time travelling shapeshifting bolthole. I can live with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry, that was a lot of nerding out there in a thread about asking questions and getting answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Retaining the original power makes sense then - it can alter variable things about itself (including appearance, temporal and dimensional position, etc.).<br /> <br /> One thing to note: you could always keep the side/secondary effect of 4 Minutes Ago - even if your actions are different, things still happened more or less as they &quot;did&quot; in the original timeline. So any time travel enabled by such a mechanism inherently would include &quot;Historical Inertia&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:25:33-08:00","id":1058392,"title":"","content":"The TARDIS is totally a Lare, it was one of the inspirations I had for them, along with generic evil genius loci and Charlie from Charlie's Angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:26:45-08:00","id":1058492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1058392#post1058392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The TARDIS is totally a Lare, it was one of the inspirations I had for them, along with generic evil genius loci and Charlie from Charlie's Angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Lare works well for a TARDIS, save for actual time travel and moving through dimensions...unless the aforementioned Lambda were installed into it somehow. Then that might work...<br /> <br /> Edit: To avoid double posting, I'm writing this here:<br /> <br /> When an Analyst goes Loud, they're able to combine Exploits into new ones. It's mentioned in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\">Storyteller's Extra Materials thread </a>on this form they're effectively interlocks for Exploits, so I wonder; should an Analyst survive the Going Loud, do they keep the new Exploit Interlock, or is that lost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 03-05-2017, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:09:44-08:00","id":1058594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1058492#post1058492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When an Analyst goes Loud, they're able to combine Exploits into new ones. It's mentioned in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\">Storyteller's Extra Materials thread </a>on this form they're effectively interlocks for Exploits, so I wonder; should an Analyst survive the Going Loud, do they keep the new Exploit Interlock, or is that lost?</div> </div> </div> </div>This <i>superpower </i>is only for when they're Going Loud - other Incarnations don't unlock all the Embeds for general use when not Loud, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:36:42-08:00","id":1058646,"title":"","content":"That does seem rather obvious in hindsight. Thanks Eremite. :-)<br /> <br /> ...I hate being the kid who never stops asking questions, but I have one regarding Lares, though I can't remember if I or someone else has asked this (my apologies if it has). Technically they're Exiles and Angels, albeit ones stuck in the forms of buildings. Can a Lare thus have the opportunity to fall and become a Demon in some form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:34:34-08:00","id":1059038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1058646#post1058646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does seem rather obvious in hindsight. Thanks Eremite. :-)<br /> <br /> ...I hate being the kid who never stops asking questions, but I have one regarding Lares, though I can't remember if I or someone else has asked this (my apologies if it has). Technically they're Exiles and Angels, albeit ones stuck in the forms of buildings. Can a Lare thus have the opportunity to fall and become a Demon in some form?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a thread for questions, don't feel bad. That's one I'd leave up to the individual ST, personally.Certainly there are no official rules or guidelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T20:35:14-08:00","id":1059328,"title":"","content":"How exactly are you supposed to build a Lambda?<br /> <br /> What determines the appearance, Virtue(s) and Vice(s) of a Patchwork Cover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:54:41-08:00","id":1059766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1059328#post1059328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly are you supposed to build a Lambda?<br /> <br /> What determines the appearance, Virtue(s) and Vice(s) of a Patchwork Cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Lambda is made by deconstructing two Gadgets, and then adding the pieces to an object to make a new Gadget with a new, amalgamated effect. However, the two effects need some synergy to work (so an effect that makes infinite bullets in a gun magazine won't work well combined with an effect that makes a device sound like someone in particular), they must be two different embeds/exploits, any limits in the two base gadgets will be present in the Lambda, and each effect that isn't an exploit must be related to the object it is being worked into like a normal Embeded gadget. You can't use One-Shots or Form gadgets for Lambdas however.<br /> <br /> A Patchwork Cover has the same Virtue(s) and or Vice(s) a Demon would have normally, unless said Demon has Living The Lie, which allows new covers to have a new Vice and or Virtue that the Demon can act on alongside their normal one. Their appearance is partially based on the pacts they're based from (taking someone's violent gang past will almost certainly involve any tattoos or scars they gained from that time), but otherwise a Demon has a lot of free reign with what they have; they can determine the gender of the cover, hair color, skin tone and even if they're related to a particular person (if they have the right pacts of course). As noted by Baroness Nerak, the existence of child Covers implies that either a Demon acts on a Soul Pact with a child, or they can craft them through Patchwork. There was one short story where a patchwork cover from a group of humans adopted some aspect of their appearances, but it's hard to say if that's the exception or the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T22:47:54-07:00","id":1062184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1051257#post1051257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one method; if the mortal is a Stigmatic with Sleeve Integrator, a Demon could wear them as a temporary cover and then apply pacts to it as a patch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Demon grant Supernatural Merits as part of a Pact? Because then you could do a Pact that grants Sleeve Integrator and go this route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T16:46:39-07:00","id":1062552,"title":"","content":"Do Angels and Exiles also have the ability to control their autonomous functions and tics and lie perfectly? Or is that exclusive to Demons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T17:26:02-07:00","id":1062563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1062184#post1062184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can a Demon grant Supernatural Merits as part of a Pact? Because then you could do a Pact that grants Sleeve Integrator and go this route.</div> </div> </div> </div>A normal pact can easily do that; Supernatural Merits are actually a benefit that Demons can easily grant, along with skill dots, and mundane merits. The Sleeve Integrator aspect is more for giving someone a child, or actually adding to their past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T21:01:12-07:00","id":1063108,"title":"","content":"Should 9-Again on Crafts gained from something like Professional Training work on rolls for creating Gadgets? Would Good Time Management work towards Gadget creation, either?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T05:30:28-07:00","id":1063188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1063108#post1063108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should 9-Again on Crafts gained from something like Professional Training work on rolls for creating Gadgets? Would Good Time Management work towards Gadget creation, either?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably no on the first - unless there is a field of professional Gadget Installers. I don't see why not on the second, though, since that just represents you are more organized and efficient than most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:53:53-07:00","id":1063652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1062552#post1062552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Angels and Exiles also have the ability to control their autonomous functions and tics and lie perfectly? Or is that exclusive to Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Demons. It's a puzzling development for most unchained and God Machine processes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T23:03:22-07:00","id":1066132,"title":"","content":"When a Demon goes up in Primum, say from their first Interlock, do they gain a permanent glitch in turn? The rules are vague, because it states that a Demon can get a permanent Glitch by going up in Primum...but the only place that references this fact is the Primum spreadsheet which shows what limits a Demon has per Primum level, and that only states 1 for when a Demon gets to Primum 6 and higher. I am very confused by this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:57:20-07:00","id":1066501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1066132#post1066132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Demon goes up in Primum, say from their first Interlock, do they gain a permanent glitch in turn? The rules are vague, because it states that a Demon can get a permanent Glitch by going up in Primum...but the only place that references this fact is the Primum spreadsheet which shows what limits a Demon has per Primum level, and that only states 1 for when a Demon gets to Primum 6 and higher. I am very confused by this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. The spreadsheet refers to permanent glitches gained from high Primum. The demon just gets those when Primum hits that number. You may still gain other permanent glitches normally such as by dramatically failing a compromise roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:12:07-07:00","id":1067245,"title":"","content":"How much can/will Demons do that isn't directly related to the God-Machine? In terms of story hooks. Not that I dislike the concept- I'm just thinking about getting the book and feeling out how versatile a Demon as a character in the wider <i>CofD</i> lineup is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:28:58-07:00","id":1067253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1067245#post1067245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much can/will Demons do that isn't directly related to the God-Machine? In terms of story hooks. Not that I dislike the concept- I'm just thinking about getting the book and feeling out how versatile a Demon as a character in the wider <i>CofD</i> lineup is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Agenda. Tempters have loads to do that has nothing to do with the God-Machine. They set up cover-trading agencies, build Hell in pocket universes, set up pacts upon pacts, mow their lawns, trim their hedges, look over their shoulders...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:40:56-07:00","id":1067324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1067253#post1067253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the Agenda. Tempters have loads to do that has nothing to do with the God-Machine. They set up cover-trading agencies, build Hell in pocket universes, set up pacts upon pacts, mow their lawns, trim their hedges, look over their shoulders...</div> </div> </div> </div>Inquisitors too. As you never know just what kind of information may be useful, better to just collect as much as you can.<br /> <br /> But depending on the Demon and their personal ties, it is just as easy as any other character. The only real limitation is refueling is harder without a G-M presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-23-2017, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:11:51-07:00","id":1067338,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies! I don't actually play any of the games (for now); I mostly just buy the books because I enjoy a good setting and a good set of rules. There's a certain pleasure in an interesting concept presented in a slick, attractive way.<br /> <br /> With that in mind: how awkward is the 1e/2e split manifested in Demon? I'm still not quite sure on how it's laid out t