angel use it to make an assistant out of the dead body of a demons close friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:59:38-07:00","id":1073748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1069187#post1069187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Demon fails the roll to use a One-Shot, is the gadget still used up, or do they get to keep trying until it works?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Me personally I would say it did get used up but it misfired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:21:00-07:00","id":1073757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1073747#post1073747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use Ex Nihilo on a dead body ? For example would it count as just an object after someone is dead and the soul is gone. I was thinking of having an angel use it to make an assistant out of the dead body of a demons close friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:40:55-07:00","id":1078305,"title":"","content":"A fairly simple questions- does the Hush embed only silence the sounds of violence specifically? I know it's broken if a weapon goes off, but if I just punch someone before kicking down a door, does it mask that or does the sound come back as soon as I stop attacking the victim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T23:37:04-07:00","id":1082528,"title":"","content":"Do you need to spend a dot of willpower when making One-Shot gadgets? The book doesn't mention that you do, but it could be for the sake of not repeating the same rules over and over. However, it doesn't sit well with me that a character can spend a dot of willpower (effectively an experience point) making a number of items they can only use once, and may not even work at all (read my earlier question on failing the roll to use a One-Shot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":".  Irrational bit on lore and early playr progression 04-24-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T00:50:59-07:00","id":1084919,"title":"","content":"Here's a question: can you, or can you not, reverse engineer a One-Shot? Flowers Of Hell goes both ways about it - there are specifically penalties for reverse engineering them on page 144, specifically &quot;If the gadget is a one-shot or a knock-off, each roll suffers a \u20132 penalty.&quot; and &quot;One-shots with Exploited effects do not cause as disastrous effects, but do release aetheric energies that might draw the attention of agents of the God-Machine at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.&quot;. However, on page 149 it says &quot;Due to their fragile and temporary nature, a demon can\u2019t reverse-engineer a one-shot gadget to learn the Embed or Exploit behind its creation, or to create a lambda.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know whether this is an errata issue, or whether there are more reasons to reverse engineer a gadget that just to learn its Embeds/Exploits or make a Lambda. I really like the book, but at the same time it's a mite confusing; read above for my other issue of confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-28-2017, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T16:17:31-07:00","id":1085617,"title":"","content":"If a Demon dies...can a mage raise the Demon with any type of magic? I'm not sure if this is a simple question - probably the most appropriate section for it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T16:19:52-07:00","id":1085618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1082528#post1082528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need to spend a dot of willpower when making One-Shot gadgets? The book doesn't mention that you do, but it could be for the sake of not repeating the same rules over and over. However, it doesn't sit well with me that a character can spend a dot of willpower (effectively an experience point) making a number of items they can only use once, and may not even work at all (read my earlier question on failing the roll to use a One-Shot).</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think you do - it sucks in terms of the cost; but I think it does. However - if you don't like that idea; you don't have to play with it - maybe it could pay some other resource for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T20:00:33-07:00","id":1085664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1085617#post1085617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Demon dies...can a mage raise the Demon with any type of magic? I'm not sure if this is a simple question - probably the most appropriate section for it though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deny the Reaper (Unmaking Death) may be able to accomplish this, but presents a judgment call to the Storyteller, as it raises the dead after their soul has moved on, thus requiring a replacement or leaving them soulless. Demons, who have no soul but Primum, may be able to function better than a resurrected human due to their lack of need for a soul. On the other hand, if the Primum gutters out on death and the sorcerer does not know some method to recall it, perhaps the demon would rise as a motionless husk without will or identity - or even as some new kind of broken exile, a demonic lifeform lacking the Primum to infuse it with its own meaning, and the connection to the God-Machine that fills an angel with purpose.<br /> <br /> Either way, the spell is not Lasting, so the resurrection could thereafter be dispelled at any time by a mage capable of the dispellation.<br /> <br /> An archmaster of Time could likely rewrite the timeline such that the demon's death never occurred. How much the God-Machine would resist, and how effective its resistance would be, is uncertain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T23:25:38-07:00","id":1087024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1085618#post1085618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally think you do - it sucks in terms of the cost; but I think it does. However - if you don't like that idea; you don't have to play with it - maybe it could pay some other resource for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>One reason I feel a Demon shouldn't require a dot of experience, outside of the aforementioned issue of paying for only a chance of something limited in quantity working, is that it also runs in line with how gadget creation goes. To make a gadget, a Demon needs to spend a dot of willpower to cement it into the world...but a gadget can exist without it, though it simply fades by the end of the scene and falls apart. One-Shots, meanwhile, are gadgets that are designed to only work once; they're not designed to take the rigors of use and aether, and thus don't require being cemented into the world. A regular gadget, however, <i>is</i> meant to go on, and it needs that extra bit to keep it from collapsing on itself.<br /> <br /> Think of it as a cabin versus a makeshift shelter; the cabin is designed to keep being used and can be impressive for its workmanship, and it may well outlive its creator while seeing continued use. A makeshift shelter, meanwhile, can outlive its creator, but only if it doesn't whether proper use, and it may still fail if left for too long. Once the weather gets it, it's done. Shelters like that can be remade, but they still cost resources. A cabin will stand the test of time, given proper care.<br /> <br /> Analogies aren't my strong suit when I'm tired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T01:01:23-07:00","id":1087043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1087024#post1087024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One reason I feel a Demon shouldn't require a dot of experience, outside of the aforementioned issue of paying for only a chance of something limited in quantity working, is that it also runs in line with how gadget creation goes. To make a gadget, a Demon needs to spend a dot of willpower to cement it into the world...but a gadget can exist without it, though it simply fades by the end of the scene and falls apart. One-Shots, meanwhile, are gadgets that are designed to only work once; they're not designed to take the rigors of use and aether, and thus don't require being cemented into the world. A regular gadget, however, <i>is</i> meant to go on, and it needs that extra bit to keep it from collapsing on itself.<br /> <br /> Think of it as a cabin versus a makeshift shelter; the cabin is designed to keep being used and can be impressive for its workmanship, and it may well outlive its creator while seeing continued use. A makeshift shelter, meanwhile, can outlive its creator, but only if it doesn't whether proper use, and it may still fail if left for too long. Once the weather gets it, it's done. Shelters like that can be remade, but they still cost resources. A cabin will stand the test of time, given proper care.<br /> <br /> Analogies aren't my strong suit when I'm tired.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Analogies on point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I get your opinion of it - I think you can argue either side of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T02:03:15-07:00","id":1089044,"title":"","content":"Another gadget question; if you precision engineer a gadget, it is effectively considered overclocked. Does that mean that if you precision engineer a lambda, you suffer three points of lethal damage and gained the surveyed condition every time you use it? Or is precision engineering's benefits just similar to overclocking, not actually doing so?<br /> <br /> Subsequently, can you overclock a precision engineereed gadget?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T17:26:56-07:00","id":1089482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1087024#post1087024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One reason I feel a Demon shouldn't require a dot of experience, outside of the aforementioned issue of paying for only a chance of something limited in quantity working, is that it also runs in line with how gadget creation goes. To make a gadget, a Demon needs to spend a dot of willpower to cement it into the world...but a gadget can exist without it, though it simply fades by the end of the scene and falls apart. One-Shots, meanwhile, are gadgets that are designed to only work once; they're not designed to take the rigors of use and aether, and thus don't require being cemented into the world. A regular gadget, however, <i>is</i> meant to go on, and it needs that extra bit to keep it from collapsing on itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to avoid the possibility of permanent loss of EXP for one use items, you could simply refund the willpower dot when the one-shot is consumed, or perhaps grant a persistent condition that consumes the dot of willpower and is resolved by the loss/use of the item. It's a reasonable (if house-ruled) extension of Sanctity of Merits/Construction rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1089044#post1089044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another gadget question; if you precision engineer a gadget, it is effectively considered overclocked. Does that mean that if you precision engineer a lambda, you suffer three points of lethal damage and gained the surveyed condition every time you use it? Or is precision engineering's benefits just similar to overclocking, not actually doing so?<br /> <br /> Subsequently, can you overclock a precision engineereed gadget?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules say that Precision Engineering and Overclocking are different classes of benefits/drawbacks for gadgets, just that when you're performing Precision Engineering you just pick a boon from the same table - There's no reason to suggest that a Precision Engineered Lambda would have the same drawback as an Overclocked Lambda outside of being extraordinarily difficult to create compared to even the standard Lambda creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:04:08-07:00","id":1089618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1089482#post1089482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to avoid the possibility of permanent loss of EXP for one use items, you could simply refund the willpower dot when the one-shot is consumed, or perhaps grant a persistent condition that consumes the dot of willpower and is resolved by the loss/use of the item. It's a reasonable (if house-ruled) extension of Sanctity of Merits/Construction rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some fair ideas. I'm not entirely sure how that would work if multiple gadgets were made, or if used as currency to procure other services/resources though. Seems like it could get very...book-keepy. Still, pretty good way to make them viable without allowing a Demon to simply spend scene after scene after scene just making the silly things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules say that Precision Engineering and Overclocking are different classes of benefits/drawbacks for gadgets, just that when you're performing Precision Engineering you just pick a boon from the same table - There's no reason to suggest that a Precision Engineered Lambda would have the same drawback as an Overclocked Lambda outside of being extraordinarily difficult to create compared to even the standard Lambda creation. </div> </div> </div>Precision Engineering a Lambda would be something of a benchmark for how potent a Demon is, wouldn't it? Preferably it would be done with Good Time Management, as well as a workshop to speed up the time (and maybe with an Efficiency embed used for good measure), but if you could get an exceptional success or two off it, that could make it doable in a reasonable amount of time...<br /> <br /> Anyways, thanks for making that distinction between Precision Engineering and Overclocking. I tend to find Flowers of Hell confusing, but very inspiring at the same time. That also answers the question of if someone can Precision Engineer an Infrastructure gadget - it'd just be a finicky gadget to use because it'd get a drawback every time it's used. Then again, given it'd come with two benefits, it'd be worth hauling out for the right circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T00:27:13-07:00","id":1092256,"title":"","content":"Just started reading Demon and im enjoying it so far. I have a quick question on Angel-Jacking though. It says its a extended and contested roll and both parties need a number of successes equal to what is going to be the angels cover. It says the first to get to this number wins, but what happens on a tie, If both parties get say 5 successes (example in the story at the end) on their first roll, what happens? Will it really come down to who rolled their dice/counted first?<br /> <br /> Ive searched the forum for answers on extended &amp; contested rolls but haven't found an answer yet. I think there might be some examples in vampires blood sorcery rules but i dont have those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T00:38:01-07:00","id":1092259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1092256#post1092256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just started reading Demon and im enjoying it so far. I have a quick question on Angel-Jacking though. It says its a extended and contested roll and both parties need a number of successes equal to what is going to be the angels cover. It says the first to get to this number wins, but what happens on a tie, If both parties get say 5 successes (example in the story at the end) on their first roll, what happens? Will it really come down to who rolled their dice/counted first?<br /> <br /> Ive searched the forum for answers on extended &amp; contested rolls but haven't found an answer yet. I think there might be some examples in vampires blood sorcery rules but i dont have those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normal contested rolls have both parties reroll, so I'd guess that in an extended contested roll that first tied roll just counts as void and the actors continue rolling. <br /> <br /> This is just my intuition, though, so take it with plenty of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T01:04:55-07:00","id":1092264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1092259#post1092259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Normal contested rolls have both parties reroll, so I'd guess that in an extended contested roll that first tied roll just counts as void and the actors continue rolling.<br /> <br /> This is just my intuition, though, so take it with plenty of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, seems abit unfair if one person gets 8 successes and the other gets 5 they both reached the goal at the same time. Both even got exceptional successes too, Maybe keep rolling till one person is the angels cover ahead of the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T04:23:08-07:00","id":1092304,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness, page 130:<br /> &quot;If it\u2019s a tie or neither side gets any successes, the effort fails altogether or successive attempts (see p. 132) may be made in subsequent turns, if appropriate.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, if running with 100% second edition rules there's actually no rules for ties. My group uses the rule of &quot;defender's advantage&quot; to determine what happens just to reduce rerolls. In this case it would be the angel who wins and the demon fails to jack the cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T21:26:06-07:00","id":1092656,"title":"","content":"The action is both <i>contested</i> as well as <i>extended</i>.<br /> <br /> The contested action rules from<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChroD, Pg 69:</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When two people fight over a specific goal, they engage in a contested action. You roll your dice pool and the Storyteller (or other player) rolls the dice pool for the other party. <b>Whoever rolls the most successes is the victor.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>And from the next page under its own heading on<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;ChroD, Pg 70:</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contested Actions<br /> When two characters are competing, and you only need to know who comes out on top, use a contested action. In a contested action, each player rolls a pool for their character (such as an Attribute + Skill pool), and <b>the character for whom the most successes are rolled wins the contest.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So unless the roll that got over the line for both sides tied in successes, the one with the highest number of successes that reached the goal wins. If it does tie, you could rule as either Defender wins the contested action (likely the Angel in this case) or just roll again next round to resolve the equal number of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T23:41:35-07:00","id":1092674,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, it's no secret I love the idea of a Demon making a TARDIS in-game, and it's been enthused by the good Eremite that Lares were at the very least inspired by them (and that one would be the Doctor's TARDIS if he were a Demon).<br /> <br /> This leads to a pair of questions:<br /> <br /> Is infrastructure usually/capable of being bigger on the inside without that being its sole feature, outside of the use of boltholes? If yes;<br /> <br /> Are Lares bigger on the inside? Or are they limited to the natural structure/mass/dimensions that an otherwise mundane building would have?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to figure out how to make bigger-on-the-insideness function in the game (In My Pocket is winning out), if only to make a Lare...well, less conspicuous when travelling. It's all well and good to have a TARDIS!Lare that's a bar, but an entire bar vanishing and re-appearing elsewhere overnight tends to get brows raised. If it had another body/casing it could transit into, or at least reside in, which was a good deal smaller, or at least capable of changing size if not mass...<br /> <br /> I'm not aware of any size changing embeds/exploits is all I'm saying (Quick Change probably wouldn't suffice for it).<br /> <br /> I really need to stop posting stuff at midnight. It makes things very confusing to re-read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T03:09:04-07:00","id":1092715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1092674#post1092674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not aware of any size changing embeds/exploits is all I'm saying (Quick Change probably wouldn't suffice for it).</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a few Demonic Form powers for that, though. Or you could just create a homebrew Exploit for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T08:03:35-07:00","id":1092810,"title":"","content":"Can demons see into twilight ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:48:55-07:00","id":1092999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1092810#post1092810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can demons see into twilight ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by default, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T02:22:14-07:00","id":1093162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1092810#post1092810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can demons see into twilight ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It is a known weakness. I suppose one in the right Ephemeral Cover could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T14:59:38-07:00","id":1093423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1092810#post1092810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can demons see into twilight ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a sparse, niche ability for demons. Ephemeral Cover allows a demon to adopt a Cover as a Twilit ghost or spirit (though it affords no ability to see into Twilight on its own, meaning you have to get ghosts or spirits to manifest so that you know where to swing to eat them and make the Cover). Decoy allows the demon to project an astral Twilight form similarly to vampiric Auspex. I think the only published ability to see into Twilight while remaining material is the Ghost Sight demonic form ability, and that's assuming you're allowing material from the Demon Translation Guide. Clever use of very flexible abilities like Show of Power or Play on Words might situationally be able to look or move into Twilight.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind &quot;Twilight&quot; is a category of several distinct states, and a power generally specifies which &quot;layer&quot; it looks or moves into. None of the above powers directly expose Twilit angels. Even the Sense the Angelic power doesn't do this, although it can detect their supernatural activity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T01:02:44-07:00","id":1093573,"title":"","content":"Question: How intelligent/self-autonomous is the avatar produced by the Terrible Avatar exploit? Do you give it instructions and send it off, or do you maintain a constant mental link? Or is it felt as being an extension of yourself? Also, with the exceptional success option of the avatar knowing all of your embeds, does that include any known interlocks? Running my first Demon the Descent game, and would like to know. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13154-freric","user":"Freric","date":".  Edit: Added in the bit about interlocks. 05-17-2017, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13154-freric","name":"Freric","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T17:25:28-07:00","id":1094351,"title":"","content":"Q.<br /> Just to get an idea of it - are there cases when would one apply design principles of embeds? Like for example with the embed: Just Bruised: Let's say someone fires an RPG or uses some supernatural attack expected to do massive damage, but the user sees that it does literally nothing but scratch the demon: when would it be recommended to invoke a compromise roll with an embed? Is it only for specific embeds that have compromise stated as a result of failure/dramatic failure: or would there be other purposes where you would deem it just?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T17:50:48-07:00","id":1094365,"title":"","content":"I'd say whenever they are unusual. Embed are supposed to be subtle. When they no longer are, I'd say the machine takes interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:27:21-07:00","id":1094414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1094365#post1094365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say whenever they are unusual. Embed are supposed to be subtle. When they no longer are, I'd say the machine takes interest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. I appreciate your POV on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T18:54:37-07:00","id":1095710,"title":"","content":"This is a minor question but why does cover cost 2xp to raise (DtD pg. 89) but take 3 cover xp to raise through pacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T19:42:14-07:00","id":1095724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1095710#post1095710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a minor question but why does cover cost 2xp to raise (DtD pg. 89) but take 3 cover xp to raise through pacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normal XP can be used for many things, whereas cover beats are not only just used for Cover, but they can be accrued via pacts fairly easily. The respective costs make Cover hard to boost passively and pacts require some effort, but expensive enough that a player with a glut of normal experience points can't easily boost a low Cover, and won't want to either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T20:18:28-07:00","id":1095732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1095710#post1095710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a minor question but why does cover cost 2xp to raise (DtD pg. 89) but take 3 cover xp to raise through pacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're looking at the pre-errata version of the book, probably; comparing the two PDFs side-by-side shows that that's one of the things that was fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1095724#post1095724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal XP can be used for many things, whereas cover beats are not only just used for Cover, but they can be accrued via pacts fairly easily. The respective costs make Cover hard to boost passively and pacts require some effort, but expensive enough that a player with a glut of normal experience points can't easily boost a low Cover, and won't want to either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cover explicitly can't be raised with normal Experiences by default; there's a sidebar specifically addressing this on page 115.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T20:31:03-07:00","id":1095737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1095732#post1095732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because you're looking at the pre-errata version of the book, probably; comparing the two PDFs side-by-side shows that that's one of the things that was fixed.<br /> <br /> Cover explicitly can't be raised with normal Experiences by default; there's a sidebar specifically addressing this on page 115.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I should redownload my copy then, ty for that I didn't realize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T08:52:51-07:00","id":1095931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1093573#post1093573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: How intelligent/self-autonomous is the avatar produced by the Terrible Avatar exploit? Do you give it instructions and send it off, or do you maintain a constant mental link? Or is it felt as being an extension of yourself? Also, with the exceptional success option of the avatar knowing all of your embeds, does that include any known interlocks? Running my first Demon the Descent game, and would like to know. Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it is more like an extension of self, kind of like the Alibi embed. Whether it gains access to interlocks or not, I'm not sure, but I would er on the side of no. Interlocks are a potent and personal thing which, as far as I can tell, can't be replicated beyond something like Show Of Power. That really is up to you though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T15:55:30-07:00","id":1096513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1095931#post1095931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interlocks are a potent and personal thing which, as far as I can tell, can't be replicated beyond something like Show Of Power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show Of Power explicitly can't replicate Demon abilities, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T16:35:25-07:00","id":1096523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1096513#post1096513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Show Of Power explicitly can't replicate Demon abilities, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T12:12:59-07:00","id":1097210,"title":"","content":"Does Reality Enforcement disable gadgets as well? Gadgets are based on Embeds and Exploits and were created with aether, but they themselves don't require aether to function (beyond an exploited gadget's upkeep costs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T04:23:19-07:00","id":1097482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1097210#post1097210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Reality Enforcement disable gadgets as well? Gadgets are based on Embeds and Exploits and were created with aether, but they themselves don't require aether to function (beyond an exploited gadget's upkeep costs).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say they are disabled too - Reality Enforcement blocks all G-M related activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T18:14:34-07:00","id":1099702,"title":"","content":"I admit I haven't been through the 15 pages of this thread so maybe my question has been asked (and answered) before but there it is: I've just downloaded D:tD' screen and it's coming as two pages portrait. How do you guys turn this into a screen ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T01:57:53-07:00","id":1100374,"title":"","content":"I cannot remember if this has been clarified or outright said but can pacts grant supernatural merits? I know they cannot grant template related powers to a template character but from what I can see supernatural merits (as long as they are given to mortals) are fair game. Its a minor detail that will either make a character's plan easier or harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T03:27:36-07:00","id":1100386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1100374#post1100374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot remember if this has been clarified or outright said but can pacts grant supernatural merits? I know they cannot grant template related powers to a template character but from what I can see supernatural merits (as long as they are given to mortals) are fair game. Its a minor detail that will either make a character's plan easier or harder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also interested in an official answer - I've asked this before, too.<br /> <br /> (I've been running under the logic/response that nothing says you <i>can't</i>, and they are just Merits, after all.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T04:13:39-07:00","id":1100399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1100386#post1100386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also interested in an official answer - I've asked this before, too.<br /> <br /> (I've been running under the logic/response that nothing says you <i>can't</i>, and they are just Merits, after all.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cult merit implies that at 5 points the source of their supernatural merits are their pacts with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T08:48:55-07:00","id":1100457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1100386#post1100386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also interested in an official answer - I've asked this before, too.<br /> <br /> (I've been running under the logic/response that nothing says you <i>can't</i>, and they are just Merits, after all.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The only limitation I would maybe give it would be like show of power where you need to see it to replicate it/know it exists. Just, an official answer would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:21:18-07:00","id":1116793,"title":"","content":"I have a player who is using Rip the Gates to enter the astral of someones mind and then they want to open a gate way into the Abyss or Inferno in that persons mind. My question is what do you think should happen to that human &gt;?<br /> <br /> Also can get this this thread Pinned ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:37:57-07:00","id":1116796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1116793#post1116793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a player who is using Rip the Gates to enter the astral of someones mind and then they want to open a gate way into the Abyss or Inferno in that persons mind. My question is what do you think should happen to that human &gt;?<br /> <br /> Also can get this this thread Pinned ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Rip the Gates can't open gateways to the Abyss or the Inferno, nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:12:08-07:00","id":1116857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1116796#post1116796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that Rip the Gates can't open gateways to the Abyss or the Inferno, nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No it can open gate ways to anywhere it just gave a list of common places you would go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:40:53-07:00","id":1116866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1116857#post1116857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No it can open gate ways to anywhere it just gave a list of common places you would go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, read it again. Rip the Gates opens portals to the Hedge, Shadow, Underworld and/or Astral Realms. It does not do anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T00:00:09-07:00","id":1117114,"title":"","content":"Does a Demon innately know they're in a Splinter reality? Or do they need to connect the dots if they unknowingly enter one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T04:58:34-07:00","id":1117148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1116866#post1116866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, read it again. Rip the Gates opens portals to the Hedge, Shadow, Underworld and/or Astral Realms. It does not do anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did it says &quot;The character opens the gateway into the realm of her choice&quot; at no point does it say it only opens to the ones on the list. I thinks more convenient to just list a few and let the GM pick what other realm might be in there game. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T05:13:50-07:00","id":1117152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1117148#post1117148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I did it says &quot;The character opens the gateway into the realm of her choice&quot; at no point does it say it only opens to the ones on the list. I thinks more convenient to just list a few and let the GM pick what other realm might be in there game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description of the exploit specifically says it can open a gate to those four planes, and then the section you quote says to &quot;(see the sidebar for some brief information on these realms)&quot;, where it then says it can only open a rift to certain planes and then says &quot;In brief, the realms that demons can reach with the Rip the Gates Exploit are:&quot; then it provides a list of &quot;realms that demons can reach&quot; with a brief description for each.<br /> <br /> Rip the Gates can only take you to the realms it says it can take you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T05:20:27-07:00","id":1117155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1117152#post1117152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description of the exploit specifically says it can open a gate to those four planes, and then the section you quote says to &amp;quot;(see the sidebar for some brief information on these realms)&amp;quot;, where it then says it can only open a rift to certain planes and then says &amp;quot;In brief, the realms that demons can reach with the Rip the Gates Exploit are:&amp;quot; then it provides a list of &amp;quot;realms that demons can reach&amp;quot; with a brief description for each.<br /> <br /> Rip the Gates can only take you to the realms it says it can take you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, it should be noted, a ST can explicitly override this in their games (especially if some of those Realms don't exist, or have alternatives). But RAW, yeah, just those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:06:12-07:00","id":1117230,"title":"","content":"Either way I recommend not allowing this exploit to open gates to either Lower Depths, since they are supposed to be hard to get to, and the Abyss that is not a place as much as it is a phenomenon that can take the form of unimaginable creatures that simultaneously are alternate realities that never existed (unlike splinters that are realities that do exist in alternate timelines). Other exploits might very well deal with the Inferno or the Abyss, but I think those should be specific.<br /> Rip the Gates, on the other hand, focuses on the four realms that are naturally connected to the material and at least three of them have naturally occuring portals to them without requiring the intervention of an entity to establish the portal. (I'm not sure about the Hedge, though. I'm not familiar enough with Changeling to tell.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:42:58-07:00","id":1117254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1117230#post1117230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way I recommend not allowing this exploit to open gates to either Lower Depths, since they are supposed to be hard to get to, and the Abyss that is not a place as much as it is a phenomenon that can take the form of unimaginable creatures that simultaneously are alternate realities that never existed (unlike splinters that are realities that do exist in alternate timelines). Other exploits might very well deal with the Inferno or the Abyss, but I think those should be specific.<br /> Rip the Gates, on the other hand, focuses on the four realms that are naturally connected to the material and at least three of them have naturally occuring portals to them without requiring the intervention of an entity to establish the portal. (I'm not sure about the Hedge, though. I'm not familiar enough with Changeling to tell.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hedge too, there are natural paths into it that comeone could stumble into accidently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T17:39:55-07:00","id":1117513,"title":"","content":"So back to the question what would happen doing that ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T18:20:04-07:00","id":1117523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1117513#post1117513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So back to the question what would happen doing that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A gate to the Inferno should be considered a Hellmouth. Infernal demons can try to break through by rolling Power minus 3. Any demons that succeed in entering the Oneiros will most likely do whatever they can to steer the host to the sins that the various demons resonates with. Strong ones could try to outright possess the host. All this is my interpretation of Inferno so you could just read that book if you want to know more.<br /> <br /> A gate to the Abyss is a thing that might not be possible. As I said the Abyss isn't a realm. It's a collection of stuff that can be summed up as &quot;anti-reality&quot;. Rather, the demon should target an Annunaki since those beings are the sub-realms of the Abyss. In that case you'd have an Abyssal Verge. And Abyssal Verges works under the rule of ST fiat. (Yes, that's basically what the Mage core book says.) In general it takes time for Acamoth and Gulmoth and other Abyssal entities to actually cross Verges so it's unlikely that the person being subject to this will be affected at all.<br /> But!, once the Verge has been opened, however briefly, the Annunaki might start probing and opening it again from the other side. Or it might be quicker than usual and force an Acamoth through it while it's still open. In those cases the person's Oneiros will start becoming warped (reflecting in weird behaviour) but exactly how is impossible to say. It's the Abyss, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T00:54:01-07:00","id":1123795,"title":"","content":"Hello, me again, and with another gadget question; what kind of limitations does one have for the triggers/conditions for a gadget to be used by someone? For example, I've read somewhere that a gadget can be keyed to only work for a particular cover and or when it is night-time. I'm presuming a Demon cannot make the gadget have the condition that a non-Angel is using it though.<br /> <br /> Could permission from one or two individals, such as the creator and or a trusted individual, be a condirion for a gadget to be usable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T03:40:28-07:00","id":1123820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1123795#post1123795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, me again, and with another gadget question; what kind of limitations does one have for the triggers/conditions for a gadget to be used by someone? For example, I've read somewhere that a gadget can be keyed to only work for a particular cover and or when it is night-time. I'm presuming a Demon cannot make the gadget have the condition that a non-Angel is using it though.<br /> <br /> Could permission from one or two individals, such as the creator and or a trusted individual, be a condirion for a gadget to be usable?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds about right. Especially if that permission is formalized in a document, pass-phrase, ceremony, or other observable. I think there is only a problem with intangibles (like &quot;only to someone that doesn't mean me ill&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T01:12:44-07:00","id":1125816,"title":"","content":"Are dedicated workspaces (areas that a Demon can make a gadget faster) completely immobile, tied to a single spot such as a basement? Or can they be mobile too?<br /> <br /> Also, if a Demon hits an exceptional success on Aetheric shielding, do they need to pay aether if their next gadget is precision engineered? It simply says &quot;the demon doesn\u2019t need to spend Aether the next time she creates a gadget.&quot; It sounds a mite exploitable that way.<br /> <br /> Also also (apologies), for Infrastructure workspaces, it says &quot;For each dot above 2 the character has in the Merit, choose one of the following benefits in addition to the normal time reduction benefits of using a workspace.&quot; However, the merit only goes to 3 dots; is this simply to say that a single infrastructure workspace can only have one of the benefits listed? This seems weird because the wording of the benefits implies it should go higher, otherwise the ones that grant Angels an easier time finding the workplace should have a flat +3 bonus, not &quot; gain +1 die per dot in the Merit on any angelic detection rolls&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 08-07-2017, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:59:11-07:00","id":1128113,"title":"","content":"If a Demon takes a new Cover what rating this Cover would be ?<br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:12:01-07:00","id":1128121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1128113#post1128113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Demon takes a new Cover what rating this Cover would be ?<br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on the method used to get it. Patchwork Covers are constructed wholesale from Cover Experiences gained from Pactbound mortals, Covers called in from a Soul Pact have a bare minimum rating of the demon's Primum plus their successes on a Wits + Manipulation roll made at the point of assumption, and angel-jacking a Cover gets you whatever rating would equate to what the angel would have gotten if you hadn't interfered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:31:32-07:00","id":1128263,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot,<br /> <br /> This another one: what prevents a Demon from gaining a lot of skill points and merits, signing pacts only expending Willpower points ?<br /> For instance, I trade a better career for you in exchange for your uncanny knack at poetry (expression 4). It would only cost me WP points and I will get a new skill at 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:37:40-07:00","id":1128265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1128263#post1128263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot,<br /> <br /> This another one: what prevents a Demon from gaining a lot of skill points and merits, signing pacts only expending Willpower points ?<br /> For instance, I trade a better career for you in exchange for your uncanny knack at poetry (expression 4). It would only cost me WP points and I will get a new skill at 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons cannot gain Skills or Merits from Pacts. I could trade you for your reputation as a poet, but that's all I'd get - a reputation. It would not actually teach me how to do poetry, which is a pretty significant hole in my Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 08-12-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:41:33-07:00","id":1128266,"title":"","content":"Ok I though I missed something on this. So, if I got a friend through a Pact it won't give me the Ally Merit. That's much more sensible.<br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:51:29-07:00","id":1128272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1128266#post1128266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I though I missed something on this. So, if I got a friend through a Pact it won't give me the Ally Merit. That's much more sensible.<br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>You get Legend in order to stay in cover tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:56:14-07:00","id":1133341,"title":"","content":"Can we get this pinned so people can put their simple questions in here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T15:39:55-07:00","id":1133969,"title":"","content":"Quick Question regarding On the Mend. Would a Demon-Blooded count as an ordinary human for the purposes of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T16:25:26-07:00","id":1133981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1133969#post1133969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick Question regarding On the Mend. Would a Demon-Blooded count as an ordinary human for the purposes of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes. Offspring try to present as &quot;just a normal human&quot;, so them rapid-healing would be odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T04:13:39-07:00","id":1134108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1133969#post1133969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick Question regarding On the Mend. Would a Demon-Blooded count as an ordinary human for the purposes of it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes they would","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T00:25:14-07:00","id":1139120,"title":"","content":"How would Monkeywrencher work for Analysts? It allows the user to penalize embeds that either match their Incarnation or a known key, but Analysts don't have any embeds that match their Incarnation - would they instead be allowed to penalize exploits? Otherwise, they're left only penalizing embeds that match their keys (which is very limited) or Angel numen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T01:59:40-07:00","id":1139133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1139120#post1139120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Monkeywrencher work for Analysts? It allows the user to penalize embeds that either match their Incarnation or a known key, but Analysts don't have any embeds that match their Incarnation - would they instead be allowed to penalize exploits? Otherwise, they're left only penalizing embeds that match their keys (which is very limited) or Angel numen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go exploits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T10:08:52-07:00","id":1139474,"title":"","content":"So, Knockout Punch and Vampires. Can you succesfully use Knockout Punch on a Vampire (Or a Promethean, or a Sin-Eater), since the sources on those are conflicting in regards to whether or not their &quot;Can't be knocked out&quot; applies only to damage or overall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T10:39:09-07:00","id":1139481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1139474#post1139474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Knockout Punch and Vampires. Can you succesfully use Knockout Punch on a Vampire (Or a Promethean, or a Sin-Eater), since the sources on those are conflicting in regards to whether or not their &quot;Can't be knocked out&quot; applies only to damage or overall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking I don't think vampires have a &quot;can't be knocked out&quot; rule; they have a &quot;don't become unconscious from bashing damage&quot; rule. But they also don't strictly speaking seem to have a rule that says they can't get the flu, either, so take that with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> Either way Knockout Punch isn't a martial arts technique based on precisely striking nerve clusters or anything like that - it's a supernatural ability. And like most of those, it only specifies what it does, not how. I'd personally rule that a vampire's inherent resilience entitles it to a Clash of Wills, but I'm pretty liberal with what I'm willing to call a Clash over, and depending on your personal understanding of vampirism, the God-Machine and Knockout Punch in particular you could rule anywhere from &quot;they're immune&quot; to &quot;they have no special resistance&quot; and be justified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T20:13:13-07:00","id":1139619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1139474#post1139474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Knockout Punch and Vampires. Can you succesfully use Knockout Punch on a Vampire (Or a Promethean, or a Sin-Eater), since the sources on those are conflicting in regards to whether or not their &quot;Can't be knocked out&quot; applies only to damage or overall?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the vamp got Resilience, let it clash, if not, subtract Stamina as the sidebar explains.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T19:29:15-07:00","id":1139817,"title":"","content":"Didn't the devs say once that Knockout Punch was really only meant to work on mortals to stop players from trivially dealing with the likes of Angels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 09-12-2017, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T20:38:18-07:00","id":1139825,"title":"","content":"The Storyteller's Guide specifically states Sin Eaters can't be knocked out by Knock-Out Punch, so that's one thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T21:12:49-07:00","id":1139826,"title":"","content":"Ah, no, I'm remembering incorrectly. Matt said that he (normally) wouldn't let it work on an Angel. He also cast doubt on whether it would work on Vampires, or any other &quot;don't get knocked out&quot; splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T05:03:37-07:00","id":1139879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1139825#post1139825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Storyteller's Guide specifically states Sin Eaters can't be knocked out by Knock-Out Punch, so that's one thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its a base power for Sin Eaters. Vampires don't have that. For me I would say yes Knock out punch can work on a vampire but it would come down to the roll to figure out if the subject gets knocked out. <br /> <br /> Also remember the simple story telling rule. Is it important ? If not let the power work with out a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T00:29:00-07:00","id":1145462,"title":"","content":"So, I have a question; what does happen when a pact is destroyed, such as the medium it's written on being burned? I've heard from a group I'm in saying that it not only reverses any benefits from either side but it also causes backlash against the Demon...but I can't find rules on that. I may just not be looking in the right places though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T06:10:08-07:00","id":1145503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Descent pg 191, 192</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a contract is destroyed, the pact is immediately nullified. The human loses all benefits instantly, even if it would kill her (such as by losing extra Stamina while seriously injured) or leave her in a terrible situation. Riches are destroyed or stolen, assets are frozen, physical gifts immediately wither. The demon likewise loses all benefits of the pact, usually pieces of Cover taken from the mortal\u2019s life. These come crashing back into the life they left \u2014 an abusive boyfriend immediately goes back to his ex-lover without much more of an explanation than a wicked hangover. This can also cause problems for a demon\u2019s Cover, considering that only those directly affected by the pact have had their memories altered. In the case of a broken pact, the participating mortal remembers everything. If a demon has patched part of a mortal\u2019s life into his Cover, destruction of the pact immediately results in loss of a dot of that Cover\u2019s rating. The demon must also check for a permanent glitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it looks like it is mostly and issue for the Demon if it has been integrated into one of their Covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T18:36:26-07:00","id":1145693,"title":"","content":"There's also this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD Core p.194</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a permanent pact is nullified by the destruction of its contract, there is a mystic backlash that resonates through a demon\u2019s Primum. This inflicts a number of bashing damage equal to the demon\u2019s Primum rating in a painful, head-splitting burst of pain. The destruction of many such contracts at once could even kill a demon, yet another reason they closely guard their sealed pacts</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T19:57:15-07:00","id":1145957,"title":"","content":"Question regarding the operation of Deep Pockets: does it actually teleport the object you're picturing to your pocket-space, or does it make a clone of the object? (Using the core book's chainsaw example, does the chainsaw disappear from the hardware store when you pull it from your pocket? And if it does, what happens if a human walking by happens to see it vanish?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T11:44:19-07:00","id":1146114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1145957#post1145957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question regarding the operation of Deep Pockets: does it actually teleport the object you're picturing to your pocket-space, or does it make a clone of the object? (Using the core book's chainsaw example, does the chainsaw disappear from the hardware store when you pull it from your pocket? And if it does, what happens if a human walking by happens to see it vanish?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The human says &quot;WTF?&quot;.<br /> <br /> The description says that it is <i><b>that</b></i> chainsaw in the example so yes it vanishes from the hardware store and appears with you. Though the exceptional success says it becomes the ideal one, so something must happen to it during transit?<br /> <br /> Speaking of deep pockets. Can you deep pocket items other people have on them? Like take guns of people pointing them at you? Or does the item have to be on its own &amp; unused?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 10-02-2017, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T13:34:47-07:00","id":1146153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1146114#post1146114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of deep pockets. Can you deep pocket items other people have on them? Like take guns of people pointing them at you? Or does the item have to be on its own &amp; unused?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go with your intepretation (which I agree with) then... yes. The power has no stipulation that says the item has to be unguarded.<br /> <br /> Though I would probably rule that blatantly teleporting a gun out of a mortal's hand constitutes an additional Compromise on top of the normal one for the Exploit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T14:24:55-07:00","id":1146161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1146153#post1146153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we go with your intepretation (which I agree with) then... yes. The power has no stipulation that says the item has to be unguarded.<br /> <br /> Though I would probably rule that blatantly teleporting a gun out of a mortal's hand constitutes an additional Compromise on top of the normal one for the Exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could make it into a Gadget.<br /> <br /> Though my favorite variant on the trick uses the Embed Cuckoo's Egg to replace the bullets in their magazines with blanks or defective rounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T23:42:43-07:00","id":1146269,"title":"","content":"This is perhaps less simple than ideal, but how does the God-Machine detect aether? Someone on a Discord chat asked the question when the topic of Compromise came up (among a lengthy argument at how Interference did more than it does), but then the detection of aether came up and it kind of stumped me, since the books states the Machine can't directly detect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T00:00:26-07:00","id":1146272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1146269#post1146269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is perhaps less simple than ideal, but how does the God-Machine detect aether? Someone on a Discord chat asked the question when the topic of Compromise came up (among a lengthy argument at how Interference did more than it does), but then the detection of aether came up and it kind of stumped me, since the books states the Machine can't directly detect it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book states that <i>angels</i> can't directly detect it through the same sort of channel as aetheric resonance, which means a universal portable tracking method is mercifully not something demons have to worry about just yet.<br /> <br /> The books <i>also</i> make it pretty clear that exposure to Aether-based processes can create stigmatics or give rise to disasters of supernatural scope and quality \u2014 messing with facilities can result in storms and earthquakes, for instance \u2014 and the Machine is explicitly detail-oriented and capable of employing cryptids and other non-angelic means of tracking Aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T05:45:42-07:00","id":1146307,"title":"","content":"It also doesn't really need to. The Machine can detect Compromise just fine, and its minions can ferret out demons in all the usual ways - turning allies, uncovering inconsistent personal information, setting traps, infiltrating Agencies, cutting deals, broadcasting threats, following rumors about that one guy whose gun spewed blood and fired blasts of hellfire etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T06:59:46-07:00","id":1146323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1146307#post1146307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also doesn't really need to. The Machine can detect Compromise just fine, and its minions can ferret out demons in all the usual ways - turning allies, uncovering inconsistent personal information, setting traps, infiltrating Agencies, cutting deals, broadcasting threats, following rumors about that one guy whose gun spewed blood and fired blasts of hellfire etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The machine doesn't have a &quot;compromise sense&quot; it detects low covers by context (assuming you don't have an angel witness your transformation and reported your ass) such as &quot;hey, that guy keep pulsing a EMP field with each breath he takes&quot; or &quot;Isn't it funny Mike can't literally say three words without cussing?&quot; or &quot;Well, that's a nice set of fish scales on your lower back, Cindy, just like Arthur's.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 10-03-2017, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T07:24:08-07:00","id":1146328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1146323#post1146323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The machine doesn't have a &quot;compromise sense&quot; it detects low covers by context (assuming you don't have an angel witness your transformation and reported your ass) such as &quot;hey, that guy keep pulsing a EMP field with each breath he takes&quot; or &quot;Isn't it funny Mike can't literally say three words without cussing?&quot; or &quot;Well, that's a nice set of fish scales on your lower back, Cindy, just like Arthur's.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Failing a Compromise roll explicitly attracts the attention of the God-Machine:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Demon: The Descent p. 115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Failure:</b> The character\u2019s Cover has been weakened. The God-Machine or its agents have a sense of her general whereabouts and activity. </div> </div> </div> </div>Also I'm pretty sure angels can't &quot;report&quot; demons, or at least that what they do report isn't spread around much. There are plenty of examples in the literature of demons getting sniffed out by angels and not being immediately outed to every hunter angel in the world. The God-Machine might be immeasurably vast and privy to staggering amounts of data, but it doesn't share much (if anything) with the ground-level grunts except the exact thing it needs them to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T01:05:29-07:00","id":1146587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1146328#post1146328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm pretty sure angels can't &amp;quot;report&amp;quot; demons, or at least that what they do report isn't spread around much. There are plenty of examples in the literature of demons getting sniffed out by angels and not being immediately outed to every hunter angel in the world. The God-Machine might be immeasurably vast and privy to staggering amounts of data, but it doesn't share much (if anything) with the ground-level grunts except the exact thing it needs them to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in those cases it was less &quot;can't report a Demon&quot; and more &quot;can report them, but has the situation underway and doesn't feel the need to&quot;. Angels are busy beings, and pulling others off-duty willy-nilly is only going to delay the God-Machine's plans further. In a confrontation an Angel will typically be stronger than the Demon it is facing against, so if it feels it can take the Demon on it has no reason to report them unless either party needs to escape. Granted, in two of the stories I remember reading involving an Angel fighting a Demon, the Demon ended up winning by puling some pretty serious sacrifices (usually by Going Loud), so we didn't see the consequences of a Demon escaping while being seen and thus reportable. The only time an Angel met a Demon it knew to be a Demon, that was convincing it to turn itself in rather than outright dragging it in kicking and screaming...though even in that case it was implied the Angel in question was close to falling anyways.<br /> <br /> Another way to look at it is that Angels perhaps don't have an innate, wireless connection to the God-Machine. They might require form powers to communicate in such a matter, or maybe with mundane communication methods via phoneline or through radio communications...or indeed through wifi. I don't remember the books stating it definitively, save for the Storyteller Guide having a cryptid that fed on Demons and could actually trick Angels into falling by jamming their communications with the God-Machine and inflicting unease on said Angel. Then again, as proven above, I've proven to have a tough time remembering certain factoids that are front and center.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T02:29:46-07:00","id":1146593,"title":"","content":"It goes even further than that. Angels <i>always</i> feel like they have the situation under control. They don't call for help from other angels because they are incapable of envisioning failure. They literally do not comprehend that a demon (or any other factor) could be anything other than a speedbump on the way to completing the mission, and so they never feel the need to request assistance. The only time an angel actually sends out a distress call is just before it is destroyed, and even that is to preserve the mission, not the angel. This is from the ST guide.<br /> <br /> The exact nature of their communication with the God-Machine is a little less clear. Iirc they are generally described as having a constant channel to the Machine, but not as being in constant communication. The salient point though is that whatever data the God-Machine collects from its angels, it definitely doesn't share indiscriminately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T01:38:10-07:00","id":1147345,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the comprehensive answers.<br /> <br /> I do have another question though; should Gadgets be considered for the sanctity of merits? While one doesn't pay experience for them directly, the willpower dot does cost one experience to regain. Therefore, couldn't they be used as a means of acquiring merits by way of trading, merits which would count under the sanctity of merits? Or is a gadget exempt due to the willpower dot's cost not falling under paying an experience dot for the gadget itself, thus meaning if the gadget is stolen and or destroyed by an NPC the experience dot is effectively lost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-06-2017, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T03:13:27-07:00","id":1147354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1147345#post1147345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the comprehensive answers.<br /> <br /> I do have another question though; should Gadgets be considered for the sanctity of merits? While one doesn't pay experience for them directly, the willpower dot does cost one experience to regain. Therefore, couldn't they be used as a means of acquiring merits by way of trading, merits which would count under the sanctity of merits? Or is a gadget exempt due to the willpower dot's cost not falling under paying an experience dot for the gadget itself, thus meaning if the gadget is stolen and or destroyed by an NPC the experience dot is effectively lost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Gadgets do offer other advantages over possessing the Embeds/Exploits directly - they <i>can</i> be given to others, do things the base power can't (Near Field effects), and most important for Exploited Gadgets, they don't cause Compromise (inherently).<br /> <br /> For temporary loss (like loaning it out), I wouldn't do anything. But if they are sinking XP into Gadgets and loose them, You could &quot;refund&quot; them 1XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-06-2017, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T18:41:15-07:00","id":1151810,"title":"","content":"Another gadgets question here; if a Demon makes a gadget that has an effect that relies on Primum, be it a modifier for the effect proper or through precision engineering, what happens if another supernatural uses it? A stigmatic probably wouldn't gain much benefit, even if they are under the effect of Soul Brand, but what about a Changeling and her Wyrd score, or Sin Eater's Psyche? Would those stand in for Primum in those cases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T02:54:56-07:00","id":1151888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1151810#post1151810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another gadgets question here; if a Demon makes a gadget that has an effect that relies on Primum, be it a modifier for the effect proper or through precision engineering, what happens if another supernatural uses it? A stigmatic probably wouldn't gain much benefit, even if they are under the effect of Soul Brand, but what about a Changeling and her Wyrd score, or Sin Eater's Psyche? Would those stand in for Primum in those cases?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could lock in the Primum-based effect as a constant for one of the Gadget's limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T15:56:38-07:00","id":1152051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1151888#post1151888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you could lock in the Primum-based effect as a constant for one of the Gadget's limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, but I'm pondering if, say, a Changeling gets a gadget that is precision engineered to work on additional targets up to the user's Primum. Would that be up to her Wyrd, then, or just the single target the gadget normally targets since Changelings don't have Primum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T17:37:06-07:00","id":1152069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1152051#post1152051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is true, but I'm pondering if, say, a Changeling gets a gadget that is precision engineered to work on additional targets up to the user's Primum. Would that be up to her Wyrd, then, or just the single target the gadget normally targets since Changelings don't have Primum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if made by a Demon with 4 Primum, it work on 4 targets whether the Demon uses it, or a Changeling, or a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T18:08:19-07:00","id":1152080,"title":"","content":"Seems like something that depends on the exact cosmology of your version of the setting, and is therefore ultimately a question for your ST.<br /> <br /> My default position would be that while they're mechanically similar, the various supernatural traits represent very different things. Wyrd is not Primum is not Gnosis, and under normal circumstances a Blood Potency 5 vampire doesn't &quot;count as&quot; having Primum 5 any more than a mortal does. However, if I wanted to entwine the various mythologies, I would make exceptions. For example, it says something interesting about the nature of the universe if a werewolf's Primal Urge can't substitute for Primum - but a promethean's Azoth <i>can</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T22:01:46-07:00","id":1152108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1152080#post1152080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like something that depends on the exact cosmology of your version of the setting, and is therefore ultimately a question for your ST.<br /> <br /> My default position would be that while they're mechanically similar, the various supernatural traits represent very different things. Wyrd is not Primum is not Gnosis, and under normal circumstances a Blood Potency 5 vampire doesn't &quot;count as&quot; having Primum 5 any more than a mortal does. However, if I wanted to entwine the various mythologies, I would make exceptions. For example, it says something interesting about the nature of the universe if a werewolf's Primal Urge can't substitute for Primum - but a promethean's Azoth <i>can</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I like that idea; it may even be appropriate for certain gadgets, based on how or what they function on, to react to different supernaturals in terms of allowing substitutions for Primum. The cellphone that steals the location of anyone calling it wouldn't allow a Vampire to use its Primum based effects, but if that gadget were to purify blood, well, that could be a different matter...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T10:34:29-08:00","id":1165895,"title":"","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> So, page 43 says that many demons 'let their hair down' and spend some private time in demon form every day. It also brings up neutral locations where demons gather to hang out in demon form. This is a really cool idea, but as far as I can tell, the actual rules really don't support this - switching to demonic form always results in a compromise roll, regardless of witnesses, and there's no way to mitigate that for game-balance reasons. I can't imagine demons damaging their covers just to stretch and shoot the breeze. Did I miss something?<br /> <br /> Another, related question: Does this imply that you must roll compromise every single time your cover does something 'out of character', even if there are no witnesses or you are not recognized? That would seriously hamstring most espionage missions, because doing any sort of spy stuff is out-of-character for nearly every cover. Surely that isn't the intent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:45:13-08:00","id":1165935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1165895#post1165895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there,</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1165895#post1165895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, page 43 says that many demons 'let their hair down' and spend some private time in demon form every day. It also brings up neutral locations where demons gather to hang out in demon form. This is a really cool idea, but as far as I can tell, the actual rules really don't support this - switching to demonic form always results in a compromise roll, regardless of witnesses, and there's no way to mitigate that for game-balance reasons. I can't imagine demons damaging their covers just to stretch and shoot the breeze. Did I miss something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are ways to create &quot;dead zones&quot; that block the G-M's senses. I think there is a bar in Seattle that has a kind of cryptoflora that does so. Certain kinds of Suborned Infrastructure might as well, or Near-Field (or Lambda) Gadgets with Interference. The ST could also just rule that &quot;no witnesses, no compromise&quot;, if there isn't any realistic risk. Boltholes are also safe spaces, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1165895#post1165895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another, related question: Does this imply that you must roll compromise every single time your cover does something 'out of character', even if there are no witnesses or you are not recognized? That would seriously hamstring most espionage missions, because doing any sort of spy stuff is out-of-character for nearly every cover. Surely that isn't the intent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is every time you are &quot;spotted&quot; doing something out of character, regardless of whether the observers know it is out of character. I think of it link the G-M has installed spyware in every mortal and has it all hooked up to pattern recognition and escalation algorithms. Joe the Security Guard might not know that this strange woman is Sally the Waitress (actually a Demon) and thus shouldn't be breaking into a chemical plant or be an expert marksman, but the Machine's security apparatus notes it and flags it as irregular. (Maybe - that's what the Compromise Check is for)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T20:08:19-08:00","id":1166010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1165895#post1165895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there,<br /> <br /> Another, related question: Does this imply that you must roll compromise every single time your cover does something 'out of character', even if there are no witnesses or you are not recognized? That would seriously hamstring most espionage missions, because doing any sort of spy stuff is out-of-character for nearly every cover. Surely that isn't the intent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it doesn't actually matter whether there are witnesses to see you violating your Cover (well, witnesses impose a penalty to the compromise roll). You can be completely alone in a windowless room and still risk compromise.<br /> <br /> But pay attention to the emphasis in the wording. Compromise risks result from behavior that is <i>grossly</i> out of character for your Cover. If you imagine a hypothetical invisible observer watching you perform a given action, the invisible observer isn't somebody who's been tracking your every move and knows just what your Cover personality would and wouldn't do in every situation. It's more like the invisible observer is familiar with you in passing, or in the broad strokes, knows roughly what kind of person you are, and is not particularly on guard or looking for contradictions. If something you do would still clearly strike <i>this sloppy</i> hypothetical observer as definitely out of place, that's when you roll for compromise. Your Cover frays, whether there are witnesses or not, when your actions contradict the tentpole characteristics that define who that Cover is, because those known values and relationships are what gird your Cover and make it strong.<br /> <br /> A kind grade school teacher sneaking into the back room is behaving oddly, but not contradicting his very identity. But drawing a semiautomatic and spray-n-prayin' a room full of strangers isn't just an unexpected puzzle piece, it's one that outright doesn't fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 12-07-2017, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T02:26:55-08:00","id":1166040,"title":"","content":"The reason why you still risk violating your cover without witnesses is because the God-Machine doesn't just use word of mouth/mindreading/etc. to gather information. It's a multidimensional system which might be sensing the emotional wavelengths and suddenly note a dip when you go into demon form because you no longer have hormones hyping you up. Or might detect how probability just changed or some change in the region's quantum fields because of a quantum entity just made a massive shift in reality. Or it could do any number of different mystical methods to divine a flow of aether being emitted from their primium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T03:42:06-08:00","id":1166047,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your responses.<br /> <br /> What are Near-Field gadgets and Interference? I can't find them in the book. Are they in a supplement?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166010#post1166010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you imagine a hypothetical invisible observer watching you perform a given action, the invisible observer isn't somebody who's been tracking your every move and knows just what your Cover personality would and wouldn't do in every situation. It's more like the invisible observer is familiar with you in passing, or in the broad strokes, knows roughly what kind of person you are, and is not particularly on guard or looking for contradictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand and accept this in theory, but I have trouble coming to terms with the idea that even the sloppiest observer would think that...<br /> ... breaking and entering of strangers' property<br /> ... clandestine meetings with sketchy strangers<br /> ... long term stalking of total strangers<br /> ... theft of non-profitable objects<br /> ... sabotage of unseen metaphysical patterns<br /> ... interrogations about clandestine operations of any sort<br /> ... every single conversation about the God Machine and Angels<br /> <br /> ... aren't all <i>gross</i> violations of the following covers: corporate drone, school teacher, lawyer, doctor, college student, manager, waiter, plumber, construction worker, factory worker, airline pilot, etc.<br /> <br /> Compromise rolls are inconvenient even on a <i>success</i>, so by the book a demon trying to do double-life secret agent stuff is constantly being penalized for doing what the game is actually about. Heck, even approaching mortals to make the all important pacts leaves the demon shaken or glitchy every single time.<br /> <br /> This leads to some possibly unfortunate choices I'd have to make as a GM:<br /> 1) conclude that some covers are just more useful than others: criminal, vagrant, <i>actual</i> spy, lunatic, detective, occultist, satanic priest, etc.<br /> 2) Interpret the guidelines so forgivingly that compromise checks start to feel arbitrary.<br /> 3) Possibly take Vent0's suggestion and ignore the constant panopticon effect altogether, thereby drastically house-ruling the game and possibly leading to unforeseen game balance consequences down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","user":"MatterofTact","date":". 12-08-2017, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T05:46:02-08:00","id":1166065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166047#post1166047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your responses.<br /> <br /> What are Near-Field gadgets and Interference? I can't find them in the book. Are they in a supplement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Near-Field Gadgets are discussed in Flowers of Hell. Basically they are one-off effects from Embeds and Exploits. Their powers aren't covered in the source Embed/Exploit, but they are conceptually close enough. (Such as a switch/key/whatever being unnoticeable when surrounded by similar objects - Lost In The Crowd, but changed to apply to objects instead of people)<br /> <br /> Interference is in the Mundane Embeds section, though it helps throw Angels off your scent after a failed Compromise Roll. Flowers of Hell has Context Matters, where mortals participants can actually help your Compromise roll. I also made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=839313#post839313\">Blackout</a>, which eliminates the risk mortal observers pose for a time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166047#post1166047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand and accept this in theory, but I have trouble coming to terms with the idea that even the sloppiest observer would think that...<br /> ... breaking and entering of strangers' property<br /> ... clandestine meetings with sketchy strangers<br /> ... long term stalking of total strangers<br /> ... theft of non-profitable objects<br /> ... sabotage of unseen metaphysical patterns<br /> ... interrogations about clandestine operations of any sort<br /> ... every single conversation about the God Machine and Angels<br /> <br /> ... aren't all <i>gross</i> violations of the following covers: corporate drone, school teacher, lawyer, doctor, college student, manager, waiter, plumber, construction worker, factory worker, airline pilot, etc.<br /> <br /> Compromise rolls are inconvenient even on a <i>success</i>, so by the book a demon trying to do double-life secret agent stuff is constantly being penalized for doing what the game is actually about. Heck, even approaching mortals to make the all important pacts leaves the demon shaken or glitchy every single time.<br /> <br /> This leads to some possibly unfortunate choices I'd have to make as a GM:<br /> 1) conclude that some covers are just more useful than others: criminal, vagrant, <i>actual</i> spy, lunatic, detective, occultist, satanic priest, etc.<br /> 2) Interpret the guidelines so forgivingly that compromise checks start to feel arbitrary.<br /> 3) Possibly take Vent0's suggestion and ignore the constant panopticon effect altogether, thereby drastically house-ruling the game and possibly leading to unforeseen game balance consequences down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, B&amp;E, secret meeting, stalking, and petty theft aren't outside the range of human behaviors. Eliminate the &quot;strangers&quot; part, and all become understandable - your Ring might simply need to manufacture probable cause for their Covers' actions before-hand.<br /> <br /> Remember that Demons often speak in codes anyways. What is unusual about acquaintances chatting about former employers, or the weather?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T14:27:34-08:00","id":1166160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166065#post1166065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Near-Field Gadgets are discussed in Flowers of Hell. Basically they are one-off effects from Embeds and Exploits. Their powers aren't covered in the source Embed/Exploit, but they are conceptually close enough. (Such as a switch/key/whatever being unnoticeable when surrounded by similar objects - Lost In The Crowd, but changed to apply to objects instead of people)<br /> <br /> Interference is in the Mundane Embeds section, though it helps throw Angels off your scent after a failed Compromise Roll. Flowers of Hell has Context Matters, where mortals participants can actually help your Compromise roll. I also made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=839313#post839313\">Blackout</a>, which eliminates the risk mortal observers pose for a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166065#post1166065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, B&amp;E, secret meeting, stalking, and petty theft aren't outside the range of human behaviors. Eliminate the &quot;strangers&quot; part, and all become understandable - your Ring might simply need to manufacture probable cause for their Covers' actions before-hand.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember that Demons often speak in codes anyways. What is unusual about acquaintances chatting about former employers, or the weather?</div> </div> </div> </div>While both of these suggestions are cool in a cinematic sense, I suspect that at the table they would be too cumbersome to be kept up for long.<br /> <br /> Besides, the very act of conspiring with a cell to manufacture probable cause is in itself grossly out of character.<br /> <br /> So, I'm getting the feeling from the responses that many people don't really want to run compromise rules as strictly as the book would indicate and that's fine, no one would want me to as a GM either. I'm tempted to house-rule the &quot;out of character&quot; bit so it specifically must be witnessed, that way player characters are motivated to use disguises, masks, stealth, tradecraft, etc.<br /> <br /> I must also conclude that page 43 is leftover from an earlier draft when demonic form wasn't an auto-compromise. That's a shame, but I guess there must have been a game balance or thematic reason for it. I suppose the infinite aether could be abused, or demons might be tempted to skip living among humans and just create a hell-on-earth underground.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T15:05:57-08:00","id":1166169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166160#post1166160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm getting the feeling from the responses that many people don't really want to run compromise rules as strictly as the book would indicate</div> </div> </div> </div>The book indicates the &quot;grossly out of character&quot; category is comparable to human breaking points and gives <i>suddenly displaying doctorate-level knowledge of physics </i>and <i>casually torturing someone</i> as examples. Further, the Mundane Embed that specifically interacts with that class of compromise refers to them as &quot;actions <i>antithetical to</i> that Cover,&quot; which combines with the breaking point comparison to suggest they're based on a Cover being an identity with broadly known principles that could be brought into doubt by their violation. There's a reason the bonus Skill Specialty the Unchained template gives you is specifically something that could risk compromise, to say nothing of how much less risky partial transformation is. It's not a death-sentence on its own, but it adds up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I must also conclude that page 43 is leftover from an earlier draft when demonic form wasn't an auto-compromise. </div> </div> </div>Or that, y'know, a transient glitch is a thing that demons are comfortable dealing with for a couple of hours or a couple of days as a thing that serves as an expression of their individual nature in a context where they're attempting to be comfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T15:51:41-08:00","id":1166180,"title":"","content":"Satchel, I'm not sure if you're agreeing or disagreeing with my witness-based compromise interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166169#post1166169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or that, y'know, a transient glitch is a thing that demons are comfortable dealing with for a couple of hours or a couple of days as a thing that serves as an expression of their individual nature in a context where they're attempting to be comfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>A transient glitch if you're lucky enough to pass the roll. Failure brings much harsher consequences, and failure is likely with that -3 penalty. I have a hard time imagining any demon hard enough to survive the hazards of the fall in the first place casually taking such a risk on a regular basis, let alone a group of them doing so as described on page 43.<br /> <br /> While I'm on the subject, does the transformation penalty of -3 apply to partial transformations AFTER the bonus for features unused? I find it odd that partial transformations could be the most forgiving of all compromises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T18:04:51-08:00","id":1166211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166180#post1166180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel, I'm not sure if you're agreeing or disagreeing with my witness-based compromise interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm disagreeing, as I should hope would be obvious from the fact that mortal breaking points are not usually so severe as to make meeting peaceably with strangers a comparable risk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A transient glitch if you're lucky enough to pass the roll. </div> </div> </div>There's a Mundane Embed that specifically bumps the consequences of failure up to the consequences for success. The odds of a cautious demon who still wants to spend time in their demonic form not learning it are low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Failure brings much harsher consequences, and failure is likely with that -3 penalty. </div> </div> </div>A permanent glitch is inherently less likely to be severe and there is, again, a Mundane Embed whose whole purpose is buffering Cover loss from supernatural activity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I'm on the subject, does the transformation penalty of -3 apply to partial transformations AFTER the bonus for features unused? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't at all. It lacks the restorative benefits of full transformation and is more costly and awkward to invoke on the fly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find it odd that partial transformations could be the most forgiving of all compromises. </div> </div> </div>As with the option to take glitches instead of Conditions, it encourages demons to spend time in mostly-human form with subtler giveaways whose neglect can result in untenable situations. Besides which, a roll is a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T04:17:42-08:00","id":1166264,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have the page number for that place in Seattle that apparently dampens compromise?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166211#post1166211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm disagreeing, as I should hope would be obvious from the fact that mortal breaking points are not usually so severe as to make meeting peaceably with strangers a comparable risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just noticed something: I only have the 1st edition World of Darkness core book and the Demon core book and while I've looked, I don't think either of them contains these Integrity and Breaking Point rules. The 1st ed book has the Humanity trait rules, but I don't think that's comparable to what you're talking about. I'm afraid I don't have the examples to look at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166211#post1166211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Mundane Embed that specifically bumps the consequences of failure up to the consequences for success. The odds of a cautious demon who still wants to spend time in their demonic form not learning it are low.<br /> <br /> A permanent glitch is inherently less likely to be severe and there is, again, a Mundane Embed whose whole purpose is buffering Cover loss from supernatural activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about Interference, it can only mitigate conditions and glitches. your cover still loses a dot, and that's not chicken feed. Still, I suppose their is potential for a very carefully-worded gadget.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166211#post1166211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with the option to take glitches instead of Conditions, it encourages demons to spend time in mostly-human form with subtler giveaways whose neglect can result in untenable situations. Besides which, a roll is a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>But partial transformation can grant very significant bonuses to the roll, so turning your arms into bio-mecha claws with no witnesses is actually much safer for your cover than shooting somebody in the back with no witnesses. That still strikes me as odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T04:54:36-08:00","id":1166266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166264#post1166264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just noticed something: I only have the 1st edition World of Darkness core book and the Demon core book and while I've looked, I don't think either of them contains these Integrity and Breaking Point rules. The 1st ed book has the Humanity trait rules, but I don't think that's comparable to what you're talking about. I'm afraid I don't have the examples to look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>They got cut from the Demon appendix for space. They get reincluded in the Demon Player's Guide, but you can also get them just fine in the free <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">God-Machine Rules Update</a> PDF (which is otherwise mostly the same text from the Demon appendix).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166264#post1166264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But partial transformation can grant very significant bonuses to the roll, so turning your arms into bio-mecha claws with no witnesses is actually much safer for your cover than shooting somebody in the back with no witnesses. That still strikes me as odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the rules make partial transformation compromise rolls too lenient, the bonus you get is huge even before you start getting into Terrible Form.<br /> <br /> But as for compromise risks for acting out of character, give it a spin in play, it's fine. You don't need compromise risks happening too frequently from character behavior, given a) they carry enough of a dramatic punch when they do happen and b) they emerge from other triggers too. Remember that mortal humans discovering more about your nature is distinct from the out-of-character clause. <i>That's</i> the compromise trigger that stops you from talking about angels where you can be heard, not the one about being antithetical to your Cover identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T09:44:00-08:00","id":1166295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166264#post1166264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about Interference, it can only mitigate conditions and glitches. your cover still loses a dot, and that's not chicken feed. Still, I suppose their is potential for a very carefully-worded gadget.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about Interference and Occam's Razor, respectively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But partial transformation can grant very significant bonuses to the roll, so turning your arms into bio-mecha claws with no witnesses is actually much safer for your cover than shooting somebody in the back with no witnesses. That still strikes me as odd. </div> </div> </div>Calling up and dismissing form abilities costs you at least two Aether that you're not getting back without risk, if you're at the level where you can burn that much Aether freely you're also at the level where losing Cover is less of a concern, and arguably the best use of that bonus is to circumvent the penalties observers apply.<br /> <br /> And yes, of course transforming into a human with supernatural parts in complete privacy is safer for your Cover than doing something that affects another person \u2014 <i>actually using</i> that overtly supernatural element to affect somebody is going to be substantially less good for you, and in the meantime you've taken a hit to the resource that you have to tempt fate to recover in the name of saving the resource that you can recover by living quietly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166266#post1166266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the rules make partial transformation compromise rolls too lenient, the bonus you get is huge even before you start getting into Terrible Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be worth remembering that the net modifier for compromise rolls is explicitly capped at +/-5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T16:56:48-08:00","id":1166361,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or can a Stigmatic with Potent Blood never naturally heal any Lethal damage they take (without medical treatment), since they take additional lethal damage at the exact same rate due to the merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T17:35:50-08:00","id":1166366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1166295#post1166295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be worth remembering that the net modifier for compromise rolls is explicitly capped at +/-5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The total modifier for 'circumstances' explicitly shouldn't exceed +/-5. The partial transformation section then goes on to detail a roll receiving a +6 bonus. While it's reasonable to consider those bonuses 'circumstantial', and to assume the +6 modifier was before taking into account any existing penalties, etc (and hence not a final number) it's not hard to understand why many people don't interpret it that way at a glance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T03:24:13-08:00","id":1172958,"title":"","content":"I'm working on compiling a full list of Aether sources and curious to see if I've missed any and I do not feel it is worth its own post as it is a rather simple question. What I currently have is:<br /> <br /> Infastructure, Subhorned infastructure merit, angelic Dross, essance drain technology, sun's bounty process, full demon form transformation, stigmatic with Potent Blood, Devour infastructure exploit and demon to demon transfer / stockpiles.<br /> <br /> Are there any that I have missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T15:03:51-08:00","id":1173092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1172958#post1172958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on compiling a full list of Aether sources and curious to see if I've missed any and I do not feel it is worth its own post as it is a rather simple question. What I currently have is:<br /> <br /> Infastructure, Subhorned infastructure merit, angelic Dross, essance drain technology, sun's bounty process, full demon form transformation, stigmatic with Potent Blood, Devour infastructure exploit and demon to demon transfer / stockpiles.<br /> <br /> Are there any that I have missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going Loud? Unless you count that as Demonic Form Transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T19:19:01-08:00","id":1173898,"title":"","content":"This has probably been answered somewhere, I swear I've read an answer, but my google fu has failed me but anyways, Question: Can angels use/have embeds and demon form abilities? Obviously, it makes sense I feel but I do not know if there is anything saying its a valid choice.<br /> <br /> If not, would allowing an angel to do so be too much? I know as ST I can do 'anything' but I still try to keep the scales closer to balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T10:02:47-08:00","id":1174056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1173898#post1173898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been answered somewhere, I swear I've read an answer, but my google fu has failed me but anyways, Question: Can angels use/have embeds and demon form abilities? Obviously, it makes sense I feel but I do not know if there is anything saying its a valid choice.<br /> <br /> If not, would allowing an angel to do so be too much? I know as ST I can do 'anything' but I still try to keep the scales closer to balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure some Angels have actual Embeds listed for their Numina. You might to enhance them, since Embeds are supposed to be pale shadows of what Angels are able to accomplish.<br /> <br /> For Form abilities, sure, give them such where necessary and not covered under existing Numina (or Ephemeral caveat). <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a> has that Angelic Form Abilities thread, if you want to just outfit all of them with Form Abilities (making them serious terrors, between Influences, Numina, Form Abilities, and Incepts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-07-2018, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T09:48:41-08:00","id":1174298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1173898#post1173898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been answered somewhere, I swear I've read an answer, but my google fu has failed me but anyways, Question: Can angels use/have embeds and demon form abilities? Obviously, it makes sense I feel but I do not know if there is anything saying its a valid choice.<br /> <br /> If not, would allowing an angel to do so be too much? I know as ST I can do 'anything' but I still try to keep the scales closer to balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> said. Per RAW, the abilities and Angel has are all intended to be covered with their Numina, Influences, Incepts, general Ephemeral-ness (Extra limbs for example would likely just be a factor in how their body is and you rule it as needed), and them knowing the way the world works do to their connection to the God-Machine. They don't need Numina to do somethings because the world already does those thing, it just takes knowing how to do it; this is represented in Demons with Embeds, but with Angels their connection to the God-Machine makes it innate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T10:05:40-08:00","id":1177875,"title":"","content":"Another few questions on somethings I hadn't concidered before. If you take +1 primum at character creation you have the option to buy a second coversion for a Merit dot. Is this second cover a 7 dot cover as well? The wording I feel suggests it but that feels off to me so I'm not sure. <br /> Next, would you be able to chose this for a ephemeral cover, as long as you had the exploit of course. I think it should since characters at gen are not always truly fresh off the boat so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T11:21:33-08:00","id":1177895,"title":"","content":"Yes, I would assign that second Cover with seven dots, and yes, if you also had Ephemeral Cover in chargen I would allow it to be a ghost or spirit Cover. Seems reasonable to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:14:44-08:00","id":1178634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1177875#post1177875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another few questions on somethings I hadn't concidered before. If you take +1 primum at character creation you have the option to buy a second coversion for a Merit dot. Is this second cover a 7 dot cover as well? The wording I feel suggests it but that feels off to me so I'm not sure.<br /> Next, would you be able to chose this for a ephemeral cover, as long as you had the exploit of course. I think it should since characters at gen are not always truly fresh off the boat so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Genius idea. I totally missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:27:21-08:00","id":1178638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1178634#post1178634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Genius idea. I totally missed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help. As I've looked at it more I have realized too that you can also improve a ephemeral cover through pacts. You can make pacts with supernatural creatures after all, you just buy the connections between spirits (possibly infiltrate a spirit court) and since a supernatural being investigating your cover doesn't fray it (as long as they do not tell a mortal) you only have to worry about conflict if discovered. Ephemeral cover after all does not call out being unable to be improved with pacts - it is just easy to not see the possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T08:45:52-08:00","id":1179839,"title":"","content":"If I make a pact for part of a person's life (e.g. their dog), do I need to immediately graft that element onto one of my Covers, or can I just leave it be, hanging around somewhere in the ether until I want to use it or trade it to someone else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T10:50:08-08:00","id":1179874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1179839#post1179839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I make a pact for part of a person's life (e.g. their dog), do I need to immediately graft that element onto one of my Covers, or can I just leave it be, hanging around somewhere in the ether until I want to use it or trade it to someone else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think keeping it around to trade is fine, but I don't know what happens to the dog in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T10:54:53-08:00","id":1179876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1179874#post1179874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think keeping it around to trade is fine, but I don't know what happens to the dog in the meantime.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my issue. Does the dog just vanish like a Cover not in use, so that no-one has it? Does it wander around as a stray, and then when someone makse use of it in a COver it suddenly remembers that 'this person is my owner'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T11:02:55-08:00","id":1179882,"title":"","content":"I would say that you're stuck with the dog, even if it ends up acting as the stray you're feeding. The alternative would be to say that if you bargained for someone's family, said individuals would vanish until a demon put them to good use, and since most of the world is unaffected by the transfer, that would really stand out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T11:35:05-08:00","id":1179889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1179882#post1179882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that you're stuck with the dog, even if it ends up acting as the stray you're feeding. The alternative would be to say that if you bargained for someone's family, said individuals would vanish until a demon put them to good use, and since most of the world is unaffected by the transfer, that would really stand out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it is like Soul Pacts - the traits remain with the Pactee until called on/integrated. So they have their dog until a Demon integrates it into their Cover, then it is the Demon's dog. For temporary Pacts, the elements bounce between &quot;ownership&quot; for the duration of use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T22:20:56-08:00","id":1180349,"title":"","content":"I'd rule it that switching Covers simply means that the person isn't anywhere in the world, but the Cover/person themselves exist. If the cover is destroyed, any association with that cover is also gone. Switching a cover will not remove a person's house, dog or car from existence, even if they're currently with/within that thing associated with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:05:01-08:00","id":1180998,"title":"","content":"One of the best tricks for demons as written, I think, is to use a shared pool of covers that apply to whoever holds the contract, next to making use of the awesome regenerating cover that are Sleeve Integrators. That way, demons can take someone's life in shifts, for identities that don't do well disappearing for vast quantities of time. Not only can one demon be many people, many demons can be one person.<br /> <br /> I find it kind of cool, if surreal, to imagine an Agency having safehouses where you don the provided cover and slip into the role of a beloved family member who showed up again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T17:58:45-08:00","id":1182133,"title":"","content":"Should Good Time Management work on processes like gadget creation, or on Exploits like Raise Dead? There's nothing that says it can't in the wording, but the previous version from the Reliquary supplement does, so I'm wondering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T18:03:18-08:00","id":1182135,"title":"","content":"Choose one:<br /> <br /> Rule of thumb: does managing your time well significantly benefit the activity? Gadget creation, quite possibly. Raise Dead, probably not.<br /> <br /> Rule of simplicity: it's good enough already covering natural activities, exclude supernatural activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T05:57:50-08:00","id":1184349,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Raise Dead, what would be the minimum time to use Raise Dead with an ally that has Swift Resolution? One day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:17:53-08:00","id":1190529,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this has been asked before, but how do Angels communicate with the God-Machine? Is there a telepathic link, or do they rely on other means such as radio signals, telephone or wifi? I've not seen any real consensus on this, and the books are vague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T20:46:43-08:00","id":1190546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1190529#post1190529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been asked before, but how do Angels communicate with the God-Machine? Is there a telepathic link, or do they rely on other means such as radio signals, telephone or wifi? I've not seen any real consensus on this, and the books are vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the variety of angels, the breadth of Infrastructure, and the general nature of an angel's connection to the Machine, I would guess that it varies per specimen.<br /> <br /> The set of Destroyers tasked with exterminating a renegade cryptid colony out in the woods might receive their orders by satellite linkup, while the Messenger sent to subvert a factory-spirit's cult to the Machine's purposes might order a grilled cheese from a specific diner at a particular time to read her instructions in the bill's receipt barcode.<br /> <br /> The Guardian holding a ring of demons beneath the church's pipe-organ might follow up on a successful interrogation by tapping on the valves in a certain order, but the Psychopomp that's supposed to chip sixteen newlyweds in the middle of Times Square at 11:16 PM on December 31st would instead tell the nearest local accessories vendor an activation phrase to confirm a difficulty in procurement.<br /> <br /> One example we <i>do </i>have is the hunting horns of an angelic retrieval team being perceptible as radio waves, so make of that what you will, but in general I'd say it's as weird or mundane and as direct or indirect as necessary for your story and its locale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T19:12:28-08:00","id":1193390,"title":"","content":"Can/should Exiles have Incepts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T19:41:53-08:00","id":1193398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1193390#post1193390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can/should Exiles have Incepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>...Depends? I mean, apparently, Angels <i>have</i> Incepts, but the God-Machine doesn't authorize their use very often. Exiles still are Angels, thus, should still have Incepts. They don't communicate with the Machine, though. Does this mean they can just use Incepts because they don't have that feedback, or that they never can* because they cannot get authorization?<br /> <br /> * With the exception of &quot;as a precursor to Falling&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T19:58:40-08:00","id":1193401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1193390#post1193390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can/should Exiles have Incepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the original discussion thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=808547#post808547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd recommend the ST decides on a case-by-case basis. The level of Abandonment by the God-Machine varies - sometimes It cancels Incept privileges, sometimes it doesn't. There doesn't seem to be any discernible pattern to it. Wise demons are wary around Exiles; they can be dangerous foes, but also very useful allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T23:02:06-07:00","id":1209125,"title":"","content":"How long does Reality Enforcement last? Are any who are affected by its activation remain so for the rest of the scene? Is it just anything within the initial zone that is affected? There's no duration listed anywhere in the exploit's writeup, and the limits of what it affects (such as gadgets or Infrastructure) is vague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T10:02:27-07:00","id":1210078,"title":"","content":"Other than Angel-Jacking I can't find any rules about angelic Covers. Are angels able to use Influences/Numina/Incepts while in their Covers? Do a Cover protect from Essence bleed? Can they exit and enter their Cover as they please? If it's actually explained just a page reference would be enough. I just have a hard time navigating the book so I might've just missed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:03:08-07:00","id":1210188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1210078#post1210078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than Angel-Jacking I can't find any rules about angelic Covers. Are angels able to use Influences/Numina/Incepts while in their Covers? Do a Cover protect from Essence bleed? Can they exit and enter their Cover as they please? If it's actually explained just a page reference would be enough. I just have a hard time navigating the book so I might've just missed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the top of my head, I remember angelic Cover being almost entirely narrative. If the Machine needs an angel shaped like a businessman, the angel just looks like one in its natural form, without need for things like Mortal Mask or Materialize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T00:09:02-07:00","id":1210313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1209125#post1209125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does Reality Enforcement last? Are any who are affected by its activation remain so for the rest of the scene? Is it just anything within the initial zone that is affected? There's no duration listed anywhere in the exploit's writeup, and the limits of what it affects (such as gadgets or Infrastructure) is vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they can.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T07:37:23-07:00","id":1210410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1210313#post1210313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be rude but I see three questions and I can't pin your answer to either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1210188#post1210188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the top of my head, I remember angelic Cover being almost entirely narrative. If the Machine needs an angel shaped like a businessman, the angel just looks like one in its natural form, without need for things like Mortal Mask or Materialize.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo, how would you guys treat it?<br /> Would you allow it use Manifestations and let it return to the Cover once the Manifestation has ended? Is the Cover lost if it discorporates? Should it protect against Essence bleed as if it was Materialized? Angels in Covers probably spend more time away from Infrastructure meaning they would bleed more, but might compensate by only using the odd Numen (such as Aggressive Meme or Implant Mission) compared to a hunter angel that boosts Attributes and Blasts away.<br /> At least since the angel is physically present Banes should cause aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, what do you think about researching Bane/Ban for angels? I know that the target number is already raised for angels but it makes no sense to me that it's even possible to research them by mundane means. At least not without access to special libraries (such as the one Deva Corporation has compiled), and like Deva Corporation's library they're likely both hidden and restricted.<br /> I'm instead thinking that (for mortal campaigns, I might add) angels in Covers replace their Ban with a Glitch (based on the Ban if possible, severity based on Rank). That would dramatically increase the odds of the players interacting with that trait short of ST fiat basically telling the players what the Ban is.<br /> Does that make sense to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-23-2018, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T08:39:06-07:00","id":1210433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1210410#post1210410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSo, how would you guys treat it?<br /> Would you allow it use Manifestations and let it return to the Cover once the Manifestation has ended? Is the Cover lost if it discorporates? Should it protect against Essence bleed as if it was Materialized? Angels in Covers probably spend more time away from Infrastructure meaning they would bleed more, but might compensate by only using the odd Numen (such as Aggressive Meme or Implant Mission) compared to a hunter angel that boosts Attributes and Blasts away.<br /> At least since the angel is physically present Banes should cause aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... would an angel in Cover even move away from its position at its supporting Infrastructure in the first place, though?<br /> <br /> Been a while since I read Demon stuff, so I may be completely off here. I should abstain from asserting or guessing until I read at least the core again. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Also, what do you think about researching Bane/Ban for angels? I know that the target number is already raised for angels but it makes no sense to me that it's even possible to research them by mundane means. At least not without access to special libraries (such as the one Deva Corporation has compiled), and like Deva Corporation's library they're likely both hidden and restricted.<br /> I'm instead thinking that (for mortal campaigns, I might add) angels in Covers replace their Ban with a Glitch (based on the Ban if possible, severity based on Rank). That would dramatically increase the odds of the players interacting with that trait short of ST fiat basically telling the players what the Ban is.<br /> Does that make sense to you? </div> </div> </div>Sounds good enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T11:56:57-07:00","id":1210521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1210433#post1210433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... would an angel in Cover even move away from its position at its supporting Infrastructure in the first place, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's in Cover it's because it's working with humans. There are very few places humans can stay at 24/7 without drawing attention to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:42:57-07:00","id":1211938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1210433#post1210433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... would an angel in Cover even move away from its position at its supporting Infrastructure in the first place, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>A hunter would. But it's also unclear what it means to be &quot;at its supporting Infrastructure&quot;. Does an Angel need its own Infrastructure, or can it be any Infrastructure? How much time do they have to spend there? Do they have to just be around it or do they need to jack in and refuel? And what's the limit of &quot;their infrastructure&quot;, anyway? Would an angel summoned to stalk a specific city count the whole thing as Infrastructure?<br /> <br /> When I ran into this problem a while back it was specifically in the context of a squad of hunter angels in Cover getting beamed in due to an absolutely monumentally series of Cover failures (three rolls, 22 dice, not once success). I ruled that they did not suffer Essence bleed and were able to use their Influences and Numina, but since they had been called in post-haste they didn't have access to any local Infrastructure to refuel. I did this to make starving them out an option, although they may then have resorted to human sacrifice - it didn't come to much since they ended up dispatching them pretty handily since i vastly overestimated the threat posed by a Rank 2 anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:23:41-07:00","id":1212017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1211938#post1211938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does an Angel need its own Infrastructure, or can it be any Infrastructure?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Infrastructure Condition implies it has to be its own Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1211938#post1211938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much time do they have to spend there? Do they have to just be around it or do they need to jack in and refuel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just that they have to visit it once per day to get the 1 Essence. The main things about it as a Manifestation Condition is that it protects from bleed while the angel stays, and is the foundation for additional Manifestation Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1211938#post1211938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what's the limit of &quot;their infrastructure&quot;, anyway? Would an angel summoned to stalk a specific city count the whole thing as Infrastructure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Raze Infrastructure would be able to destroy the entire city, I sure hope not. No, the Infrastructure tagged to the angel would only be the Infrastructure that summoned it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T23:44:01-07:00","id":1214939,"title":"","content":"Could Ephemeral Cover be used to generate a Cover of a strix? Or an infernal demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23991-bacchicone","name":"BacchicOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T00:09:25-07:00","id":1214951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BacchicOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1214939#post1214939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Ephemeral Cover be used to generate a Cover of a strix? Or an infernal demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It specifically allows you to create a Cover as either a ghost or spirit.<br /> <br /> However, allowing it to work on other ephemeral entities seems like a perfectly fine effect for an Interlock or near-field gadget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T00:38:04-07:00","id":1214958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BacchicOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1214939#post1214939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Ephemeral Cover be used to generate a Cover of a strix? Or an infernal demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strix aren\u2019t ephemeral creatures, technically speaking. They use a similar template for traits OOC, but IC they\u2019re literally made of smoke and shadows. I\u2019d be very (albeit somewhat pleasantly) surprised if later books allow Strix Covers. <br /> <br /> Now Infernal demons... diaboli are corrupted ephemeral entities, so maybe they can be reaped. Whisperers, Dominions and Malus Loci, most likely not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T22:26:19-07:00","id":1219186,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to make sure of something... at character creation, is it 3 merit dots or 5 to increase Primum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T22:51:12-07:00","id":1219189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1219186#post1219186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanted to make sure of something... at character creation, is it 3 merit dots or 5 to increase Primum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon was in an awkward phase when it came out. It was the first game properly in the format standard for Chronicles of Darkness, so players started with 10 dots of merits instead of 7, but it had a few niggles left over from New World of Darkness, so it told players to spend 3 experiences to raise their starting Primum instead of 5. As per every other game since, I would go with 5 experiences. You <i>could</i> go with as the book states, but that means an enterprising player could start gameplay with 1 merit dot and Primum 4, try to rush their Cipher, and end up at Primum 7 before everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T01:22:30-07:00","id":1219204,"title":"","content":"Y'all have an old version of the PDF. It's five Merit dots per dot of Primum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T06:21:42-07:00","id":1219252,"title":"","content":"New question...<br /> If you Partially Transformed with the Deathgrip Process (If the demon\u2019s body remains more or less intact, he rises from the dead with no Aether) and then died... would you revert back to human and be dead, or would the process stay in effect and bring you back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T09:46:02-07:00","id":1219297,"title":"","content":"It isn't part of the core book, so that Process does need some tweaking...along with the one that allows you to regain aether just by being out in sunlight. Rule it as you will - perhaps it only works in full Demon form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:34:47-07:00","id":1220927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1219252#post1219252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question...<br /> If you Partially Transformed with the Deathgrip Process (If the demon\u2019s body remains more or less intact, he rises from the dead with no Aether) and then died... would you revert back to human and be dead, or would the process stay in effect and bring you back?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any reason for this not to work when partially manifested just like any other demon form ability.<br /> <br /> The suggested physical description for the thing is <i>very</i> obvious, so I wouldn't really worry about people walking around with it on 'incognito' or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:37:08-07:00","id":1220949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1220927#post1220927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any reason for this not to work when partially manifested just like any other demon form ability.<br /> <br /> The suggested physical description for the thing is <i>very</i> obvious, so I wouldn't really worry about people walking around with it on 'incognito' or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Deep Cover and Show of Power, you could pull off a nice Mummy impersonation with it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T04:44:54-07:00","id":1221121,"title":"","content":"Ok it's a really silly question.<br /> Pretty often in manuals it's said that God-machine gears are invisible to mortals.<br /> How should we interpret it?<br /> God-machine gears are actually invisible to humans? Or it's just a metaphor to tell that god-machine stuff is very well concealed to human eyes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T05:02:04-07:00","id":1221123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1221121#post1221121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok it's a really silly question.<br /> Pretty often in manuals it's said that God-machine gears are invisible to mortals.<br /> How should we interpret it?<br /> God-machine gears are actually invisible to humans? Or it's just a metaphor to tell that god-machine stuff is very well concealed to human eyes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve always considered it to be a bit of both. Most would be well hidden, but a normal human that comes too close to one anyway would subconsciously avoid getting their limbs mangled by any moving parts without noticing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T05:25:49-07:00","id":1221129,"title":"","content":"Most (all?) Infrastructure is hidden, either in space-time folds humans can't normally access, using mundane deception or iirc behind &quot;psychic blocks&quot; that a mortal's attention just sort of slides off. If nothing else it's strongly implied that mortals in the nWoD, probably as a result of the God-Machine's meddling, have a strong instinct to ignore and suppress memories of inexplicable phenomena. So even if they do catch a glimpse of something, 99% of humans will just tell themselves they imagined it and get on with their lives.<br /> <br /> But I have to assume that if the mortal does somehow pierce the veil (stumble through the portal, crack open the apartment walls to find the pipes are made of gold lattice, get dragged into the not-a-pizza-place by a demon) the gears are not literally invisible to them. Otherwise you're adding a lot of weird, unnecessary baggage to the God-Machine Chronicles as a concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T05:52:14-07:00","id":1221134,"title":"","content":"I run it like this: Some are directly invisible (possibly because it's in Twilight, in which case it's also mostly intangible), some are camouflaged by supernatural effects (the giant, floating gear looks like a weird statue or the corona of an out-of-place tree; these tend to look weird), some are hidden behind a front (the production facility produces both parts for other Infrastructure as well as regular car parts), and some are under a &quot;perception filter&quot; to borrow a term from Doctor Who (it's there and fully visible, but people just refuse to look at it; at least until someone forces them to or the filter is shut down).<br /> It's only in the first example someone with Unseen Sense wouldn't be able to see the Infrastructure, but still know for certain that something close is giving them the telltale goosebumps or headaches that indicates the presence of the God-Machine. In the &quot;mundane front&quot; example they'd be able to see the Infrastructure, but without taking Spooked they might not be able to figure out that's the Infrastructure that's pinging their Unseen Sense. They will still have an easier time figure it out since they know something's up.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sometimes multiple methods of concealment might apply. The giant brain scanner that reads the minds of everyone in this sleepy little town might both be camouflaged as a nearby radio/phone tower, and function like one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-22-2018, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T06:06:54-07:00","id":1221136,"title":"","content":"Is Particianed Memory from the Storyteller's Guide bad to use in normal gameplay? It is in the Silent hacks, and my ST has been very reluctant to allow us to take it, but I am not sure what is so dangerous about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T11:16:17-07:00","id":1221213,"title":"","content":"Just wondering... is there a way for an Unchained to learn High Speech?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T11:39:38-07:00","id":1221219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1221213#post1221213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering... is there a way for an Unchained to learn High Speech?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not on paper as of now, afaik. Which isn't to say it couldn't happen in your game, but it would be a Big Deal, because the reason demons (and in fact, everyone except mages) cannot speak or learn High Speech is that it isn't a language in the traditional fallen world sense - it relies on supernal symbolism that can only be interpreted by those who are attuned to the Supernal. Demons cannot learn to speak High Speech for the same reason humans cannot learn to speak radio waves; they lack the sensory apparatus.<br /> <br /> Now in theory it should be possible to modify a demon in some way to allow for it. The 4-dot Prime spell &quot;Apocalypse&quot; grants Mage Sight. It doesn't explicitly give the ability to comprehend High Speech, but it is my understanding that doing so is connected to having Mage Sight. At the very least, a custom 4 or 5-dot Prime spell should be able to grant the ability. If the demon were to gain the ability as some kind of permanent, inherent effect, that would be a very custom Form Ability or something, the existence of which would have <i>interesting</i> cosmological ramification, depending on where it came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T13:53:24-07:00","id":1221247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1221219#post1221219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not on paper as of now, afaik. Which isn't to say it couldn't happen in your game, but it would be a Big Deal, because the reason demons (and in fact, everyone except mages) cannot speak or learn High Speech is that it isn't a language in the traditional fallen world sense - it relies on supernal symbolism that can only be interpreted by those who are attuned to the Supernal. Demons cannot learn to speak High Speech for the same reason humans cannot learn to speak radio waves; they lack the sensory apparatus.<br /> <br /> Now in theory it should be possible to modify a demon in some way to allow for it. The 4-dot Prime spell &amp;quot;Apocalypse&amp;quot; grants Mage Sight. It doesn't explicitly give the ability to comprehend High Speech, but it is my understanding that doing so is connected to having Mage Sight. At the very least, a custom 4 or 5-dot Prime spell should be able to grant the ability. If the demon were to gain the ability as some kind of permanent, inherent effect, that would be a very custom Form Ability or something, the existence of which would have <i>interesting</i> cosmological ramification, depending on where it came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, a Demon might build an Apocalypse Gadget (using Show of Power), they use that to start to decide the &quot;gibberish&quot; that is High Speech.<br /> <br /> But, as no human &quot;natively&quot; speaks it, Demons don't get it as part of their language package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T14:51:48-07:00","id":1221264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1221247#post1221247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, a Demon might build an Apocalypse Gadget (using Show of Power), they use that to start to decide the &quot;gibberish&quot; that is High Speech.<br /> <br /> But, as no human &quot;natively&quot; speaks it, Demons don't get it as part of their language package.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be native to humans; demons explicitly <i>do</i> speak First Tongue, which is native only to spirits. And like I said, even if you were to somehow raise a native speaker of High Speech, demons still could not use it because it cannot be understood without Peripheral Mage Sight. They can't do it, because they lack the necessary connection to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Unless of course raising a native speaker of High Speech <i>gave</i> demons a connection to the Supernal. Now <i>there's</i> an end-game crossover chronicle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T15:29:04-07:00","id":1221283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1221264#post1221264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't have to be native to humans; demons explicitly <i>do</i> speak First Tongue, which is native only to spirits. And like I said, even if you were to somehow raise a native speaker of High Speech, demons still could not use it because it cannot be understood without Peripheral Mage Sight. They can't do it, because they lack the necessary connection to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Unless of course raising a native speaker of High Speech <i>gave</i> demons a connection to the Supernal. Now <i>there's</i> an end-game crossover chronicle!</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the First Tongue goes, I'm betting we have the Pure to thank for that. Some enclave has probably raised their human offspring to speak the First Tongue as a first language. High Speech, on the other hand, <i>can't</i> be taught to someone as a first language - you need to be Awakened to make sense of it, so unless someone learned literally no language at all until they Awakened, it wouldn't count. And once they Awakened, it still might not count, since they are no longer vanilla human.<br /> <br /> Clarification: When I used &quot;native language&quot; I meant a person's first language, which they use internally and compare others to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T15:40:34-07:00","id":1221285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1221283#post1221283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as the First Tongue goes, I'm betting we have the Pure to thank for that. Some enclave has probably raised their human offspring to speak the First Tongue as a first language. High Speech, on the other hand, <i>can't</i> be taught to someone as a first language - you need to be Awakened to make sense of it, so unless someone learned literally no language at all until they Awakened, it wouldn't count. And once they Awakened, it still might not count, since they are no longer vanilla human.<br /> <br /> Clarification: When I used &quot;native language&quot; I meant a person's first language, which they use internally and compare others to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The language of the book implies they can speak it because spirits do (&quot;By the same token, demons can use Natural Aptitude to speak First Tongue (the \u201cnative language\u201d of spirits&quot;)). But then it also says &quot;native human language&quot; so who knows.<br /> <br /> Either way you're right that raising a native speaker of High Speech would be tricky at best. Can children Awaken? Even if they officially cannot, an Awakened baby could happen as a plot point, especially if the sort of shady types who'd kidnap a child and teach it only an esoteric proto-language as an experiment were also attempting to induce Awakenings. Somebody like, I don't know, mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T16:27:14-07:00","id":1221298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1221285#post1221285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The language of the book implies they can speak it because spirits do (&amp;quot;By the same token, demons can use Natural Aptitude to speak First Tongue (the \u201cnative language\u201d of spirits&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). But then it also says &amp;quot;native human language&amp;quot; so who knows.<br /> <br /> Either way you're right that raising a native speaker of High Speech would be tricky at best. Can children Awaken? Even if they officially cannot, an Awakened baby could happen as a plot point, especially if the sort of shady types who'd kidnap a child and teach it only an esoteric proto-language as an experiment were also attempting to induce Awakenings. Somebody like, I don't know, mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible to force an Awakening through Imperial Magic, but even then High Speech is not a language in the usual sense. Imagine the structural formulae of chemistry. Now apply a much more complex version of that to all of reality. You can speak it, but only through nomenclature mapped to the symbols rather than through the freeform and loose words of regular languages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T06:52:27-07:00","id":1221465,"title":"","content":"It should also be noted that the book Mage The Awakening Second Edition goes out of its way to never refer to High Speech directly as a language. Either &quot;language&quot; is in quotes or it's described in relation to real languages: &quot;it\u2019s more the symbol of a language than a real language&quot;<br /> On top of all that you still need some sort of supernatural power to even interpret High Speech. As such not even the Mage spell Universal Language enables non-mages to understand High Speech, and that spell extends to stuff like body language, hand gestures, other types of symbols, and even encoded signals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T14:37:12-07:00","id":1222711,"title":"","content":"Would Polybius make good infustruscre","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T20:15:04-07:00","id":1222798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1222711#post1222711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Polybius make good infustruscre</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, the urban legend/ conspiracy theory?<br /> <br /> Every urban legend and conspiracy theory can be mined for Demon inspiration, much more than science fiction and space opera, so go wild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T08:56:16-07:00","id":1224716,"title":"","content":"More of a terminology thing (and thus not directly related to Demon: the Descent), but what are some other names/terms for someone descended from Demons? Not Demon-blooded, Offspring, Fractal, or Nephilim - those are already terms that exist in setting/material. I'm looking for new ones. The best I can figure is Cambion (which is already used in Changeling), but I'm hoping there are a few more.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I'm working on a &quot;Demon-blooded lineage&quot; template, which changes the &quot;normal&quot; Demon-blooded Cipher into something more like the Unchained one <i>and</i> doubles as the Power Stat. Their effective Primum being equal to the number of Key's they've unlocked. Still, having a ready, identifiable name would help.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T17:29:12-07:00","id":1225994,"title":"","content":"When a Demon makes a pact, is the duration paid for on just the Demon's end, or is it something that is put onto both sides? The books make the matter a trifle confusing since it notes that the duration for Demons and Humans can be different, and Interface is inconsistent with whether or not the pact durations are different (such as on 125).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 06-08-2018, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T23:48:46-07:00","id":1226031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1225994#post1225994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Demon makes a pact, is the duration paid for on just the Demon's end, or is it something that is put onto both sides? The books make the matter a trifle confusing since it notes that the duration for Demons and Humans can be different, and Interface is inconsistent with whether or not the pact durations are different (such as on 125).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the duration is paid for based on the longest involved, rather than paying for each side. If not, then the price of a pact would become dangerously high just for having permanent benefits on both sides, before the cost of said benefits are even calculated into it. As I recall, the sample pacts in the core would support this interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T07:19:48-07:00","id":1226068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1226031#post1226031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that the duration is paid for based on the longest involved, rather than paying for each side. If not, then the price of a pact would become dangerously high just for having permanent benefits on both sides, before the cost of said benefits are even calculated into it. As I recall, the sample pacts in the core would support this interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't quite what I meant; I had presumed that when a Demon calculated duration of the pact, it was always put on the Demon's side of the equation and that the duration for the Demon was the duration for both sides. However, a friend noticed inconsistencies where the Human side of the equation would also get the duration of the pact put on in the samples for pacts, and bits of elaboration where the human side of a pact isn't always the same duration as the Demon's side. Considering that this is a difference of up to three willpower for a pact, I wanted to ask and double check on that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:11:09-07:00","id":1227022,"title":"","content":"Soooo, to regain aether a demon can interface itself with an infrastructure, in the core book, it says you gain 4 aether per turn while connected to an infrastucture and you have to make a wits+craft roll to disengage yourself. <br /> Then in Flowers of hell it says that aether gained from infrastructure varies and you generally don't have to roll to disengage, but in case of emergency they require a Resolve+Primum roll. So wich one is it ? Unless i'm confused and these are both different things ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T11:42:01-07:00","id":1227185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1227022#post1227022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo, to regain aether a demon can interface itself with an infrastructure, in the core book, it says you gain 4 aether per turn while connected to an infrastucture and you have to make a wits+craft roll to disengage yourself. <br /> Then in Flowers of hell it says that aether gained from infrastructure varies and you generally don't have to roll to disengage, but in case of emergency they require a Resolve+Primum roll. So wich one is it ? Unless i'm confused and these are both different things ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Flowers Of Hell version is an update to the system. The new way not only makes Infrastructure less assured to grant aether, as well as more varied in the skills required to examine it, but it also means that a Demon doesn't need to be good in Wits or Crafts to disengage from Infrastructure once they have collected the information/aether from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:15:22-07:00","id":1227474,"title":"","content":"Ok so I'm really confused on demon emotions. Do they feel actual emotion only in cover (and their emotions in cover stay the same through each cover. For example, no matter what cover a demon is, if they love a specific person, they will feel that way no matter what cover they are in). And do they lose the these emotions while going loud, due to lacking being human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:34:52-07:00","id":1227479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1227474#post1227474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so I'm really confused on demon emotions. Do they feel actual emotion only in cover (and their emotions in cover stay the same through each cover. For example, no matter what cover a demon is, if they love a specific person, they will feel that way no matter what cover they are in).</div> </div> </div> </div>They feel emotion regardless of their form, they just retain control over any possible outward expression of it they might make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And do they lose the these emotions while going loud, due to lacking being human </div> </div> </div>The opposite, in fact \u2014 reference the Demonic Conditions on pages 209-10 of the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:41:34-07:00","id":1227481,"title":"","content":"Thank you Satchel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T12:26:45-07:00","id":1227494,"title":"","content":"Demons <i>do</i> feel emotion, but this <i>is</i> somewhat modified by their current Cover (the books cite the effects of hormones and other chemicals affecting the brain and such). So the Demon would feel the same <i>general</i> emotions toward a subject regardless, but it will be more &quot;cool&quot; or objective in Demonic Form, and (depending on how you want to rule attraction vis a vis the Demon's Covers) the physiological response might be a bit different unless the Demon explicitly overrides that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T11:54:53-07:00","id":1229836,"title":"","content":"Can Demons do abjuration, lacking the soul required for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T18:42:02-07:00","id":1229912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1229836#post1229836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Demons do abjuration, lacking the soul required for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing no. I actually wrote a homebrew merit that enabled it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T21:50:43-07:00","id":1231015,"title":"","content":"Took a stab at writing up a Cover Manifestation for Angels and I'm curious as to what people think of it (or if it's even useable). Took some inspiration from the Angel-Jacking rules and the Soul Pact rules.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Cover: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">By spending three points of Essence, the Angel gains the Materialized Condition and is hidden behind a mask of the God-Machine\u2019s making. Consider it a Cover with a base rating equal to the Angel\u2019s Rank and additional dots equal to successes on the activating Power + Finesse roll. Cover is permanent unless ended and protects the Angel from Essence bleed. By spending a point of Essence, the Angel abandons their Cover and may take their true form for a number of hours up to Cover - Rank before needing to either return to Cover or take Twilight Form.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T08:22:26-07:00","id":1231118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1231015#post1231015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Took a stab at writing up a Cover Manifestation for Angels and I'm curious as to what people think of it (or if it's even useable). Took some inspiration from the Angel-Jacking rules and the Soul Pact rules.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Cover: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">By spending three points of Essence, the Angel gains the Materialized Condition and is hidden behind a mask of the God-Machine\u2019s making. Consider it a Cover with a base rating equal to the Angel\u2019s Rank and additional dots equal to successes on the activating Power + Finesse roll. Cover is permanent unless ended and protects the Angel from Essence bleed. By spending a point of Essence, the Angel abandons their Cover and may take their true form for a number of hours up to Cover - Rank before needing to either return to Cover or take Twilight Form.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What about some text regarding how they register as human (or whatever they are) to senses that detect supernaturals? Cover is Cover, and Angels can be just as hard to spot out as Demons. It's part of why they are so scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T13:01:43-07:00","id":1231188,"title":"","content":"So how powerful is a pacts reality warping? Like when given back an arm as part of the deal, is all history changed to reflect this, or are there little things left out, such as medical history","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T11:21:49-07:00","id":1237790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1231188#post1231188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how powerful is a pacts reality warping? Like when given back an arm as part of the deal, is all history changed to reflect this, or are there little things left out, such as medical history</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you can do that. Everything from pacts has to come from somewhere, its like the demon's powers nudge the right things to happen, no matter how improbable. You can heal his arm, and no history is changed, but you could do it to sweeten the pact. On to the actual question asked, not very. The example given is an abusive boyfriend. She and he both forget they were in a relationship, with the boyfriend now thinking that it was always the demon, not the pact maker. Both families are confused as to why their relative is no long in a relationship with the other, and the not loverbirds are confused, but adamant that they remember it correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T11:26:51-07:00","id":1237791,"title":"","content":"How would one take on an animal as a cover? It mentions animal covers briefly, but not the particulars? For example (Totally hypothetical and just a random animal having nothing to do with the character i'm making at all.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) a wolf. Could you make a soul pact with a wolf? Could you somehow use other people to patchwork yourself into a wolf? Or do you just have to wait for the right angel to come down to jack its wolf cover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T13:56:33-07:00","id":1237809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1237791#post1237791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would one take on an animal as a cover? It mentions animal covers briefly, but not the particulars? For example (Totally hypothetical and just a random animal having nothing to do with the character i'm making at all.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) a wolf. Could you make a soul pact with a wolf? Could you somehow use other people to patchwork yourself into a wolf? Or do you just have to wait for the right angel to come down to jack its wolf cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>The simplest way to get an animal Cover would be to have that as your original Cover, with a human identity as your secondary Cover. You could also purchase one from the pact market, provided that you had a Storyteller willing to indulge that idea. I don\u2019t believe that a soul pact would work, nor would patch jobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T13:00:26-07:00","id":1238038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1237809#post1237809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The simplest way to get an animal Cover would be to have that as your original Cover, with a human identity as your secondary Cover. You could also purchase one from the pact market, provided that you had a Storyteller willing to indulge that idea. I don\u2019t believe that a soul pact would work, nor would patch jobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animal Covers really can't be made by demons, sadly, because they aren't sentient enough to truly agree to Pact or even to sign on the dotted line. I could see an argument made for apes that speak sign language or the very smartest parrots...<br /> <br /> So the only options are trading it between other demons, as noted, or angel-jacking.<br /> <br /> The sheer difficulty and rarity of animal Covers is fully intended (in part because they were introduced in a section called 'Urban Legends', in part for balance/thematic reasons) but an ST is the real God-Machine of any game and if you're the ST do what you think is coolest/best. As any demon will tel you, the rules aren't absolute. Break them and rewrite them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 07-23-2018, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T05:50:10-07:00","id":1244459,"title":"","content":"I may be missing something obvious, but I'm about to play demons with my friends and we can't see any way for demons to find other demons other than to come out and say &quot;Hi, I'm a demon.&quot; Is there any other way? Please help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24517-neodarrell","name":"Neodarrell","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:32:49-07:00","id":1244512,"title":"","content":"Setting up Special Message points perhaps? The Resonance Sensitivity merit lets you tell if you're looking at a Demon too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:57:20-07:00","id":1244564,"title":"","content":"In theme with the system of safe-setups for meetings, I imagine that Agencies arrange for points of notice-things that will catch the attention of newly fallen angels and will probably, eventually, investigate in ways that will be apparent to them. From there, it's a dance of experimentation and faith-building between the Agency's representatives and the fallen, until the new demon can willingly choose to get in enough to be on the roster for the first circle of communications and safe spots.<br /> <br /> If you want to shortcut that though, remember that new demons are more prone to standing out as demons-the game assumes you've gotten past the phase of being awkward and now can play the game of the Agency, but starting from the surge of weirdness that comes with a fall to those initial moments of figuring out mortality, there's a brief period where they probably stand out, and it's easy to have a representative come in and, through the process of reining the new one in, also get them into the circle of connections.<br /> <br /> Once first contact is well and over, it's all a matter of keeping up to date on the codewords, signals, drop boxes, couriers and safe spots of the agency, which is &quot;simple&quot; enough even with mundane methods-and that's before accounting for the various ways Embeds let demons improve on the network.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T07:44:18-07:00","id":1247017,"title":"","content":"Has anyone ever survived to tell the tale as one of the burned? Like go on without a cover and successfully finding another","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T16:31:07-07:00","id":1248784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1229836#post1229836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Demons do abjuration, lacking the soul required for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they lack the soul to do so directly (it has been debated if spoof could allow it) they could mimic it with an ability like show of power. However in the text if Boltholes it refers to a demon repairing it with abjuration so because of that I'd lead to likely yes - in sone way.<br /> <br /> The question remains, what would your integrity count as for the related mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T04:13:54-07:00","id":1253011,"title":"","content":"Hi All, obviously we have Heirs to Hell for the Children of Demons - has anyone contemplated/ Used the Children of Angels? Personally I was thinking of re-skinning Nephilim as Angelic Children in the modern day but wanted to know If there is anything already written or if someone has used them as such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T06:49:26-07:00","id":1253042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1253011#post1253011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi All, obviously we have Heirs to Hell for the Children of Demons - has anyone contemplated/ Used the Children of Angels? Personally I was thinking of re-skinning Nephilim as Angelic Children in the modern day but wanted to know If there is anything already written or if someone has used them as such?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can probably just treat them as Offspring or Fractals without any major issue. Embeds are supposed to be lesser forms of what Angels can do, so their progeny possessing lesser abilities isn't out of place. Very little changing if their parent Falls could be a subject of investigation.<br /> <br /> Maybe give them the Medium Merit, so they can reinforce their parent's Infrastructure Conditions? Or look into a Angel flavored version of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231346-those-who-call-to-spirits-human-occultists\">Shadow Occultists</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T16:41:25-07:00","id":1253157,"title":"","content":"I am thinking of running a Demon game this Fall, so while I have read the rules, I don't have any experience with it (or any White Wolf game).<br /> <br /> I get the impression that a lot of the game is about Aether management - choosing when to use it, worrying about how to regain it. Several ways seem inefficient (e.g. they get you your Primum in Aether and cost one Aether, which is not much good when your Primum is one). <br /> <br /> Can anyone tell me their experience of regaining Aether in gameplay? Is it the focus of an entire evening of play just to find away to pick up a few points of Aether? Or is it a minor nuisance? How do players in your game tend to refill?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T22:06:38-07:00","id":1253215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1253157#post1253157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking of running a Demon game this Fall, so while I have read the rules, I don't have any experience with it (or any White Wolf game).<br /> <br /> I get the impression that a lot of the game is about Aether management - choosing when to use it, worrying about how to regain it. Several ways seem inefficient (e.g. they get you your Primum in Aether and cost one Aether, which is not much good when your Primum is one). <br /> <br /> Can anyone tell me their experience of regaining Aether in gameplay? Is it the focus of an entire evening of play just to find away to pick up a few points of Aether? Or is it a minor nuisance? How do players in your game tend to refill?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also regain it with a heist like operation to siphon off waste aether from infastructure. If your game allows the translation guide's sun's bounty demon form aether won't be a worry but allowing it I feel can remove a good chunk of drama. Plus, if aether is scarce you can pay characters with stockpiles filled with aether. These stockpiles are external reserves your players can fall back on and it gives them a good reason to cooperate with other demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T10:02:21-07:00","id":1253311,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of a sort of &quot;watering hole&quot; scenario where there is a very public place where a trickle of Aether is available, but there is a good chance an angel or some Aether predator is lying in wait. Players would have to find ways to tank up inconspicuously or distract attention away while they drink up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T10:13:22-07:00","id":1253313,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24502\" data-vbnamecard=\"24502\">KieranMullen</a> That could work but you'd have to consider two things 1, if regularly drained how big is the infrastructure that produces this reliable source and then as you already considered 2, what is guarding it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T18:36:54-07:00","id":1254376,"title":"","content":"What happens if a Cryptic drains all Aether from a demon? AFAIK:<br /> <br /> If the demon is in demon form, it's stuck because it costs one Aether to return to human form.<br /> <br /> If the demon is in Cover nothing happens. However, they can't use any powers that require abilities that require Aether (duh).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T18:49:17-07:00","id":1254378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1254376#post1254376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a Cryptic drains all Aether from a demon? AFAIK:<br /> <br /> If the demon is in demon form, it's stuck because it costs one Aether to return to human form.<br /> <br /> If the demon is in Cover nothing happens. However, they can't use any powers that require abilities that require Aether (duh).</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to your first point &quot; <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If she runs out of Aether while in demonic </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">form, her player may roll the demon\u2019s Primum, with each </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">success restoring a point of Aether.&quot; Though that might cause the condition Atheric Bleed if you aren't careful.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T12:55:17-07:00","id":1254599,"title":"","content":"Do you need to know the embed or exploit you are embedding/ exploiting into a gadget? <br /> One player mentioned it's not explicit in the core and I couldn't find an reference that it was needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T15:38:22-07:00","id":1254643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1254599#post1254599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need to know the embed or exploit you are embedding/ exploiting into a gadget? <br /> One player mentioned it's not explicit in the core and I couldn't find an reference that it was needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes no sense to me why a Demon would be able to implant an Embed/Exploit they don\u2019t know into an item. How would they know of the Embed/Exploit they are implanting into the gadget and what effects to aim for when making it? Surely if they know if it enough to install its effects into an object, they would have the Embed/Exploit itself already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T14:51:48-07:00","id":1254854,"title":"","content":"Hi! Quick question: Can a demon grant a mortal change of sex throug demonic pacts? I have a transgender PC who made a pact with a right-wing catholic woman to enter the Opus Dei by changing her to a man, but I'm not sure if pacts can make such a drastic change in a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T17:23:37-07:00","id":1254884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1254854#post1254854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! Quick question: Can a demon grant a mortal change of sex throug demonic pacts? I have a transgender PC who made a pact with a right-wing catholic woman to enter the Opus Dei by changing her to a man, but I'm not sure if pacts can make such a drastic change in a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it's an identifier same as anything else. If you can trade eye colors, you can trade sexs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-16-2018, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T17:35:18-07:00","id":1254888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1254884#post1254884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, it's an identifier same as anything else. If you can trade eye colors, you can trade genders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in this particular case, the pact would allow a change of sex, not gender. The demon involved is actually transitioning from male to female, but what they did to the pact-bound human is a biological change. I &quot;think&quot; we are speaking of the same thing, but still I wanted to point out the difference, just to be clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T17:54:04-07:00","id":1254889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1254888#post1254888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in this particular case, the pact would allow a change of sex, not gender. The demon involved is actually transitioning from male to female, but what they did to the pact-bound human is a biological change. I &quot;think&quot; we are speaking of the same thing, but still I wanted to point out the difference, just to be clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, right- lapse of thought on my part, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T11:08:02-07:00","id":1255534,"title":"","content":"Could someone point me to a written description of an extended combat scene in the CoD rules? I'd like to see a write-up with several combatants describing how initiative, conditions, tactics, weapons and supernatural abilities interact. It would be useful if this resource is web-accessible. :-).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T13:09:51-07:00","id":1255563,"title":"","content":"Most actual plays cut that out (or summarize it). You can probably find some twitch streams or youtube recordings of them, but in that case it's not a write-up. You might also look in the play by post threads <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> You might repost this question in the General Chronicles of Darkness forum <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness\">here</a>, if it's not Demon-specific. You'd get a wider audience and it's not really a simple answer thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T22:39:02-07:00","id":1256892,"title":"","content":"I want to set up a scenario similar to the start of the book <i>A Game of Cages</i>, which starts with a late night auction of a mysterious McGuffin to multimillionaires at an isolated mansion. Things go badly and the factions vie for the McGuffin that itself causes its own chaos. In my scenario the PC's are given a temporary cover that gets them in to the auction and have instructions to determine the nature of the auction and intervene if necessary.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I need some decent antagonists at the auction. A couple of parties would be millionaires who are wannabe mages but have no powers but a pack of henchmen. One party would be a pack of dabblers who have a few Gadgets. However one or two attendees should be heavy hitters. I'd like them to be mages, but looking at Mage: The Awakening this is WAY more detail than I want. I could <br /> <br /> Is there a source where I can get some sort of basic Mage who can take on any pack of mortals and might be a danger to a demon or two? Or should I just wing it, putting together some abilities based on Exploits?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T06:56:03-07:00","id":1256948,"title":"","content":"So, at his point you need to determine how much you want to simulate vs integrate. You can use all kinds of mechanical models for simulating Mages, but what is your answer as to the metaphysics behind their magic? Do Awakening Mages exist, but you are using system X merely as a model to prevent having to deal with two rule books? Or is the nature of &quot;Mortals are using Exploits/Influences/Whatever&quot; going to be a mystery or plot point?<br /> <br /> As to exact systems, you could give them Influences, like Angels (and other Ephemerals) have. Those are close to Arcana, don't require any additional rule books, and are just familiar enough to be recognizable. You'll probably have to do something about the Essence costs (which can get high) and vague degree of effects.<br /> <br /> Another option is just giving them Exploits (or Embeds and letting them so supercharge them with &quot;Aether&quot;), as you said. Up to you (due to the above) if you want them as actual Exploits, or if you are just using those as a mechanical model. Check Heirs to Hell for charging Embeds with Aether.<br /> <br /> A third option is to give them a bunch of Supernatural Merits, making whatever Advanced versions and other tweaks as necessary to get the power you want.<br /> <br /> Other book sources are Second Sight and Hunter: Witch Finders, but those are 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-24-2018, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T11:06:25-07:00","id":1256990,"title":"","content":"The Storyteller's Guide has a section for all the (then existing) splats, describing them from the perspective of the Unchained and providing hints for how to emulate their powers with only the Demon core book. It breaks down the five Arcana dots into Lesser and Greater proficiency. For Lesser spells the book recommends using Embeds, and for Greater spells Exploits. Demonic form powers can represent both.<br /> <br /> Personally I agree with Vent0. If you don't have the Storyteller's Guide, just use Influences (but lower the Essence/Mana costs). If you have the Storyteller's Guide, still use Influences but add the simplified Mage Sight and Reach systems from the Guide. For Mage Armor, just add the Influence/Arcanum dots as Armor or Defense, with a cost of one Essence/Mana per scene.<br /> And remember that the Arcana are wider and more powerful than their equivalent Influences so be liberal with your interpretation of what the Influence dots can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T18:31:10-07:00","id":1257480,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand, angels are naturally in Twilight, if they are not in Cover. They can materialize using the Materialize (duh) Manifestation, and then Discorporate if they have that Manifestation as well. <br /> <br /> However, the Materialize Manifestation requires the Open condition. As I read the rules, that requires Infrastructure or Cultists to create that condition so that the angel can materialize. OTOH, some of the fluff describes angels materializing from the Twilight to surprise and murder a victim.<br /> <br /> I think the nature of the game changes a lot whether angels can attack at random from Twilight or not. Perpetual snooping adds to the paranoid spy-thriller feel, but having killers appear at any instant anywhere seems to raise it to unplayable levels. Or am I wrong?<br /> <br /> How do you play it in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T21:10:31-07:00","id":1257493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257480#post1257480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand, angels are naturally in Twilight, if they are not in Cover. They can materialize using the Materialize (duh) Manifestation, and then Discorporate if they have that Manifestation as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257480#post1257480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the Materialize Manifestation requires the Open condition. As I read the rules, that requires Infrastructure or Cultists to create that condition so that the angel can materialize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, mostly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257480#post1257480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OTOH, some of the fluff describes angels materializing from the Twilight to surprise and murder a victim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which implies the victim or the area was made Open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T10:42:18-07:00","id":1257602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257480#post1257480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand, angels are naturally in Twilight, if they are not in Cover. They can materialize using the Materialize (duh) Manifestation, and then Discorporate if they have that Manifestation as well. <br /> <br /> However, the Materialize Manifestation requires the Open condition. As I read the rules, that requires Infrastructure or Cultists to create that condition so that the angel can materialize. OTOH, some of the fluff describes angels materializing from the Twilight to surprise and murder a victim.<br /> <br /> I think the nature of the game changes a lot whether angels can attack at random from Twilight or not. Perpetual snooping adds to the paranoid spy-thriller feel, but having killers appear at any instant anywhere seems to raise it to unplayable levels. Or am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using influences you could temporarily move an area to open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T13:47:10-07:00","id":1257642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257602#post1257602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using influences you could temporarily move an area to open.</div> </div> </div> </div>Argh! You are correct. At the four dot level the DtD says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:FuturaT\">The entity can cause a temporary Anchor, Infrastructure, or Resonant Condition in a subject for the duration of the Influence. The cost is four Essence.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>The only save grace here (pun unintended) is that you need an angel of at least Rank 4 to have an Influence at the four dot level. So rank 4 and above angels can pop out from the Twilight to stab you in the back at a cost of eight Essence (four to cause the Infrastructure Condition, one to shift it to Open, and three to use the Materialize Manifestation). <br /> <br /> The one dot level Influence does not allow an angel to crate the Open condition, only shift to it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:FuturaT\">This Influence can shift the Anchor, Resonant or Infrastructure Condition to Open for its duration. The cost is one Essence.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>This is only a problem if you habitually have Rank 4 angels on your tail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T15:41:57-07:00","id":1257660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257642#post1257642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only a problem if you habitually have Rank 4 angels on your tail.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you habitually have Rank 4 Angels on your tail, you have other concerns. Like - <i>where is your Cover</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T17:44:44-07:00","id":1257692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257642#post1257642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only a problem if you habitually have Rank 4 angels on your tail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 3+. Control allows the generation of Open without the underlying Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Most angels - even greater angels - can't build Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T19:04:10-07:00","id":1257703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257692#post1257692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 3+. Control allows the generation of Open without the underlying Infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only mention of Control being able to create Open is in the description for that Condition, and that's most likely a mistake that should refer to Strengthen. But even if that's not a typo it does not mention that it can create Open without Infrastructure. The entire Influence/Manifestation system is built around stacking Conditions so if an Influence effect could bypass that it'd be explicitly stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T20:21:30-07:00","id":1257710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257703#post1257703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only mention of Control being able to create Open is in the description for that Condition, and that's most likely a mistake that should refer to Strengthen. But even if that's not a typo it does not mention that it can create Open without Infrastructure. The entire Influence/Manifestation system is built around stacking Conditions so if an Influence effect could bypass that it'd be explicitly stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have still thought that if we didn't have the entirety of Geist 2e's Kickstarter draft available to offer a near direct counterpoint in the form of how geists work \u2014 at Rank 3, a geist explicitly has access to an Influence rated at three dots, explicitly cannot have enough Influence to forge new instances of the Anchor Condition, implicitly cannot regain Essence from being remembered as readily as a normal ghost, and all but assuredly does not have Anchors to regain Essence through even if it weren't beyond the need for them to stay out of the Underworld. The nature of the Influence still limits the things that can be tagged, but &quot;you can use the level of Influence that lets you control a thing to make it align more with your intangible form&quot; seems well within spec.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of examples on the books of instances of the Open Condition divorced from an underlying baseline Condition and the general trend of Rank 3 being the threshold for ephemeral beings using Manifestations to effect short-notice activity in the material world meshes with the reading given the evidence available to us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-27-2018, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T02:51:40-07:00","id":1257735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257710#post1257710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have still thought that if we didn't have the entirety of Geist 2e's Kickstarter draft available to offer a near direct counterpoint in the form of how geists work \u2014 at Rank 3, a geist explicitly has access to an Influence rated at three dots, explicitly cannot have enough Influence to forge new instances of the Anchor Condition, implicitly cannot regain Essence from being remembered as readily as a normal ghost, and all but assuredly does not have Anchors to regain Essence through even if it weren't beyond the need for them to stay out of the Underworld. The nature of the Influence still limits the things that can be tagged, but &amp;quot;you can use the level of Influence that lets you control a thing to make it align more with your intangible form&amp;quot; seems well within spec.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of examples on the books of instances of the Open Condition divorced from an underlying baseline Condition and the general trend of Rank 3 being the threshold for ephemeral beings using Manifestations to effect short-notice activity in the material world meshes with the reading given the evidence available to us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geists have already been forced to survive by Ectophagia in the Underworld and there's no reason they can't continue topside, so their Essence management is still manageable.<br /> The fact that they're incapable of using any Manifestations requiring any Manifestation Conditions serves as a natural reason for them to seek out Bound. Both because of their ability to grant Open to absolutely anything through Plasm (one of the exceptions you mentioned) but also due to the Liminal Aura at Synergy 2+. It also serves as a very good reason to enter the Bargain. And it should be noted that the Bargain, despite being one of the most powerful and intimate Manifestations, has no prerequisite Manifestation Conditions.<br /> <br /> I still believe the Open Condition contains a mistake, if only because such a thing would've been clarified. It was written alongside the entire Influence/Manifestation system complete with flowchart and listed prerequisites for all Manifestation Conditions, and at the time it was written there existed no other exceptions to it. Another reason as to why I believe it's a mistake is that what Conditions you can create with an Influence is clearly listed in the Influence descriptions, in the flowchart and in the &quot;Causing the Condition&quot; text for each Condition. Control to create Open is lacking from both Influence description and flowchart, and the Open Condition lacks the text describing Strengthen being able to create Open. These are the only exceptions so it's pretty safe to assume that whoever wrote the text messed up and accidentally wrote Control instead of Strengthen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T17:51:34-07:00","id":1257875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1257735#post1257735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are the only exceptions so it's pretty safe to assume that whoever wrote the text messed up and accidentally wrote Control instead of Strengthen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, I'm approaching this from the perspective of somebody who pushed to remove &quot;Ghosts often have Influence (Anchor)&quot; as an error in multiple books only to find as near to an explicit statement as can be made that it wasn't one in the Geist mechanics' reformatted (and therefore uncopied) breakdown of how Influences work.<br /> <br /> &quot;Rank 3+ ephemeral beings with enough Influence can generate the means of setting up most Manifestations, but cannot create a net-neutral relation to their upkeep cycle from scratch without Influence 4 or 5&quot; informs the ephemeral being mechanics in a way that meshes with Geist's &quot;most ghosts returning from the Underworld are Rank 3 or higher&quot; and Werewolf's &quot;most spirits capable of causing trouble outside the Shadow are Rank 3 or higher&quot; as readily as Demon's &quot;a 'lesser angel' dispatched to pursue a Hunted demon is Rank 2-3, while a 'greater angel' is Rank 4-5.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only thing that is lost by not carrying forward the assumption of error is that there's a much smaller gap between Rank 3 and Rank 4 than there is between Rank 4 and Rank 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T15:27:24-07:00","id":1258601,"title":"","content":"Can a demon detect that a person is a Mage? <br /> <br /> Can a Mage tell that someone else is a Mage? (I don't have the Mage books - I am faking them as discussed above). <br /> <br /> Can a demon detect that a person is a Vampire? Can the Vampire block this detection?<br /> <br /> (Thanks for your help!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T18:06:18-07:00","id":1258631,"title":"","content":"The primary means for a demon to identify supernatural beings on sight, without having to innovate near-field gadgets, is the Aura Sight form power. Your form power choices are limited, and activating it is visibly unnatural, but it will distinguish characters with supernatural auras from ordinary humans and from each other. (E.g., you can look at a mage and at a vampire, and tell that they are both supernatural and are of different types of one another, but you don't automatically know that the one aura means &quot;wizard&quot; and the other means &quot;dead and drinks blood.&quot; If you then saw another vampire's aura you could tell it was of the same type as the first vampire, and if you saw the first vampire drink somebody's blood, you can probably put 2 + 2 together.)<br /> <br /> A vampire with the Obfuscate Discipline could contest Aura Sight with a Clash of Wills, largely the same as contesting another vampire using Auspex. Various Mage spells, such as Cloak Nimbus, could do the same.<br /> <br /> Mages with even rudimentary understanding of the Prime Arcanum can cast a spell to identify fellow mages on sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T18:07:20-07:00","id":1258632,"title":"","content":"I believe the answer to all three questions is &quot;not inherently&quot;.<br /> <br /> Demons finding mages or vampires: Perhaps an Embed, Exploit or Demonic Form could do it, but I don't know of any. (Edit: Aura Sight)<br /> <br /> Mages finding mages: Mages with Active Mage Sight can tell when another mage is casting a spell, and there's a Prime spell for determining whether the subject is a Sleeper (regular human), Sleepwalker (not regular human) or Awakened (mage). Mages also know when most supernatural effect occurs (due to Passive Mage Sight) so they can get reasons to go snooping around even if the other person isn't behaving suspiciously.<br /> <br /> Vampires hiding from demons: Vampires can use Obfuscate to hide themselves. An Obfuscate Devotion would be able to hide their nature without hiding themselves. Vampires can also use Blush of Health to appear alive in order to fool mundane senses. Otherwise vampires with low Humanity will appear deathly pale or corpselike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T20:08:55-07:00","id":1258992,"title":"","content":"This question is for a possible storyline: If an angel runs out of Essence in Twilight (say, Discorporates after a terrible fight and uses up its last Essence on some task) and is suitably isolated, will it just stay inert until the GM (or someone else) claims it?<br /> <br /> What happens if someone drags it into our material world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T21:55:39-07:00","id":1259009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1258992#post1258992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question is for a possible storyline: If an angel runs out of Essence in Twilight (say, Discorporates after a terrible fight and uses up its last Essence on some task) and is suitably isolated, will it just stay inert until the GM (or someone else) claims it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if it Discorporates it's winding up back at secure Infrastructure where it can presumably refuel, but yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens if someone drags it into our material world? </div> </div> </div>That will depend heavily upon the method, because Twilight is mostly not a separate place from the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T22:40:34-07:00","id":1259013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1259009#post1259009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if it Discorporates it's winding up back at secure Infrastructure where it can presumably refuel, but yes..</div> </div> </div> </div>D'oh! I thought Discorporation simply sent you back into Twilight. Nope - it burns all your Corpus, and your reform back &quot;in a safe place.&quot; I had thought that you simply shifted back to Twilight, and if you were at zero Essence you had a dead battery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1259009#post1259009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That will depend heavily upon the method, because Twilight is mostly not a separate place from the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I find the vocabulary confusing. I understand that Twilight is also part of &quot;the material world&quot; in contrast to The Shadow, which is separated from the material world by The Gauntlet. The Shadow is also not The Underworld, which is related to the afterlife. But what is the proper term for our part of the material plane that is not in Twilight? Since the power to move from Twilight and take on a body is Materialize, I want to call our normal physical plane the &quot;material plane&quot; but that's not the canon vocabulary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T23:02:18-07:00","id":1259021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1259013#post1259013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I find the vocabulary confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The material world&quot; suffices. I'm not quibbling over the choice of words, I'm saying that &quot;dragging an angel into the material world&quot; is going to be largely indistinguishable from forcing it to materialize, which is not a thing that is usually accomplished without specific abilities or exploits, the particular examples of which are going to strongly influence the answer to &quot;what happens if someone does this?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T07:05:23-07:00","id":1259069,"title":"","content":"I usually just say &quot;the material&quot;. When an ephemeral entity is in the material they default to their Twilight Form. If they, for whatever reason, are forced to take a physical form you can just say that they're Materialized (as per that Manifestation Condition), or perhaps physical if you want to distinguish between applying Materialized and other methods of forcing them out of Twilight Form (like removing Twilight from the area).<br /> <br /> As for what happens, it really depends on how it happens (and sometimes what you think should happen). Most methods of forcing an angel to Materialize applies that Condition to it, which protects it from Essence bleed. If they become physical without a Manifestation Condition (for example, by removing Twilight from the area) then it's up to the table to decide. Is it the state of Twilight that enforced Essence bleed, or is it that they're too alien for the material that they can't sustain themselves without anchoring themselves to the material through use of Manifestations? You decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T10:47:29-07:00","id":1259250,"title":"","content":"I believe that a demon making a physical attack would roll Strength + Brawl - Defense dice. However angels have Power, which is not broken down into Physical/Mental/Social subcategories. So would an angel roll Power + Brawl - Defense dice? I ask because &quot;The Lambent&quot; angel in the &quot;How an Angel Dies&quot; story had a Power of 12, and other sample angels have a Power of 8. This seems like a large dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T12:13:16-07:00","id":1259263,"title":"","content":"Angels don't have Skills. They have their own rules in the appendix that you might want to read through. Attacks are Power + Finesse - Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T12:16:06-07:00","id":1259265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1259250#post1259250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that a demon making a physical attack would roll Strength + Brawl - Defense dice. However angels have Power, which is not broken down into Physical/Mental/Social subcategories. So would an angel roll Power + Brawl - Defense dice? I ask because &quot;The Lambent&quot; angel in the &quot;How an Angel Dies&quot; story had a Power of 12, and other sample angels have a Power of 8. This seems like a large dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't use skills, as Tessie advised - however yes, their dice pools for most actions quickly become very, very large after Rank 2. <br /> <br /> This is true for all ephemerals, and is one of the things that makes them a large threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T16:13:59-07:00","id":1259305,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the information and the friendly corrections :-) I am finding the mechanics to be a bit confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T22:30:05-07:00","id":1259532,"title":"","content":"If a mortal had acces to a Gadget that allowed them to shift in and out of Twilight:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Could they use that to commit robberies, sneaking in places invisibly and intangibly, materializing, committing the theft, and shifting out to escape?</li> <li>If the can shift belongings with them, could they set up a &quot;parallel apartment&quot; in their own apartment, invisible to normal mortals?</li> </ol>Now, I'm not saying that these would be good ideas - the mortal might run into something that is very dangerous. But this is the sort of gadget I could see a mortal might think is a great idea and only find out later that it can be dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T22:38:32-07:00","id":1259533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1259532#post1259532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mortal had acces to a Gadget that allowed them to shift in and out of Twilight:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Could they use that to commit robberies, sneaking in places invisibly and intangibly, materializing, committing the theft, and shifting out to escape?</li> <li>If the can shift belongings with them, could they set up a &quot;parallel apartment&quot; in their own apartment, invisible to normal mortals?</li> </ol>Now, I'm not saying that these would be good ideas - the mortal might run into something that is very dangerous. But this is the sort of gadget I could see a mortal might think is a great idea and only find out later that it can be dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing could go wrong!<br /> <br /> Also both are possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T08:13:27-07:00","id":1259599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1259532#post1259532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mortal had acces to a Gadget that allowed them to shift in and out of Twilight:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Could they use that to commit robberies, sneaking in places invisibly and intangibly, materializing, committing the theft, and shifting out to escape?</li> <li>If the can shift belongings with them, could they set up a &quot;parallel apartment&quot; in their own apartment, invisible to normal mortals?</li> </ol>Now, I'm not saying that these would be good ideas - the mortal might run into something that is very dangerous. But this is the sort of gadget I could see a mortal might think is a great idea and only find out later that it can be dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Gadget that can shift in an out of Twilight is tricky. Demons usually don't have direct access to Twilight, so you are going to be using liberal interpretation and Near Field effects if you want that exactly.<br /> <br /> Another option is the Exploit Living Shadow - you turn into a 2D Shadow. Similar effect.<br /> <br /> For the &quot;parallel apartment&quot;, you could use the Exploit Rip the Gates or maybe Solitary Confinement.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, your mortal is going to go Stigmatic in a hurry, due to all this ambient Aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T12:47:12-07:00","id":1259649,"title":"","content":"The vendor of such items is a very exclusive auction house, (Warner, Hunter and Web) of three Tempter demons who cater to the rich and foolish. They are not nice demons. They are going to be one of the antagonists in a chronicle I am trying to design. <br /> <br /> The Gadget will have charges, with each charge taking your from the Material to Twilight or from Twilight to the Material.<br /> <br /> It has an <b>odd</b> number of charges. &gt;:-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T10:27:42-07:00","id":1259832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1259532#post1259532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mortal had acces to a Gadget that allowed them to shift in and out of Twilight:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Could they use that to commit robberies, sneaking in places invisibly and intangibly, materializing, committing the theft, and shifting out to escape?</li> <li>If the can shift belongings with them, could they set up a &quot;parallel apartment&quot; in their own apartment, invisible to normal mortals?</li> </ol>Now, I'm not saying that these would be good ideas - the mortal might run into something that is very dangerous. But this is the sort of gadget I could see a mortal might think is a great idea and only find out later that it can be dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>The frequency of twilight would have to be selected and as with many things a demon would likely be limited to ghostly, spiritual or astral twilight but not have direct access to angelic twilight. For all but ghostly twilight your first point would be easily a yes. Ghostly twilight has to worry about occasional ghost buildings that could be a complication but those are rare enough to not be a common issue.<br /> As to your second point, if they had a gadget that could shift themself and carried items, its possible they could have another gadget that did a similar effect to an area. For leaving items in twilight however that would depend entirely on the gadget in question. Though generally I'd say if you dropped an item either a) it immidiate returns to physical form and leaves twilight or b) remains in twlight for the duration of the ability or for the scene, whichever is shorter.<br /> <br /> As to your later post on 'charges' it sounds best if you were to do this as a oneshot gadget as they are the only limited use gadget currently. On your idea of 'odd' number of charges I do not think that would work personally. The gadget would shift you and maintain your pressence in twilight for the duration and then return you at the end, at least going by conventions of similar abilitlies regarding twilight but gadgets are varied enough that it is possible that one could be made to not function in that way. I'd recommend against 'permanent' shifts to twlight being possible as an unexpected side effect of this could actually be evasion or immunity to angelic attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T21:39:01-07:00","id":1259921,"title":"","content":"BTW, the point was not to screw over the players by having the Gadget have an odd number of charges, it was to set up a plot line where the players would be asked to rescue a mortal stuck in Twilight. This would expose the Gadget provider as a Not Nice Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T07:21:38-07:00","id":1259963,"title":"","content":"Exploited Gadgets still use their Aether stores, I think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T10:51:52-07:00","id":1259992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1259963#post1259963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exploited Gadgets still use their Aether stores, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exploited gadgets don't spend aether to be used but require 1 aether per month to maintain themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T11:06:03-07:00","id":1259994,"title":"","content":"That said, it looks like an Exploited gadget requiring it to eat up an Aether per use is an appropriate limitation/tparameter for the gadget to make it more potent. I am mostly going off of Interface\u2019s story \u201cFifth\u201d for this one though, where Carbon\u2019s Deep Pockets and Four Minutes Ago gadgets both required it and are pretty dang potent. As such, it\u2019s entirely plausible that a \u201ctransition into Twilight\u201d gadget would work by requiring an Aether per shift from Twilight to mundane and back, and having only five aether in it...though given how hard Aether can be to get, that sounds like a theft rather than a gift from a cruel gadgeteer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T23:37:06-07:00","id":1260841,"title":"","content":"When using the Efficiency embed when you already have Good Time Management, would the ensuing time for the extended action be quartered (the two effects stacking) or would one simply override the other (and thus it remains halved regardless)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T02:19:23-07:00","id":1260870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1260841#post1260841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using the Efficiency embed when you already have Good Time Management, would the ensuing time for the extended action be quartered (the two effects stacking) or would one simply override the other (and thus it remains halved regardless)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Separate sources that don't say anything about not stacking. So I'd say they stack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T09:52:59-07:00","id":1262374,"title":"","content":"A demon uses the Possession Exploit to possess Fred. In the next scene Fred's body takes enough damage to be fatal. What happens to the demon? If she reappears, where does reappear? Is she damaged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T11:40:27-07:00","id":1262383,"title":"","content":"Is it plausible to have an integrator demon player character as a spy? Their has been some conflict in our group if that should stay as antagonist only or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T12:36:40-07:00","id":1262388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1262383#post1262383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it plausible to have an integrator demon player character as a spy? Their has been some conflict in our group if that should stay as antagonist only or not</div> </div> </div> </div>Plausible? Absolutely. But if having one in that particular group kills the fun for some people, it may be best to shelve that particular beat until you have a group where everyone is okay with potential intra-party conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" 