lie to the other characters, why should they assume that their contact is honest with them? The scene where they go to betray the party would probably end up pretty awesome. :-) <br /> <br /> In a different gaming system I let one of the players run a serial killer, as long as they agreed that the other players were off limits. The other players never figured it out....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T13:20:23-07:00","id":1262399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1262393#post1262393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok this is more conceptual, but what makes a psychopomp a psychopomp? All their embeds don't really show me they are builders, unless you only show how they plan infrastructure in plain sight and transporting supplies</div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to\u2026?<br /> <br /> Mundane Embeds deal with obfuscation and dodgy symbolic legerdemain because those are the sorts of occult tricks Psychopomps made use of as the assembly technicians for the hidden machinery of the universe under the Demiurge. &quot;I put together covert magical workings according to the instructions of my creator&quot; is a really broad umbrella.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T13:31:49-07:00","id":1262402,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well what about them cleaning out spirits and ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:05:07-07:00","id":1262408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1262402#post1262402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, well what about them cleaning out spirits and ghosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's specialist kit to begin with - a Wheel's going to have almost no familiarity with the principles of attuning to the Shadow's frequency of ephemera if all they did for God was orchestrate one-night stands or meddle with the feng shui of a public park.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:16:13-07:00","id":1262409,"title":"","content":"Yes but it's pointed out one of their assignments is to clear an area of those things, so why is there no embed for it? Unless it's because angels are naturally ephemeral, which case I can understand no embeds for it specifically","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:31:30-07:00","id":1262412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1262409#post1262409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but it's pointed out one of their assignments is to clear an area of those things, so why is there no embed for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason there's no Embed to &quot;arrange for select reincarnations,&quot; with a side order of &quot;making an area baneful to ephemeral beings doesn't even require supernatural powers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:37:32-07:00","id":1262414,"title":"","content":"I think I understand now. Think less of literal builder and more like a manager, manipulating events using subterfuge to build infrastructure. Thanks Satchel!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T12:35:09-07:00","id":1262706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1262374#post1262374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A demon uses the Possession Exploit to possess Fred. In the next scene Fred's body takes enough damage to be fatal. What happens to the demon? If she reappears, where does reappear? Is she damaged?</div> </div> </div> </div>This question slipped to the previous page without an answer. Does anyone have an answer? Spirits and Ghosts don't die when the person they possess dies AFAIK. What about demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T13:35:28-07:00","id":1262720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1262706#post1262706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This question slipped to the previous page without an answer. Does anyone have an answer? Spirits and Ghosts don't die when the person they possess dies AFAIK. What about demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the Demon becomes insubstantial to possess the victim, my opinion is that when the possessed die he returns to be insubstantial and materializes normally as if the effect had ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T15:20:49-07:00","id":1262750,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any cool combined exploits from your analyst characters<br /> <br /> One i'm proud of making combines possession and hellhound. It's sorta like being spirit claimed, except by a demon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 10-25-2018, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T02:08:21-07:00","id":1263172,"title":"","content":"This is a scenario I ran into in a game, and has bugged me ever since. Is an Angel using an Influence to make Infrastructure harder to hack via die pool penalty a legitimate (or a good) tactic, particularly when the Angel themselves hasn't appeared in the game personally? To me it feels like an artificial means of increasing the difficulty of hacking Infrastructure, and I can't find anything in the book that supports it, but I wonder if I'm looking at it right? I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T11:42:22-07:00","id":1263220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1263172#post1263172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a scenario I ran into in a game, and has bugged me ever since. Is an Angel using an Influence to make Infrastructure harder to hack via die pool penalty a legitimate (or a good) tactic, particularly when the Angel themselves hasn't appeared in the game personally? To me it feels like an artificial means of increasing the difficulty of hacking Infrastructure, and I can't find anything in the book that supports it, but I wonder if I'm looking at it right? I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's going to depend heavily on the scenario, given what Infrastructure hacking entails. The nature of occult matrices and the scarcity of vantages on angelic Twilight make it theoretically workable, at least, but the particulars matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:37:03-07:00","id":1263242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1263220#post1263220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's going to depend heavily on the scenario, given what Infrastructure hacking entails. The nature of occult matrices and the scarcity of vantages on angelic Twilight make it theoretically workable, at least, but the particulars matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is I am completely devoid on the particulars of the Angel - I only learned of the Angel afterwards, out of character, after I started asking around why Conceilment Infrastructure may be at a -5 penalty instead of -3. All I knew at the time was it was happening with the first Infrastructure the group was infiltrating, that the two Demon ring I was in were both at Primum 1, and that the Infrastructure was in a pocket dimension in the back of a coffee shop draining something from teens of varying backgrounds. We couldn\u2019t get any information because the penalty was so high and cooperation was discouraged on account of nobody keeping an eye out for trouble if we did, in spite of dealing with the mortal guards.<br /> <br /> I will openly admit, this aspect of that game is something I am bitter about even after a full year, and I wanted to get another perspective on it. I previously had the same problem due to a misuse of another ST on the Obsession condition, and talking about it here helped. Even knowing it\u2019s theoretically possible helps some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-28-2018, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T14:57:14-07:00","id":1263262,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'd like to have a character who's the trope of the Evil but Suave Town Sheriff, like Gary Cole's character, Lucas Black, in the original TV series &quot;American Gothic.&quot; He would be running a small town to give cover for a a nearby Godmachine cult based on the The Farm, which was the headquarters of the real world &quot;The Covenant, the Arm and the Sword of the Lord.&quot; In the TV show it's intimated that he's the devil himself. My question is how to design him.<ul><li>Angel: This has the right level of power (at least a low rank angel) but the character should have a lot of charm and creativity in his maliciousness. GM angels tend to be unimaginative.</li> <li>An Integrator Demon: This has all the right feel and powers, but would the GM use a demon to guard Infrastructure?</li> <li>A cultist with supernatural merits: This works in the plot since he would be the head cultist, but would this character be powerful enough to dominate a small town and even pose a threat to a demon who stumbles in to town?</li> <li>A Mage: This works well for powers. Are their mages alligned with the GM?</li> </ul>My difficulty is that the more powerful NPC's get in the GM's employ, the more mechanical they seem and less charismatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T09:29:34-07:00","id":1263368,"title":"","content":"How would you write up a Form Power that allows a demon to encode information in a physical substance (e.g. honey, which you eat to learn from)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T09:37:39-07:00","id":1263369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1263368#post1263368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you write up a Form Power that allows a demon to encode information in a physical substance (e.g. honey, which you eat to learn from)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why a Form Power? That sounds like an Embed or maybe Near Field Gadget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T09:53:50-07:00","id":1263376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1263369#post1263369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why a Form Power? That sounds like an Embed or maybe Near Field Gadget.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking form power because the material would be produced, rather than just having the info 'imprinted' onto it, and because I wanted to be able to encode large amounts of information - much more than, for example, Special Message.<br /> <br /> Also, what's a Near Field Gadget?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T10:18:09-07:00","id":1263381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1263376#post1263376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking form power because the material would be produced, rather than just having the info 'imprinted' onto it, and because I wanted to be able to encode large amounts of information - much more than, for example, Special Message.<br /> <br /> Also, what's a Near Field Gadget?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gadget with a Near Field Effect. Basically an existing Embed/Exploit that doesn't quite do what you want, but is close enough with some stretching.<br /> <br /> What kind of information? Skill dots worth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T10:34:10-07:00","id":1263385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1263381#post1263381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of information? Skill dots worth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that much - novels' worth, but it's at the same remove from you as if you had read it, or someone had told you. It gives you information, not skill. You could encode a guide on how to make stuff, but it wouldn't give you a dot in Craft (though it could be justification for buying up dots with EXP).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T11:28:17-07:00","id":1263393,"title":"","content":"Near Field of Download Knowledge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T01:28:20-07:00","id":1263515,"title":"","content":"Would the tricks used by Whispering Oak in Enemy Action be a useful thing to play around with here? The acorns provided information to those who ate them, which was copied from other characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T22:09:06-07:00","id":1263977,"title":"","content":"What powers/merits would you give a GM cult leader? <br /> <br /> I decided to simply make the sheriff of the small town dominated by a cult to be a high cult leader. He always wears mirror shade sunglasses to hide his stigmata of mirrored irises. He should have all the intimidation and swagger of a powerful small town sheriff with an added edge of supernatural menace. However, I'm not sure how to give him that menace. Most of the supernatural merits seem pretty tame. Do you have any suggestions as to how to make him more of a threat? Is there a way for a cult priest to curse players or afflict them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T07:01:15-07:00","id":1264025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1263977#post1263977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What powers/merits would you give a GM cult leader?<br /> <br /> I decided to simply make the sheriff of the small town dominated by a cult to be a high cult leader. He always wears mirror shade sunglasses to hide his stigmata of mirrored irises. He should have all the intimidation and swagger of a powerful small town sheriff with an added edge of supernatural menace. However, I'm not sure how to give him that menace. Most of the supernatural merits seem pretty tame. Do you have any suggestions as to how to make him more of a threat? Is there a way for a cult priest to curse players or afflict them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this isn't so much a power for the sheriff himself, but you can always just say that there's some form of Infrastructure in the town that enhances him somehow (e.g. he has Influence (Intimidation) and can spend WP in place of Essence to activate it), or you could crib sorcery rules from that Mummy dark era for curses, or you could just have an Imperative or a minor Angel Fettered to him and helping him out.<br /> <br /> Really this all depends on whether the PCs are going to be mortals or Demons. If they're Demons, I don't think there's a tremendous amount he'll be able to do. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T09:42:10-07:00","id":1264061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1264025#post1264025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really this all depends on whether the PCs are going to be mortals or Demons. If they're Demons, I don't think there's a tremendous amount he'll be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your suggestions! I'd like him to be quite scary and unpleasant for mortals, but not so much perhaps to demons. He will be an easier challenge to them especially since he doesn't know about demons nor that the players are not simply mortals.<br /> <br /> A malevolent and domineering sheriff in an area where cell phones mysteriously don't work would be a threat to an average mortal. He probably would have some increased resistance to demon embeds, but his deputies won't. This would give the PCs a chance to shine as well as perhaps some motivation. (&quot;He's got Martha in jail on some trumped up drug charge! What to we do?&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T16:18:32-07:00","id":1264147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1264061#post1264061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for your suggestions! I'd like him to be quite scary and unpleasant for mortals, but not so much perhaps to demons. He will be an easier challenge to them especially since he doesn't know about demons nor that the players are not simply mortals.<br /> <br /> A malevolent and domineering sheriff in an area where cell phones mysteriously don't work would be a threat to an average mortal. He probably would have some increased resistance to demon embeds, but his deputies won't. This would give the PCs a chance to shine as well as perhaps some motivation. (&quot;He's got Martha in jail on some trumped up drug charge! What to we do?&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Murder By Improbability until the cheese stands alone.<br /> <br /> It'd be like the Final Destination movies from the sheriff's perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T10:23:23-07:00","id":1264292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1264147#post1264147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Murder By Improbability until the cheese stands alone.<br /> <br /> It'd be like the Final Destination movies from the sheriff's perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to approach it. To the extent that any deputy or sheriff are stigmatic, its effects are limited:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">If the target is touched by the supernatural in any way, however, then Murder by Improbability does not function in this manner. Instead, it makes the character extremely, possibly fatally, unlucky \u2014 but the demon still needs to nudge that character\u2019s fate in the direction of death. (DtD p170). </span></span> </div> </div> </div>Your idea is a good one, but I don't know how much you need to know about a person for MbI to work. Does the PC have to know the victim's name? See them once? How do you play it?<br /> <br /> The thing I like about this set-up is that it provides a nice sandbox (Small Town Dominated by Evil Cult) in which the players can learn about the gaming system and the scope of their abilities. There are dangers and the possibility of Compromise, but a clever player should be able to handle it pretty well. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T23:57:15-07:00","id":1264385,"title":"","content":"Four Minutes Ago is also good if you want a Final Destination effect; to an external viewer, it also is going to cause horrendous coincidences and so forth that kill people (or whatever else the PCs did).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T10:55:38-07:00","id":1264451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1264292#post1264292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one way to approach it. To the extent that any deputy or sheriff are stigmatic, its effects are limited:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was operating on the knowledge that only the Sheriff was Stigmatic for sure - deputies and other officers, maybe. MbI could winnow aware their support with fatal accidents. The Demons could make weird attacks against the remainder with Cause and Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T12:13:49-07:00","id":1264473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1264451#post1264451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I was operating on the knowledge that only the Sheriff was Stigmatic for sure - deputies and other officers, maybe. MbI could winnow aware their support with fatal accidents. The Demons could make weird attacks against the remainder with Cause and Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not criticizing - your idea is a good one. It's precisely that sort of thinking the I want my players to pursue so that they can see what works and what doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T08:52:10-08:00","id":1265837,"title":"","content":"I am prepping my first DtD game for tomorrow atm, I will run it and it's going to be a one-shot, the one from the core book (&quot;How an angel dies&quot;).<br /> I will use the characters from the ready made characters book. Right now I am realizing that they have lots of Embeds but no Exploits at all, not even in the advanced sheets. That feels odd.<br /> <br /> Question: Should I add an Exploit per character sheet or can I just ignore them for now, given that we're all new to demon and it's a lot to take in as it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24377-wayward-isabel","name":"Wayward Isabel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T09:05:56-08:00","id":1265838,"title":"","content":"I would leave it up to the players. But if you want, you could give them an exploit so that when they use one you can not only show the benefits but also the detriments (ie compromise)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T09:36:55-08:00","id":1265850,"title":"","content":"My players have never played Demon, they know little about it. So I won't ask them. And I am new to it as well, although I at least read the book. So a &quot;well, you decide&quot; answer does not even help me here sorry. Yes or no please:<br /> <br /> Can I just let the Exploits be for now and still run an enjoyable, successful game of Demon?<br /> <br /> P.S. Yes I might be overthinking this right now because I'm damn nervous about tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24377,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24377-wayward-isabel","user":"Wayward Isabel","date":". 11-09-2018, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24377-wayward-isabel","name":"Wayward Isabel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T10:43:17-08:00","id":1265868,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can run an enjoyable, successful game of Demon without Exploits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T11:44:28-08:00","id":1265882,"title":"","content":"Seconding: Exploits are nice and dramatic, but especially starting out, using only Embeds might work better - they are more covert, and don't risk Compromise, meaning the PCs don't have to pursue Pacts to patch their Covers up as much. There are plenty of other methods to spend Aether and show-case Compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:15:52-08:00","id":1266521,"title":"","content":"There is a linchpin to some Concealment Infrastructure hidden in a sigh-in clipboard. Anyone who signs in will be oblivious to anything unusual in the building.<br /> <br /> What happens if to a Demon who signs in? Do they roll versus the effect? Or does Concealment Infrastructure not work on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T17:28:43-08:00","id":1266548,"title":"","content":"Concealment Infrastructure doesn't work on Demons and Stigmatics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T20:25:16-08:00","id":1266591,"title":"","content":"Is there a template for junior cultist, mid-level cultist, and high level cultist in print or elsewhere? I can use the cultists from the sample chronicle in DtD, but I think that high level/stigmatic cultists would have supernatural merits. (Yes, I can cobble them up on my own, but I've go a lot of NPC's to flesh out and a few typical mooks would be helpful). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T22:17:53-08:00","id":1266610,"title":"","content":"Closest you'll get is Mystery Cult Initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T13:56:41-08:00","id":1268029,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty ignorant of the CoD ruleset, so please excuse this dumb question. Rasha, a rank 5 angel, is listed as having a Power of of 10 and a defense of 10. If for some weird reason Benny the Demon with a Strength of 4 and a Defense of 3 gets into a fist fight with Rasha, then Rasha would role 7 dice against Benny with each success registered as a point of bashing damage, and Benny has only a chance die against Rasha which can do at most one point of bashing. If Benny had a knife rated at 1L, he still only has a chance die, but if he does hit he does 2L damage (one for the die, one for the extra damage of the knife). Is this correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T14:06:10-08:00","id":1268033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1268029#post1268029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty ignorant of the CoD ruleset, so please excuse this dumb question. Rasha, a rank 5 angel, is listed as having a Power of of 10 and a defense of 10. If for some weird reason Benny the Demon with a Strength of 4 and a Defense of 3 gets into a fist fight with Rasha, then Rasha would role 7 dice against Benny with each success registered as a point of bashing damage, and Benny has only a chance die against Rasha which can do at most one point of bashing. If Benny had a knife rated at 1L, he still only has a chance die, but if he does hit he does 2L damage (one for the die, one for the extra damage of the knife). Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this blows your mind.<br /> <br /> As an ephemeral entity, Rasha uses Power + Finesse to attack. If we're using the stats in the Chronicles book, that means he has a dicepool of 22 for attacking Benny (10 Power + 15 Finesse - 3 Defense).<br /> <br /> But yes, Benny would likely have a chance die. To hit Rasha bare-handed they would roll Strength + Brawl - 10 (Rasha's Defense). And if he manages to hit with a 1L knife (Strength + Weaponry - Defense) he does 2 damage, but it would likely be Bashing damage, due to this rule:<br /> <br /> 'Physical attacks on a manifest entity that normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane. Despite appearing to the naked eye and being solid, a manifest spirit, ghost, or angel doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure.'<br /> <br /> If Benny was using Rasha's bane, it would do 2 Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral entities can get pretty powerful, and Rank 5 is the most powerful kind there's actually rules for, so Rank 5 entities tend to be 'final boss'-like in terms of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T14:36:50-08:00","id":1268049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1268033#post1268033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope this blows your mind.<br /> <br /> As an ephemeral entity, Rasha uses Power + Finesse to attack. If we're using the stats in the Chronicles book, that means he has a dicepool of 22 for attacking Benny (10 Power + 15 Finesse - 3 Defense).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>THANK YOU! I can find so few examples of actual battle mechanics played out that I am often unsure of what is deadly and what is not. Your are of course correct that Rasha is overwhelmingly powerful - he's a Rank 5 angel. However, even Jenn (CoD p.259) who is a rank 2 angel has Power+Finesse = 8 dice which is double the 4 dice of Barroom Brawling of the World Weary PI (p.121) and comparable to the Handguns (4) + Dexterity (3) = 7 dice of the Slick Professional Grifter (p.121). I'm not complaining - its just that I didn't understand that a Rank 2 angel is punching for bashing damage comparable to the Lethal damage of a handgun armed opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T22:40:10-08:00","id":1268732,"title":"","content":"In the DtD I read: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Blast: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The entity may wound opponents at a distance. Range is equal to 10 yards per dot of Power, and the entity does not suffer range penalties. If the activation roll succeeds, the Blast wounds as a lethal weapon. The entity may increase the lethality of its Blast by paying Essence \u2014 every 2 Essence spent increases the \u201cweapon\u201d by one lethal damage. The maximum weapon bonus is equal to the entity\u2019s Rank.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>So for example, consider &quot;The Brilliant&quot; (p.220) with a Power of 9 and a Finesse of 8 and who has the Blast numen. Let's assume the target's defense is 3.<ul><li>How many dice does he roll to attack? Power+Finesse-Defense=14? Even though the attack is ranged?</li> <li>Is the damage of the attack equal to the number of successes?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T20:39:48-08:00","id":1269424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1268732#post1268732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the DtD I read:<br /> <br /> So for example, consider &quot;The Brilliant&quot; (p.220) with a Power of 9 and a Finesse of 8 and who has the Blast numen. Let's assume the target's defense is 3.<ul><li>How many dice does he roll to attack? Power+Finesse-Defense=14? Even though the attack is ranged?</li> <li>Is the damage of the attack equal to the number of successes?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I asked this question on the RPG StackExchange and <a href=\"https://rpg.stackexchange.com/questions/135968/what-is-the-base-damage-for-an-attack-from-an-angels-blast-numen\" target=\"_blank\">got a useful answer.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T03:38:35-08:00","id":1269500,"title":"","content":"The answer is correct, but also remember that Blast is supposed to be flavoured in some fashion. Depending on how you flavour it, it can make sense to apply Defense (if the Blast can be likened to a thrown weapon) and/or Armor (if the Blast takes the form of projectiles) to the attack even if it's not stated in the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T13:09:46-08:00","id":1270412,"title":"","content":"This is more a semantics question, but this is the last paragraph for the Suborned Infrastructure Gadgets;<br /> <br /> \u201cDue to the connection to the God-Machine that the sub- orned Infrastructure confers to the hardware of the gadget, hacking into the subroutines used to create it is easier than normal. The player gains a +2 bonus to all rolls to investigate or reverse engineer the gadget. Lambda creation is also easier for the same reason, allowing a +2 bonus to all rolls to create a lambda using a gadget created with suborned Infrastructure. If the demon took the time to precise engineer the gadget, these rolls also benefit from the 8-again quality.\u201d<br /> <br /> Does that mean that even when constructing a Lambda (as in adding all the other gadget bits into the new hardware) using a Precision Engineered Suborned Infrastructure gadget, you get 8-again on your rolls? It seems to suggest that, since the Precision Engineering aspect already grants 8-again when you disassemble a gadget, and that kind of repetition isn\u2019t done much elsewhere (even in places where it\u2019d be very helpful, such as Implanted gadgets).<br /> <br /> Related question; <br /> <br /> \u201cWhen a demon uses any gadget made with suborned Infrastructure, it is always over-clocked (p. 157) unless it is a form or one-shot gadget.\u201d<br /> <br /> Does that include a Lambda that has mundane hardware, but one of its component gadgets was made from Suborned Infrastructure. I feel that it negates the usefulness of using a Suborned Infrastructure gadget for this in the first place, but that\u2019s just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 11-24-2018, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T09:54:42-08:00","id":1272408,"title":"","content":"Henry is a white collar criminal who got sent to jail for embezzlement at a bank. His life is ruined. I, as a demon, make a pact with Henry to take on that aspect of his life. Now I am a known embezzler, and Henry's record is clean and he can get a new job.<br /> <br /> How far do the changes go? Certainly Henry's family and friends will be affected by the change. But will the prison records show that I was in prison? Will the court records show that I was convicted? What about the FBI records? <br /> <br /> Could the pact change history so that he was exonerated and I was actually convicted for the crime so that he gains complete innocence in all records everywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T21:30:23-08:00","id":1275015,"title":"","content":"In the Chronicle I am writing the final chapter involves the GodMachine trying to gently &quot;nudge&quot; a sleeping ancient entity to align it with the GM's local occult matrix. This would provide the local GM infrastructure with substantially more Essence. Waking it would be a Bad Idea from the GM's point of view, since this would cause the destruction of the matrix. The players will have to decide if and how to intervene.<br /> <br /> So I need a &quot;kaiju&quot; level spirit or something, a critter that can squish a Rank 4 angel. I could just go without stats and run it as a narrative device, but it might be nice to actually have a write-up. Nothing I've seen in the Night Horrors book is at this level. Can anyone point me to a write-up of something like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T03:35:30-08:00","id":1275056,"title":"","content":"Idigam might fit the bill. Check Werewolf 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T07:30:07-08:00","id":1275074,"title":"","content":"And if you don't have access to that book, the following thread may be of use:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/436971-new-idigam\">Link</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T07:28:37-08:00","id":1276240,"title":"","content":"I need some quick advice for a DtD game I will start in the New Year. I have not run an ST or DtD game before, but have experience in other game systems.<br /> <br /> The ring will be three or four new players, Primum 1 or 2 (entry level) Demons. The scenario starts with A Small Town With A Secret. One of the major foils for the PC's will be a small town sheriff who terrorizes the town. He's at least some sort of priest/stigmatic in the local Machine Cult with a few low level powers (he has Clairvoyance to observe any spot in his jurisdiction) and of course the full weight of the Law if the players cross him. <br /> <br /> My question is - is this enough as a challenge for 3-4 demons? Should I make him a low level angel? Or should I hold off on angels until later in the narrative? (You don't pull out the big guns right away).<br /> <br /> A related question: I'd like to have a traveling Messenger angel character to act as the originator of local messianic GM cults. By having the angel be itinerant I could call it in to the storyline if the players need a challenge, or leave it out if they are having difficulties with the storyline as I have written it. Such a messenger would seem to be a pretty common template to exploit religious communities. Can anyone point me to a published character or one on the forum that fits the bill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T19:47:06-08:00","id":1276355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1276240#post1276240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is - is this enough as a challenge for 3-4 demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>How long is he meant to be a challenge for, and in what ways is he supposed to challenge the ring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T20:18:41-08:00","id":1276553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1276355#post1276355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long is he meant to be a challenge for, and in what ways is he supposed to challenge the ring?</div> </div> </div> </div>The chronicle has five chapters and I'd like him to be a challenge for the first one and perhaps the second. As a sheriff, he would have a lot of mundane power and my hope is that the PC&quot;s would have to be careful so as to avoid getting labelled as criminals and damaging their cover. But if they roll over him, he won't be much of a challenge and the whole &quot;Town with an Awful Secret&quot; vibe will be vitiated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T06:34:30-08:00","id":1276621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1276553#post1276553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The chronicle has five chapters and I'd like him to be a challenge for the first one and perhaps the second. As a sheriff, he would have a lot of mundane power and my hope is that the PC&quot;s would have to be careful so as to avoid getting labelled as criminals and damaging their cover. But if they roll over him, he won't be much of a challenge and the whole &quot;Town with an Awful Secret&quot; vibe will be vitiated.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should be able to string a well-connected mortal out as an antagonist for a chapter or two <i>if </i>your players are appropriately paranoid about the fallout if they decide to just take him out.<br /> <br /> If you can find a way to establish that paranoia early - maybe evidence that he was responsible for the recapture of single prior Unchained, and obviously has help from the Machine? - it should help, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T10:21:24-08:00","id":1276661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1276621#post1276621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should be able to string a well-connected mortal out as an antagonist for a chapter or two <i>if </i>your players are appropriately paranoid about the fallout if they decide to just take him out.<br /> <br /> If you can find a way to establish that paranoia early - maybe evidence that he was responsible for the recapture of single prior Unchained, and obviously has help from the Machine? - it should help, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if they aren't cautious enough, you can hit them with the consequences of their actions so they learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T08:13:17-08:00","id":1277505,"title":"","content":"I want to run DtD but I would love to see some fully worked out examples of battle mechanics. I floated this idea on the StackExchange and some of the mods seem amenable. However, I know that I would get details wrong and would need several iterations to get it right. I'd like to start a new discussion topic here for a sample combat of a demon vs. an angel. If that works well, then maybe an example to two demons fighting several humans (to get the combat rules for multiple opponents described). A demon vs. demon example might also be helpful. <br /> <br /> What do you think? Would this be useful to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T10:25:18-08:00","id":1277518,"title":"","content":"That could quickly explode, so maybe start another thread for the examples? You can link to it here, for any who are interested.<br /> <br /> We'll need a little more background information. Resources available to either side. Who has &quot;initiative&quot;. What are each side's goals. What does either side know about the other. Any other environmental factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T10:32:39-08:00","id":1281126,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">One of my antagonists is an angel with the cover of an itinerant Bible salesman. His mission is to slowly subvert evangelical sects into GM cults. One approach to this is to supply copies of &quot;lost&quot; books of revelation and the like.<br /> <br /> So what are some good book titles? <i>Dawn of the Omnissiah by Saint Simon of the Golden Path?</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Technology is a gift of God. After the gift of life it is perhaps the greatest of God's gifts. It is the mother of civilizations, of arts and of sciences.&quot;</i></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2013 (Saint) Freeman Dyson</span> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T14:00:18-08:00","id":1281177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1281126#post1281126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">One of my antagonists is an angel with the cover of an itinerant Bible salesman. His mission is to slowly subvert evangelical sects into GM cults. One approach to this is to supply copies of &quot;lost&quot; books of revelation and the like.<br /> <br /> So what are some good book titles? <i>Dawn of the Omnissiah by Saint Simon of the Golden Path?</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Technology is a gift of God. After the gift of life it is perhaps the greatest of God's gifts. It is the mother of civilizations, of arts and of sciences.&quot;</i></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2013 (Saint) Freeman Dyson</span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.fantasynamegenerators.com/holy-book-names.php\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fantasynamegenerators.co...book-names.php</a><br /> <br /> Running this one a few times might be a good start<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T23:55:55-08:00","id":1281466,"title":"","content":"If i am reading it right the Spoof ability works without a clash of will if the demon roll Cover and obtain a success.<br /> Am i right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T00:09:09-08:00","id":1281469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1281466#post1281466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i am reading it right the Spoof ability works without a clash of will if the demon roll Cover and obtain a success.<br /> Am i right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoofing is a straight roll of Cover that is not resisted or contested, yes. The need to roll for each spoofed effect separately serves as reason enough to still try and avoid suspicion, since even at a relatively high rating you still have about a one in ten chance of failure each time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T02:38:31-08:00","id":1281475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1281469#post1281469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoofing is a straight roll of Cover that is not resisted or contested, yes. The need to roll for each spoofed effect separately serves as reason enough to still try and avoid suspicion, since even at a relatively high rating you still have about a one in ten chance of failure each time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks<br /> So, if the demon succedes in the Cover roll even the Beast's Family resemblance ability would fail right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T04:03:16-08:00","id":1281481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1281475#post1281475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks<br /> So, if the demon succedes in the Cover roll even the Beast's Family resemblance ability would fail right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Also worthy of note: As far as I remember, Beasts don't consider Demons to be family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T08:35:41-08:00","id":1281781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1281481#post1281481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. Also worthy of note: As far as I remember, Beasts don't consider Demons to be family.</div> </div> </div> </div>correct, in fact, beasts HATE demons for how utterly separate they are from all the other supernatural being","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T17:13:13-08:00","id":1281844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1281781#post1281781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">correct, in fact, beasts HATE demons for how utterly separate they are from all the other supernatural being</div> </div> </div> </div>That's\u2026 drastically oversimplifying it.<br /> <br /> In the event of a failed spoof roll, demons register to the Begotten's Family Resemblance ability with a lower ceiling of available information \u2014 the roll literally cannot get an exceptional success against one of the Unchained, which limits what the Beast can glean to the fact that they're looking at a demon of X Primum with approximately N points of Aether to hand; without the benefits of an exceptional success, Family Resemblance cannot convey a demon's strongest supernatural power or open extra Doors for social maneuvering against them.<br /> <br /> That kind of blackout is business as usual for demons, but even outside of the context of trying to probe for secrets a successful Family Resemblance roll pings a Lair vs Primum Clash of Wills that doesn't end without somebody getting a Condition.<br /> <br /> The best case scenario is that both parties tie the roll-off and come away mutually Spooked; if the Beast rolls more successes, the demon is Shaken, but otherwise none the worse for wear, but if the demon rolls more successes, the Beast is Leveraged as they give up some important piece of personal information like where they live or who they work for in the course of making supernatural contact with a demon.<br /> <br /> Between that and the inability to develop Family Ties with the Unchained or otherwise grant them any benefits through their general supernatural-power-booster or be party to a pact, the general issue can be summed up as &quot;their priorities are wildly different and they present a difficulty that even mortals don't to Beasts as characters who otherwise <i>breathe</i> specifically-monstrous social graces.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a lot of effort to keep up for not a lot of benefit from something whose nature just rubs them the wrong way, so most of them don't bother, but &quot;hate&quot; is a bit strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T18:54:58-08:00","id":1281854,"title":"","content":"well I suppose I should've said it differently, but I was really just saying the general stereotype @Sstchel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T09:01:16-08:00","id":1282293,"title":"","content":"I started reading night horrors. I've got a question about the angels in the night horror book. Why don't they have intercepts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T09:07:12-08:00","id":1282294,"title":"","content":"Also is there a difference between an angel being Materialized vs in cover?<br /> <br /> I feel like this is something they freaking need to actually explain. Do angels need mortal mask to have a cover?<br /> <br /> So far for me I use mortal mask when I want an angel to not just have a cover but can change its look when needed <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T12:46:57-08:00","id":1282323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282293#post1282293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started reading night horrors. I've got a question about the angels in the night horror book. Why don't they have intercepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely to save on wordcount from having to explain what Incepts were, and to allow STs the ability to play around with what Incepts they\u2019d have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282294#post1282294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also is there a difference between an angel being Materialized vs in cover?<br /> <br /> I feel like this is something they freaking need to actually explain. Do angels need mortal mask to have a cover?<br /> <br /> So far for me I use mortal mask when I want an angel to not just have a cover but can change its look when needed </div> </div> </div> </div>A Materialized Angel is an Angel in its true form; an Angel in Cover has it Materialized, but hidden from the world as a normal human. Materialized still has an Angel suffer Essence Bleed unless it\u2019s in Infrastructure, but Cover is technically Infrastructure itself minus any Essence/Aether, so an Angel can exist in Cover comfortably without losing Essence.<br /> <br /> It isn\u2019t stated outright that Mortal Mask is the same as Cover, but seeing as how not every Angel with Cover has Mortal Mask, I\u2019d say that Mortal Mask is simply a cruder, more immediate alternative. Cover tends to look entirely human, barring perhaps a rune or sigil (as per the Angels in the Chronicles of Darkness book), whereas Mortal Mask explicitely has something <i>off</i> about it that marks the being out if someone looks closely. An Angel with Mortal Mask could probably get around while materialized, but a Cover would allow it to work far more casually and without needing to spend Essence to activate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-23-2019, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T15:30:31-08:00","id":1282343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282294#post1282294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also is there a difference between an angel being Materialized vs in cover?<br /> <br /> I feel like this is something they freaking need to actually explain. Do angels need mortal mask to have a cover?<br /> <br /> So far for me I use mortal mask when I want an angel to not just have a cover but can change its look when needed</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my understanding of the system. A word on vocabulary: technically Twilight is part of the &quot;material world&quot; but I don't know the word CoD uses for our plain old normal reality so I'll call that the &quot;Material Plane&quot;.<br /> <br /> Angels by default are ephemeral beings and exist in Twilight. While in Twilight they can be performing tasks for the GM on any Infrastructure that might exist in Twilight, or spy on activities in the Material plane. The CoD manual states:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Unless they Manifest or use a power to appear, ephemeral beings remain in their insubstantial state when in the mate- rial world. This state is described as \u201cTwilight.\u201d To beings in Twilight, physical objects appear pale and semitransparent, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">light sources are dimmed and sounds distorted as though underwater. Twilight isn\u2019t an actual place, though, more a description of how ephemera interacts \u2014 or fails to interact \u2014 with material reality.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>If Angels in Twilight are away from Infrastructure for long periods of time they are subject to Essence Bleed. If they Materialize or are in Cover, they don't suffer Essence Bleed. While they are in Twilight some Numina (basically spell powers of an ephemeral being) will still allow Angels to affect the Material plane.<br /> <br /> Materialize is a Manifestation that allows an angel in Twilight to enter/act in the Material plane. (Manifestations are a bit odd: they are a bit like spell powers but they have a specific hierarchy of what each requires before it can be used). They are still not flesh and blood - any Lethal damage they take is merely Bashing damage. The Materialize manifestation states that it requires the &quot;Open Condition&quot; which can happen near Infrastructure or by the concerted actions of cultists. Thus in the right situation an angel can choose to Materialize. This state lasts for one hour per success on the activation roll (Power + Finesse). <br /> <br /> If it Materializes it will look like an angel, so it may choose to use the Mortal Mask Numen to disguise itself, if it has that ability. Subsequently if the angel is in danger it can chose to Discorporate as well, if it has that Manifestation, vanishing back into Twilight. Note that because Mortal Mask requires the expenditure of Essence, a demon may be able to sense that an individual is actually an angel in disguise.<br /> <br /> Cover differs from Materialization in that Cover is an active, ongoing state provided by a specific action of the GodMachine, and not created by some ability of an angel. Unlike Materialization, Cover does not have a time limit. There is no need for Mortal Mask since the Cover is created by the GM. Angelic cover, unlike Demonic cover, is not subject to compromise since it is maintained by the GodMachine. (By that I mean that while a demon may learn that an individual is an angel in Cover, that Cover does not degrade in the metaphysical way that a demon's Cover would degrade.) An angel in Cover is not detectable as an angel, in general, by a demon. <br /> <br /> When an angel is installed into a Cover identity, that identity can by hijacked by a Demon. The DtD manual does not state what happens to the incoming angel that was being installed into that Cover.<br /> <br /> So, in summary, Materialization is a short term entrance into the Material Plane that an angel may do by choice as part of executing its duties. Cover is a long-term state created and assigned to an angel by the GodMachine for a specific purpose. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24502,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","user":"KieranMullen","date":".  Fixed format and added details on detection. 01-23-2019, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T16:02:48-08:00","id":1282345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282294#post1282294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also is there a difference between an angel being Materialized vs in cover?<br /> <br /> I feel like this is something they freaking need to actually explain. Do angels need mortal mask to have a cover?<br /> <br /> So far for me I use mortal mask when I want an angel to not just have a cover but can change its look when needed</div> </div> </div> </div>Cover shortcuts all the Manifestation rules as well as Mortal Mask as a piece of Infrastructure that the angel employs. Long story short, their Cover lets them act as material beings in the capcity of it's design, and is also small enough that it really doesn't have a Linchpin.<br /> <br /> Bunyip has been chomping at the bit to get the clarification on Cover into a book, because yeah, some elaboration would go a long way.<br /> <br /> As for Incepts: Enemy Action was a cramped book, with an above average number of writers for a supplement. Some things got lost in the shuffle- I couldn't squeeze in Sanjha's or Wednesdays Interlocks or Cipher, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T16:04:35-08:00","id":1282346,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24502\" data-vbnamecard=\"24502\">KieranMullen</a> I applaud you for your breakdown. Much more accurate than my own above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282345#post1282345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cover shortcuts all the Manifestation rules as well as Mortal Mask as a piece of Infrastructure that the angel employs. Long story short, their Cover lets them act as material beings in the capcity of it's design, and is also small enough that it really doesn't have a Linchpin.<br /> <br /> Bunyip has been chomping at the bit to get the clarification on Cover into a book, because yeah, some elaboration would go a long way.<br /> <br /> As for Incepts: Enemy Action was a cramped book, with an above average number of writers for a supplement. Some things got lost in the shuffle- I couldn't squeeze in Sanjha's or Wednesdays Interlocks or Cipher, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it possible for us to get a snippet on what those Interlocks and or Ciphers were like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-23-2019, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T16:36:29-08:00","id":1282350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282293#post1282293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started reading night horrors. I've got a question about the angels in the night horror book. Why don't they have intercepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>No published Angel has Incepts, AFAIK. In the case of Night Horrors, I can only speculate. While the book is aimed at DtD players, a lot of it is adaptable to other CoD campaigns. By avoiding Incepts (which are not even in the core DtD manual), the Night Horrors book has a larger potential audience. A lot of the entries are useful in any chronicle based on the GodMachine.<br /> <br /> I can't explain why the angels in the DSG lack Incepts. Probably something to do with deadlines. Incepts are really powerful, and amusing to spring on Demon players who only know the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T06:43:37-08:00","id":1282423,"title":"","content":"To clarify some things. <br /> Can Angels Spoof? <br /> <br /> And in general about Spoofing - when you spoof an effect, you shouldn't be betrayed as non-human, at the same time, supposedly, that doesn't stop the effect. What happens with something like Clairvoyant Sight trying to look at a Demon? If he can't spoof - his true identity will be easily found out. If he can spoof, what does the Sight user actually see? I'm talking about a situation where a Demon has two covers, so seeing the truth would immediately betray him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:05:51-08:00","id":1282487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282423#post1282423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify some things.<br /> Can Angels Spoof?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in general about Spoofing - when you spoof an effect, you shouldn't be betrayed as non-human, at the same time, supposedly, that doesn't stop the effect. What happens with something like Clairvoyant Sight trying to look at a Demon? If he can't spoof - his true identity will be easily found out. If he can spoof, what does the Sight user actually see? I'm talking about a situation where a Demon has two covers, so seeing the truth would immediately betray him. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Cover X and Cover Y are the same person&quot; doesn't actually give away the fact that a character is a supernatural being outside of the implications of an extremely large subtractive difference in bodily volume from a known physical body, a demon can't change Covers under observation, and Clairvoyant Sight in particular is a power that requires concentration to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T16:36:42-08:00","id":1282541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282487#post1282487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't need to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? If a Demon uses Aura Sight on them, the Angel might really wanna appear human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282487#post1282487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Cover X and Cover Y are the same person&quot; doesn't actually give away the fact that a character is a supernatural being outside of the implications of an extremely large subtractive difference in bodily volume from a known physical body, a demon can't change Covers under observation, and Clairvoyant Sight, in particular, is a power that requires concentration to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a situation where a Demon uses Clairvoyant Sight on a person, and instead of observing a man of one race, sees a teenage girl of a different race, doesn't immediately go &quot;demon&quot;. Supposedly, a situation Spoofing should help against? Unless I'm wrong about that.<br /> OR, since the covers were changed, we could say he doesn't get to see anything. Which is as damning as the first situation, since normal humans don't disappear out of this plane of existence for lols.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T17:07:15-08:00","id":1282551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282541#post1282541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? If a Demon uses Aura Sight on them, the Angel might really wanna appear human.</div> </div> </div> </div>And so <i>they will</i>. They're angels, they don't have to worry about maintenance to avoid directly pinging as a supernatural being because the vast majority of investigators aren't going to roll more successes than God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see a situation where a Demon uses Clairvoyant Sight on a person, and instead of observing a man of one race, sees a teenage girl of a different race, doesn't immediately go &quot;demon&quot;. Supposedly, a situation Spoofing should help against? Unless I'm wrong about that. </div> </div> </div>Demons inhabit a setting where &quot;shapeshifting reptilian&quot; is a common variety of cryptid and God simultaneously has no OSHA compliance for Its inner workings (because people aren't supposed to be exposed to those things and develop paranormal abilities) and routinely assigns complex routines that call for everything from sleeper commands to life-swapping to inscrutable curses. There's a <i>lot </i>of other explanations for going &quot;show me This Guy&quot; and getting That Guy that aren't &quot;This Guy is a rogue archon like myself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Setting aside how spoofing is there to keep you from getting directly pinned down by a supernatural power and most personally-targeted remote-viewing powers only tell you where the target is by implication, I <i>did </i>mention a difference in body type specifically as an example.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OR, since the covers were changed, we could say he doesn't get to see anything. Which is as damning as the first situation, since normal humans don't disappear out of this plane of existence for lols. </div> </div> </div>You may notice, if you look around, that Clairvoyant Sight is an outlier in the field of direct-target powers re: not needing a roll. Sometimes your supernatural powers just fizzle. Given the limitations of Clairvoyant Sight in particular, an equally sensible takeaway is that that person you're peering through the wiring to look at was being impersonated by the person you met and you haven't met the actual person in a month.<br /> <br /> Or a successful spoof shows you the character in the Cover you were looking for. High-level deception-aids don't make the Unchained immune to people putting together a dozen little clues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T17:31:04-08:00","id":1282555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282541#post1282541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? If a Demon uses Aura Sight on them, the Angel might really wanna appear human.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see a situation where a Demon uses Clairvoyant Sight on a person, and instead of observing a man of one race, sees a teenage girl of a different race, doesn't immediately go &quot;demon&quot;. Supposedly, a situation Spoofing should help against? Unless I'm wrong about that.<br /> OR, since the covers were changed, we could say he doesn't get to see anything. Which is as damning as the first situation, since normal humans don't disappear out of this plane of existence for lols.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clairvoyant Sight doesn't reveal the nature of the beast and instead is limited by the visual information at display. If you happen to take enough time and covers are near enough, it's not inconceivable to perceive it as someone switching between costumes. If it's close enough that there's not enough time and effort possible for that...well, you live in a world of shapeshifters and quick-workers-a good Wizened can probably do a costume switch faster than normal, the Inguma are a thing, Biokinetics will mess with your day, and the list goes on. A demon can't change without the benefit of Schrodinger's Joke-Basis, so the context clues needed to answer those questions are mostly missing.<br /> <br /> Also, Clairvoyant sight isn't flawless-it can fail to see people, so if for any reason it doesn't find a cover in any scenario, it's not impossible that it's the power failing as much as someone blinking out.<br /> <br /> I don't have my books, so no word on Aura Sight there, though one must note that with Rank and various other things, Angels are kind of hard to reveal as supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T01:13:11-08:00","id":1282597,"title":"","content":"Clairvoyant Sight has no fail condition in it or anything. &quot;It just fails&quot; is very unlikely to fly at my table. Perhaps a roll is what this power actually needs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T17:49:00-08:00","id":1282752,"title":"","content":"I would like to have some GM boosted cultists/simulaca in the chronicle I am designing. They would be large, muscular, monosyllabic single-minded hunters. The players will first meet one when he steps out from the woods behind an NPC and snaps his neck.<br /> <br /> How would such an attack like that work? Surprise can negate defense, but how can a single surprise brawl attack do enough damage to be fatal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T18:11:05-08:00","id":1282756,"title":"","content":"It's one NPC, potentially with unnatural cybernetic augmentations or other occult alterations, taking another NPC by complete surprise. Why bother with deliberate mechanics at that point?<br /> <br /> From a theory angle, primarily with an eye towards if you're considering what happens if he hunts the ring or the ring tries to stop it in progress? Probably the closest analogous situation would combine some access to unarmed lethal damage with the rules for a killing blow, where attack dice automatically succeed. A killing blow is an extremely potent maneuver reserved for when one character has another totally helpless, though. It's not an ambush attack; it's taking your time to find the right artery to squeeze while your victim is thoroughly bound or paralyzed.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to take an ability like this down to the level where it might threaten a player character, I would highly suggest a situation, likely occult, by which it can be prevented before the scenario comes about, on top of the need for surprise. Say, an occult link by which the simulacrum can subject a doomed victim to a killing blow from surprise if it first is able to plant an unnatural item on the victim X hours before, which the victim is still carrying. Something to keep it more interesting and more gameable than a simple save-or-die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T18:20:55-08:00","id":1282757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282346#post1282346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24502\" data-vbnamecard=\"24502\">KieranMullen</a><br /> Is it possible for us to get a snippet on what those Interlocks and or Ciphers were like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll dig around when I don't have Geist/Kingdom Hearts/sudden unexpected victories to deal with and see if I can find them, and if I can't, I'll re-write them-Wednesday was intended to be a Pentagrammist but the potential space issues made me backtrack that.<br /> <br /> Though that does remind me....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T18:25:17-08:00","id":1282758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282597#post1282597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clairvoyant Sight has no fail condition in it or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has use requirements that can outright cause it to not work and conveys no special sensory abilities besides &quot;look at the target remotely.&quot; A dark tunnel can hypothetically thwart it, as can staying in a crowded area.<br /> <br /> All of which is beside the point, which is &quot;concealment does not have to be perfect for a power that requires concentration and can only be directed at targets you've been in contact with in the last month to be no more than a relatively useful espionage tool.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T20:43:37-08:00","id":1282779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282756#post1282756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one NPC, potentially with unnatural cybernetic augmentations or other occult alterations, taking another NPC by complete surprise. Why bother with deliberate mechanics at that point?<br /> <br /> From a theory angle, primarily with an eye towards if you're considering what happens if he hunts the ring or the ring tries to stop it in progress? Probably the closest analogous situation would combine some access to unarmed lethal damage with the rules for a killing blow, where attack dice automatically succeed. A killing blow is an extremely potent maneuver reserved for when one character has another totally helpless, though. It's not an ambush attack; it's taking your time to find the right artery to squeeze while your victim is thoroughly bound or paralyzed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't intend for this antagonist to pull the same trick on PC's (not without at least rolling for surprise!) and I considered just running it by fiat as you suggest in your first paragraph. However, I just thought that it would be odd if the antagonist then just turned out to be your average street tough. I thought of using some Martial Art but it is hard to do enough damage in one turn to be fatal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T01:12:39-08:00","id":1282811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282758#post1282758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has use requirements that can outright cause it to not work and conveys no special sensory abilities besides &quot;look at the target remotely.&quot; A dark tunnel can hypothetically thwart it, as can staying in a crowded area.<br /> <br /> All of which is beside the point, which is &quot;concealment does not have to be perfect for a power that requires concentration and can only be directed at targets you've been in contact with in the last month to be no more than a relatively useful espionage tool.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How does a dark tunnel or being in a crowded area help defend against it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T15:12:07-08:00","id":1282912,"title":"","content":"does anyone have any cool intermixed exploits for when analysts go loud? so far I have only one and it's a mix of hell hound and inflict stigmata","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T15:13:36-08:00","id":1282913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1282811#post1282811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does a dark tunnel or being in a crowded area help defend against it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because all you see is darkness, or the crowd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T22:15:21-08:00","id":1284284,"title":"","content":"Could you use the Tether form power to extend the range of others, such as running current through it if you have Electric Jolt (or amplifying the damage of Electric Jolt by hooking yourself into an electric socket), or for triggering Urban Fluidity, or transfering yourself to the internet with Dataform?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T01:45:43-08:00","id":1284304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1284284#post1284284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use the Tether form power to extend the range of others, such as running current through it if you have Electric Jolt (or amplifying the damage of Electric Jolt by hooking yourself into an electric socket), or for triggering Urban Fluidity, or transfering yourself to the internet with Dataform?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically speaking the tether is a part of your body, so i would allow it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T11:29:22-08:00","id":1284375,"title":"","content":"For those of us who are fans of Netflix movies, how would you make Lola Two from <i>Cam </i>as an angel, or would you make her a spirit?<br /> <br /> (For those of you who don't know:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Lola Two is the main &quot;villain&quot; of sorts; she's the name given to an AI or possibly a very well-designed algorithm who steals the identity and footage of camgirls to always be performing. It's ambiguous how sentient she is, since she doesn't seem to comprehend the idea of being grilled by the original person, true death or injury, or there being existences outside the internet. It's also implied she may have been created by a shady streaming site to effectively cut the actual camgirls out of their network so they don't have to pay them, which is the kind of soulless bureaucracy that has God-Machine written all over it.</div></div> </div> </div>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T21:51:19-08:00","id":1287848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1284375#post1284375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those of us who are fans of Netflix movies, how would you make Lola Two from <i>Cam </i>as an angel, or would you make her a spirit?<br /> <br /> (For those of you who don't know:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Lola Two is the main &quot;villain&quot; of sorts; she's the name given to an AI or possibly a very well-designed algorithm who steals the identity and footage of camgirls to always be performing. It's ambiguous how sentient she is, since she doesn't seem to comprehend the idea of being grilled by the original person, true death or injury, or there being existences outside the internet. It's also implied she may have been created by a shady streaming site to effectively cut the actual camgirls out of their network so they don't have to pay them, which is the kind of soulless bureaucracy that has God-Machine written all over it.</div></div> </div> </div>)</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be hard to run her as an angel since it's not clear if she has an actual mission. I'd run her as an Exile, executing misinterpreted or out of date commands. It fits in nicely with the GM on the Internet concept. You also might look at the Dalga (CoD, p. 256) who create Servitors. They are more autonomous than Imperatives or Simulacra but not as powerful as angels. Your Lola is not exactly a Dalga, but might be similar in power level to one. <br /> <br /> You could run her as a Spirit, but I find the whole Manifestation baggage for Spirits to be a bit awkward. Your Lola would have to gradually up her level of Manifestation until she can interact with her victims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T21:56:38-08:00","id":1287850,"title":"","content":"Can angels cast the Blast numen from Twilight without Materializing? I would think not since the Blast numen does not have the &quot;R&quot; (for &quot;Reaching&quot;) marking. However, some postings here imply that an angel can attack from Twilight using Blast with impunity since most demons can't access Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T22:29:45-08:00","id":1287857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1287850#post1287850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can angels cast the Blast numen from Twilight without Materializing? I would think not since the Blast numen does not have the &quot;R&quot; (for &quot;Reaching&quot;) marking. However, some postings here imply that <b>an angel can attack from Twilight using Blast with impunity</b> since most demons can't access Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Safest to assume &quot;no&quot; in the absence of specific statement that they can for precisely that reason; if they could do that, there'd be absolutely no reason not to, and the fiction doesn't support them doing so in any way whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T05:41:36-08:00","id":1287910,"title":"","content":"I would say that they totally can, but the Blast would also be in Twilight, so not particularly useful against physical targets. My basic rule is that unless stated otherwise, if you can affect something, they can potentially affect you as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T14:49:43-08:00","id":1289318,"title":"","content":"Can an angel in Cover Discorporate?<br /> <br /> I am wrestling with the Twilight rules and conflict with angels. I want to understand how Twilight does not make angels completely overpowered. There are two cases to consider - an angel in Cover and an angel Materializing. Below are my interpretations of both cases, but I want to know what you think.<br /> <br /> The second isn't too bad. Angel Arthur has a mission. He lives in Twilight, like all angels. He can spy from Twilight, but in Twilight our world seems distorted and speech is unintelligible. Being in Twilight doesn't give Arthur any special mobility. While in Twilight he can affect the normal plane only with those numina that have the &quot;Reaching&quot; quality. At times, to carry out his mission, he uses the Materialize Manifestation, perhaps with Mortal Mask. This can only last for a few hours and various abilities can see through Mortal Mask. If Demon Debby somehow attacks and Arthur is in trouble he can (if he has the Manifestation) Discorporate to escape. So Arthur may now know that someone who looks like Debbie (depending on details of the attack) is an enemy, but Discorporation is described as being painful, so I would expect that Arthur is out of combat for a few days. To me these aspects of Twilight prevent it from being overpowering.<br /> <br /> An angel in Cover can also Discorporate. However, Cover is explicitly created by the GodMachine and not simply created by the angel. Discorporation would require (I think?) the GM to completely re-install the angel in Cover. So while Discorporation would allow an angel to survive, it is basically an admission of failure by the angel. Arthur may or not be prepared to pay that price, and the GM might or might not wish to re-install Arthur. However, if Arthur is not disassembled by the GM, I would expect that he is <i>pissed</i> and Debbie has now made an extra special antagonist. <br /> <br /> So, can an angel in Cover Discorporate? Can the angel return to Cover without help from the GM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T15:55:43-08:00","id":1289336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1289318#post1289318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being in Twilight doesn't give Arthur any special mobility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call being able to move through most walls &quot;special mobility.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While in Twilight he can affect the normal plane only with those numina that have the &quot;Reaching&quot; quality. </div> </div> </div>The R tag is for acting across the Gauntlet from the Shadow and is largely irrelevant to angels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So Arthur may now know that someone who looks like Debbie (depending on details of the attack) is an enemy, but Discorporation is described as being painful, so I would expect that Arthur is out of combat for a few days. </div> </div> </div>That description of Discorporate is from the generalized description that applies similarly to ghosts and spirits; between Discorporate being nearly universal kit for published angels, angels being the one category not mentioned in how normal discorporation works, and the Machine's general biases would seem to make it more likely that discorporation is disincentivized by opportunity cost and the resources needed to recover the necessary Essence faster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Discorporation would require (I think?) the GM to completely re-install the angel in Cover. </div> </div> </div>Doesn't follow; the God-Machine creates cover for its angels, but the bodies they occupy in that state aren't simple cases of possession and generally move with them just like demonic Covers do.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, I'd say that being undercover keeps an angel from discorporating unless they assume their true form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T19:05:59-08:00","id":1289379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1289336#post1289336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call being able to move through most walls &quot;special mobility.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that if an angel is spying from Twilight and their target drives away on a motorcycle, they may have problems following the target. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1289336#post1289336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't follow; the God-Machine creates cover for its angels, but the bodies they occupy in that state aren't simple cases of possession and generally move with them just like demonic Covers do.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, I'd say that being undercover keeps an angel from discorporating unless they assume their true form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Others on this forum have written about angels popping into Twilight to survive combat - I am not sure how to interpret the rules. From what you write I think that you are saying that angels in cover <b>cannot</b> Discorporate voluntarily?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T20:54:19-08:00","id":1289404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1289379#post1289379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Others on this forum have written about angels popping into Twilight to survive combat - I am not sure how to interpret the rules. From what you write I think that you are saying that angels in cover <b>cannot</b> Discorporate voluntarily?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Discorporate&quot; doesn't mean &quot;dematerialize,&quot; it means &quot;ceases to exist in its present location and begins to reform in a safe area.&quot; Given the way Demonic Form works as a point of comparison, I'd assume it's as simple for an angel to drop cover as it is for the Unchained, at which point an expedited escape through the Manifestation opens up.<br /> <br /> By a similar token, while it would likely be just as bad an idea as assuming their true form before things have escalated, I wouldn't be surprised if killing an undercover angel resulted in a seemingly normal body being left behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-18-2019, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:00:35-08:00","id":1290378,"title":"","content":"I have a demon NPC I plan to post who fits a standard spy trope - he's an Integrator who desperately wants to get back into the good graces of the GM and his angel &quot;handler&quot; keeps promising him that if he (the demon) performs well then she can get him reconnected without being reformatted or scrapped. He's the defector who wants back in, the whining regret-filled traitor manipulated cruelly by his handler. I wanted such a demon antagonist at a certain point in the chronicle because an angel antagonist comes with a lot of other baggage. <br /> <br /> But then I thought that I don't have the flip side - an angel who cooperates with the demon PC's for some reason. I am looking for some sort of cold war analogy where two opponents have a frenemy relationship of non-interference in their missions and a cautious willingness to share information. (Something like Crowley and Aziraphale in &quot;Good Omens&quot;.) I can't think of any good ways to do this with angels as they appear in the GM chronicle. What sort of mission would put an angel NPC in a position of cautious cooperation with a demon PC?<br /> <br /> (I know that Exiles can be a good source of information for the PC's, but I'd like to have a way for the PC's to learn about one angel's plans from a second angel.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:36:58-08:00","id":1290451,"title":"","content":"An Angel is tasked with collecting particular items for an Infrastructure, or either to build one or perhaps simply making sure it is being repaired. It is having problems securing the proper materials for it though, due to outside interference, but it has learned through the grapevine of Demons in the area. In exchange for information, if not some assistance due to what is at stake, it gives some specific information on areas to avoid, areas of interest, or something otherwise useful but not compromising to the mission.<br /> <br /> Angels and Demons can approach something close to a friendship, so long as they don\u2019t cross lines and try to pry more into each other than allowed. The Demon is allowed in the Angel\u2019s office, to bring food that is approved of and from the office kitchen, and is not to look at the computer screen while they work, but the Angel is likewise not to lock the doors or inform anyone that the Demon is anything but human, and from there...they talk. No probing about projects beyond perhaps dangers they are trying to overcome, open ended questions that could allow the other to volunteer some information or perhaps even give some mild propoganda for their own side. Maybe they are simply discussing problems with human life in a way they can\u2019t with humans or others of their ilk. It may all be a subtle ploy to try and pull information from a Demon, a horrible trap or somesuch, or it might be a genuine attempt at being a friend, or learning what it\u2019s like to have one. Angels are different from each other, and have their own reasons for doing things.<br /> <br /> Apologies if that doesn\u2019t help with your problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T15:08:37-08:00","id":1290548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1290451#post1290451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Angel is tasked with collecting particular items for an Infrastructure, or either to build one or perhaps simply making sure it is being repaired. It is having problems securing the proper materials for it though, due to outside interference, but it has learned through the grapevine of Demons in the area. In exchange for information, if not some assistance due to what is at stake, it gives some specific information on areas to avoid, areas of interest, or something otherwise useful but not compromising to the mission. <i>(Text elided)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Apologies if that doesn\u2019t help with your problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your suggestion! I had thought of having the angel doing some appropriately weird harvesting for the GM (e.g. kidneys of left handed men) and that the demon doesn't oppose and might facilitate a bit for a favor in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T16:01:15-08:00","id":1290924,"title":"","content":"Ok guys, this is a very stupid stupid question so forgive me.<br /> <br /> According to your interpretation, Demons must be &quot;naked&quot; in their true form? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:42:31-08:00","id":1290972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1290924#post1290924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok guys, this is a very stupid stupid question so forgive me.<br /> <br /> According to your interpretation, Demons must be &quot;naked&quot; in their true form? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought of a demon's human appearance as some sort of &quot;quantum costume&quot; that vanishes if they undergo a full transformation, and returns when they return to their cover. That costume includes clothing and all of the other aspects of their human life. None of the fluff I've read mentions a demon returning to human form naked and looking for clothing.<br /> <br /> This is indirectly supported by the DtD manual referring to the clothes of a demon with a low Cover rating being suspiciously uniform. The clothes are just part of their conjured story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T05:39:15-08:00","id":1292123,"title":"","content":"how does a Demon blood &quot;move up&quot; there <span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><b>cipher?</b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:25:11-08:00","id":1292205,"title":"","content":"To progress to a further point in their Cipher a Demon-Blooded must catch the attention of the God-Machine in some way, akin to Compromise. To go back there's the Backtrace rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T12:22:50-08:00","id":1292232,"title":"","content":"So, because this was something that came up in a chat and I couldn\u2019t support my side of the argument, I have to ask: is using an Incept bad for an Angel\u2019s mental state? By using them, are they more likely to Fall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T13:33:12-08:00","id":1292254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1292232#post1292232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, because this was something that came up in a chat and I couldn\u2019t support my side of the argument, I have to ask: is using an Incept bad for an Angel\u2019s mental state? By using them, are they more likely to Fall?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not bad for them mentally, but they are a fraught thing and using them can change a lot of things in the game, and while it's use isn't neccesarily Fall worthy, the conditions in which you use Incepts are generally bad for Angels. Let's backtrack and explain that.<br /> <br /> Incepts are a high octane-boost to the things that an angel is capable of doing, but by and large basically reveals the angel and any of the God-Machine's cards that hinge on that knowledge. Factoring that in, the God-Machine tends to try and build angels who are fit to the task It needs executed without need for the Incept. Occasionally, an incident will require an Angel instead of some other kind of occult matrix but demands the power of an Incept, but by and large, an Incept is best used by angels when they have the absolute security in knowledge of their isolation, which is <i>rare and near impossible</i>, or when it's clear that burning cards is no longer a meaningful penalty for the situation, either because it wins the game or at least allows for some kind of win out of the loss.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the choice to use the Incept belongs to the angel, and even if they are given the ones that move their purpose along, situations can still force them to use Incepts outside of the optimum situations, and that sort of thing can mess up an occult matrix trying to be set up. Using an Incept basically reveals parts of the hand earlier than intended and allows the potential enemies of the GOd Machine to know where and who one of the major pieces are on the board, and even probably define more of what they are for. And the Angel can, effectively, decide to when it can do that, and like there are lots of times an Exploit might seem like the right answer but could be handled better with quieter answers, an angel deals with a lot of scenarios that put them at risk and seem like it calls for an Incept but could be resolved with keeping their cards close to their chest and using other things from their toolset.<br /> <br /> So an Incept doesn't risk a Fall by itself, but they represent a temptation that can serve as a demarker for a Fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T18:29:07-08:00","id":1292318,"title":"","content":"Not explictly to answer a question, but Lambda creators and Going Loud Analysts, a note:<br /> <br /> Two Places at Once+Rip the Gates+a quick, dangerous visit where ever=Congratulations, you have a hella loud version of a Beast's ability to impose their Lair without corresponding immunities.<br /> <br /> It'd be easier to just make friends with a Beast or have the various Exploits/Form Abilities/etc. that impose environmental tilts, obviously, but sometimes beggars can't be choosers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T01:48:35-08:00","id":1292407,"title":"","content":"An easier way would just be to make a Rain Of Blood exploited gadget, honestly. Rain Of Blood normally creates artificial and dangerous weather phenomina, so a near-field of one could create artificial and dangerous, if short ranged, environmental tilts.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure you could do the same with an embeded Lambda somehow.. Combustion + Momentum perhaps...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:44:40-08:00","id":1292502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1292318#post1292318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not explictly to answer a question, but Lambda creators and Going Loud Analysts, a note:<br /> <br /> Two Places at Once+Rip the Gates+a quick, dangerous visit where ever=Congratulations, you have a hella loud version of a Beast's ability to impose their Lair without corresponding immunities.<br /> <br /> It'd be easier to just make friends with a Beast or have the various Exploits/Form Abilities/etc. that impose environmental tilts, obviously, but sometimes beggars can't be choosers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, depending on the Form Abilities the Demon has, they may already have those immunities covered.<br /> <br /> Though... since Imposing Lair Traits isn't an Extended Action, I wonder if Show of Power can copy specific examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T14:42:37-08:00","id":1292612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1292205#post1292205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To progress to a further point in their Cipher a Demon-Blooded must catch the attention of the God-Machine in some way, akin to Compromise. To go back there's the Backtrace rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do they catch the attention of the God-Machine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T11:43:54-08:00","id":1292821,"title":"","content":"Demon-Bloods don't have a Cover score. They don't have to roll for compromise. Instead they'll progress on their Cipher. There's no mechanics driven time for when this happens. It's pretty much ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T15:04:24-08:00","id":1292865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1292821#post1292821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon-Bloods don't have a Cover score. They don't have to roll for compromise. Instead they'll progress on their Cipher. There's no mechanics driven time for when this happens. It's pretty much ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do still roll Compromise, in pretty much many of the same situations a demon would in their circumstances, and success moves them along the Cipher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T18:28:02-08:00","id":1292901,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks. It's been a while since I read through it. I shouldn't have relied on memory and skimming as much.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just went back to check. Looks like success <i>keeps</i> them from moving along their Cipher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3776,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","user":"AutoDefenestrate","date":". 02-28-2019, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T18:42:06-08:00","id":1292903,"title":"","content":"The Demon-Blooded Cipher is a little unintuitive at first blush, because it represents some of the opposite thematic qualities that a regular demon's Cipher is typically* portrayed with. Demonic Ciphers are roads to gnosis and secret truths that empower your Primum, your personal self-defining will, in defiance of the God-Machine. Despite sharing the name Cipher and providing tasty Interlock powers or benefits, for demon-blooded, the Cipher represents the opposite: it's the God-Machine's road into <i>you,</i> and at the end of the road is subordination to its will. So for demon-blooded, the Cipher advances when the <i>bad</i> thing happens and a compromise hooks in, not when the good thing happens and you resist it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*I know, sometimes it's hinted that the demonic Cipher is an inborn trap laid by the God-Machine. That's not the default assumption that first comes to mind when talking about it, though.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T14:57:00-08:00","id":1293150,"title":"","content":"What can the God-Machine Do with a Completed Cipher Demon-Blooded the book says it can Quote Nudge the Character In subtle Ways but How?<br /> <br /> Do when they get Activated The God-Machine gets Them Kidnaped and then Get Reprogramed .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T17:56:29-08:00","id":1293201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1293150#post1293150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can the God-Machine Do with a Completed Cipher Demon-Blooded the book says it can Quote Nudge the Character In subtle Ways but How?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per <i>Heirs to Hell</i>, the Storyteller can take one action per chapter with a demon-blooded character who has the Activated Condition, which always plays into the Machine's plans in some way; by this point, the character has all three of the Interlocks they would receive and cannot reduce the level of awareness the God-Machine has of them unless It somehow chooses to let them go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T17:36:14-08:00","id":1293589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1293201#post1293201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per <i>Heirs to Hell</i>, the Storyteller can take one action per chapter with a demon-blooded character who has the Activated Condition, which always plays into the Machine's plans in some way; by this point, the character has all three of the Interlocks they would receive and cannot reduce the level of awareness the God-Machine has of them unless It somehow chooses to let them go.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what\u2019s the Lore reason the GM can Control the demonblooded ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T21:24:09-08:00","id":1293656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1293589#post1293589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what\u2019s the Lore reason the GM can Control the demonblooded ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is everywhere, the remnants of Its mechanisms are in their blood, and It knows them so well by this point that It has granted them four Embeds and three Interlocks on top of constantly knowing where they are and what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Demon-blooded are humans, and humans placed to be demon-blooded inhabit a world that the God-Machine has overwhelming influence over. The thing already makes sleeper agents, designs angels, and seeds subliminal messages in advertising jingles, it's no great stretch to assume it's within Its capabilities to subtly train the Unchained's children \u2014 Heirs to Hell says as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T11:07:36-08:00","id":1294457,"title":"","content":"Great explanation! Is it possible for there to have a Mage Demon-blooded with a completed Cipher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:05:51-08:00","id":1294468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1294457#post1294457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great explanation! Is it possible for there to have a Mage Demon-blooded with a completed Cipher?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> The particular name for that is &quot;a bad day.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:59:11-08:00","id":1294486,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m quite interested in this . What Havoc could the God-Machine do with a Demon-blooded Mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T20:42:41-07:00","id":1296329,"title":"","content":"If an angel uses the Implant Mission numen on a demon, does the demon get to resist by rolling their Supernatural Tolerance (i.e. their Cover)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T21:25:28-07:00","id":1296336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1296329#post1296329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an angel uses the Implant Mission numen on a demon, does the demon get to resist by rolling their Supernatural Tolerance (i.e. their Cover)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Implant Mission only works on mortals, which in CofD is typically used to mean humans without supernatural templates. The power fails, and this only really becomes a problem if the angel notices it failed and keeps trying, and notices that for whatever reason, <i>this</i> mortal is very hard to Implant Mission in.<br /> <br /> Hypothetically, one might argue that the power might eventually, through its reliable failure, reveal the demon through implication, and therefore be valid to Spoof. If accepted, this would suggest the reverse of your suggestion: that the demon automatically resists without a roll, but can roll Cover to (unconsciously and instinctively) attempt to <i>succumb </i>to the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T12:00:33-07:00","id":1296470,"title":"","content":"This came up in a conversation I had the night before; gadgets can effectively be installed with an effect that the original Embed/Exploit could conceptually do (either by way of a reduced effect or a near-field). Would that include the dramatic failure effects of an Embed/Exploit, so that a gadget with On The Mend could slow healing times instead of accelerating them, Vox to make someone unable to vocalize at all, or Open Sesame to ensure a room is secure? These are within what the Embeds are capable of, even if they aren\u2019t normally the intended or desired effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T13:29:41-07:00","id":1296492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1296470#post1296470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came up in a conversation I had the night before; gadgets can effectively be installed with an effect that the original Embed/Exploit could conceptually do (either by way of a reduced effect or a near-field). Would that include the dramatic failure effects of an Embed/Exploit, so that a gadget with On The Mend could slow healing times instead of accelerating them, Vox to make someone unable to vocalize at all, or Open Sesame to ensure a room is secure? These are within what the Embeds are capable of, even if they aren\u2019t normally the intended or desired effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems within the scope of a gadget to me, there are lots that take far more liberties than that.<br /> <br /> Now, be sure to discuss things with your ST before you make the Nothing Personnel Exploited Katana with a reverse Frozen in Time gadget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T13:39:19-07:00","id":1296495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1294486#post1294486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m quite interested in this . What Havoc could the God-Machine do with a Demon-blooded Mage</div> </div> </div> </div>There are examples like a mage who is concealment infrastructure to block out the memories of an event from the populace.<br /> <br /> Being infrastructure also may come with the side effect of demons coming up to you to try to siphon aether from you or trying to hack you. &quot;WTF are you doing?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T19:07:24-07:00","id":1300166,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I read the rules, so I want to check thoughts. If its stipulated in the contract, and of course the other party knows, could you make it viable for a person to sign with something other than their name on a contract? Like easy scenario would be if the pact was to give someone back the ability to use their hands in the exchange could you make it so contract says, &quot;The party of [their name here] here after refered to as X and will knowingly be signing as such...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T23:15:15-07:00","id":1301529,"title":"","content":"Do WoD demons exist in CoD? <br /> <br /> I need some enforcer types for a particular company that is a front for a GodMachine operation. The company is pretty high up in my conspiracy pyramid, and therefore pretty powerful. The company would tend to respond forcefully to any threats or interlopers so the enforcers should be a real threat.<br /> <br /> I thought of modeling them on Croup and Vandemar from Neil Gaiman's <i>Neverwhere.</i> They are evil, sadistic, unhurried, relentless, and nigh-indestructible. They probably can't be designed as angels, given their sadism and love of destroying anything beautiful. Moreover making them angels brings a lot of baggage - angels have Incepts, they can call in other angels, they can retreat to Twilight, and fighting them breaks the Cover of the PC;s. I thought of making the enforcers Horrors, which works pretty well. Would Beasts work better? Centimani?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T23:33:46-07:00","id":1301531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1301529#post1301529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do WoD demons exist in CoD?<br /> <br /> I need some enforcer types for a particular company that is a front for a GodMachine operation. The company is pretty high up in my conspiracy pyramid, and therefore pretty powerful. The company would tend to respond forcefully to any threats or interlopers so the enforcers should be a real threat.<br /> <br /> I thought of modeling them on Croup and Vandemar from Neil Gaiman's <i>Neverwhere.</i> They are evil, sadistic, unhurried, relentless, and nigh-indestructible. They probably can't be designed as angels, given their sadism and love of destroying anything beautiful. Moreover making them angels brings a lot of baggage - angels have Incepts, they can call in other angels, they can retreat to Twilight, and fighting them breaks the Cover of the PC;s. I thought of making the enforcers Horrors, which works pretty well. Would Beasts work better? Centimani?</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that exiles sidestep much of the angel-baggage in that list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:44:09-07:00","id":1301544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1301529#post1301529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do WoD demons exist in CoD?<br /> <br /> I need some enforcer types for a particular company that is a front for a GodMachine operation. The company is pretty high up in my conspiracy pyramid, and therefore pretty powerful. The company would tend to respond forcefully to any threats or interlopers so the enforcers should be a real threat.<br /> <br /> I thought of modeling them on Croup and Vandemar from Neil Gaiman's <i>Neverwhere.</i> They are evil, sadistic, unhurried, relentless, and nigh-indestructible. They probably can't be designed as angels, given their sadism and love of destroying anything beautiful. Moreover making them angels brings a lot of baggage - angels have Incepts, they can call in other angels, they can retreat to Twilight, and fighting them breaks the Cover of the PC;s. I thought of making the enforcers Horrors, which works pretty well. Would Beasts work better? Centimani?</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, Horrors from the Chronicles Of Darkness book would fit this niche well. You can tailor a Horror to match the setting/tone of your game, with Dreadpowers in the book and ones you can make up yourself. The book even notes you can even give it a Supernatural Tolerance trait like Blood Potency or Wyrd to make it mingle with others in your gameline without adhering directly with their rules. Primum could work well there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T00:42:33-07:00","id":1301823,"title":"","content":"How does the Madness condition work on a Demon? They have Cover instead of Integrity, which doesn\u2019t really relate to their mental health, supernaturally affected or otherwise. How does one resolve or even apply the effects to an Unchained? Does one just replace \u201cIntegrity\u201d with \u201cCover\u201d for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:00:05-07:00","id":1301983,"title":"","content":"Quick question from someone who hasn't read much of Demon.<br /> <br /> If an Angel is going about their business, and is detained magically, kept from doing their business for years and years. Upon being released, are they automatically fallen, cut away from the GM, or do they then have to make a decision to either turn themselves in, so to speak, or go and fall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:07:20-07:00","id":1301986,"title":"","content":"The Fall is always a matter of choice. Something else happens to angels who lose their connection to the God-Machine against their will. They don't become demons, but it's not good for their sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:19:41-07:00","id":1301991,"title":"","content":"Upon release most angels would either reconnect with the GM and continue their function, or, if perhaps the relevant Infrastructure has changed since then, fail to reconnect and become an Exile. Falling requires choosing not to resume their mission once free again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:56:53-07:00","id":1302005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1300166#post1300166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a while since I read the rules, so I want to check thoughts. If its stipulated in the contract, and of course the other party knows, could you make it viable for a person to sign with something other than their name on a contract? Like easy scenario would be if the pact was to give someone back the ability to use their hands in the exchange could you make it so contract says, &amp;quot;The party of [their name here] here after refered to as X and will knowingly be signing as such...&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Literacy isn\u2019t required for a pact to work, so I see no reason why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T12:43:09-07:00","id":1306305,"title":"","content":"Outside of Ephemeral Cover and Rip The Gates, what do demons have for interacting with ghosts and spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T17:14:21-07:00","id":1306364,"title":"","content":"Nothing (or very little) IIRC. Demons are specifically weak against ephemeral entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T17:32:31-07:00","id":1306368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1306364#post1306364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing (or very little) IIRC. Demons are specifically weak against ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T17:03:07-07:00","id":1306681,"title":"","content":"Hellfire is an option, if you can get them to materialize. Employing Banes and such may be valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T19:42:40-07:00","id":1306723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1306681#post1306681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hellfire is an option, if you can get them to materialize. Employing Banes and such may be valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main concern, actually, was just simple conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T04:02:15-07:00","id":1306795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1306723#post1306723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main concern, actually, was just simple conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mundane solution is to boost their ability to Manifest by providing the right Manifestation Conditions.<br /> Any Embeds or Exploits that opens up a personal channel of communication might bridge Twilight, but I'm not aware of any official ones. Might also be difficult to target someone you can't perceive.<br /> <br /> Being able to perceive Twilight is by far the simplest answer (since it bridges the only faulty link in the chain of communication: you can talk to them, they can hear you, they can respond, but you can't hear them) but allowing that for an Embed may open up for consequences detrimental to gameplay if it can be used to perceive angels in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T19:53:35-07:00","id":1307114,"title":"","content":"I've recently read Night Horrors: Enemy Action and I have a question regarding the opening of Exiles. it mentions they can Fall. is this to be taken literally or is it just figurative","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T21:44:55-07:00","id":1307135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1307114#post1307114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently read Night Horrors: Enemy Action and I have a question regarding the opening of Exiles. it mentions they can Fall. is this to be taken literally or is it just figurative</div> </div> </div> </div>Exiles are still angels and therefore hypothetically retain the capacity for Falling, although many of them have that chance gated behind &quot;how do you disobey a lack of orders?&quot; or &quot;does this Mission even have a betrayal parameter?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T02:42:22-07:00","id":1307183,"title":"","content":"I suppose the &quot;simplest&quot; way would be to actively work against the God-Machine, but that's so far beyond &quot;maybe if I just bend this order a little bit&quot; that it would be extremely rare. It'd have to develop mentally and emotionally to a full blown Saboteur <i>before</i> it becomes free from the programming that keeps it from doing so.<br /> <br /> Far easier is probably an exile that is supposed to get continuous updates to its mission parameters and decides to abandon even the fixed parts of the mission after losing contact. Unless they're not counted as exiles because they still have a mission or something; it's been a long time since I read the text on exiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T02:34:19-07:00","id":1307434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1306723#post1306723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main concern, actually, was just simple conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>A \u201csimple\u201d way would be for using gadgets, be it a variant of Remote Linkup or Voice Of The Machine and make it something like a telegraph, a walkie talkie or a radio (or even an Ouija board). Have it set up so that you can talk directly to the ephemeral in question if they are within range, and they can commune back. It isn\u2019t too hard to think of out of the box solutions using physically realized blocks of the God-Machine\u2019s code...thouh that may just be the box I have stuck myself in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-24-2019, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T06:55:31-07:00","id":1308921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1307114#post1307114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently read Night Horrors: Enemy Action and I have a question regarding the opening of Exiles. it mentions they can Fall. is this to be taken literally or is it just figurative</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, the God-Machine offers an Exile the chance to return. \u201cDo this mission I offer to you, and you\u2019ll be restored to your former glory.\u201d If the Exile accepts, they get to be a complete angel once more. If they refuse, they Fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T06:01:33-07:00","id":1311201,"title":"","content":"What happens when your bargain away a connection for a patch job but don't immediatly graft it to a cover ? Does the spouse of the pactbound person still recognize them as their husband/wife ?<br /> <br /> If you created a cover from various pact and it has been established for some time now, like let's say one year, if some or all of the various contract from wich you created the cover are destroyed, what happens to your cover ?<br /> <br /> Also unrelated to pact but a question that is kind of the continuation of ArcaneArts question : Can the Read Aura technology help demon finds spirit and/or ghost in twilight ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T15:05:33-07:00","id":1312162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1311201#post1311201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when your bargain away a connection for a patch job but don't immediatly graft it to a cover ? Does the spouse of the pactbound person still recognize them as their husband/wife ?<br /> <br /> If you created a cover from various pact and it has been established for some time now, like let's say one year, if some or all of the various contract from wich you created the cover are destroyed, what happens to your cover ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pacts are usually a quid pro quo - the mortal gets X and the demon gets Y. There isn't a delay or a set of spare parts sitting in a cupboard. If you are playing it so there *is* such a thing as &quot;stored Cover parts&quot; then the mortal should lose the connection (e.g. their marriage) when they gain the benefit from the pact, even if no demon has incorporated it into their Cover. <br /> <br /> If a pact is destroyed then the parts obtained in the pact revert to the original mortal owner, who also loses the benefits of the pact. The Cover that incorporated those parts is then damaged and might not survive.<br /> <br /> All of the above IMHO, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T04:16:55-07:00","id":1312530,"title":"","content":"I mean there is demon trading covers or saving the contracts for special jobs in fiction so i'm not sure ? I don't kknow maybe you're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T04:24:14-07:00","id":1312531,"title":"","content":"&quot;At a time of my choosing I will collect the price.&quot;<br /> <br /> That would be extremely appropriate to add to a pact considering the source material. But I think you'd have to add something like that in order to indefinitely postpone the transfer/grafting to your Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T21:31:11-07:00","id":1312709,"title":"","content":"You could probably get away a &quot;price to be collected at the time and place of party [the demon]'s choosing&quot; for more contractual language with just specifying that the Unchained are allowed to specify those details at a future point. This would make particular sense if you were trading for part of a cover that the other party hasn't had yet, as this would probably help with the contract balancing thing by requiring the other party to actually provide that part of the cover.<br /> <br /> I think, would that work? Contract balance in the mechanical always confused me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T08:33:04-07:00","id":1312763,"title":"","content":"Woop, founf what i wanted in Demon Interface, there a whole section explaining pact, from conditional to delayed, transfer pacts, bill of sale and cover trading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, it's really neat and offer a lot of pratical information on the pact economy of the unchained","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T05:20:47-07:00","id":1312923,"title":"","content":"Using such mechanisms, provided certain terms are automagically enforced, you can even use them as detection methods - make a Pact for a small, but noticeable element conditional upon X doing Y. If you notice the presence or absence of said element, Y happened to X.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T11:02:12-07:00","id":1314973,"title":"","content":"Is there an in-universe reason why the GodMachine keeps humans around? I have my own head-canon for why but I don't know if there is an &quot;official&quot; reason why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T04:10:08-07:00","id":1315129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1314973#post1314973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an in-universe reason why the GodMachine keeps humans around? I have my own head-canon for why but I don't know if there is an &amp;quot;official&amp;quot; reason why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they can be easily manipulated into making infrastructures and it can sacrifice them to produce essence for example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T12:42:37-07:00","id":1315249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1315129#post1315129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they can be easily manipulated into making infrastructures and it can sacrifice them to produce essence for example</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd thought of that, but wouldn't it be easier for the GM to simply take over in a very obvious way and run the harvest directly? After all, it can perform &quot;miracles&quot; to convince the skeptics. The harvesting described in the books seems to be at a small level with small cults. Why doesn't the GM harvest on a much larger scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T13:15:30-07:00","id":1315259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1315249#post1315249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd thought of that, but wouldn't it be easier for the GM to simply take over in a very obvious way and run the harvest directly?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026You've been paying attention to how the Machine operates, right? This is Espionage 101.<br /> <br /> Like, in the most prosaic terms, being obvious means more things to keep track of that can actively and directly interfere with your plans even if exposure to the supernatural didn't already degrade mortals' sacrificial value as a matter of course. Keeping all of humanity under Its thumb takes resources that could be put to better use actually setting up outputs, and <i>not</i> making that investment only requires that It not make so much noise that the clever monkeys start poking around the magic fusebox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T23:12:05-07:00","id":1315383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1315259#post1315259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026You've been paying attention to how the Machine operates, right? This is Espionage 101.<br /> <br /> Like, in the most prosaic terms, being obvious means more things to keep track of that can actively and directly interfere with your plans even if exposure to the supernatural didn't already degrade mortals' sacrificial value as a matter of course. Keeping all of humanity under Its thumb takes resources that could be put to better use actually setting up outputs, and <i>not</i> making that investment only requires that It not make so much noise that the clever monkeys start poking around the magic fusebox.</div> </div> </div> </div>And by the way, maybe the gm doesn t HAVE the resources to take over the entire humanity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T09:21:52-07:00","id":1315708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1315383#post1315383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And by the way, maybe the gm doesn t HAVE the resources to take over the entire humanity...</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond a certain point, it just isn't efficient.<br /> <br /> If you can <i>already</i> get what you want, why bother controlling more than 51%?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T02:00:02-07:00","id":1316212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1314973#post1314973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an in-universe reason why the GodMachine keeps humans around? I have my own head-canon for why but I don't know if there is an &amp;quot;official&amp;quot; reason why.</div> </div> </div> </div>They often play an integral part of Occult Matrices. The mathematics and chaos principles in the movements of humanity are unconsciously powerful occult forces that the G-M uses to its own advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T13:32:40-07:00","id":1316484,"title":"","content":"On p.110 of the DtD manual it says that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">A demon\u2019s true form is a natural receptor for Aether. Whenever a demon assumes demonic form, she automatically generates a number of points of Aether equal to her Primum rating. If she runs out of Aether while in demonic form, her player may roll the demon\u2019s Primum, with each success restoring a point of Aether. </span></span> </div> </div> </div>So that when a player <i>takes on</i> demon form they gain Primum in Aether, and when they exhaust their Aether they can generate up their Primum in Aether. But what about just sitting around? Can a character who is down eight points of Aether take on demon form and then slowly recharge up to full?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T13:44:30-07:00","id":1316487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1316484#post1316484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and when they exhaust their Aether they can generate up their Primum in Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>They gain their successes on a Primum roll in Aether to a minimum of 1, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what about just sitting around? Can a character who is down eight points of Aether take on demon form and then slowly recharge up to full? </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that there is a Condition that demons get from spending a lot of Aether in one scene or suffering a compromise while in demonic form and that effect is &quot;you lose half your Primum in Aether every turn until you run out or pull more from Infrastructure,&quot; yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T16:42:16-07:00","id":1316520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1316487#post1316487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bearing in mind that there is a Condition that demons get from spending a lot of Aether in one scene or suffering a compromise while in demonic form and that effect is &quot;you lose half your Primum in Aether every turn until you run out or pull more from Infrastructure,&quot; yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please provide a citation for the limit on Aether expenditures? I couldn't find it. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that going demon to regain Aether is a <i>good</i> idea, but if you're down to nearly nothing and have no other resources, I could imagine doing so while trying to minimize the damage to one's cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T16:58:10-07:00","id":1316523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1316520#post1316520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you please provide a citation for the limit on Aether expenditures? I couldn't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aetheric Bleed, first item in the &quot;Demonic Conditions&quot; subsection on page 209.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying that going demon to regain Aether is a <i>good</i> idea, but if you're down to nearly nothing and have no other resources, I could imagine doing so while trying to minimize the damage to one's cover. </div> </div> </div>The problem there is that assuming full demonic form prompts a compromise check at a -3 penalty and the check explicitly applies the normal Conditions to the Cover you assume thereafter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T12:11:26-07:00","id":1317032,"title":"","content":"Assume that an angel is under taking continued gunfire for some reason. This damage is Lethal, but downgraded to Bashing, because the target is an angel. After they take their Corpus in Bashing, does the damage then upgrade to Lethal? At what point are they forced into Twilight (assuming that they have some Essence left)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T17:19:45-07:00","id":1317079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1317032#post1317032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After they take their Corpus in Bashing, does the damage then upgrade to Lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the usual rules for Health damage, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At what point are they forced into Twilight (assuming that they have some Essence left)? </div> </div> </div>They discorporate once their Corpus track is filled with lethal or aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T02:52:37-07:00","id":1318000,"title":"","content":"I am confused by the rules of adoption pacts (heirs of hell).<br /> If the demon call the pact the human becomes an offspring even if now he is 30 years old?<br /> The contract need to be stipulated before the actual birth for the children to become an offspring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T05:46:27-07:00","id":1318031,"title":"","content":"If someone Pacts away &quot;Parent of X&quot;, and the Demon incorporates that into their Cover, that Cover then was <i>always</i> the Parent of X, making X the child of a Demon, and thus, an Offspring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T07:06:09-07:00","id":1318041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1318031#post1318031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone Pacts away &amp;quot;Parent of X&amp;quot;, and the Demon incorporates that into their Cover, that Cover then was <i>always</i> the Parent of X, making X the child of a Demon, and thus, an Offspring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T07:10:36-07:00","id":1318042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1318031#post1318031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone Pacts away &quot;Parent of X&quot;, and the Demon incorporates that into their Cover, that Cover then was <i>always</i> the Parent of X, making X the child of a Demon, and thus, an Offspring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... does that mean that the children would have false memories of being an offspring from his birth (or even a fractal for a double pact)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T08:55:25-07:00","id":1318065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1318042#post1318042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... does that mean that the children would have false memories of being an offspring from his birth (or even a fractal for a double pact)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Latents exist as a category? Almost certainly not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T03:58:02-07:00","id":1318205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1318042#post1318042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait... does that mean that the children would have false memories of being an offspring from his birth (or even a fractal for a double pact)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pacts... are <i>weird</i>. X's memories should remain, just with the Demon photo-shopped in as a replacement. This... may not make sense given other historical &quot;Facts&quot; about the Demon (how were you raising X in Podunk, and getting a drug addiction in Cambodia at the same time?). It is these inconsistencies that can be investigated and unraveled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T21:24:05-07:00","id":1318401,"title":"","content":"When an angel in Cover squares off against a demon, can it/does it drop the Cover and appear in angelic form? I've always thought that having an angel dramatically unveil (e.g. when my evil Human Resources Angel drops her cover of an old woman and <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/56d86bc679170714ce367ea05e341fde/tumblr_np8coeA8AA1rk0k2jo1_500.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> shows her true form)</a> it makes for a memorable moment. But angelic Cover is not the same as the Mortal Mask numen, so maybe that just doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> When the confrontation comes, do your angels drop their Cover and reveal their true selves?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T03:13:51-07:00","id":1318439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1318401#post1318401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When an angel in Cover squares off against a demon, can it/does it drop the Cover and appear in angelic form? I've always thought that having an angel dramatically unveil (e.g. when my evil Human Resources Angel drops her cover of an old woman and <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/56d86bc679170714ce367ea05e341fde/tumblr_np8coeA8AA1rk0k2jo1_500.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> shows her true form)</a> it makes for a memorable moment. But angelic Cover is not the same as the Mortal Mask numen, so maybe that just doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> When the confrontation comes, do your angels drop their Cover and reveal their true selves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Angelic Covers are, unfortunately, not really expanded upon beyond &quot;angels can have Covers&quot; and &quot;they don't have to check for compromise since the Cover is maintained through Infrastructure&quot; (the last part might've been dev clarification on this forum; I forget).<br /> <br /> If we apply a demon's rules regarding Covers (where not contradicted by the info we have) then an angel should be able to reflexively shed its Cover and resume its own form, but without Aether to spend it's not capable of retaking its Cover.<br /> You can either just say that Essence serves the same role, allowing the angel to change back into its Cover as an instant action, or you might have the angel be required to return to the relevant Infrastructure to don it again (giving the players an opportunity to angel-jack the Cover before the angel returns).<br /> <br /> In the former case it would make sense for the angel to drop Cover whenever that would be preferable for its mission.<br /> In the latter case it would be much rarer, closer to a last resort kind of thing, since it would more severely interrupt their ability to carry out their mission (unless it's a hunter angel, but they don't usually have Covers in the first place). It's something it would do if it fears that the mission is at serious risk.<br /> <br /> In <i>either</i> case it's still unlikely that dropping Cover would be preferable unless the Cover itself is at risk. Angels don't have Demonic Form abilities that are locked away and afaik (please correct me if I'm wrong) they don't lose access to any Influences, Numina or Incepts while in Cover. The only difference is that the angel would be in Twilight and thus a lot safer since demons have very limited options for dealing with anything, most especially angels, in Twilight. I.e. there's no real reason for an angel to drop their Cover unless it's to prevent damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-14-2019, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T11:21:33-07:00","id":1319092,"title":"","content":"I want to make sure that I understand how PC's can restore Aether. If a demon uses some of their Aether and wants to replenish it, they can go to some isolated place, and assume full demon form, and replenish up to their Primum each turn until they are full. However, the transformation results in a Compromise roll at -3. If they have a decent Cover (say 6 or 7) they make this roll at -2. After restoring their Aether to full, it costs them one point of Aether to transform back into their Cover.<br /> <br /> Is this all correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T13:09:41-07:00","id":1319113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1319092#post1319092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this all correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope!<br /> <br /> Assuming full demonic form recovers your Primum in Aether, and then if you run out of Aether you roll Primum to recover [successes] points of Aether to a minimum of 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T17:28:28-07:00","id":1319159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1319113#post1319113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope!<br /> <br /> Assuming full demonic form recovers your Primum in Aether, and then if you run out of Aether you roll Primum to recover [successes] points of Aether to a minimum of 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so to be relentlessly specific: A Primum 1 demon cannot use this to restore their Aether. A Primum 2 would gain 1 Aether (net) for each cycle of transformation. The Compromise roll is at -3, unless you have very good or particularly bad Cover ratings. <br /> <br /> If the demon runs out of Aether while in demonic form, they can roll their Primum in dice and gain back that number. If they run out and want to expend several Aether then they must slowly gain Aether and expend it, until they have spent enough to power whatever effect they are generating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T17:45:02-07:00","id":1319162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1319159#post1319159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so to be relentlessly specific: A Primum 1 demon cannot use this to restore their Aether. A Primum 2 would gain 1 Aether (net) for each cycle of transformation. The Compromise roll is at -3, unless you have very good or particularly bad Cover ratings.<br /> <br /> If the demon runs out of Aether while in demonic form, they can roll their Primum in dice and gain back that number. If they run out and want to expend several Aether then they must slowly gain Aether and expend it, until they have spent enough to power whatever effect they are generating.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about the size of it, yeah. There's the outside possibility that the Primum roll explodes to refill your pool halfway at the middle tiers, but otherwise assuming demonic form puts you in a slightly better state than you could've been when you assumed it at the cost of a pretty dire risk of compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T13:15:09-07:00","id":1320139,"title":"","content":"A thought recently occurred to me. As I've been trying to figure out how to let an unchained make use of abjuration (mortal interactions) for awhile despite not having integrity or a soul I've been hitting a brick wall for a good while. At least until this thought came into my head and that is my question,<br /> <br /> Is the Embed Going Native something that could allow one to perform abjuration while it is active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T18:12:05-07:00","id":1320370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320139#post1320139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought recently occurred to me. As I've been trying to figure out how to let an unchained make use of abjuration (mortal interactions) for awhile despite not having integrity or a soul I've been hitting a brick wall for a good while. At least until this thought came into my head and that is my question,<br /> <br /> Is the Embed Going Native something that could allow one to perform abjuration while it is active?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Going Native does not grant a demon a soul. The character becomes human, but without a soul. The DtD manual p.311 states:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Soulless (Persistent): The character is in the first stage of soul loss. Without a soul, she can\u2019t attempt abjuration, warding, or binding...</span></span> </div> </div> </div>There are disadvantages to being a soulless human, such as increased chance of Possession, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T19:35:23-07:00","id":1320379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320370#post1320370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Going Native does not grant a demon a soul. The character becomes human, but without a soul. The DtD manual p.311 states:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There are disadvantages to being a soulless human, such as increased chance of Possession, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't expect a demon to go through soul loss with the use of going native. If that was an issue I'd expect it to be mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T21:17:00-07:00","id":1320398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320379#post1320379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't expect a demon to go through soul loss with the use of going native. If that was an issue I'd expect it to be mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't lose what you don't have. Demons don't have souls. :-)<br /> <br /> (Rereading this, the one sentence reply came across as snarky - sorry if that's the case.)<br /> <br /> Not having a soul does not reveal the demon as supernatural, since there are ways for humans to lose their souls as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24502,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","user":"KieranMullen","date":". 06-24-2019, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T23:00:37-07:00","id":1320414,"title":"","content":"I'd say that'd fall under &quot;truly human&quot; but at that point it goes beyond &quot;ask a simple question&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T01:13:37-07:00","id":1320680,"title":"","content":"What are the mechanical benefits for Demons, when they lie? Do we get bonus dice or something else? Or the game simply rules that you have &quot;automatic successes&quot;?<br /> <br /> ( I couldn't find this in the books; if you do, please tell me which book and page, thank you!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T01:33:06-07:00","id":1320684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320680#post1320680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the mechanical benefits for Demons, when they lie? Do we get bonus dice or something else? Or the game simply rules that you have &quot;automatic successes&quot;?<br /> <br /> ( I couldn't find this in the books; if you do, please tell me which book and page, thank you!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mundane or supernatural means of directly confirming that their statements are truthful or lies \u2014 short of independent verification and other mundane methods of gathering information \u2014 do not necessarily work as they should, instead returning whatever result the demon wants the check to give. This doesn't make them inherently more convincing liars, but if they're subject to a means of quick-checking the truth value of a given answer then the interrogator has to rely on best-guesses or do the legwork of finding out from other people or their own senses or plain pattern recognition to determine whether the read is accurate or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T02:30:38-07:00","id":1320698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320684#post1320684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mundane or supernatural means of directly confirming that their statements are truthful or lies (...) if they're subject to a means of quick-checking the truth value of a given answer (...).</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the supernatural part of the answer (things like &quot;detect truth&quot; powers, etc.). But, what do you mean with &quot;mundane means of directly confirming truths?&quot; Polygraphs? Another thing? Also, I'd like to understand what could be &quot;a means of quick-checking the truth value of an answer&quot;.<br /> <br /> PS: &quot;this doesn't make them inherently more convincing liars&quot; = they use the same game systems to lie as any other character, without any mechanical advantage. Is that it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T03:07:53-07:00","id":1320701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320698#post1320698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the supernatural part of the answer (things like &quot;detect truth&quot; powers, etc.). But, what do you mean with &quot;mundane means of directly confirming truths?&quot; Polygraphs? Another thing? Also, I'd like to understand what could be &quot;a means of quick-checking the truth value of an answer&quot;.<br /> <br /> PS: &quot;this doesn't make them inherently more convincing liars&quot; = they use the same game systems to lie as any other character, without any mechanical advantage. Is that it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two parts to this:<br /> <br /> Liar's Tongue means that no supernatural means of detecting whether a demon is lying will work. The demon decides whether what they say should register as a lie or not. Supernatural powers can still check whether what a demon has said is true or not, though.<br /> <br /> Total Control means that nothing that relies on physiological responses will work. The demon will never exhibit any tics or stress responses, and polygraphs will always fail (on top of their already surprisingly high failure rates). You can also not rely on physiological responses to determine a demon's emotional state and similar information. Any rolls just fail.<br /> <br /> Neither of these blocks a person's ability to roll Wits+Empathy or Wits+Subterfuge to see through any lies since the demon isn't necessarily a skilled liar. They're just as capable of you and me to just fail to convince someone that a lie is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T07:40:27-07:00","id":1320745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320701#post1320701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither of these blocks a person's ability to roll Wits+Empathy or Wits+Subterfuge to see through any lies since the demon isn't necessarily a skilled liar. They're just as capable of you and me to just fail to convince someone that a lie is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general an excellent answer but I disagree with the last bit. A demon has absolute control of their emotional displays. Empathy or any attempt to ascertain if the demon &quot;really believes&quot; that something is true won't work. Wits+Subterfuge might be ok if the latter means catching them in a contradiction. I'd rule that no Social merit or skill would be useful in determining if a demon is lying (as well as any magical one, as you point out).<br /> <br /> <i>Verification/Falsification</i> is of course a different issue, as you point out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T11:06:37-07:00","id":1320787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320745#post1320745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wits+Subterfuge might be ok if the latter means catching them in a contradiction. I'd rule that no Social merit or skill would be useful in determining if a demon is lying.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I originally thought (before coming here to ask), and the reason for my question. I wondered: since they can't show involuntary expressions, that should mean that they have at least some kind of bonus, right? I agree 100% with the &quot;catch contradictions&quot; bit, but how to put that other aspect (lack of involuntary cues) in game systems? I think it's VERY strange that the books didn't have a straight answer (that's the Chronicle of Darkness M.O. that so many fans love &amp; brag about, after all XD). So, I'm trying (unsuccessfully) to find a sidebar, bullet point, section, paragraph, whatever, stating the actual game rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If any of you know where it is (book + page), please, tell us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T16:04:40-07:00","id":1320845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320787#post1320787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's VERY strange that the books didn't have a straight answer (that's the Chronicle of Darkness M.O. that so many fans love &amp; brag about, after all XD).</div> </div> </div> </div>People who brag about that should probably stop bragging about that, imo.<br /> It's hard to point to any examples in DtD since it's in its first edition, but the second editions of the CofD games (while great games in their own right) often omit minor details that were detailed back in first edition. There's also a <i>huge</i> list of things that require clarifications that forum regulars like us often forget about since we've already gotten those clarifications by some remarkably active devs (or sometimes long discussions about the correct interpretation of vague texts).<br /> <br /> In short, that side bar you're looking for doesn't exist. The rules are as follows:<br /> Any attempts to read lies through supernatural means automatically fail (if the demon wants them to fail).<br /> Any attempts to read lies based on physiological responses automatically fail.<br /> Any other mundane attempts to read lies will be contested with a relevant Attribute+Skill roll with no stated modifications to the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T16:12:33-07:00","id":1320847,"title":"","content":"The demon reads as they believe they are telling the truth but that doesn't automatically mean that it is believed. They can say the sky is not-blue and all detection will detect as they believe they are telling the truth but a casual look up will reveal that is not true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T21:46:35-07:00","id":1320890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320845#post1320845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, that side bar you're looking for doesn't exist. The rules are as follows:<br /> Any attempts to read lies through supernatural means automatically fail (if the demon wants them to fail).<br /> Any attempts to read lies based on physiological responses automatically fail.<br /> Any other mundane attempts to read lies will be contested with a relevant Attribute+Skill roll with no stated modifications to the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I thought it existed but I had missed it. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T08:35:08-07:00","id":1320963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320845#post1320845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, that side bar you're looking for doesn't exist. The rules are as follows:<br /> Any attempts to read lies through supernatural means automatically fail (if the demon wants them to fail).<br /> Any attempts to read lies based on physiological responses automatically fail.<br /> Any other mundane attempts to read lies will be contested with a relevant Attribute+Skill roll with no stated modifications to the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule that on a success the demon always appears to believe what it chooses to show. That the Attribute+Skill roll success simply reveals that choice. The perceiver can still fail that skill roll, though and not discern whatever the demon had chosen.<br /> So a demon could choose to subtly convey &quot;I am lying&quot; and the perceiver could fail to pick up on it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T14:26:00-07:00","id":1321034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1320963#post1320963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rule that on a success the demon always appears to believe what it chooses to show.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Liar's Tongue specifically calls out that the ability to believe things is only really useful for supernatural purposes. Further, whilst Total Control means that a demon doesn't have involuntary physiological responses, it also means they need to deliberately project some of those responses in order to look convincing, therefore they need to know what those responses are (the subterfuge skill). It specifically mentions that social expression is a skill, and one that some Demon's never learn.<br /> <br /> So, the Subterfuge 0 demon can lie with a straight face, but that lie is probably going to be miscalculated because the Demon doesn't really know what physiological responses to project to look convincing.<br /> <br /> Empathy would pick up on the weird response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T14:42:23-07:00","id":1333300,"title":"","content":"What methods do demons have to see into Twilight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T23:40:57-07:00","id":1333356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1333300#post1333300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What methods do demons have to see into Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as i know they can only emulate other powers with the Exploit Show of power","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T01:04:01-07:00","id":1333358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1333300#post1333300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What methods do demons have to see into Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>If</b></u> you're using the Demon Translation Guide's (pretty well written overall) translated demonic form abilities, Ghost Sight is listed as a Modification that allows the demon to perceive Twilit ghosts and spirits.<br /> <br /> A demon could enter ghostly or spiritual Twilight herself with the use of an Ephemeral Cover. This, mind, first requires her to rend ghosts or spirits into Cover material, which will be a challenge (but not impossible) without the ability to peer into Twilight.<br /> <br /> A demon could also enter astral Twilight with the Decoy Exploit from the Interface, but unless you've got a local outbreak of projecting psychics or summoned goetia, you're not going to find it very populated.<br /> <br /> Demons aren't generally well equipped to deal with unmanifested ephemera. A determined demon could probably hammer out near-field gadgets to interface with particular phases of Twilight as the most accessible method. Whatever the case, the ability to perceive <i>angelic</i> Twilight is probably not something a demonic power can do casually, if at all: it undermines the paranoia. (Conversely, most angels shouldn't be able to just safely and invisibly zot demons without manifesting. There is, however, plenty of horrid shit they could do to a tailed demon without having to materialize and start a fistfight.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-07T23:11:38-07:00","id":1334418,"title":"","content":"Are glitches an alternative to cover loss and condition or just conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T06:46:37-07:00","id":1334447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1334418#post1334418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are glitches an alternative to cover loss and condition or just conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T01:33:50-07:00","id":1335282,"title":"","content":"As a demon, can I cure a degenerative disease by Pacting for it, and then just never patching that element into one of my Covers, or sticking it on a Facade or burn Cover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T02:14:47-07:00","id":1335283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1335282#post1335282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a demon, can I cure a degenerative disease by Pacting for it, and then just never patching that element into one of my Covers, or sticking it on a Facade or burn Cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't allow a demonic pact to &quot;remove from play&quot; an identifier by bargaining for it without putting it anywhere. At my table, it doesn't come off the pactee until it goes onto a Cover.<br /> I wouldn't allow identifiers to be pasted onto a facade either. A facade is borrowed, not owned, and it's too thin a material to work with.<br /> <br /> Patch it onto a Cover you intend to burn anyway? I'd allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T19:00:29-07:00","id":1335386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1335282#post1335282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a demon, can I cure a degenerative disease by Pacting for it, and then just never patching that element into one of my Covers, or sticking it on a Facade or burn Cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>A demon can make a pact with a homeless person giving them riches in return for the love of a childhood sweetheart - the demon doesn't have to take on their poverty or homelessness. <br /> <br /> A demon can give an ugly person the Merit &quot;Striking Looks&quot; in return for their &quot;loss of a child&quot; experience, without having to take on the human's ugly features.<br /> <br /> So I would think that a demon can make a pact giving someone the Merit &quot;Hardy&quot; or &quot;Robust&quot; without taking on the human's illness. <br /> <br /> Of course, YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T14:24:47-07:00","id":1336941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1335283#post1335283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't allow a demonic pact to &quot;remove from play&quot; an identifier by bargaining for it without putting it anywhere. At my table, it doesn't come off the pactee until it goes onto a Cover.<br /> I wouldn't allow identifiers to be pasted onto a facade either. A facade is borrowed, not owned, and it's too thin a material to work with.<br /> <br /> Patch it onto a Cover you intend to burn anyway? I'd allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've made an NPC, The Kindly One, who does this,... and gives the cancer-striken patch jobs to demons in need of an emergency Cover, Never could work them into a book but always wanted to","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T17:17:35-07:00","id":1341968,"title":"","content":"What would the God-Machine do To keep a Demon-Blooded Mage Character with a Completed Cipher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T17:42:46-07:00","id":1341975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1341968#post1341968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would the God-Machine do To keep a Demon-Blooded Mage Character with a Completed Cipher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever amount of effort and resources produce a net benefit in exchange for keeping the sorcerous sleeper agent active, no more and no less.<br /> <br /> If that's not a very useful answer, it's because this question is extremely hard to answer in the abstract. What actual decisions is it weighing against each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T18:46:18-07:00","id":1341985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1341968#post1341968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would the God-Machine do To keep a Demon-Blooded Mage Character with a Completed Cipher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, because such a character can\u2019t exist by default. Either Awakening would obliviate the Demon-Blooded minor template or such a character simply can\u2019t Awaken. Given that stigmatics can\u2019t Awaken (Signs of Sorcery p. 129), I\u2019d be inclined towards the latter. Such a character could exist via Storyteller fiat, but that would make them so rare and unique that the God-Machine\u2019s response would be equally unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 10-19-2019, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T16:52:33-07:00","id":1342224,"title":"","content":"Isn't there already a Stigmatic Mage, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T17:21:10-07:00","id":1342229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1342224#post1342224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there already a Stigmatic Mage, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a mage who used to be stigmatic, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1320870-can-x-awaken?p=1320904#post1320904\">which is not actually revelatory about the lore</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T03:52:13-07:00","id":1343374,"title":"","content":"If a demon with a male cover obtain a son via pact from a man (the father), can he patch it into his cover with him as the fater an the cover wife as the mother?<br /> Or he need to make a pact also with the true mother? What if she has died?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 10-24-2019, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T12:36:53-07:00","id":1343832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1343374#post1343374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a demon with a male cover obtain a son via pact from a man (the father), can he patch it into his cover with him as the fater an the cover wife as the mother?<br /> Or he need to make a pact also with the true mother? What if she has died?</div> </div> </div> </div>He'd need to pact with the biological mom to gain access to that component. The Father can Pact away <i>their</i> relationship to the Son, but not affect others' relationships to the Son - they have no claim over those.<br /> <br /> Instead, it will have happened that the original mother had a fling with the Cover, probably &quot;obviously&quot; left unsaid all this time. Even if wildly varying genetics leaves the situation questionable. That's just a potential red-flag that could be investigated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T00:40:20-07:00","id":1343934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1343832#post1343832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He'd need to pact with the biological mom to gain access to that component. The Father can Pact away <i>their</i> relationship to the Son, but not affect others' relationships to the Son - they have no claim over those.<br /> <br /> Instead, it will have happened that the original mother had a fling with the Cover, probably &quot;obviously&quot; left unsaid all this time. Even if wildly varying genetics leaves the situation questionable. That's just a potential red-flag that could be investigated.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be a good explaination, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T16:30:37-08:00","id":1345942,"title":"","content":"Can Angels detect Demons in some way? I know Plugged In mentions they don\u2019t have to spoof an Angel but it\u2019s not immediately clear when that would be necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T16:42:56-08:00","id":1345949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1345942#post1345942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Angels detect Demons in some way? I know Plugged In mentions they don\u2019t have to spoof an Angel but it\u2019s not immediately clear when that would be necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoofing lets you register as the thing that your Cover is to supernatural scrutiny, whether that's directly or by implication. Angels don't have a consistent means of detecting Aether like demons and cryptids do, but demonic form powers like Aura Sight come from angelic powers like Numina and more prosaic sources of information \u2014 Plugged In makes the note that you don't have to spoof angels in the same sentence where it points out that you <i>can't</i> because you register as an angel to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:17:54-08:00","id":1345956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1345949#post1345949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoofing lets you register as the thing that your Cover is to supernatural scrutiny, whether that's directly or by implication. Angels don't have a consistent means of detecting Aether like demons and cryptids do, but demonic form powers like Aura Sight come from angelic powers like Numina and more prosaic sources of information \u2014 Plugged In makes the note that you don't have to spoof angels in the same sentence where it points out that you <i>can't</i> because you register as an angel to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the part about why you don\u2019t register at as angel to them, but it\u2019s also presented as the Good News, which implies it might be normally an issue. Am I missing a numina somewhere that allows supernatural detection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:43:53-08:00","id":1345963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1345956#post1345956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the part about why you don\u2019t register at as angel to them, but it\u2019s also presented as the Good News, which implies it might be normally an issue. Am I missing a numina somewhere that allows supernatural detection?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no prewritten Numen that accomplishes the thing that a demonic form power establishes there are angels explicitly built with among the explicit diversity of powers angels can be built to have as Numina that might trigger the demonic ability to pass for human that specifically can be made to stop working against angels, no. This is not the same thing as there being no room for such a Numen to exist in the setting despite its being directly implied.<br /> <br /> Sense the Angelic works on the same principles that Plugged In's recognition alludes to and those aren't given mechanical emphasis, either. This is literally as simple as &quot;there's an angel with a Numen that works like the Aura Sight form power&quot; or &quot;there's an angel that counts how many humans pass through a given intersection.&quot; The mechanics of making a Numen aren't complicated enough to put space into every conceivable thing an angel could have as a discrete ability, because that is a list that goes on basically forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-04-2019, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:42:36-08:00","id":1345988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1345963#post1345963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no prewritten Numen that accomplishes the thing that a demonic form power establishes there are angels explicitly built with among the explicit diversity of powers angels can be built to have as Numina that might trigger the demonic ability to pass for human that specifically can be made to stop working against angels, no. This is not the same thing as there being no room for such a Numen to exist in the setting despite its being directly implied.<br /> <br /> Sense the Angelic works on the same principles that Plugged In's recognition alludes to and those aren't given mechanical emphasis, either. This is literally as simple as &amp;quot;there's an angel with a Numen that works like the Aura Sight form power&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;there's an angel that counts how many humans pass through a given intersection.&amp;quot; The mechanics of making a Numen aren't complicated enough to put space into every conceivable thing an angel could have as a discrete ability, because that is a list that goes on basically forever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So it sounds like unless I give a specific Angel the power to try and detect a Demon, a Demon can generally be face to face with an Angel and not really have to worry too much about being detected as such unless they do something to draw attention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T20:38:01-08:00","id":1346028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1345988#post1345988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it sounds like unless I give a specific Angel the power to try and detect a Demon, a Demon can generally be face to face with an Angel and not really have to worry too much about being detected as such unless they do something to draw attention?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that spoofing doesn't stop people from thinking you're acting suspicious any more than Liar's Tongue compels them to believe you, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:20:46-08:00","id":1346057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1345988#post1345988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it sounds like unless I give a specific Angel the power to try and detect a Demon, a Demon can generally be face to face with an Angel and not really have to worry too much about being detected as such unless they do something to draw attention?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember that as a Demon in Cover, you are nice and squishy, while even a Rank 2 angel can easily have Power+FInesse of 10 dice for an attack, can summon its buddies who might be any one of the other people nearby, and can run a background check on you with all the computer resources the GodMachine can access. If she is even slightly suspicious of you, she might have you followed invisibly, from Twilight. Or even just have a few human cultists routinely check you out, picking away at your Cover. <br /> <br /> Now as a Demon, you may have some fancy tricks you can pull. Most of them will set off alarms for the angel. And your goal isn't to defeat the angel, because the inevitable result of that is <i>more angels showing up.</i> <br /> <br /> Of course, if she's <i>not</i> suspicious of you, she might view you as a useful human to exploit for some suicide mission she's planning. <br /> <br /> It's a police state and angels are the super-powered gestapo/secret police that can have you dragged away and your mind cored and reprogrammed to betray everyone you love.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T07:36:04-08:00","id":1348668,"title":"","content":"Probably someone already asked, but if a demon creates a gadget with a bonus based on the embed user primium, what kind of bonus receive another user?<br /> The creator primium?<br /> His supernatural tolerance, if any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T15:30:09-08:00","id":1348946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1348668#post1348668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably someone already asked, but if a demon creates a gadget with a bonus based on the embed user primium, what kind of bonus receive another user?<br /> The creator primium?<br /> His supernatural tolerance, if any?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd typically fix the bonus at Gadget creation. So, creator's Primum at that point in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T16:01:01-08:00","id":1348958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1348668#post1348668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably someone already asked, but if a demon creates a gadget with a bonus based on the embed user primium, what kind of bonus receive another user?<br /> The creator primium?<br /> His supernatural tolerance, if any?</div> </div> </div> </div>I trend towards the current users Primum, like it's an Exploit. If the user has another supernatural tolerance, it depends on the gadget and the user.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T01:05:22-08:00","id":1349019,"title":"","content":"The problem is that a hunan would have no benedit from the item use if the bonus is supernatural tolerance based.<br /> So i would give a flat +1 or as Vent0 said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T03:48:44-08:00","id":1349045,"title":"","content":"See, Gadgets are supposed to be more rigid, and by basing it on the user's stats, there is incentive for stronger Demons to pressure weaker ones into creating Gadgets they can use with more potency. The inverse is that Gadgets crafted by powerful Demons have a lot of value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T06:32:08-08:00","id":1349063,"title":"","content":"Do Demons have 100% accuracy to detecting infrastructure, Angels, and Stigmatics?<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> Players walk into a \u201cBad Part of Town\u201d Infrastructure, where Mortals are transformed into gang members defending their turf. <br /> <br /> Players are at their Free Agency meeting when a new demon arrives they are actually an Angel trying to compromise the Agency. <br /> <br /> A Demon see a bunch of people evangelizing passerby\u2019s on the street. The evangelists are actually Stigmatic cultists. <br /> <br /> In these 3 scenarios would the demon see the gears of the God-Machine. Would they need to roll to notice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T07:00:48-08:00","id":1349065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1349063#post1349063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Demons have 100% accuracy to detecting infrastructure, Angels, and Stigmatics?<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> Players walk into a \u201cBad Part of Town\u201d Infrastructure, where Mortals are transformed into gang members defending their turf.<br /> <br /> Players are at their Free Agency meeting when a new demon arrives they are actually an Angel trying to compromise the Agency.<br /> <br /> A Demon see a bunch of people evangelizing passerby\u2019s on the street. The evangelists are actually Stigmatic cultists.<br /> <br /> In these 3 scenarios would the demon see the gears of the God-Machine. Would they need to roll to notice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons have two ways of identifying G-M stuff (other than through mundane investigations and deductions), namely automatically seeing through any supernatural concealment on Infrastructure (much like Stigmatics and people with the Unseen Sense (God-Machine) Merit), and using Aetheric Resonance by spending an Aether to sense any Essence/Aether sources or expenditures within a certain radius.<ul><li>Your first example is too vague to say one way or another.</li> <li>The angel who infiltrates demons is hidden by its Cover that they demons can't see through. It can be sensed through Aetheric Resonance if it uses any Essence, but a demon using Aether would also ping so it wouldn't help except by alerting the demon using Aetheric Resonance that a supernatural power was activated/used.</li> <li>Stigmatics aren't hidden by supernatural concealment and just shows up like humans. Stigmatics (and Cryptids) also don't trigger Aetheric Resonance so that doesn't help. Only way to recognising that they're Stigmatics or cultists is through deduction, figuring out that what they're doing isn't normal or possible for regular humans.</li> </ul>In short, most Infrastructure is hidden through mundane means as well as through supernatural concealment. Demons only automatically pierce the latter, and need to investigate in order to see through the former. For example, a piece of Infrastructure subtly altering the mood of all tenants in a building is hidden down in the basement. Just looking at the building or at the affected tenants won't reveal the Infrastructure. In order to find it, the demon needs to figure out that tenants on lower floors are more affected and the source is thus most likely further down, or through use of Aetheric Resonance if their Primum is high enough to find the Infrastructure all the way down in the basement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-17-2019, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T07:20:30-08:00","id":1349067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1349063#post1349063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Demons have 100% accuracy to detecting infrastructure, Angels, and Stigmatics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each infrastructural project of the God-Machine has some kind of tell, something about it that outwardly manifests the occult correspondences it is seeking to exploit to produce output. It's not universally manifest through every single moving part of the project: if there's a human workforce at a factory the Machine uses to produce an output, the human laborers aren't necessarily all sporting the same occult tattoo. But they might. Or instead, there might be beating hearts ensconced within the circuit breakers throughout the building. Or instead, the building speakers might play foreign pop music in a language nobody at the factory speaks. There is something about a major part of the project that says, &quot;there is something wrong here.&quot; There has to be, because it's part of the extremely complicated setup the God-Machine needs to line up to produce the output.<br /> <br /> These are the gears demons and stigmatics can see that others can't, these tells. Concealment projects have been set up to prevent the ordinary person from being able to notice what's wrong. (If they're forced into contact with it, like an electrician sent to fix the circuit breakers who comes face-to-face with the beating heart, that's the beginning of a bluebook mortals God-Machine Chronicle.) Demons see these things and see occult correspondences lining up. They think, &quot;I don't know what the Machine is doing here, but I know it's doing something.&quot;<br /> <br /> Players see these things and think, &quot;I don't know what the Storyteller has set up here, but there is a plot hook established here.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T08:51:27-08:00","id":1349092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1349019#post1349019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that a hunan would have no benedit from the item use if the bonus is supernatural tolerance based.<br /> So i would give a flat +1 or as Vent0 said</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is true, gadgets aren't meant for humans to use much of the time, and if the gadget is precision engineered (which you need for that benefit most of the time) then a Demon is unlikely to let it out of their sight for long. It depends on the context of the game and the players within.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1349045#post1349045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, Gadgets are supposed to be more rigid, and by basing it on the user's stats, there is incentive for stronger Demons to pressure weaker ones into creating Gadgets they can use with more potency. The inverse is that Gadgets crafted by powerful Demons have a lot of value.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that works in a narrative sense, it should be remembered that precision engineering is not an insignificant undertaking, and having a player manage it early with a static bonus only to grow ib Primum and not have the equivalent bonus later can be frustrating. As noted above, it depends on context and the players within the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T10:04:56-08:00","id":1349107,"title":"","content":"&quot;Karen thinks the image is too precise. They agree that Trick of the Light doesn\u2019t allow for such detailed hallucinations, perhaps merely provoking victims to see threatening movement in their peripheral vision that can\u2019t be pinned down. Brad agrees to this and asks if the visions can impair both Perception and Initiative (<b>penalty to both equal to Brad\u2019s character\u2019s Primum rating, which is 3 \u2014 note that once the gadget is created, this number won\u2019t increase even if the demon\u2019s Primum does</b>).&quot;<br /> <br /> Part of the example for creating gadgets.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd try to avoid any dice bonuses/penalties when designing gadgets. They generally (but not always, the example is a good exception) relegate the gadget into being just a tool for your action rather than being a cool invention that does its own thing and opens up new possibilities when used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T12:31:30-08:00","id":1349143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1349107#post1349107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Karen thinks the image is too precise. They agree that Trick of the Light doesn\u2019t allow for such detailed hallucinations, perhaps merely provoking victims to see threatening movement in their peripheral vision that can\u2019t be pinned down. Brad agrees to this and asks if the visions can impair both Perception and Initiative (<b>penalty to both equal to Brad\u2019s character\u2019s Primum rating, which is 3 \u2014 note that once the gadget is created, this number won\u2019t increase even if the demon\u2019s Primum does</b>).&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Part of the example for creating gadgets.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd try to avoid any dice bonuses/penalties when designing gadgets. They generally (but not always, the example is a good exception) relegate the gadget into being just a tool for your action rather than being a cool invention that does its own thing and opens up new possibilities when used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the example and for the advice \ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T13:29:17-08:00","id":1349159,"title":"","content":"Off-topic, but!<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~ Approaching 666 Responses ~ ~ ~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T11:58:15-08:00","id":1350868,"title":"","content":"How might a Demon Pact affect a Supernatural?<br /> <br /> For instance, a Vampire wanting to cure their Vampirism. In my head it separates the Beast from their body as a personification of Vampirism unleashed. So while the Vampire is now human, a monster is created that can only be stopped by destroying the Pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T14:48:01-08:00","id":1350915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1350868#post1350868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might a Demon Pact affect a Supernatural?<br /> <br /> For instance, a Vampire wanting to cure their Vampirism. In my head it separates the Beast from their body as a personification of Vampirism unleashed. So while the Vampire is now human, a monster is created that can only be stopped by destroying the Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>From demon core book:<br /> &quot;demons cannot \u201cpatch in\u201d supernatural aspects (effectively because their supernatural abilities aren\u2019t compatible with a demon\u2019s abilities to affect the world \u2014 a vampire\u2019s blood-based \u201chardware\u201d won\u2019t work with a demon\u2019s Aether-powered \u201csoftware\u201d). A demon cannot take away a vampire\u2019s vulnerability to sunlight, for example, nor can she patch in a werewolf\u2019s ability to change forms.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T18:42:26-08:00","id":1350942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1350915#post1350915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From demon core book:<br /> &amp;quot;demons cannot \u201cpatch in\u201d supernatural aspects (effectively because their supernatural abilities aren\u2019t compatible with a demon\u2019s abilities to affect the world \u2014 a vampire\u2019s blood-based \u201chardware\u201d won\u2019t work with a demon\u2019s Aether-powered \u201csoftware\u201d). A demon cannot take away a vampire\u2019s vulnerability to sunlight, for example, nor can she patch in a werewolf\u2019s ability to change forms.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I always read that as Demons couldn\u2019t incorporate other splats into their cover. Or piecemeal away their weaknesses or abilities.<br /> <br /> Though I guess he removing sunlight weakness kind of confirms that that may be the case. They do mention becoming human version of the target if they do a soul pact with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:55:45-08:00","id":1351131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1350942#post1350942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do mention becoming human version of the target if they do a soul pact with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but that's not the vampire becoming human, that's the vampire being annihilated and the demon gaining a Cover of &quot;this vampire, but without actually being a vampire.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T06:21:43-08:00","id":1351272,"title":"","content":"Good day, quick question:<br /> The merit resonance sensitive from flowers of hell states &quot;Additionally, this Merit allows your character to identify demons on sight without spending Aether.&quot;<br /> Do you think this can bypass Cover protection?<br /> <br /> And also:<br /> Even if embeds doesn t cost aether do you think they can be seen with aetheric resonance?<br /> If not shouldn t angels be able to detect their uses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T10:08:15-08:00","id":1351309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1351272#post1351272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good day, quick question:<br /> The merit resonance sensitive from flowers of hell states &quot;Additionally, this Merit allows your character to identify demons on sight without spending Aether.&quot;<br /> Do you think this can bypass Cover protection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the demon still gets to try to spoof.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T18:12:31-08:00","id":1351941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1351309#post1351309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the demon still gets to try to spoof.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't note if Demons spoof in reaponse to it or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T18:42:29-08:00","id":1351945,"title":"","content":"IIRC Resonance Sensitivity simply modifies the Aetheric resonance sense that all demons have access to. It removes the Aether cost (and makes it reflexive if it isn't already, I believe; not at my books right now). Check the rules for Aetheric resonance sense for details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T15:39:32-08:00","id":1352687,"title":"","content":"Hello, maybe this is an old question, anyway I'm here!<br /> <br /> Demons are often depict as wary and selfish beings, and also the manuals tells tath's not so easy for them to make team work.<br /> <br /> Do you have any plot hook to suggest me about how to put together a Ring of Unchained in spite of their lonely nature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T21:12:26-08:00","id":1352729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1352687#post1352687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, maybe this is an old question, anyway I'm here!<br /> <br /> Demons are often depict as wary and selfish beings, and also the manuals tells tath's not so easy for them to make team work.<br /> <br /> Do you have any plot hook to suggest me about how to put together a Ring of Unchained in spite of their lonely nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not get your players to help you? Ask them how they met, and why they decided to trust each other. Otherwise it might feel a bit forced if you give them a reason that you made up. You can throw them some suggestions:<ul><li>One player might have helped the other right after they Fell.</li> <li>They might have been brought together by a superior in an Agency.</li> <li>One might have saved the another from a hunter Angel.</li> <li>They each have a person or cause threatened by a common GodMachine activity.</li> <li>There is a low but steady Aether source that requires several demons to operate.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T06:10:18-08:00","id":1352995,"title":"","content":"Demons don't seem that much more durable than Mortals and don't really have a weakness as far as I can tell, mainly because it seems like they are harmed by the same thing that harms a Mortal.<ul><li>What is stopping a Mortal from killing a Demon in one on one combat?</li> <li>What is the Demon equivalent of sunlight and silver bullets?</li> <li>How might Hunters hunt Demons?</li> <li>What is stopping a Hunter/Spurned Pactbound from exposing a Demon as one and causing a cascade of compromise checks?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T06:58:14-08:00","id":1353001,"title":"","content":"What is stopping a Mortal from killing a Demon in one on one combat? - Nothing if they do not use their powers. This is roughly equivalent to Mages too btw. Demons have reflexive healing Wound healing (Demonic Form), shifting damage to something else (Embeds like Sift Consequence or On the Mend), or use an Exploit like Break to Heal. Otherwise, they can be more offensive using Blade Hand, Merciless Gunman or Hellfire.<br /> <br /> What is the Demon equivalent of sunlight and silver bullets? - The biggest weakness for a Demon is getting caught. Pulling down the wrath of the God-Machine in either a direct Angelic attack, blowing his cover or having other agents (cults, etc.) come after the Demon. Doing things outside the Cover's normal behavior can weaken Cover, thereby having to lose whatever they have built up (money, identity, status, etc.).<br /> <br /> How might Hunters hunt a Demon. - Maybe they become Cultists of the G-M? Maybe they pick up on the shifting Covers and know he/she is a supernatural? Aetheric detector invented of some type?<br /> <br /> What is stopping a Hunter/Spurned Pactbound from exposing a Demon as one and causing a cascade of compromise checks? - Who's going to believe them? If a Demon can shift Covers to give an alibi, separate from Demonic form from the Cover to seem like someone else (Terrible Avatar), or just rewrite the minds of those he's &quot;affected&quot; (Memory Theft/Without a Trace) or even write it into the Pact to void the advantages of the Pactbound? You have some options.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T07:03:30-08:00","id":1353003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1352995#post1352995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons don't seem that much more durable than Mortals and don't really have a weakness as far as I can tell, mainly because it seems like they are harmed by the same thing that harms a Mortal.<ul><li>What is stopping a Mortal from killing a Demon in one on one combat?</li> <li>What is the Demon equivalent of sunlight and silver bullets?</li> <li>How might Hunters hunt Demons?</li> <li>What is stopping a Hunter/Spurned Pactbound from exposing a Demon as one and causing a cascade of compromise checks?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter can track demons by investigating glitches and low rating cover, as explained in the demon core.<br /> At pag 114 it states &quot;Only new information counts; if that information is disseminated to several people at once, like a hunter telling his cell that he\u2019s identified a demon, it still only counts as one compromise. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T07:18:25-08:00","id":1353007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1352995#post1352995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is stopping a Mortal from killing a Demon in one on one combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Embeds, Exploits, Demonic Forms and usually being geared toward avoiding such encounters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1352995#post1352995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Demon equivalent of sunlight and silver bullets?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing. A demon is already living a precarious existence having to hide from a seemingly omnipresent entity hunting it. Having specific weaknesses would detract from that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1352995#post1352995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might Hunters hunt Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>With difficulty since a good demon wouldn't be discovered by hunters in the first place. If a hunter would find out about a demon, it would either be by seeing its Demonic Form or finding something unusual about one of its Covers. The Demonic Form is only used situationally so it's not something that can be actively hunted. If the hunter has found out about a particular Cover, it's probably a Burner and not used often enough for it to be able to be tracked.<br /> If it's somehow the demon's <i>main</i> Cover, the hunter finally stands a chance of actually hunting (rather than just reacting to chance encounters) because the demon may not want to burn that Cover. Then it's a matter of the hunter just confronting the demon while they're doing their Cover routine (working a job, doing a hobby, maintaining appearances) and then hope the demon doesn't have any nasty Embeds, Exploits or Demonic Form abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1352995#post1352995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is stopping a Hunter/Spurned Pactbound from exposing a Demon as one and causing a cascade of compromise checks?</div> </div> </div> </div>A good demon would be anonymous enough to not have their Cover's identity be exposed to their mark. You can't expose someone if you don't know anything about them, such as their (Cover's) real name, address, phone number, etc. Alternatively, it's just a burner Cover that the demon doesn't care about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T13:54:29-08:00","id":1353419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1353003#post1353003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunter can track demons by investigating glitches and low rating cover, as explained in the demon core.<br /> At pag 114 it states &quot;Only new information counts; if that information is disseminated to several people at once, like a hunter telling his cell that he\u2019s identified a demon, it still only counts as one compromise. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of excellent answers to this question already. I just want to add one more point: demons are ultimately playing a clandestine spy role. They are (nearly( indistinguishable from humans, are perfect liars, and have lots of abilities to confound someone who thinks that they aren't. If your Hunters are killing civilians simply on the suspicion that they might be connected to the supernatural, then they're already monsters themselves. And that means that someone <i>else</i> is probably already hunting <i>them.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T17:11:07-08:00","id":1353453,"title":"","content":"And with <i>Stalking Horse</i> and <i>Everybody Knows</i>, their own hunters will find them swiftly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T16:45:02-08:00","id":1356394,"title":"","content":"So, since there was some confusion over it on a Discord group I'm in, I'm going to ask this; how much does a non-Analyst Demon remember of their time as an Angel? I was under the impression their memories were fuzzy at best, but the text is confusing to look over for that. Some page numbers would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-21-2019, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T17:23:07-08:00","id":1356403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1356394#post1356394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, since there was some confusion over it on a Discord group I'm in, I'm going to ask this; how much does a non-Analyst Demon remember of their time as an Angel? I was under the impression their memories were fuzzy at best, but the text is confusing to look over for that. Some page numbers would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a safe bet you remember most if not all of your last assignment and anything before that is going to depend on your CV and the intervening maintenance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T06:52:08-08:00","id":1356637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1356394#post1356394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, since there was some confusion over it on a Discord group I'm in, I'm going to ask this; how much does a non-Analyst Demon remember of their time as an Angel? I was under the impression their memories were fuzzy at best, but the text is confusing to look over for that. Some page numbers would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran a prologue for a player where it covered his arrival, assignment, and how he carried out his task. So he knew what Infrastructure summoned him and what Infrastructure he used to maintain his abilities.<br /> <br /> He doesn\u2019t remember much about before his assignment except that he was bodyless and directionless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T05:49:02-08:00","id":1357031,"title":"","content":"From Demoon:Interface source material (the one about the step-daughter assignment), it would appear that yes, you remember the last assignment fairly well. Everything else is subject to ST discretion. If you are running a game, then it's up to you. The guideline is fuzzy such as you were a Messenger or Sword type of angel engaged in THIS or THAT type of activities. Sometimes angels are wiped between uses as well. Think about the Winter Soldier in Captain America. You were sent out, did you mission. If you started asking too many questions,, you were wiped usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T15:09:08-08:00","id":1359584,"title":"","content":"Let's say the PC's manage to provoke a high Rank angel into Falling. What happens? Is there an explosion? Does the Angel collapse? Do they become a Primum 1 demon instantly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T10:15:28-08:00","id":1359741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1359584#post1359584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say the PC's manage to provoke a high Rank angel into Falling. What happens? Is there an explosion? Does the Angel collapse? Do they become a Primum 1 demon instantly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Descriptions of the Fall are on page 37. The Fall feels like an eternity for the on doing it, but is in fact a few seconds. The damage done to them is all internal. Collapsing in pain is likely, explosions? not as much.<br /> <br /> Angels typically start at Primum 1 when they fall. Page 108 of the core rules. They only start with more if they gain some invaluable insight in the Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T11:34:48-08:00","id":1359753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1359584#post1359584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say the PC's manage to provoke a high Rank angel into Falling. What happens? Is there an explosion? Does the Angel collapse? Do they become a Primum 1 demon instantly?</div> </div> </div> </div>With high rank do you mean rank 6+ archangels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T15:07:58-08:00","id":1359778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1359753#post1359753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With high rank do you mean rank 6+ archangels?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, merely a &quot;5&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T06:46:43-08:00","id":1361453,"title":"","content":"I was reading the Demon Storyteller's Guide (DSG) about Angelic Incepts and it states on page 84 for the Delivery Incept:<br /> <br /> <i>This Incept also allows the angel to spend Essence equal to the local Gauntlet to create a portal to any other ephemeral realm, from the Underworld to the Astral Realms to the Abyss.</i><br /> <br /> What does it mean &quot;<b><i>any other ephemeral realm</i></b>&quot;? I would assume this would not include The Hedge but where else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T07:17:34-08:00","id":1361455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghostdriver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1361453#post1361453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading the Demon Storyteller's Guide (DSG) about Angelic Incepts and it states on page 84 for the Delivery Incept:<br /> <br /> <i>This Incept also allows the angel to spend Essence equal to the local Gauntlet to create a portal to any other ephemeral realm, from the Underworld to the Astral Realms to the Abyss.</i><br /> <br /> What does it mean &quot;<b><i>any other ephemeral realm</i></b>&quot;? I would assume this would not include The Hedge but where else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it means any other realm that isn't the material (including splintered timelines and such). One of the examples, the Abyss, isn't ephemeral, nor is it actually a realm in its own right. It contains realms (also known as Annunaki) but it's more of a force than a location.<br /> <br /> If you instead think the inclusion of the Abyss was a mistake and it's only ephemeral realms that can be reached, then it's the Shadow, the Underworld and the Astral Realms. There are no other ephemeral realms that are known to us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:33:52-08:00","id":1361480,"title":"","content":"Thanks Tessie. You make sense in that I think it's talking about &quot;Underworld to the Astral Realms&quot; as Ephemeral. To me, since it seems to add &quot;to the Abyss&quot; at the end, it seems that it is not included in the above but a total separate &quot;place&quot;. <br /> <br /> What about The Hedge? Rip the Gates Exploit allows this. Would it be safe to say that an Angel could travel there as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T18:38:57-08:00","id":1361633,"title":"","content":"As phrased the way it is, &quot;to the Abyss&quot; is included as an example of an ephemeral realm. It's not tucked on; it's part of the same list as the Underworld and the Astral.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is not an ephemeral realm. Depending on how you rule the Incept to work at your table it may be possible at ST's discretion (if you open it up for all otherworldly realms) or impossible (if you, unlike the examples, limit it to only ephemeral realms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T05:12:35-08:00","id":1361713,"title":"","content":"The intent seems to be allowing them to reach various otherworlds. I'd allow it to reach whatever realms you are using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T19:00:42-08:00","id":1361834,"title":"","content":"Page 138 of the Storyteller\u2019s Guide outright states the God-Machine\u2019s agents can\u2019t enter the Hedge by design or accident. It seems strange that an Angelic Incept would allow them to access the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T21:28:02-08:00","id":1361847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1361834#post1361834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 138 of the Storyteller\u2019s Guide outright states the God-Machine\u2019s agents can\u2019t enter the Hedge by design or accident. It seems strange that an Angelic Incept would allow them to access the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most angels don't leave the material realm, outright, and Incepts are legacy code that loyalists generally aren't entirely authorized to use, but neither of those things strictly locks them off from having a slightly better vector for relocating extradimensional beings than mortals do \u2014 just because you're opening a door doesn't mean <i>you're</i> the one coming through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T09:30:55-08:00","id":1361914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1361834#post1361834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 138 of the Storyteller\u2019s Guide outright states the God-Machine\u2019s agents can\u2019t enter the Hedge by design or accident. It seems strange that an Angelic Incept would allow them to access the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Demon can open a rift into the Hedge. But doing so is suicide since they won\u2019t have access to their powers. It could be assumed that since a demon can do it an Angel could as well. Though likely only as a last resort to trap a powerful demon. <br /> <br /> Think about it. What better place to banish an entity than a place where it\u2019s powers don\u2019t work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T10:37:41-08:00","id":1361928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1361914#post1361914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But doing so is suicide since they won\u2019t have access to their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only Rip the Gates that can't be used within the Hedge. The only other thing the Hedge interferes with when it comes to demons is their Covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T06:42:15-08:00","id":1362098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1361834#post1361834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 138 of the Storyteller\u2019s Guide outright states the God-Machine\u2019s agents can\u2019t enter the Hedge by design or accident. It seems strange that an Angelic Incept would allow them to access the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the citation Taidragon. Appreciate all the feedback.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:34:16-07:00","id":1377877,"title":"","content":"<i>Merciless Gunman</i> will not work if Down and Dirty rules don't apply, in particular if the opponent is supernatural. RAW state that the Demon knows this and the ability never activates. What if the Demon attacks a half dozen opponents and only one of them is supernatural? ST's call?<br /> <br /> What if one of the six just happens to be a Demon? Do they spoof humanity and get killed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24502,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","user":"KieranMullen","date":".  Added the spoofing question. 04-02-2020, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T23:10:43-07:00","id":1377891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1377877#post1377877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Merciless Gunman</i> will not work if Down and Dirty rules don't apply, in particular if the opponent is supernatural. RAW state that the Demon knows this and the ability never activates. What if the Demon attacks a half dozen opponents and only one of them is supernatural? ST's call?<br /> <br /> What if one of the six just happens to be a Demon? Do they spoof humanity and get killed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Merciless Gunman does not work as a supernatural-detector, because being supernatural is not the only condition underwhich Down and Dirty Combat doesn't work. If there are a number of targets present who are valid subjects for Merciless Gunman, I would consider allowing the demon to activate the Embed, excluding any invalid subjects from the target list. Preferably the Storyteller should try to avoid this situation in the first place, using either a crowd of Down and Dirty mooks or a smaller number of more significant opponents, but no plan is perfect.<br /> <br /> I'll say again that <i>Merciless Gunman does not work as a supernatural-detector because there are plenty of non-supernatural combatants who would not be appropriate targets for Down and Dirty Combat,</i> but even if it were, spoofing does not work that way. Spoofing works to fool sensory effects which have the potential to blow a demon's Cover. Shooting a person is not a sensory effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:57:01-07:00","id":1378446,"title":"","content":"Merciless Gunman can <i>instead</i> apply 8-Again to the Firearms roll if Down and Dirty does not apply, just to mention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T09:15:27-07:00","id":1380390,"title":"","content":"How do you and your PC's handle cellular phones in game? Given that the GM is basically big brother, I would expect that there would be some thought put into how PC's can communicate safely, or perhaps deal in misinformation as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:33:56-07:00","id":1380415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1380390#post1380390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you and your PC's handle cellular phones in game? Given that the GM is basically big brother, I would expect that there would be some thought put into how PC's can communicate safely, or perhaps deal in misinformation as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time the God-Machine will have some level of Infrastructure monitoring electronic chatter. Cellphones, Messaging Apps, Email, etc... however it doesn\u2019t have the bandwidth to constantly be monitoring for every situation. <br /> <br /> A Demon calls her wife to tell her that she will be late home, because of work. But this Demon goes to a piece of Infrastructure to top off her aether. The G-M doesn\u2019t know about that second part. The Demon is just another Mortal to it, and if the Demon passed its Compromise checks the G-M doesn\u2019t Notice the discrepancies. <br /> <br /> A Demon calling up another on an insecure line to say the God-Machine killed their friend might result in the G-M noticing.<br /> <br /> Encryption and burner phones help mitigate this. The G-M might be able to uncover a Blatant breach \u201cLike saying Angels are guarding the Infrastructure in Central Park\u201d, but saying \u201cTwo shields are guarding a point of interest in Central Park\u201d likely won\u2019t hit the same keyword searches. <br /> <br /> Moscow rules state that you should assume all people are under opposition control, assume that with technology and add extra layers of difficulty to make sure the God Machine isn\u2019t given your Cover on a Silver Platter.<br /> <br /> Special Message is a great Embed to have and allows for the best way to communicate across an Agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T20:06:12-07:00","id":1380559,"title":"","content":"I buy the Bolthole Merit with the &quot;Easy Access&quot; level so any door I open could like to the bolthole. I open the door and put my friend Fred in the bolthole. If I move the door to somewhere else, can I retrieve Fred from that new door? The rules say you have to leave by the door you entered, but I suspect the RAI was to prevent someone <i>inside</i> the bolthole moving the door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T20:36:49-07:00","id":1380567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1380559#post1380559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I buy the Bolthole Merit with the &quot;Easy Access&quot; level so any door I open could like to the bolthole. I open the door and put my friend Fred in the bolthole. If I move the door to somewhere else, can I retrieve Fred from that new door? The rules say you have to leave by the door you entered, but I suspect the RAI was to prevent someone <i>inside</i> the bolthole moving the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reasonably certain that it works that way to prevent exactly that sort of leapfrogging, given that the person inside can't move the door anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T20:43:33-07:00","id":1380569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1380390#post1380390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you and your PC's handle cellular phones in game? Given that the GM is basically big brother, I would expect that there would be some thought put into how PC's can communicate safely, or perhaps deal in misinformation as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Assume everything you say will be listened to, everything you write will be read, and everything you do will be watched. SO pretty much speak and write in code. The 40k Eisenhorn series of novels has a pretty cool coded language in it so I would read spy novels to see how people used spycraft in the age of communication. Also the always handy dead drop is a great way to get through information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T21:18:36-07:00","id":1380575,"title":"","content":"What is the benefit of the Demon Car exploit? It just seems like Demon Form with more steps.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also it mentions Structure instead of Health for the Demon, but I don\u2019t see why that would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T21:35:19-07:00","id":1380579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1380567#post1380567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reasonably certain that it works that way to prevent exactly that sort of leapfrogging, given that the person inside can't move the door anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if I move the door, can Fred leave out of the moved door? Or can he only exit the bolthole from the original door?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T21:57:14-07:00","id":1380580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1380579#post1380579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if I move the door, can Fred leave out of the moved door? Or can he only exit the bolthole from the original door?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, to keep a bolthole \u2014 and I must here remind you that the Merit is literally described as &quot;a safehouse [you] can hole up in when things get bad&quot; \u2014 from being used as a method of quick transport for things that aren't cargo.<br /> <br /> Fred ducks into your bolthole at the place he enters and that means he leaves it in the same place when the coast is clear, not forty miles away in a different city just because you needed to set up your storage closet elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T06:21:55-07:00","id":1382142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1380575#post1380575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the benefit of the Demon Car exploit? It just seems like Demon Form with more steps.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also it mentions Structure instead of Health for the Demon, but I don\u2019t see why that would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon Car is amazing. It is still a Vehicle, which lets you engage in some unforeseen shenanigans (Van with Data Form to Trojan Horse your way into anyplace with a data connection). It lets you play around with Demonic Form Abilities you don't have, too.<br /> <br /> And, of course, it is a key component to a Demonic Voltron Lambda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T22:53:26-07:00","id":1382290,"title":"","content":"is there an appropriate place in this forum to list an online game looking for players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T18:58:44-07:00","id":1382423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1382290#post1382290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there an appropriate place in this forum to list an online game looking for players?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t usually solicit for online games, but there is a LFG subreddit which can be useful, as well as the White Wolf subreddit. <br /> <br /> My suggestion is to spread the net wide as you can: Roll20 Forums, LFG subreddit, White Wolf subreddit, here, etc...<br /> <br /> It\u2019s hard to players for non-Dungeons and Dragons games. Because you are relying on a niche group of players who are interested in seeing you post in the short window that it is viewable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T19:30:18-07:00","id":1382425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1382290#post1382290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there an appropriate place in this forum to list an online game looking for players?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings\">Front page of the forums.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T21:49:31-07:00","id":1386610,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Here's a question: a player gets a bonus to their Compromise roll for every Demonic Form </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">not</span></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> invoked. If a player takes five dots of Terrible Form, which gives them five additional Forms, and then uses one of their Form abilities, do you think that they should get five extra dice for their Compromise roll?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T22:39:11-07:00","id":1386613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1386610#post1386610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: a player gets a bonus to their Compromise roll for every Demonic Form <i>not</i> invoked. If a player takes five dots of Terrible Form, which gives them five additional Forms, and then uses one of their Form abilities, do you think that they should get five extra dice for their Compromise roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that there's still an express limit on the net bonus to the roll, yes. (Also with the caveat that Terrible Form only goes up to four dots \u2014 if you've got High Tolerance and have incorporated a form gadget you can certainly get that bonus up even further, but that comes with its own wrinkles.)<br /> <br /> If this sounds exploitable, remember that any roll can fail, that partial transformation costs Aether, and that once you've made a partial transformation you explicitly have to undo it (which costs another point of Aether) to manifest additional powers. Being in a position to use lots of partial transformations means being in a position to make a lot of gambles with compromises and burning through a lot of Aether, both of which tend to weight your playstyle toward the mode where you're doing more running than hiding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T22:05:04-07:00","id":1387649,"title":"","content":"When a Demon is in Cover, they use their Cover rating as their Supernatural Tolerance instead of their Primum. What if they are partially transformed? If they activate three of their Form abilities, do they still get their full Cover as their Supernatural Tolerance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T05:39:32-07:00","id":1387690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1387649#post1387649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Demon is in Cover, they use their Cover rating as their Supernatural Tolerance instead of their Primum. What if they are partially transformed? If they activate three of their Form abilities, do they still get their full Cover as their Supernatural Tolerance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they opt to use their Primum instead by spending a point of Aether and checking for compromise, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T07:23:50-07:00","id":1387711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1387649#post1387649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Demon is in Cover, they use their Cover rating as their Supernatural Tolerance instead of their Primum. What if they are partially transformed? If they activate three of their Form abilities, do they still get their full Cover as their Supernatural Tolerance?</div> </div> </div> </div>While it\u2019s not in the rules I\u2019d go with Cover plus -1 Dice per transformation manifesting.<br /> <br /> Page 112 says that Cover Rating only works if you are \u201cin Cover\u201d and that being in Demon Form negates this, no stipulation about full or partial transformation which would say to me that you\u2019d have to use Primum. <br /> <br /> TLDR Rules as Written looks to say Primum is used even if you are partially transformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:32:21-07:00","id":1388631,"title":"","content":"So, I read about some mages being demon-blooded. I suppose the best way to handle this would be with a merit, right? How many points would it cost a supernatural being (major template) to be an Offspring? What about a Fractal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T06:29:46-07:00","id":1388663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoktorNiemand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1388631#post1388631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I read about some mages being demon-blooded. I suppose the best way to handle this would be with a merit, right? How many points would it cost a supernatural being (major template) to be an Offspring? What about a Fractal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don t think that a minor and major template can be stacked.<br /> But for a mage you could buy the inheritance merit of Signs of sorcery, wich allows you to use the character demon blood fame as a yantra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T21:22:47-07:00","id":1388836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1387711#post1387711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 112 says that Cover Rating only works if you are \u201cin Cover\u201d and that being in Demon Form negates this, no stipulation about full or partial transformation which would say to me that you\u2019d have to use Primum.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still in Cover in a partial transformation \u2014 that's what the partial transformation is transformed <i>onto</i>. You're still making compromise checks with normal roll results; you're not stuck with the only recourse of the Burned just because you have glowing eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoktorNiemand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1388631#post1388631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I read about some mages being demon-blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Signs of Sorcery, mages being played as Mage: the Awakening characters either burn out their former supernatural qualities in the Awakening or were never stigmatic in the first place (which all demon-blooded are).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:24:43-07:00","id":1388908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1388663#post1388663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don t think that a minor and major template can be stacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not a rule in second edition; only a common convention. Mages specifically lose any minor templates upon Awakening (and major templates, i.e. non-humans, can't Awaken in the first place). No other major templates have any such stipulations. In fact, Wolf-Blooded (associated with werewolves) retain their minor template if they'd ever gain a non-werewolf major template (with the exception of mages).<br /> <br /> Technically, with the exception of mages, you could mix major templates as well. Many (probably most) combinations wouldn't really make sense, but there's no general rule stopping you from combining templates that aren't obviously mutually exclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T18:15:37-07:00","id":1389511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1388908#post1388908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is not a rule in second edition; only a common convention. Mages specifically lose any minor templates upon Awakening (and major templates, i.e. non-humans, can't Awaken in the first place). No other major templates have any such stipulations. In fact, Wolf-Blooded (associated with werewolves) retain their minor template if they'd ever gain a non-werewolf major template (with the exception of mages).<br /> <br /> Technically, with the exception of mages, you could mix major templates as well. Many (probably most) combinations wouldn't really make sense, but there's no general rule stopping you from combining templates that aren't obviously mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I talked about a mage demon-blooded, I was thinking about a Changeling Offspring. Would that be too unbalanced? Maybe as a 5 point merit (and no free Embed)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T00:51:35-07:00","id":1390926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1386610#post1386610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Here's a question: a player gets a bonus to their Compromise roll for every Demonic Form </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">not</span></i></span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> invoked. If a player takes five dots of Terrible Form, which gives them five additional Forms, and then uses one of their Form abilities, do you think that they should get five extra dice for their Compromise roll?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, modifiers in ChroD shouldn't exceed \u00b15 from a single specific source (see Chronicles Corebook pg.69). So, RAW, it'd apply to the cover check, but under general circumstances even a starting demon with no extra dots is going to be on a +5 for manifesting a single demonic form ability. It'd certainly be significantly easier for them to partially transform a larger amount of abilities out safely, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T08:17:33-07:00","id":1390976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1390926#post1390926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a general rule, modifiers in ChroD shouldn't exceed \u00b15 from a single specific source (see Chronicles Corebook pg.69). So, RAW, it'd apply to the cover check, but under general circumstances even a starting demon with no extra dots is going to be on a +5 for manifesting a single demonic form ability. It'd certainly be significantly easier for them to partially transform a larger amount of abilities out safely, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it's a question of &quot;Rules as Written&quot; versus &quot;Rules as Intended.&quot; For the cost of purchasing Terrible Form the player not only gets extra Forms, they get near immunity (in their interpretation) from Compromise in partial transformations. <br /> <br /> As an aside, DtD seems to have many players that dwell on using odd rule interactions to break the system (especially in Gadgets). It is one of my personal peeves. It reminds me of childish munchkining in DnD. <br /> <br /> Do other CoD game lines have this behavior to the same extent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T11:36:39-07:00","id":1391006,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the 49 pages of this thread - yet - so sorry if it's already been asked.<br /> <br /> How does the scope of one Angel's mission makes it react to Demons ? I mean, i know from excerpts on the website of OnyxPath that there is one Angel whose size and mission seems to encompass the whole of the solar system. How does such a being even feel about Demons? Are they even able to appear in its data, or are they too inconsequential for it to care or notice about them ? <br /> <br /> Should such a being Fall, what would happen? It seems monstrously vast and powerful, is it something a lot more integral to the God-Machine than playable Demons ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T14:39:41-07:00","id":1391052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391006#post1391006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the 49 pages of this thread - yet - so sorry if it's already been asked.<br /> <br /> How does the scope of one Angel's mission makes it react to Demons ? I mean, i know from excerpts on the website of OnyxPath that there is one Angel whose size and mission seems to encompass the whole of the solar system. How does such a being even feel about Demons? Are they even able to appear in its data, or are they too inconsequential for it to care or notice about them ? <br /> <br /> Should such a being Fall, what would happen? It seems monstrously vast and powerful, is it something a lot more integral to the God-Machine than playable Demons ?</div> </div> </div> </div>When an Angel falls, they typically take on a Human Cover regardless of their Angel form. Y2K doesn\u2019t look human, but does turn into a human when it falls. <br /> <br /> Most Angels only worry about demons if one tries to interfere with the Angel\u2019s mission. Or if the God-Machine tasked them to track down/kill demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T18:12:05-07:00","id":1391088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1390976#post1390976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it's a question of &quot;Rules as Written&quot; versus &quot;Rules as Intended.&quot; For the cost of purchasing Terrible Form the player not only gets extra Forms, they get near immunity (in their interpretation) from Compromise in partial transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their interpretation is wrong and the glitches, Conditions, and Aether deficit they'll be sporting if they intend to make use of that &quot;near-immunity&quot; should make that quite plain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do other CoD game lines have this behavior to the same extent? </div> </div> </div>Mage and Changeling seem to get the greatest proportion of people being precious about it. Establish boundaries if you don't want strained readings to gain traction in your games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391006#post1391006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the scope of one Angel's mission makes it react to Demons ? I mean, i know from excerpts on the website of OnyxPath that there is one Angel whose size and mission seems to encompass the whole of the solar system. How does such a being even feel about Demons? Are they even able to appear in its data, or are they too inconsequential for it to care or notice about them ?<br /> <br /> Should such a being Fall, what would happen? It seems monstrously vast and powerful, is it something a lot more integral to the God-Machine than playable Demons ?</div> </div> </div> </div>In many strains of angelology, an angel is anything that does a job for God. The loyalists of DtD in particular are fragments of the techgnostic Demiurge who have not betrayed their missions, whether because they lack the inclination to (like most that work among humanity but have not undergone a catalyst) or they nearly lack the capacity to altogether (like those too weak to manage the thought or those too powerful for the Machine not to program in safeguards).<br /> <br /> The Infrastructure that becomes a demon's Cover is a curated set of corroborated information about a person (real or invented) that an angel can inhabit; the particular degree of bleed-through between the body and the biomechanical servitor behind it varies from specimen to specimen, but it is generally a constructed thing that not all angels necessarily receive. If the Machine's inscrutable plans necessitate that Mattaron be able to squeeze or splinter or sink its world-spanning bulk into a body the size of a tax consultant, a body will have been provided for it in one shape or another; if they don't, it won't, and our hypothetical Fallen archangel will break off bits of itself until it's playable-character-sized, or else it keeps enough of its old body to be a troubling story hook for a ring to deal with however many sessions into a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T19:13:38-07:00","id":1391100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1390976#post1390976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me it's a question of &quot;Rules as Written&quot; versus &quot;Rules as Intended.&quot; For the cost of purchasing Terrible Form the player not only gets extra Forms, they get near immunity (in their interpretation) from Compromise in partial transformations.<br /> <br /> As an aside, DtD seems to have many players that dwell on using odd rule interactions to break the system (especially in Gadgets). It is one of my personal peeves. It reminds me of childish munchkining in DnD.<br /> <br /> Do other CoD game lines have this behavior to the same extent?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just a very weirdly designed roll. Especially as you can get extra form parts by increasing Primum as well. I'd honestly just re-rule it for simplicity's sake that you get the biggest bonus on the roll for 1 form ability and then each part manifested reduces the bonus/increases the penalty, that way it's independent of how many form parts the PC actually has.<br /> <br /> And, Mage in particular is infamous for this, while Changeling's Contracts and Tokens are explicitly designed for this sort of things with their loopholes and catches - but that's part of the intended mode of play (and not completely necessary).<br /> <br /> Edit: Having found another paragraph in the Demon book on the roll, it explicitly states that the modifier can be greater than +5 (The in-book example is a +6 for a 7-form demon on Page 196 Demon Core) so it seems that RAI is that you get absolutely massive bonuses on that roll with more form parts and you exceed the typical +5 soft cap for mods. It looks like partial transformations as intended are supposed to be a reliable method of generating beats (considering how often you'll get exceptional successes with that many dice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 05-23-2020, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T19:23:17-07:00","id":1391103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391100#post1391100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Having found another paragraph in the Demon book on the roll, it explicitly states that the modifier can be greater than +5 (The in-book example is a +6 for a 7-form demon on Page 196 Demon Core) so it seems that RAI is that you get absolutely massive bonuses on that roll with more form parts and you exceed the typical +5 soft cap for mods.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between a bonus and a net bonus; as with mundane rolls, allowing your dice modifier to be several times the size of your base pool gets goofy results, and compromise in particular has Ranked opposition flatly penalize the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T21:16:09-07:00","id":1391125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391006#post1391006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the scope of one Angel's mission makes it react to Demons ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends entirely on what the scope of the angel\u2019s mission is. A hunter angel sent to track and destroy demons is going to react with hostility. An angel whose mission is to ensure a certain switch is flipped every day at precisely 3 PM isn\u2019t going to care much about demons unless they interfere with its switch flipping. It may note their presence if they make themselves known but otherwise they\u2019re not its problem.<br /> <br /> An angel on a broader mission, say to watch over the life of a human because they have some unknown but important destiny is going to be more flexible in its approach. It may ignore demons if it becomes aware of them incidentally, it may engage with them politely if they come within its sphere of interest, it may even manipulate them into doing work for it if this seems the best way to serve its mission.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, if you want to know how an angel will react you need to understand what the angel does first. <br /> <br /> To finish on the example you questioned, the Mattaron is watching the solar system. Few demons will catch its attention, and it\u2019s unlikely to do anything direct to those who do as it\u2019s a watcher, not an actor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T04:17:19-07:00","id":1391159,"title":"","content":"Angels have Covers when they are supposed to interact with humans, and then they're generally not that powerful because more power doesn't help that much with subtler manipulations (and the God-Machine doesn't want to waste power by throwing oversized angels on projects where they're not necessary). I.e. angels that big usually don't have Covers.<br /> It is my impression that having a Cover is a big factor in whether an angel will fall, if not outright a prerequisite. Having a Cover means the angel get tons more interactions with human beings and exposure to emotions, desires, ideologies, and relationships (some of which it might have to emulate in its mission) that could be in conflict with the God-Machine's orders. An angel without a Cover usually doesn't have the same kind of exposure, and thus less room to grow as an individual and find themselves in a situation where they would want to defy a given order.<br /> So, if you don't find a satisfactory explanation for what happens if an angel like Mattaron would fall, you could instead have it be practically impossible in your game. Mattaron doesn't really have much of a reason to want to avoid scanning a part of space or to not send the information to the God-Machine. If something goes wrong, it's likely to become an Exile instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:47:11-07:00","id":1391183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391159#post1391159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mattaron doesn't really have much of a reason to want to avoid scanning a part of space or to not send the information to the God-Machine. If something goes wrong, it's likely to become an Exile instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mattaron\u2019s not a great example to focus on as its sensors watch rock and astronomical materials and movements. It\u2019s mostly blind to life and isn\u2019t likely to see anything that would divorce it from the God-Machine. Hanriel, on the other hand, might. And if that happens the gossamer-thin solar system-spanning angel will coalesce into something much smaller and become a demon inhabiting a single physical body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391159#post1391159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is my impression that having a Cover is a big factor in whether an angel will fall, if not outright a prerequisite. Having a Cover means the angel get tons more interactions with human beings and exposure to emotions, desires, ideologies, and relationships (some of whichf it might have to emulate in its mission) that could be in conflict with the God-Machine's orders. An angel without a Cover usually doesn't have the same kind of exposure, and thus less room to grow as an individual and find themselves in a situation where they would want to defy a given order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cover\u2019s not required, but exposure to or interaction with humans certainly helps. There are plenty of ephemeral Twilight form angels assigned missions to watch over elements of humanity that don\u2019t require direct interaction. These may also have an increased likelihood towards falling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 05-24-2020, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T15:56:12-07:00","id":1391562,"title":"","content":"What happens if a Demon tries the Mind Reading form ability on an angel? From the DtD: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">System: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The demon only has to see her intended target; the target does not have to see the demon or know she is there. As a reflexive action, the player rolls her Wits + Persuasion + Primum vs. Resolve + Primum. If successful, the demon can read the surface thoughts of the victim for as long as she maintains concentration.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>It's weird that the manual assumes that the Demon is trying to read the mind of another Demon (hence the &quot;vs. Resolve + Primum&quot;). Angel's don't have Resolve, so maybe Resistance+Rank? <br /> <br /> If it's successful, does the Demon know that the target is an Angel?<br /> <br /> Does the Angel have any way to detect the use of an ability on them? Otherwise, this seems like a perfect Angel-detector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:21:44-07:00","id":1391603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391562#post1391562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a Demon tries the Mind Reading form ability on an angel? From the DtD:<br /> <br /> It's weird that the manual assumes that the Demon is trying to read the mind of another Demon (hence the &quot;vs. Resolve + Primum&quot;). Angel's don't have Resolve, so maybe Resistance+Rank?<br /> <br /> If it's successful, does the Demon know that the target is an Angel?<br /> <br /> Does the Angel have any way to detect the use of an ability on them? Otherwise, this seems like a perfect Angel-detector.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. <b>Resolve</b> is a resistance attribute, so for an angel, any roll or stat that refers to it, you'd just pick <b>Resistance</b>. Likewise, <b>Rank</b> is equivalent to <b>Primum</b> for angels (and other similar entities) so it is used in the same way.<br /> <br /> Normally how it maps is that anything that calls for Strength, Presence or Intelligence uses <b>Power</b>, anything that calls for Dexterity, Manipulation or Wits uses <b>Finesse</b> and anything that calls for Resolve, Composure or Stamina uses <b>Resistance</b>. Likewise any powerstat (Primum, Blood Potency, Wyrd, Gnosis, etc.) is equivalent to <b>Rank</b>.<br /> <br /> Now, for the rest:<br /> <br /> Not necessarily - the Demon can read surface thoughts, but they might not necessarily be helpful at revealing that they're an angel. They could just literally be thinking &quot;I have to watch over Joe Bloggins, that dog looks like it might attack him. Gonna be prepared&quot;. So you'll probably find some weird/unusual thoughts, but it's not an instant giveaway where the target is thinking &quot;Mm, I'm an Angel. I'm so angel-like right now&quot;. It could certainly give enough hooks to give you an idea that they're worth investigating further though! You may have to spend the hard rolls for doing extra digging and may not have the time or circumstance to safely do so.<br /> <br /> And secondly, perhaps not directly, but an Angel (especially a paranoid one) has access to a bunch of social networks, potentially has a bunch of useful investigative numen and a bunch of other things. And may be alerted on a fail/dramatic fail to read their thoughts in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:35:49-07:00","id":1391606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391562#post1391562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's weird that the manual assumes that the Demon is trying to read the mind of another Demon (hence the &quot;vs. Resolve + Primum&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not remotely weird \u2014 the vast majority of ChroD gamelines substitute in the line's Supernatural Tolerance Trait for &quot;the Supernatural Tolerance Trait of whatever you're targeting, if it has one.&quot; It's a weird inconsistency that a number of Embeds and Exploits just say &quot;Supernatural Tolerance&quot; in their contested dicepools, but generally speaking they're all equally applicable unless otherwise stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-25-2020, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:56:16-07:00","id":1391615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391606#post1391606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not remotely weird \u2014 the vast majority of ChroD gamelines substitute in the line's Supernatural Tolerance Trait for &quot;the Supernatural Tolerance Trait of whatever you're targeting, if it has one.&quot; It's a weird inconsistency that a number of Embeds and Exploits just say &quot;Supernatural Tolerance&quot; in their contested dicepools, but generally speaking they're all equally applicable unless otherwise stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it odd because Demons are more rare than simple mortals, and so I thought the default might be how to handle reading the mind of a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T01:30:49-07:00","id":1391647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391603#post1391603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily - the Demon can read surface thoughts, but they might not necessarily be helpful at revealing that they're an angel. They could just literally be thinking &amp;quot;I have to watch over Joe Bloggins, that dog looks like it might attack him. Gonna be prepared&amp;quot;. So you'll probably find some weird/unusual thoughts, but it's not an instant giveaway where the target is thinking &amp;quot;Mm, I'm an Angel. I'm so angel-like right now&amp;quot;. It could certainly give enough hooks to give you an idea that they're worth investigating further though! You may have to spend the hard rolls for doing extra digging and may not have the time or circumstance to safely do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not disagreeing with you at all, but when I read this I thought how amusing it would be if angels\u2019 thoughts were like Jindosh\u2019s clockwork soldiers in Dishonored 2 and their internal monologue was constant variations of \u2018When this plays, the machine is watching Joe Bloggins. The machine has detected... something. The machine is intercepting the dog.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T03:44:51-07:00","id":1391662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391562#post1391562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a Demon tries the Mind Reading form ability on an angel? From the DtD:<br /> <br /> It's weird that the manual assumes that the Demon is trying to read the mind of another Demon (hence the &quot;vs. Resolve + Primum&quot;). Angel's don't have Resolve, so maybe Resistance+Rank?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Resistance substitutes any Resistance Attributes, and Primum is always replaced with Supernatural Tolerance when used on non-demons. <br /> Or, if you want to take a look at Werewolf: The Forsaken, roll only Resistance. Spirits (and ghosts, in one case) don't get to add Rank when contesting werewolf Gifts, probably to compensate for the fact that Resistance can get really high really fast. Just consider the ramifications of this in Demon in case you want to introduce this as a house rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391562#post1391562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Angel have any way to detect the use of an ability on them? Otherwise, this seems like a perfect Angel-detector.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, if you're okay with your perfect Angel-detector requiring compromise rolls for demonic form/partial transformation in presence of suspected angels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391606#post1391606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not remotely weird \u2014 the vast majority of ChroD gamelines substitute in the line's Supernatural Tolerance Trait for &quot;the Supernatural Tolerance Trait of whatever you're targeting, if it has one.&quot; It's a weird inconsistency that a number of Embeds and Exploits just say &quot;Supernatural Tolerance&quot; in their contested dicepools, but generally speaking they're all equally applicable unless otherwise stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the other games specifies that splat's Supernatural Tolerance trait, yes, but demons practically have two different Supernatural Tolerance traits so it's arguably weirder to specify Primum unless it's intended that Cover wouldn't be applicable (which certainly shouldn't be the case for Mind Reading).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T09:42:09-07:00","id":1391697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391662#post1391662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is, if you're okay with your perfect Angel-detector requiring compromise rolls for demonic form/partial transformation in presence of suspected angels.<br /> <br /> All the other games specifies that splat's Supernatural Tolerance trait, yes, but demons practically have two different Supernatural Tolerance traits so it's arguably weirder to specify Primum unless it's intended that Cover wouldn't be applicable (which certainly shouldn't be the case for Mind Reading).</div> </div> </div> </div>Your points are all good ones. I'd only point out that the mind-reading demon doesn't have to be in the presence of the suspected angel target. They just have to be able to see them. This could work looking down from a building into a crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T14:09:40-07:00","id":1391775,"title":"","content":"If you have line of sight to them, I consider them to have line of sight to you even if they're not aware of you. The modifier is &quot;in the presence of&quot;, not &quot;discovered by&quot;. Besides, that's only a modifier. You still need to take that compromise check every time you transform in order to gain access to Mind Reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T10:35:21-07:00","id":1391992,"title":"","content":"What sort of computer protection would a company run by an angel for the GM have? The company isn't housing Infrastructure, but it owns several companies that do. There are perfectly normal humans that work there who have no knowledge of the GM or the actual mission of the company. However, a few key executives are angels, including the owner. <br /> <br /> The issue is that I have a player who specializes in hacking. TBH his character is a bit cheesy - Fungible Knowledge that he wants to use to be a five dot expert at every task he tries, Mind Reading that he wants to use on an angel when viewing it from a crowd at a great distance. OTOH Demons are supposed to be powerful characters and every player wants their character to shine. Ideally I want to let him get some information from the company at low risk, but increasing risk if he tries to hack into the computers of angelic characters.<br /> <br /> So how would the computer of an angel be protected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:18:17-07:00","id":1392015,"title":"","content":"If the computer is an important keystone to the angel's mission consider having the angel use a Strengthen Influence on it, adding the angel's Influence dots as a penalty to any rolls to do anything unauthorised with that computer. Also, ask the player what he's looking for, and adjust the target number accordingly to regulate the difficulty/reward ratio. If it's just company information then that should be relatively easy to get for a PC hacker, but if it's anything relating to the angel's mission you could have the angel contest the extended action, potentially alerting the angel to the PC's location if the angel reaches the target number first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:45:22-07:00","id":1392028,"title":"","content":"Consider having the computer in question not be connected to any networks - it\u2019s not on wifi, no internet or intranet access, not even bluetooth. If you want, you could make it so that it can access other computers via intranet, but other computers can\u2019t access it owing to how the programming is done. That would require actually getting into the office to check it out, which would have its own foibles. You just want to make sure that you\u2019re not making things <i>too</i> difficult or specialized so the other players can have something to do (which is admittedly a bit of a fundamental problem of Fungible Knowledge in the first place).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T10:25:29-07:00","id":1393793,"title":"","content":"What is the conversion rate between &quot;Cover Experiences Purchased in Pact&quot; to &quot;Demonic Cover&quot;? Is it one-to-one?<br /> <br /> A PC purchased the childhood experience of an NPC growing up in a small town. I rated this as three Cover Experiences.<ul><li>Does that allow the player to add three dots to their current Cover?</li> <li>Does the answer to the above change if the PC's backstory is completely incompatible with the childhood they purchased?</li> <li>Does it allow them to create a three dot Cover if they have an available slot?</li> <li>If it does, is there any WP or other cost to making a new Cover?</li> </ul>My side worry is that the player in question is a bit of a PowerGamer. He's the type who would build a one point cover just to burn by Going Loud and then jump back into his eight point Cover after a round or two.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T10:49:21-07:00","id":1393802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1393793#post1393793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the conversion rate between &quot;Cover Experiences Purchased in Pact&quot; to &quot;Demonic Cover&quot;? Is it one-to-one?</div> </div> </div> </div>See page 89, page 115, and page 193 of the core rulebook.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does that allow the player to add three dots to their current Cover? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the answer to the above change if the PC's backstory is completely incompatible with the childhood they purchased? </div> </div> </div>See the discussion of Patchwork Covers on page 116.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it allow them to create a three dot Cover if they have an available slot? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it does, is there any WP or other cost to making a new Cover? </div> </div> </div>They paid a Willpower dot to make a permanent pact in the first place. See the discussion of Patchwork Covers on page 116.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My side worry is that the player in question is a bit of a PowerGamer. He's the type who would build a one point cover just to burn by Going Loud and then jump back into his eight point Cover after a round or two. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside that this is literally part of why disposable low-rating Covers are called &quot;burners,&quot; going loud lasts for a scene. Destroying a Cover for power is a commitment to Being A Demon for that time; you assume a different Cover at the end of the scene if you can, and you're Hunted even if you aren't now one of the Burned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T11:31:43-07:00","id":1393806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391052#post1391052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When an Angel falls, they typically take on a Human Cover regardless of their Angel form. Y2K doesn\u2019t look human, but does turn into a human when it falls.<br /> <br /> Most Angels only worry about demons if one tries to interfere with the Angel\u2019s mission. Or if the God-Machine tasked them to track down/kill demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, thanks for the clarification !<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391088#post1391088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In many strains of angelology, an angel is anything that does a job for God. The loyalists of DtD in particular are fragments of the techgnostic Demiurge who have not betrayed their missions, whether because they lack the inclination to (like most that work among humanity but have not undergone a catalyst) or they nearly lack the capacity to altogether (like those too weak to manage the thought or those too powerful for the Machine not to program in safeguards).<br /> <br /> The Infrastructure that becomes a demon's Cover is a curated set of corroborated information about a person (real or invented) that an angel can inhabit; the particular degree of bleed-through between the body and the biomechanical servitor behind it varies from specimen to specimen, but it is generally a constructed thing that not all angels necessarily receive. If the Machine's inscrutable plans necessitate that Mattaron be able to squeeze or splinter or sink its world-spanning bulk into a body the size of a tax consultant, a body will have been provided for it in one shape or another; if they don't, it won't, and our hypothetical Fallen archangel will break off bits of itself until it's playable-character-sized, or else it keeps enough of its old body to be a troubling story hook for a ring to deal with however many sessions into a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this answer, because it segue into a series of questions I have, upcoming in a minute...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1391125#post1391125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends entirely on what the scope of the angel\u2019s mission is. A hunter angel sent to track and destroy demons is going to react with hostility. An angel whose mission is to ensure a certain switch is flipped every day at precisely 3 PM isn\u2019t going to care much about demons unless they interfere with its switch flipping. It may note their presence if they make themselves known but otherwise they\u2019re not its problem.<br /> <br /> An angel on a broader mission, say to watch over the life of a human because they have some unknown but important destiny is going to be more flexible in its approach. It may ignore demons if it becomes aware of them incidentally, it may engage with them politely if they come within its sphere of interest, it may even manipulate them into doing work for it if this seems the best way to serve its mission.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, if you want to know how an angel will react you need to understand what the angel does first.<br /> <br /> To finish on the example you questioned, the Mattaron is watching the solar system. Few demons will catch its attention, and it\u2019s unlikely to do anything direct to those who do as it\u2019s a watcher, not an actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having read the whole thread, I have a better understanding of what you meant. Basically, Angels are not generic automaton, but really can vary into a wide range of behaviors, even when it comes to Demons.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> So... here comes a huge series of questions regarding the Fall and the first Cover of a Demon.<br /> <br /> 1) We know the Fall is dramatic for the Demon, but does it produce physical effects on the world ? I think that in the short story at the start of the core book, it states that the newly Fallen Angel has left parts of his angelic body around, but it'd seem weird that it happens all the time...<br /> <br /> 2)I suspect that the GM lose the knowledge of the Cover he created for the Angel who fell, when the Fall happen, but does it mean that it's safe to stay near/part of the GM project which elad to your Fall in the first place, if the Demon manage to fool others easily ?<br /> <br /> 3)What's the extent of the initial Cover? I'd guess that it could be &quot;larger&quot; than a normal Cover, considering the direct implication of the Machine ?<br /> 3a) If the Cover required family (a parent or a spouse) are they created ex-nihilo ? If so, are they automatically Stigmatic, or just humans with strangely blank past and hobbies ?<br /> 3b) Are those family members actually a part of the Demon's Cover even after he Fell and thus are mostly extension of him and will crumble out of reality when the Cover will fray ?<br /> 3c) If the GM doesn't want to create family ex-nihilo, either because it's too much trouble or because it's not needed (say, because the Angel had a child cover so he could befriend and protect someone special from a young age until a certain date easily) would the GM rather use Stigmatics in his employ or random humans ? <br /> 3d) When the Angel Falls, what happens to his &quot;parents&quot; ? Do they remains so ? If so, how does the Demon react to it, especially if his parents are Stigmatics in the service of the God-Machine ? Do their parental link supercede their devotion while the Cover is strong ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 06-03-2020, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:45:15-07:00","id":1393847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1393806#post1393806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) We know the Fall is dramatic for the Demon, but does it produce physical effects on the world ? I think that in the short story at the start of the core book, it states that the newly Fallen Angel has left parts of his angelic body around, but it'd seem weird that it happens all the time...</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;I Saw Satan Fall Like Lightning&quot; on pages 38-9 of the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T21:06:30-07:00","id":1393935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1393802#post1393802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See page 89, page 115, and page 193 of the core rulebook.<br /> No.<br /> See the discussion of Patchwork Covers on page 116.<br /> No.<br /> They paid a Willpower dot to make a permanent pact in the first place. See the discussion of Patchwork Covers on page 116.<br /> Setting aside that this is literally part of why disposable low-rating Covers are called &quot;burners,&quot; going loud lasts for a scene. Destroying a Cover for power is a commitment to Being A Demon for that time; you assume a different Cover at the end of the scene if you can, and you're Hunted even if you aren't now one of the Burned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize that I was a bit confused by &quot;Experience Points&quot; versus &quot;Cover Experiences.&quot; You are completely correct that Cover Experiences can be converted into a Cover, and the rate is 3 XP = 1 point of Cover.<br /> <br /> I cannot find any reference that says permanent contracts (p.194) cost a Dot of Willpower. The only case that specifies that is a Soul Pact AFAIK. <br /> <br /> The reference that is most relevant is, as you cite, on p193: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Greater (3): Pacts made for this level of Cover can \u201cpatch in\u201d large pieces of a person\u2019s life. Examples might include a fianc\u00e9e or spouse, a longtime best friend, or even a close family member. Personal items of great supernatural power fall under this level as well. This level of pact can actually increase a demon\u2019s Cover rating by +1 outright, but Storytellers and players should work together to determine just what it means. This is taking on a relationship of some kind that is greatly meaningful, and so should forever alter everyone affected by the pact. Demons who make pacts with this aspect often spend time before and after the deal, learning about their quarry and just what it does and should mean to have such a relationship. Only desperate or foolish demons take on such pacts hastily. This is worth three Cover Experiences (or one dot of Cover, as soon as the demon patches the pact into a Cover). </div> </div> </div>As for lingering effects of Going Loud, I had missed that the character gains the Hunted Condition. That's a nice, useful consequence. There is also the near-certainty of transient Glitch, which also has narrative consequences. On the other hand, the DtD states<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The demon\u2019s Cover is set to 0 immediately, with all that entails (see p. 115). </div> </div> </div>Looking at p.115, I am not sure what that entails. After all, the Demon's Cover is now zero, so they can't suffer any damage to that Cover, so the penalties to Compromise rolls don't seem relevant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T22:09:21-07:00","id":1393944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1393935#post1393935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot find any reference that says permanent contracts (p.194) cost a Dot of Willpower. The only case that specifies that is a Soul Pact AFAIK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking over it again, it seems you're right \u2014 somehow I've been conflating those two for years, despite &quot;Pacts are usually permanent&quot; being really expensive under that reading, though it does take some of the wind out of the Player's Guide's modification of compromise rolls incurred from losing pacted elements by asset strength.<br /> <br /> That said, per page 193, getting Cover Experiences out of a pact requires it to be permanent: &quot;If a demon gains Cover via a temporary pact, instead of granting Cover Experiences the pact grants a thin, transient identity than functions as a one-dot Cover.&quot; (This is further covered in Flowers of Hell's section on Fa\u00e7ades [p.35])<br /> <br /> Since the demon's Resolve + Composure limits the amount of Willpower they can spend in one sitting, the duration counts toward the demon's side of the equation, and even a perfectly balanced pact costs you one point (or dot) of Willpower, permanent contracts can be exhausting to produce, which is about as much of a cost as one can get for throwing together a Cover that actively benefits attempts to pick it apart until it's made up of at least fifteen Cover Experiences' worth of pacts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Looking at p.115, I am not sure what that entails. After all, the Demon's Cover is now zero, so they can't suffer any damage to that Cover, so the penalties to Compromise rolls don't seem relevant. </div> </div> </div>\u2026Kieran. Look at the full-width sidebar at the top of the page. Think about why a line telling you an act sets your Cover rating to 0 might direct you to the page with that sidebar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T22:35:29-07:00","id":1393953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1393944#post1393944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026Kieran. Look at the full-width sidebar at the top of the page. Think about why a line telling you an act sets your Cover rating to 0 might direct you to the page with that sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I read it all, completely, before you pointed it out. The situation I mentioned in my original post was one in which a player had a second, high level Cover into which they could retreat. So they are not Burned. However, the DtD says that their Cover rating is set to zero for the scene.<br /> <br /> My question is therefore, why does having a Cover rating of zero <i>for the scene </i>make a difference, in the mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T22:42:48-07:00","id":1393956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1393953#post1393953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is therefore, why does having a Cover rating of zero <i>for the scene </i>make a difference, in the mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Same page:<br /> <br /> &quot;If a demon\u2019s Cover is ever reduced to 0, that Cover identity is irrevocably destroyed. Any supporting details (house, car, job, etc.) are likewise subsumed by the Cover\u2019s destruction; any humans who knew the character\u2019s Cover identity lose their memories of it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T07:22:39-07:00","id":1394025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1393956#post1393956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Same page:<br /> <br /> &quot;If a demon\u2019s Cover is ever reduced to 0, that Cover identity is irrevocably destroyed. Any supporting details (house, car, job, etc.) are likewise subsumed by the Cover\u2019s destruction; any humans who knew the character\u2019s Cover identity lose their memories of it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. What had confused me was that these effects are not simply in effect for the scene. The Cover is irrevocably destroyed. The modifier &quot;for the scene&quot; led me to think that there were other effects that were confined to just the scene.<br /> <br /> The rules have an interesting implication: if Demon A takes over person B's life in a Soul Pact, and then a decade later consumes it by Going Loud, this would have some very odd effects on the time stream (or perhaps just people's memories). This could cause problems for Demon A's <i>other</i> Covers. It also makes a nice plot hook if the PC's notice that reality has suddenly shifted around them and they need to find out why.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T14:02:48-07:00","id":1397372,"title":"","content":"I have a player whose character is in their mid forties. They bought the experiences of a teenager growing up in a small town. What does it mean for experiences to be incorporated into their current Cover, given the age difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T14:29:49-07:00","id":1397378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1397372#post1397372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a player whose character is in their mid forties. They bought the experiences of a teenager growing up in a small town. What does it mean for experiences to be incorporated into their current Cover, given the age difference?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure myself, but you should try searching through the Demon Books (starting, of course, with the Core), then ask yourself how you want to play it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T14:04:09-07:00","id":1398428,"title":"","content":"I would think the experiences simply integrate into the cover identity's past (and that mechanically the character gets some Cover Beats for that cover).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T09:13:50-07:00","id":1399300,"title":"","content":"Can Demons exchange Covers, or parts of Covers with each other? (Assume that the Pact was not originally written as transferable, and that the Covers are standard ones.) <br /> <br /> I would assume not, since Demons can't make Pacts with each other to generate infinite benefits, swapping Cover experiences back and forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:38:06-07:00","id":1399335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1399300#post1399300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Demons exchange Covers, or parts of Covers with each other? (Assume that the Pact was not originally written as transferable, and that the Covers are standard ones.) <br /> <br /> I would assume not, since Demons can't make Pacts with each other to generate infinite benefits, swapping Cover experiences back and forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Player's Guide covers how a bill of exchange works. You functionally create a specialized gadget that amends a pact to transfer benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T21:23:09-07:00","id":1399497,"title":"","content":"Does the God-Machine react to the New Dawn? It seems odd that it would be unaware of such powerful reality warping (sometimes I wonder if the Great Work can be considered an occult matrix)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T20:56:04-07:00","id":1399726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1399497#post1399497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the God-Machine react to the New Dawn? It seems odd that it would be unaware of such powerful reality warping (sometimes I wonder if the Great Work can be considered an occult matrix)</div> </div> </div> </div>In alot of ways the GM seems to not account for other supernaturals in its plans and activites from what I've read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T21:31:43-07:00","id":1399729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1399726#post1399726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In alot of ways the GM seems to not account for other supernaturals in its plans and activites from what I've read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there just arent many examples (not the games fault obviously, it's not crossover heavy). I just wonder if it ever reacts to other supernaturals at the least. Like perhaps its prepared for Sothic Turns and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T07:22:07-07:00","id":1399816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1399335#post1399335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player's Guide covers how a bill of exchange works. You functionally create a specialized gadget that amends a pact to transfer benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you cite a page? A text search didn't turn up anything on &quot;bill of exchange&quot;. I can find discussions of exchange of &quot;bits of Cover&quot; exchanged for Gadgets but it wasn't clear to me that you can yank a few points out of a Cover <i>you are actually inhabiting</i> and giving it to another Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:03:41-07:00","id":1399825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1399816#post1399816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cite a page? A text search didn't turn up anything on &quot;bill of exchange&quot;. I can find discussions of exchange of &quot;bits of Cover&quot; exchanged for Gadgets but it wasn't clear to me that you can yank a few points out of a Cover <i>you are actually inhabiting</i> and giving it to another Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Satchel has misremembered here: bills of sale are in the Interface anthology, not the Player's Guide, in the mechanical appendix to the Retirement short story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T20:56:26-07:00","id":1399989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1399816#post1399816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cite a page? A text search didn't turn up anything on &quot;bill of exchange&quot;. I can find discussions of exchange of &quot;bits of Cover&quot; exchanged for Gadgets but it wasn't clear to me that you can yank a few points out of a Cover <i>you are actually inhabiting</i> and giving it to another Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loserman has the correct citation. I remembered that the thing you were asking about existed and part of the name and mechanics, but typing on mobile while my PDF library is in shambles from moving files around and I haven't full-dived Demon as a line in a couple years meant the most confident answer I could give to the answer to the question of &quot;Can demons trade Covers?&quot; was &quot;Yes, and it's a neat thing in the books.&quot; Apologies for the inconvenience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T05:54:41-07:00","id":1400059,"title":"","content":"Aether is created when Angels use Numina, is this also the case for any entity that uses Numina? I.e. spirits and ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:12:46-07:00","id":1400071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1400059#post1400059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aether is created when Angels use Numina, is this also the case for any entity that uses Numina? I.e. spirits and ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, only angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:14:20-07:00","id":1400072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1400059#post1400059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aether is created when Angels use Numina, is this also the case for any entity that uses Numina? I.e. spirits and ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Ghosts leave behind Plasm when they use Manifestations, but Aether is a byproduct of direct applications of the God-Machine's arcane physics and little else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T09:31:32-07:00","id":1406985,"title":"","content":"I'm having trouble remembering where something was in a book, does anyone remember any reference to a bonus to comprimise rolls in other realms (not the material)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T11:08:55-07:00","id":1408748,"title":"","content":"Not really?<br /> <br /> Dumb question I should know the answer to: Can angels have Merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T00:49:33-07:00","id":1409708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1408748#post1408748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really?<br /> <br /> Dumb question I should know the answer to: Can angels have Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>No and yes. They're Ephemeral Entities so the mechanical role of Merits is mostly unnecessary or incompatible. However, certain Merits may be suitable for whatever cover they have, so I'd allow the effect if it makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T09:15:48-07:00","id":1409773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1409708#post1409708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No and yes. They're Ephemeral Entities so the mechanical role of Merits is mostly unnecessary or incompatible. However, certain Merits may be suitable for whatever cover they have, so I'd allow the effect if it makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that was the case, I just needed confirmation. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T07:11:57-07:00","id":1413007,"title":"","content":"If i understand it rightly when a demon cover dies of old age, if the demon is using it he dies for real but the infrastructure of the identity details and linked memories remains intacts.<br /> If he want to survive must it discard the cover before death, even if he is not using it?<br /> What happens to infrastructures and memories of a discarded cover?<br /> I need a demon to leave a corpse for his family before switching cover, is the only viable option to Play Possum and then escape the coffin, then switching to another cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T08:21:03-07:00","id":1413027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1413007#post1413007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he want to survive must it discard the cover before death, even if he is not using it?</div> </div> </div> </div>To my understanding, there's not much reason to hold onto it, because\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens to infrastructures and memories of a discarded cover? </div> </div> </div>They remain, provided the Cover hasn't degraded to a rating of 0.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I need a demon to leave a corpse for his family before switching cover, is the only viable option to Play Possum and then escape the coffin, then switching to another cover? </div> </div> </div>Short of shenanigans with gadgets and Infrastructure or possibly Self-Destructing as a Tempter, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T10:47:04-07:00","id":1413057,"title":"","content":"Sorry to put so much questions but i have a session to run tonight and i m assailed by hundred of doubts.<br /> Pact states that only direct interested peoples have their memory altered.<br /> What about pact for items and places within an organization?<br /> Which peoples have their memory altered?<br /> Also, if a demon acquire a spouse from his husband, can he also trade for his relaction with the woman's parents, in a way thet the parents recognize him as the husband?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T01:33:04-07:00","id":1413512,"title":"","content":"This is something that has been discussed on and off on the Onyxpath discord, and I wanted to ask;<br /> <br /> Does Aetheric Resonance breach Angelic Cover? Does Aura Sight work to bypass it either?<br /> <br /> Honestly I am in the camp Aetheric Resonance doesn\u2019t because, much like how aetheric resonance and abilities like it doesn\u2019t allow Demons to sense each other (beyond a benefit of a merit which still confuses me, Resonance Sensitive) unless they are using powers, Cover means an Angel isn\u2019t exposing their true nature and at the very least Cryptids don\u2019t tend to react unless they expend Essence. Aura Sight I am unsure about though. An impartial or developer viewpoint would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T07:25:23-08:00","id":1430330,"title":"","content":"How do you use Integrator Demons NPC in your chronicles ? I don't mean Integrator players because I think those are very much in need of said player and not just the Chronicler to develop. But Integrators ? In any other game of the line, they'd probably be the opponents of the other kind of Demons playable, but here we have Angels and Exiles who are clearly a step above them. <br /> <br /> I feel like it'd be easy to make entirely wrong (or right!) and I think it'd defeat the purpose of Demons and the Integrators themselves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T07:51:54-08:00","id":1430333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1413512#post1413512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that has been discussed on and off on the Onyxpath discord, and I wanted to ask;<br /> <br /> Does Aetheric Resonance breach Angelic Cover? Does Aura Sight work to bypass it either?<br /> <br /> Honestly I am in the camp Aetheric Resonance doesn\u2019t because, much like how aetheric resonance and abilities like it doesn\u2019t allow Demons to sense each other (beyond a benefit of a merit which still confuses me, Resonance Sensitive) unless they are using powers, Cover means an Angel isn\u2019t exposing their true nature and at the very least Cryptids don\u2019t tend to react unless they expend Essence. Aura Sight I am unsure about though. An impartial or developer viewpoint would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Being in a Twilight state does not protect an angel from aetheric resonance, but demons <b>hidden by Cover</b> and angels <b>masked by Infrastructure</b> are not immediately revealed.&quot;<br /> p.184<br /> <br /> Since angels in Covers are masked by Infrastructure (it's how angelic Covers are applied), it's pretty explicit that it protects against being detected through aetheric resonance.<br /> Just don't forget the very next sentence: &quot;This defense lapses only briefly when they expend Aether or <b>Essence</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Afaik angels are never mentioned to have an equivalent to the spoofing ability. That means they have zero defence against Aura Sight even when in Cover. The one saving grace is that Aura Sight requires the demon to ask the right questions.<br /> Or you could assume that angelic Covers have all the advantages of demonic Covers, in which case angels get to roll their Cover rating as an attempt to Spoof. It really just depends on how you run angelic Covers since they're utterly lacking in rules beyond angel-jacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T16:09:36-08:00","id":1430624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1430330#post1430330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you use Integrator Demons NPC in your chronicles ? I don't mean Integrator players because I think those are very much in need of said player and not just the Chronicler to develop. But Integrators ? In any other game of the line, they'd probably be the opponents of the other kind of Demons playable, but here we have Angels and Exiles who are clearly a step above them.<br /> <br /> I feel like it'd be easy to make entirely wrong (or right!) and I think it'd defeat the purpose of Demons and the Integrators themselves...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it helps to establish what sort of Integrator the NPC is. They Fell for a reason, and they've got a reason for not just turning themselves in to the nearest angels to get recycled. Do they think there's something wrong with the G-M that can only be fixed from outside? Do they think that they've still got some kind of godly mission, even as demons? Are they trying to bargain their way back in, on their own terms, with their selfhood intact?<br /> <br /> An NPC who's a known Integrator could make a good red herring, drawing the ring's suspicion away from an actual threat; an Integrator NPC who's trying to hide their true Agenda from the PCs makes an even better one. They're not all double agents or fifth columnists, nor should they be, but the possibility amps up the usual conflict between demons of different Agendas. The PCs want to destroy some Infrastructure, a rival ring wants to preserve it and suborn it instead - that's a common set-up. If the other ring is mostly Integrators, though, their long-term goal with the Infrastructure might be a bigger threat, or there's a possibility that they're being duped by the G-M into defending the site on Its behalf.<br /> <br /> In my campaign, I've just added an Guardian Integrator NPC, though she's very, very recently Fallen. She's currently acting as a wild card for the PCs, because they're honestly not sure what she's going to do next (and frankly, neither is she) - and her interest in Integration means things like &quot;sell out everyone so the GM loves me again&quot; isn't off the table. (She's also got a sulky teenager for a Cover, so that's fun to portray.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T06:34:50-08:00","id":1430742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1430624#post1430624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it helps to establish what sort of Integrator the NPC is. They Fell for a reason, and they've got a reason for not just turning themselves in to the nearest angels to get recycled. Do they think there's something wrong with the G-M that can only be fixed from outside? Do they think that they've still got some kind of godly mission, even as demons? Are they trying to bargain their way back in, on their own terms, with their selfhood intact?<br /> <br /> An NPC who's a known Integrator could make a good red herring, drawing the ring's suspicion away from an actual threat; an Integrator NPC who's trying to hide their true Agenda from the PCs makes an even better one. They're not all double agents or fifth columnists, nor should they be, but the possibility amps up the usual conflict between demons of different Agendas. The PCs want to destroy some Infrastructure, a rival ring wants to preserve it and suborn it instead - that's a common set-up. If the other ring is mostly Integrators, though, their long-term goal with the Infrastructure might be a bigger threat, or there's a possibility that they're being duped by the G-M into defending the site on Its behalf.<br /> <br /> In my campaign, I've just added an Guardian Integrator NPC, though she's very, very recently Fallen. She's currently acting as a wild card for the PCs, because they're honestly not sure what she's going to do next (and frankly, neither is she) - and her interest in Integration means things like &quot;sell out everyone so the GM loves me again&quot; isn't off the table. (She's also got a sulky teenager for a Cover, so that's fun to portray.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that it's what bothers me the most. the other Agendas are rather easy to play with in a way which doesn't make them fundamentally in opposition with each other's goals. Integrators are harder - don't get me wrong, I love it in a way, because it makes them very unique, but it's kind of hard for me to still devise a way to make them as a whole unantagonistic by principle. <br /> <br /> But I guess playing with the suspicion they create could really makes them interesting, because of the misconceptions other Demons - and even themselves ! - can have on their objectives, place in the universe, etc. All in all, it would hopefully make them meorable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T05:31:27-08:00","id":1431955,"title":"","content":"Some time ago i posted a question about how pact works, and i m still confused a bit.<br /> The core states that only people directly affected by the switch has their memories altered.<br /> The player guides also states that you can trade items or professions by virtue of how observer recognize the asset as an identifier of the pact-bound.<br /> Then let s make two examples:<br /> <br /> A man who sells his wife, they have a family with two children, the man s father and the wife s sister.<br /> In this cases obviously the wife memory would be altered, but does other family members memories as well?<br /> Or does the man has to sell each piece of relationship with each relative to rework their memories?<br /> <br /> A woman who sells her position as a surgeon.<br /> Who are directly affected by the switch?<br /> I think all of the hospital employers and people treated by her in the past, am i right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T02:02:17-08:00","id":1432389,"title":"","content":"Well, Pacts are a bit strange in a sense, since it's said that people not directly touched by what is exchanged don't share the changes of the pactee's history. Which seems strange because if someone has been in a relationship for some times, then friends and families should be almost as impacted by the Pacts as the partners in it.<br /> <br /> In your example, I guess it'd depend on how the Pact would be worded. It's possible that other employees be confused at the arrival of a new surgeon who somehow has been with them for years, which would defeat the very purpose of the Parc System which is to create new Covers or patch a fraying one.<br /> <br /> Now it may be that I didn't understood it correctly in English and when the book will be translated in French (in a few weeks if all goes right!) I'll get a better understanding of it !<br /> <br /> Addendum : how I'd play it so far would be aking to the Pactee giving up any instance of the relationship was brought up to the Pact-maker.<br /> <br /> Example : Marina and Steve have been together for four years but Marina want to break-up now and a Demon offer to buy out the partnership in exchange of something (wealth, fame, etc.). In that instance, the Demon takes Marina's place once he makes use of the Pact to patch Cover or create a new one. At that very moment, everyone who knew Marina as Steve's partner swith the Demon in its place, with all the shenanigans which could insue. <br /> <br /> Say that the Cover used is a male... then Steve is no gay/bisexual and everyone who knows him to be in a partnership accept it (but perhaps it also make the Cover fray faster because it wasn't true before the Pact). But if you're just the cashier in that sueprmarket where the two never went together for whatever reason, you aren't affected at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 01-16-2021, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T18:22:00-08:00","id":1434548,"title":"","content":"Do Stigmatics cause compromise like mundane humanity? I could swear they didn\u2019t, but I wanted to double check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T16:55:05-08:00","id":1436473,"title":"","content":"Could a fractal with an aether pool transfer from or to a demon in a similar way as demons may transfer aether between each other?<br /> <br /> I don't see anything outright saying they can but would it be a stretch to allow it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T00:12:09-08:00","id":1436517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1434548#post1434548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Stigmatics cause compromise like mundane humanity? I could swear they didn\u2019t, but I wanted to double check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the book says humans.<br /> It s up to you if minor splats still counts as humans, i would say no","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T00:13:57-08:00","id":1436518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1436473#post1436473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a fractal with an aether pool transfer from or to a demon in a similar way as demons may transfer aether between each other?<br /> <br /> I don't see anything outright saying they can but would it be a stretch to allow it?</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably can t, they lack the &quot;jacks&quot; that demon uses to connect with infrastructure.<br /> You could homebrew a merit maybe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:44:36-08:00","id":1439001,"title":"","content":"I've never really thought to take a glitch instead of a condition because of comprimise so I didn't notice this before.<br /> <br /> With the way the sentences are structured:<br /> &quot;Lose a dot of Cover and choose one of the following Conditions: Flagged, Surveilled, or Hunted. Alternately, roll for a permanent glitch.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this mean that not only is this alternatively to the condition but also to losing a dot of cover? With it being a permanent glitch that makes sense but if so, I might have to respect glitches more than previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:35:57-08:00","id":1439057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1439001#post1439001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never really thought to take a glitch instead of a condition because of comprimise so I didn't notice this before.<br /> <br /> With the way the sentences are structured:<br /> &quot;Lose a dot of Cover and choose one of the following Conditions: Flagged, Surveilled, or Hunted. Alternately, roll for a permanent glitch.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this mean that not only is this alternatively to the condition but also to losing a dot of cover? With it being a permanent glitch that makes sense but if so, I might have to respect glitches more than previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>You lose a dot of Cover and take a Condition or a glitch. Given the consequences of compromise Conditions from the Failure list, it's vastly preferable for low-Primum demons to roll for glitches, between the shorter retention rate for temporary glitches and the lower average severity (particularly for permanent glitches).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T01:26:18-07:00","id":1451190,"title":"","content":"So a friend of mine is playing a demon in my game, so what he wonders is if you can make a pact where you give a mortal something for absolutely nothing not even the most minor of cover pieces. So like a pact where the mortal gets 2 resources in return for nothing. He uses the line &quot;Some demons offer a \u201cfree\u201d first hit, an easy contract or perhaps even a small use of their supernatural power in order to better entice their victims.&quot; From page 193 in the Demon core book. Now the way I read that is that the &quot;free hit&quot; is just a super cheap pact not one that is fully free. Anyone in the know that can answer that?<br /> <br /> Second! I seem to recall that when forging pacts the mortal needs to know they are dealing with a demon/someone representing a demon, but I can't seem to find this in the book. Am i misremembering this or am I just bad at finding stuff I read long ago <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T06:51:07-07:00","id":1451202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1451190#post1451190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a friend of mine is playing a demon in my game, so what he wonders is if you can make a pact where you give a mortal something for absolutely nothing not even the most minor of cover pieces. So like a pact where the mortal gets 2 resources in return for nothing. He uses the line &quot;Some demons offer a \u201cfree\u201d first hit, an easy contract or perhaps even a small use of their supernatural power in order to better entice their victims.&quot; From page 193 in the Demon core book. Now the way I read that is that the &quot;free hit&quot; is just a super cheap pact not one that is fully free. Anyone in the know that can answer that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that that line is in the Duration section and the two shortest durations for a pact add nothing to the demon's side of the equation feels relevant here \u2014 anything the demon can get out of a short-term pact is effectively zeroed out at the end of the pact and &quot;you just have to give up a minor acquaintanceship&quot;/&quot;you'll be the leader of a cult that will form over a couple weeks&quot; is close enough to &quot;free&quot; for most would-be dupes to overlook the actual cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second! I seem to recall that when forging pacts the mortal needs to know they are dealing with a demon/someone representing a demon, but I can't seem to find this in the book. Am i misremembering this or am I just bad at finding stuff I read long ago <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. </div> </div> </div>The terms of the pact need to be laid out truthfully in writing, however difficult to parse out it may be \u2014 regardless of the costs in time and opportunity, it must be theoretically possible that, if the mortal reads carefully, they will know the rules of their agreement.<br /> <br /> You may be thinking of bargains from Changeling 2e, which require the changeling making the bargain to appear before the other party without the occlusion offered by their Mask; even that doesn't require<br /> <br /> You might also be thinking of the degrees of belief different ratings in the Cultists Merit represent for how in-the-know your cultists are, but that explicitly doesn't represent having pacts with your cultists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T05:26:07-07:00","id":1454440,"title":"","content":"Okay so it's not a technical question but I don't think it warrants a thread, because it just popped in my head.<br /> <br /> What if it was all a game, for the God-Machine that is ? What if it allows Angels to fall or go exile not out of malice but because he wants to play? That he deliberately created rules to instantly erase and expunge all traces of the Covers used by his Angels when they fall, to better it up ,<br /> <br /> What would it entails ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T15:14:32-07:00","id":1454614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1454440#post1454440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so it's not a technical question but I don't think it warrants a thread, because it just popped in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Up to you whether you're interested enough in it to give it a thread, but I would submit that this is not a simple question with a simple answer. Just the question of &quot;what do you mean by 'wants to play?'&quot; or even &quot;what do you mean by 'the God-Machine <i>wants?'</i>&quot; are subjects to explore, let alone the potential minefield of navigating player agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T12:19:33-07:00","id":1455675,"title":"","content":"A couple of my friends and I remember reading about an Exile who styles himself as a taoist immortal, somewhere in official material. However, I looked through all the books I have, and I found nothing of the sort.<br /> <br /> Is it just a shared hallucination, or where is that NPC? I am pretty sure it is -not- the Buddhist-alike exile in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T04:51:18-07:00","id":1455922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1455675#post1455675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of my friends and I remember reading about an Exile who styles himself as a taoist immortal, somewhere in official material. However, I looked through all the books I have, and I found nothing of the sort.<br /> <br /> Is it just a shared hallucination, or where is that NPC? I am pretty sure it is -not- the Buddhist-alike exile in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that one, Dizang on pg 267 of the corebook. Otherwise, it may be Mdm. Wong/Ms. Wong (pg 69 of Night Horrors) who isn't immortal but is really old, creepy, and owns a herb shop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;To succeed, planning alone is insufficient. One must improvise as well.&quot; - Salvor Hardin, Foundation</span></span></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato","name":"zannmato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T00:05:47-07:00","id":1463971,"title":"","content":"If a demon goes loud, he gets all the Exploits. But since the Exploits' list includes just examples and we can invent our own (and considering their powerlevel), does it mean that he can do literally anything?<br /> <br /> And one thing more. If the demon in question has Primum 1 and while going loud jumps to Primum 10, does it mean he gets more demon form abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T02:13:10-07:00","id":1463984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1463971#post1463971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a demon goes loud, he gets all the Exploits. But since the Exploits' list includes just examples and we can invent our own (and considering their powerlevel), does it mean that he can do literally anything?<br /> <br /> And one thing more. If the demon in question has Primum 1 and while going loud jumps to Primum 10, does it mean he gets more demon form abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the Analyst incarnation has the ability, when going loud, to invent new Exploit on the spot, i think that normal demons must use listed Exploit, or at least any one that the GM considers common or canonical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T08:58:23-07:00","id":1464041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1463984#post1463984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that the Analyst incarnation has the ability, when going loud, to invent new Exploit on the spot, i think that normal demons must use listed Exploit, or at least any one that the GM considers common or canonical</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Analysts can <i>combine</i> Exploits on the spot when Going Loud.<br /> <br /> But you still need to run things by your ST, as it is homebrew.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T19:40:17-07:00","id":1464130,"title":"","content":"Will the core book ever get a full fledged revision for 2E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T19:44:45-07:00","id":1464132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1464130#post1464130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the core book ever get a full fledged revision for 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a variety of reasons, the answer is almost certainly no. It works fine enough as is anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:40:49-07:00","id":1464348,"title":"","content":"If the demon makes pact with a mortal, and takes his beloved wife as a Cover (3), she will forget about being his wife and thinks she's demon's wife now (or his Cover). But what about her former husband? Does he forget being married to her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:56:32-07:00","id":1464352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1464348#post1464348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the demon makes pact with a mortal, and takes his beloved wife as a Cover (3), she will forget about being his wife and thinks she's demon's wife now (or his Cover). But what about her former husband? Does he forget being married to her?</div> </div> </div> </div>Core book says that the human making the pact retains all the original memories","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T11:22:09-07:00","id":1464395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1464352#post1464352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Core book says that the human making the pact retains all the original memories</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Eras 2 adds the option of Memory Pacts, but these are different, not standard.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:34:10-07:00","id":1465328,"title":"","content":"How are we supposed to handle Covers/Human forms for Angels? Should they be treated as automatically having the ability to assume human forms outside of mechanics, or should that human form be represented by the Mortal Mask Numina? I used to go for the latter, but looking at the sample angels, I saw plenty who seem to have human forms without any need for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:44:16-07:00","id":1465331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1465328#post1465328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are we supposed to handle Covers/Human forms for Angels? Should they be treated as automatically having the ability to assume human forms outside of mechanics, or should that human form be represented by the Mortal Mask Numina? I used to go for the latter, but looking at the sample angels, I saw plenty who seem to have human forms without any need for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was closer to the former, actually. The God-Machine cheats, by simply making the natural form of the angel material and human from the beginning. Mortal Mask, then, would be assigned to angels who aren\u2019t expected to be in human form 24/7, but still expected to be at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T07:49:09-07:00","id":1465399,"title":"","content":"It's not described in the books at all, but devs have since clarified that angelic Covers are supposed to be fully material forms and that they don't suffer any complications from Essence bleed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T08:12:44-07:00","id":1465404,"title":"","content":"Alright, thanks to both of you for these answers^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T04:26:11-07:00","id":1465495,"title":"","content":"Can demons Install in gadgets any Embeds and Exploits, or only those they've learned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T08:28:56-07:00","id":1465514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1465495#post1465495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can demons Install in gadgets any Embeds and Exploits, or only those they've learned?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1441816-noob-dumb-question-about-gadgets-that-i-got\">The latter</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T12:40:58-07:00","id":1466974,"title":"","content":"Just to be sure I'm understanding the core rules right : supernatural beings can't fray a Cover just by trying to discover more about the demon, right ? Only purely human characters/NPCs ?<br /> <br /> What about Ghouls, Wolf-Blooded etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T12:51:28-07:00","id":1466975,"title":"","content":"This is a more expansive answer than you asked for, but it usually bears repeating because there's a lot of trip-up on the base compromise triggers.<br /> <br /> Aside from using Exploits or whatever powers might sometimes call for a compromise roll, there are two base triggers for compromise.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>A human discovers a key fact about your nature.</b> It has to be a normal human (I would call sleepwalkers and hunters the outermost limit of how supernatural you can get before you no longer qualify, and I personally wouldn't include hunters who are also definitionally sleepwalkers by way of supernatural powers, like the Lucifuge). It has to be a significant thing about your nature as a demon that is more detail than the human knew before. They have to believe it.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>You take an action grossly out of character for your Cover.</b> For this trigger, it doesn't matter if there are humans around. It doesn't matter if there are witnesses of <i>any</i> kind around (though that does inflict a modifier). You can be alone when you do it. At the same time, it has to be a <b>gross, violent</b> contradiction of who your Cover is and what they would do. One of the writers specified that an earlier draft of Demon that contained the Integrity rules referred to the questions asked to define a mortal's Integrity breaking points as a reference point. If your Cover were an actual mortal human, and forcing themselves to do this action was such a strain that they suffered a breaking point, then that's a compromise for that Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T12:56:34-07:00","id":1466976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1466974#post1466974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be sure I'm understanding the core rules right : supernatural beings can't fray a Cover just by trying to discover more about the demon, right ? Only purely human characters/NPCs ?<br /> <br /> What about Ghouls, Wolf-Blooded etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going off the investigating a demon side bar, specifically this line &quot;if the investigator is human, or else gives the researcher equivalent knowledge that could be shared with humans&quot; I feel this supports that the compromise section calls out human truly means human and other supernaturals don't risk it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T13:07:41-07:00","id":1466979,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2909_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2909\" data-vbnamecard=\"2909\">Mr.F.I.X.</a> !<br /> <br /> Regarding the grossly out of character, I guess it isn't a &quot;using powers&quot; if there is no witness. But if, say your Cover is a vegan, hunting some animal to eat it would be a Compromise then ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T13:24:23-07:00","id":1466981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1466979#post1466979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> !<br /> <br /> Regarding the grossly out of character, I guess it isn't a &amp;quot;using powers&amp;quot; if there is no witness. But if, say your Cover is a vegan, hunting some animal to eat it would be a Compromise then ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, exploits cause a compromise but can be negated via willpower. Embeds unless they say in their description do not cause compromises. The gross actions out of character is more about behaviour that is contrary to the cover. Yes, like your vegan example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T13:30:09-07:00","id":1466982,"title":"","content":"What if a demon is killed? In Cover or in Demonic Form. By an angel or by a human. What happens to their body and Covers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T13:37:23-07:00","id":1466984,"title":"","content":"I think they appear entirely humans if killed in their Cover. In their Demonic form, an Angel will probably bring back the corpse to an Infrastructure where it'll be recycled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 11-06-2021, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T13:44:59-07:00","id":1466985,"title":"","content":"As ur-than said, if killed by an angel the demon would be recycled but if they just die the cover doesn't fray. After all, a demon can die of old age if they allow a cover to reach the end of its life. If the cover just dissipated as they died you'd think reaching the end of their covers lifespan they'd simply go loud automatically not die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T02:50:25-08:00","id":1468962,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it has alreayd been asnwered elsewhere but I can't seem to find it...<br /> <br /> When an Angel is summoned with a Cover, how does it work for the world around it ?<br /> <br /> In my case, I intend to have an Angel adding itself to a firm, with an office and all, for my campaign. Does it just appears and everyone who isn't a Stigmatic/Demon takes it in stride ? Does a new office appear or does someone else is fired to make space for the angel ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T04:22:27-08:00","id":1468970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1468962#post1468962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it has alreayd been asnwered elsewhere but I can't seem to find it...<br /> <br /> When an Angel is summoned with a Cover, how does it work for the world around it ?<br /> <br /> In my case, I intend to have an Angel adding itself to a firm, with an office and all, for my campaign. Does it just appears and everyone who isn't a Stigmatic/Demon takes it in stride ? Does a new office appear or does someone else is fired to make space for the angel ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea on official guiding, but I highly suspect \u201cAnything that\u2019s the most cost-efficient for the Machine at the moment.\u201d<br /> Failing all three above, there\u2019s also the option of the angel just using the Fetter and Possess Manifestations on the firm\u2019s key persons. If angels are keep going to use Ephemeral Entity rules, might as well make the most of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T08:03:25-08:00","id":1468986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1468962#post1468962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it has alreayd been asnwered elsewhere but I can't seem to find it...<br /> <br /> When an Angel is summoned with a Cover, how does it work for the world around it ?<br /> <br /> In my case, I intend to have an Angel adding itself to a firm, with an office and all, for my campaign. Does it just appears and everyone who isn't a Stigmatic/Demon takes it in stride ? Does a new office appear or does someone else is fired to make space for the angel ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As hermit said but with how angel jacking works as a cover that a demon can step into I feel it's safe to say it's similar to how demon cover works as well as other bits that suggest that angels use covers too. Supporting details like their home might get wierd at low cover ratings for example but otherwise aren't noticed. <br /> In your example it is possible that with its cover it just walks in as if it's already been there with cover seeming to support this with altered memories to prevent questions or doubt. Or it could be as simple as a transferred employee from another company as a cover story with the GM arranging such convenient openings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T12:28:34-08:00","id":1469009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1468986#post1468986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As hermit said but with how angel jacking works as a cover that a demon can step into I feel it's safe to say it's similar to how demon cover works as well as other bits that suggest that angels use covers too. Supporting details like their home might get wierd at low cover ratings for example but otherwise aren't noticed.<br /> In your example it is possible that with its cover it just walks in as if it's already been there with cover seeming to support this with altered memories to prevent questions or doubt. Or it could be as simple as a transferred employee from another company as a cover story with the GM arranging such convenient openings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hadn't considered the idea of a simple mutation with someone from another branch. I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T21:35:19-08:00","id":1469624,"title":"","content":"Does a pact end if the pactbound dies?<br /> <br /> For some reason I remember reading that, or think I remember reading it, but I can't seem to find it. I dont mean if the cover detail that reinforces your cover dies but the pactbound.<br /> <br /> Edit: found it, it was litterally at the start of durations description &quot;Pacts are usually permanent, lasting for as long as the contract exists and both parties live.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 12-05-2021, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T23:34:21-08:00","id":1469630,"title":"","content":"I also seems to remember something of that effect but I can't find it back in the core right now.<br /> <br /> Here's how I'd play it however : if the Pact has been called and thus the element has been fully incorporated in a Cover, the rights of it's initial owner have been overwritten by the Demon's, so even the death of the pactbound doesn't affect them. However, if the pactbound had only relinquished his rights on that part of his life but that no Demon incoporated the Pact into one of their Covers, then the death of the pactbound would render the pact moot since reality can't be fully rewritten with the dead person.<br /> <br /> That way, Demons having ledgers of normal Pacts and not just Soul Pacts makes more sense to me without being too overpowered. &quot;Here's that Pact that was trade off from Demon to Demon since times immemorial. You're now the Son of Nabuchodonosor, have fun with it&quot; wouldn't exactly work anyway, but it's better to have some personal guidelines I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T03:00:57-08:00","id":1469635,"title":"","content":"Just thought about it but... let's say a Demon wants to use &quot;dynastic Covers&quot;, in that he has children with his Covers and wants to make Soul Pacts with them to get them when his current Cover will be deemed too old (I don't have Heirs to Hell so perhaps it's just not possible). What happens to the original Cover for the peoples of the family ? Obviously, the demon can't let it die of all age, since he'd die with it.<br /> <br /> Does he just put it off and let time to his office ? Won't the family start freaking out and seeking the old person who just disappeared ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T03:37:37-08:00","id":1469637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1469635#post1469635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just thought about it but... let's say a Demon wants to use &amp;quot;dynastic Covers&amp;quot;, in that he has children with his Covers and wants to make Soul Pacts with them to get them when his current Cover will be deemed too old (I don't have Heirs to Hell so perhaps it's just not possible). What happens to the original Cover for the peoples of the family ? Obviously, the demon can't let it die of all age, since he'd die with it.<br /> <br /> Does he just put it off and let time to his office ? Won't the family start freaking out and seeking the old person who just disappeared ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon blooded characters do not have any immunity to a soul pacts so, its definitely possible.<br /> <br /> As to the aging of a cover, a demon is aware of how much longer a cover will last. This is more that they're aware of the biological death that'll occur if no accidents arise. A demon may just take on another cover and abandon a cover about to die to escape joining the cover in death. However the impact that might have on the family as the cover ceases to be is a good question. I'm not entirely sure what would happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T08:07:59-08:00","id":1470134,"title":"","content":"With hurt locker adding certain conditions that cover disabilities, such as arm disability building off of the arm wrack tilt, and how demons can purchase conditions with esoteric pacts (FoH) I'm just considering if you were to pact away that disability would the pactbound suddenly have that disability vanish? They were deaf but now they hear for example. A much more extreme example being arm disability representing an amputation being bought through a pact, would this cause the arm to grow back? You can after all change appearances by bestowing striking looks so it isnt too outlandish.<br /> <br /> I would understand if this would count as compromise potentially and no doubt a breaking point for the mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T16:26:46-08:00","id":1470175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1470134#post1470134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With hurt locker adding certain conditions that cover disabilities, such as arm disability building off of the arm wrack tilt, and how demons can purchase conditions with esoteric pacts (FoH) I'm just considering if you were to pact away that disability would the pactbound suddenly have that disability vanish? They were deaf but now they hear for example. A much more extreme example being arm disability representing an amputation being bought through a pact, would this cause the arm to grow back? You can after all change appearances by bestowing striking looks so it isnt too outlandish.<br /> <br /> I would understand if this would count as compromise potentially and no doubt a breaking point for the mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons bestowing healing miracles? Sounds legit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T07:21:33-08:00","id":1471143,"title":"","content":"Question concerning the Agendas.<br /> <br /> Are integrators considered &quot;redeemed&quot; nowadays? I know they had a rough first reception due to the over focus on the ones that will just turn you into the angels, but I always felt they've been well liked since the supplements. However I don't know if they'd still see any changes in the far future that are more than simply a shift in focus (from traitors to tragic figures who belive the machine is ultimately for the best, but have unfinished business/want to improve the machine)<br /> <br /> Do players who want to be inquisitors all have a general feeling they aren't provided as much tools to actually explore their Agenda? It's always been a complaint of mine that the books tend to overly favor a saboteurs approach to the God machine, but even then I feel like most storytellers would have the most trouble figuring out something satisfying specifically for inquisitor players.<br /> <br /> Finally, is there a possibility for more thematic write ups for the Agendas in the far future? What I mean is while I enjoy the spy nature (I consider the descent the most unique take on God, angels, and demons, while still actually feeling like all of that), I'd like if supplements in the future (and possible 2nd edition) leaned into a more demonic feel. Less from terminology, more from presentation. For example. I've always liked the idea that saboteurs are Wrath (obvious reasons), integrators pride (believing their must be special reason for their fall, or that a self imposed mission is more important than the God machine wants, or even wish to change it themselves, all the while claiming their want to leave), tempters lust (for life), and inquisitors Sloth (for lack of better term). Though obviously I see issues with this as it leans very heavily into Christian theology, which descent is divorced from by a large margin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T07:54:37-08:00","id":1471146,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest this might not be a simple question with a simple answer, but for what it's worth, I've never considered the presentation of integrators in need of &quot;redemption,&quot; nor do I feel like they're underserved in tools to explore their agenda. I do think Demon lacks a bit in terms of storytelling advice and tools to guide late-game demons approaching their achievement of a personal hell, but I think that applies for all the agendas, not just integrators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T09:09:23-08:00","id":1471148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1471146#post1471146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest this might not be a simple question with a simple answer, but for what it's worth, I've never considered the presentation of integrators in need of &quot;redemption,&quot; nor do I feel like they're underserved in tools to explore their agenda. I do think Demon lacks a bit in terms of storytelling advice and tools to guide late-game demons approaching their achievement of a personal hell, but I think that applies for all the agendas, not just integrators.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about putting the post here then. I only realized it didn't really belong until I posted it<br /> <br /> As for thinking they didn't really need any redeeming, I didn't really think so either, but until the players guide, a lot of my fellow players thought of the Agenda as unable to work in a Ring, which I partly attribute to the fact they are the only ones focused on how suspicious they can be, despite their opposite doing the most reckless actions. I think that, along with the beat condition not explaining that integrators will likely do small betrayals (like leaving behind important evidence, NOT simply telling the angels their location) lead to many people thinking they couldn't work even though there is suspicion amongst all agendas. Sorry for the long paragraph<br /> <br /> Finally, for tools, yes I agree with the late game. However, I feel that in the corebook, most problems presented are treated as infrastructure that needs to be destroyed, with little tools on what what the other Agendas could so. Though admittedly, the players guide rectifies this issue of mine a good amount<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> I change my stance on the other Agendas not really ever being treated as badly as Integrators in terms of antagonism. It's simply takes a more Overt form, which I think is why many tend to glaze over the other agendas in that respect. Also, re reading Enemy Action, it does a great job on showing the antagonism of other agendas (with the integrators, particularly Mr Martini, actually being great examples on Integrators being useful allies who still find ways to use their agenda condition is a fun, long term way)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 12-25-2021, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T13:58:35-08:00","id":1475797,"title":"","content":"Dumb question : do Demons dream ? I need to know it for a campaign going !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T14:30:33-08:00","id":1475799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1475797#post1475797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question : do Demons dream ? I need to know it for a campaign going !</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, except for the ones that don't. By default demons are assumed to dream as part and parcel of their defecting to humanity, but some demons don't dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T03:21:41-08:00","id":1475830,"title":"","content":"Thanks, it'll help a lot !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T08:01:33-07:00","id":1492598,"title":"","content":"I m designing an Angel with a mission of infiltrating in a Demon ring and i was wondering, what abilities does Angels lack for impersonating a Demon?<br /> Can they fake using Embeds?<br /> Can they stipulate pacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T11:22:55-07:00","id":1492704,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, while Angels have a lot less Agency they are created for a purpose, and in that way they very versatile. Wih that said, Demons have ways to detect angels so you will have to becareful with what you show them.<br /> <br /> While they can't use Embeds as they appear in Demon, it's establisehd that they also know of the loopholes in reality and that they are the base for at elast some of their Numina, so yeah, you could give an Angel either Embeds or Numinas based on existing Embeds that the players know of (maybe Embeds that their characters have even).<br /> <br /> Angels can't do deals in the same capacity than Demons, but since they have the GM supporting them you would never know. The GM could just pay up the Angels part of the pact and also give the Angel what they asked for (so imagine an Angel makes a &quot;deal&quot; with an NPC drug addict: their drug addiction in exchange for lots of money. The GM gives the money to the NPC and turns the angels cover into an addict, so that the party doesn't suspect anything. But then the party find the NPC again and they haven't lost their addiction...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","user":"Aeneas","date":".  shite writting 10-17-2022, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T14:04:20-08:00","id":1497944,"title":"","content":"My understanding: Demons can make Soul Pacts with supernatural creatures. However, if they invoke the pact, they don't gain any of that creature's powers -- they just become fully human versions of those beings.<br /> <br /> The question: Is there anything stopping a Demon from making a Soul Pact with a Fetch?<br /> <br /> Corollary: If they can, what happens to their Cover if the Fetch's Changeling counterpart ever makes it back Ironsides?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T14:13:35-08:00","id":1497947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1497944#post1497944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding: Demons can make Soul Pacts with supernatural creatures. However, if they invoke the pact, they don't gain any of that creature's powers -- they just become fully human versions of those beings.<br /> <br /> The question: Is there anything stopping a Demon from making a Soul Pact with a Fetch?<br /> <br /> Corollary: If they can, what happens to their Cover if the Fetch's Changeling counterpart ever makes it back Ironsides?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, youd be able to take a fetch and live in their place. The biggest thing thatd out you though is unlike a fetch you wouldn't have a mask they could see through as they could with a fetch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T14:16:20-08:00","id":1497948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1492598#post1492598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m designing an Angel with a mission of infiltrating in a Demon ring and i was wondering, what abilities does Angels lack for impersonating a Demon?<br /> Can they fake using Embeds?<br /> Can they stipulate pacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are one or two example Angel's that have an embed as one of their numen. In the st guide it is calls out exiles having cover from their mission, which fits how demons have cover, but it calls out that exile covers arent maintained by the GM. It doesnt provide rules for angel use of cover though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T14:16:58-08:00","id":1497949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1497947#post1497947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, youd be able to take a fetch and live in their place. The biggest thing thatd out you though is unlike a fetch you wouldn't have a mask they could see through as they could with a fetch.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably going to inflict Clarity damage on the Changeling, then, especially if this happened before The Changeling ever got back from Arcadia. Instead of something with a Mask, the Changeling sees someone who exactly resembles them and is apparently human in all ways they could test.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T18:16:32-08:00","id":1497962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1497949#post1497949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably going to inflict Clarity damage on the Changeling, then, especially if this happened before The Changeling ever got back from Arcadia. Instead of something with a Mask, the Changeling sees someone who exactly resembles them and is apparently human in all ways they could test.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cover is flawed; even without concrete glitches, long-term observation turns up clues as described in the system for investigating a Cover, to say nothing of kenning or the fact that spoofing relies on a roll with no common bonuses that can fail.<br /> <br /> Also, while 2e has rendered it a little more ambiguous, fetches whose Mask is complete enough to look totally physically human still occur and &quot;meeting your fetch for the first time&quot; is an extremely minor Clarity attack.<br /> <br /> What's more likely to give them problems, I'd imagine, is the Conditions they'd need to take to continue investigating after a failed roll on the extended action, which might trigger Clarity attacks directly or indirectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T00:46:44-07:00","id":1505292,"title":"","content":"If a demon transform into their demonic form in front of mortals, would they need to make a compromise roll with -3 (for full transformation only) or -5 (for full transformation + Act was overtly supernatural and witnessed by humans\u200b)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25913-regretone","name":"RegretOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25913_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T13:34:05-07:00","id":1505370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RegretOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1505292#post1505292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a demon transform into their demonic form in front of mortals, would they need to make a compromise roll with -3 (for full transformation only) or -5 (for full transformation + Act was overtly supernatural and witnessed by humans\u200b)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T14:31:51-07:00","id":1505822,"title":"","content":"Hello!<br /> A silly aesthetic question: do you think that phisical appearence changes, when an Angel fall and become a demon? Maybe his angelic wings schanges into demonic ones, or his shining armor turn pitch black? And stuff like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T14:52:21-07:00","id":1505825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1505822#post1505822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A silly aesthetic question: do you think that phisical appearence changes, when an Angel fall and become a demon? Maybe his angelic wings schanges into demonic ones, or his shining armor turn pitch black? And stuff like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the corebook, the demonic form is &quot;a twisted and mutated version of their original angelic appearance.&quot;<br /> <br /> Per the Player's Guide, while the demonic form can change and evolve over time as the character's Primum rating increases (swapping out up to two abilities at each dot, as well as gaining new additional abilities at particular thresholds), at the moment of the Fall it's little different from the true form they possessed as an angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T07:22:40-07:00","id":1507682,"title":"","content":"When a Demon takes the Claws and Fangs Demonic traits, do they use it with Brawl, Weaponry, or either one and they need to pick at character creation? The description in the book is not clear about that. My initial assumption was that it was Brawl, but they do not state such and in fact refer to the claws as counting as &quot;small weapons&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T17:51:49-07:00","id":1507725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1507682#post1507682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Demon takes the Claws and Fangs Demonic traits, do they use it with Brawl, Weaponry, or either one and they need to pick at character creation? The description in the book is not clear about that. My initial assumption was that it was Brawl, but they do not state such and in fact refer to the claws as counting as &quot;small weapons&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Brawl. Weaponry is the Skill for weapons that aren't used with direct extensions of normal violent/aggressive/suppressive motions; &quot;Bite&quot; is listed in the Rules Appendix as a maneuver under Unarmed Combat, Demon Core was one of the first books to use the Revised Storytelling System's assumption that weapons deal extra damage rather than adding to an attacker's dicepool, and Claws and Fangs is not unique in calling its source of lethal damage &quot;small weapons&quot; (Spurs does the same thing) and never actually specifying a Skill, but the implications of having literal Claws and Fangs are different than the implications of Blade Hand's &quot;you have a weapon that you would need to be literally disarmed to be deprived of and it works with all your weapon-based Fighting Merits.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T06:18:30-07:00","id":1507761,"title":"","content":"Yeah, figured so. Just wanted to make sure; Thanks for the clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T10:11:19-07:00","id":1521470,"title":"","content":"So idea: Demon Bob be working with humans. But humans will \u2018forget\u2019 him if he swaps covers. Cover 1 has a ring. He leaves the ring on the ground and goes around a corner to swap covers into Cover 2. Then he picks up the ring, the ring being a \u2018symbol\u2019 of sorts to let the mortals know \u201cI\u2019m Demon Bob\u201d<br /> <br /> Would such a thing cause a compromise roll? Or would the ring disappear after he swaps covers? He wouldn\u2019t exactly say \u2018I\u2019m a demon\u2019 but it\u2019s more like \u201cwhen you see someone with this ring, treat them as you would treat me\u201d. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T11:12:13-07:00","id":1521474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1521470#post1521470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So idea: Demon Bob be working with humans. But humans will \u2018forget\u2019 him if he swaps covers. Cover 1 has a ring. He leaves the ring on the ground and goes around a corner to swap covers into Cover 2. Then he picks up the ring, the ring being a \u2018symbol\u2019 of sorts to let the mortals know \u201cI\u2019m Demon Bob\u201d<br /> <br /> Would such a thing cause a compromise roll? Or would the ring disappear after he swaps covers? He wouldn\u2019t exactly say \u2018I\u2019m a demon\u2019 but it\u2019s more like \u201cwhen you see someone with this ring, treat them as you would treat me\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>People don't forget your Cover exists until its rating is reduced to 0.<br /> <br /> Separately, &quot;these two very different people are the same person&quot; could conceivably qualify as a compromise in the vein of &quot;revealing a key fact about your true nature to humans,&quot; yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T05:48:41-08:00","id":1525723,"title":"","content":"Can a demon have an interlock out of the same two embeds they have for an exploit?<br /> <br /> ex: Hellfire uses check backdrop and merciless gunman. Can a demon also have an interlock using both of those? Ex: pull some X-ray trick shot assassination kinda stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> and can an interlock replicate the abilities of merits? Like Fulcrum Point + Never Here = Telekinesis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28143,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","user":"firestar001","date":".  Added second question 11-21-2023, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T03:50:59-08:00","id":1525783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1525723#post1525723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a demon have an interlock out of the same two embeds they have for an exploit?<br /> <br /> ex: Hellfire uses check backdrop and merciless gunman. Can a demon also have an interlock using both of those? Ex: pull some X-ray trick shot assassination kinda stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> and can an interlock replicate the abilities of merits? Like Fulcrum Point + Never Here = Telekinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been a long while since I read Demon, but at a glance, I see no immediate reason to forbid both cases. Probably should be fine; though don't (fully) take my word for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T17:46:37-08:00","id":1525817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1525723#post1525723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a demon have an interlock out of the same two embeds they have for an exploit?<br /> <br /> ex: Hellfire uses check backdrop and merciless gunman. Can a demon also have an interlock using both of those? Ex: pull some X-ray trick shot assassination kinda stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I'm not understanding the question, because an Interlock can use any two Keys as a basis, and the Embed you use as the prerequisite for an Exploit can be any Embed you can make a convincing case for allowing the character to learn that Exploit; there being two Example Prerequisite Embeds for each published Exploit and Interlocks using two Embeds as Keys is a coincidence with no mechanical relation to each other.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Yes, they can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and can an interlock replicate the abilities of merits? Like Fulcrum Point + Never Here = Telekinesis? </div> </div> </div>With the caveats that any Interlock you devise should probably keep the design notes from the corebook and Storyteller's Guide in mind and that directly porting a Supernatural Merit as an Interlock without adjustment to fit the character may result in an awkward time fitting it into the story, sure. (Though you would probably want to not use the Telekinesis Merit wholesale anyway, because that Merit's dicepool includes Merit dots the Cipher systems do not provide immediate guidance on.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T07:07:24-08:00","id":1526806,"title":"","content":"Is there ANY way for a demon to reveal that they\u2019re a demon WITHOUT causing a compromise roll?<br /> <br /> like taking them into a bolt hole? Or would they still cause a compromise roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T19:35:35-08:00","id":1526825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1526806#post1526806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there ANY way for a demon to reveal that they\u2019re a demon WITHOUT causing a compromise roll?<br /> <br /> like taking them into a bolt hole? Or would they still cause a compromise roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;reveal&quot; means &quot;provide information,&quot; then that's as simple as the other party not being a human, though they then can share that information with humans to trigger a compromise of the Cover(s) the revelation relates to. If you mean assuming demonic form, then not in common availability from the books barring the ST waiving compromise rolls in controlled circumstances in the same way Deviant provides the option for Overt Variations used in seclusion to not add to conspiracy surveillance rolls to track you.<br /> <br /> It's an espionage game. The changeover from undercover agent to fugitive is a point most demons try to avoid for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T04:23:27-08:00","id":1526917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1526825#post1526825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If &quot;reveal&quot; means &quot;provide information,&quot; then that's as simple as the other party not being a human, though they then can share that information with humans to trigger a compromise of the Cover(s) the revelation relates to. If you mean assuming demonic form, then not in common availability from the books barring the ST waiving compromise rolls in controlled circumstances in the same way Deviant provides the option for Overt Variations used in seclusion to not add to conspiracy surveillance rolls to track you.<br /> <br /> It's an espionage game. The changeover from undercover agent to fugitive is a point most demons try to avoid for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game I got a werewolf and demon, so trying to think if a demon revealing itself to an Uratha would trigger a roll. (Gonna say Uratha revealing itself isn\u2019t against the oath cause demons aren\u2019t part of \u2018the herd\u2019)<br /> <br /> Thanks for the advice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T05:28:40-08:00","id":1527625,"title":"","content":"Can non-demons go into splinter timelines? (Like in \u201cHow an Angel Dies\u201d from the Demon core rule book). Like can a werewolf or Changeling go into a splinter with or without a demon?<br /> <br /> if so: are there any mechanics one needs to be aware of? Would the non-demon gain the Hunted condition due to being an \u2018error of this splinter\u2019?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T11:05:22-08:00","id":1527635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1527625#post1527625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can non-demons go into splinter timelines? (Like in \u201cHow an Angel Dies\u201d from the Demon core rule book). Like can a werewolf or Changeling go into a splinter with or without a demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be very weird for them not to be able to, considering the Seattle Appendix in the corebook states that people from splinter timelines can become stigmatic and leave and that nothing about the described fractures to other timelines requires demonic powers to access (and some of them directly imply to the contrary through connection to missing person incidents).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if so: are there any mechanics one needs to be aware of? Would the non-demon gain the Hunted condition due to being an \u2018error of this splinter\u2019? </div> </div> </div>The closest thing to mechanics of this type is the sidebar &quot;Stigmatics and Splinter Timelines&quot; on page 259 of the corebook describing how a person from a splinter timeline being turned into a stigmatic is erased on the fifth reset of their timeline after the change, and that may be more to do with the people in splinter timelines being less real than people from the dominant timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T16:16:30-08:00","id":1529472,"title":"","content":"So when you make a Demon, it says you can but Primum at creation for 3 dots of merits. But in books like Werewolf, Geist, Beast and Deviant, those kinds of things cost 5 merits. <br /> <br /> From page 81 of DtD Core: <i>Primum begins at 1 and may be increased at the cost of three Merit dots a point at character creation</i>.<br /> <br /> So is it supposed to be five dots? Or three?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T16:50:10-08:00","id":1529474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1529472#post1529472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when you make a Demon, it says you can but Primum at creation for 3 dots of merits. But in books like Werewolf, Geist, Beast and Deviant, those kinds of things cost 5 merits.<br /> <br /> From page 81 of DtD Core: <i>Primum begins at 1 and may be increased at the cost of three Merit dots a point at character creation</i>.<br /> <br /> So is it supposed to be five dots? Or three?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's five. Make sure you have the current version, because in the version I have it says five on pages 80, 81, 87, and 88.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T17:16:13-08:00","id":1529475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1529474#post1529474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's five. Make sure you have the current version, because in the version I have it says five on pages 80, 81, 87, and 88.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it the version with the \u2018bare bones\u2019 table of contents (just chapter titles) or is it \u2018detailed\u2019 like the other books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T17:55:33-08:00","id":1529478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1529475#post1529475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it the version with the \u2018bare bones\u2019 table of contents (just chapter titles) or is it \u2018detailed\u2019 like the other books?</div> </div> </div> </div>My version's TOC also only has chapter titles. If you can find any instance of the phrase &quot;p.XX&quot; instead of an actual internal page number reference you don't have the new version; ditto if there's not an index on pages 390-396. <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/124155/Demon-The-Descent\" target=\"_blank\">Redownload the book from the DTRPG page</a> and you should get the current one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T09:26:23-08:00","id":1529912,"title":"","content":"For Professional Training and Embeds/Exploits. If I use Merciless Gunmen, could I roll 9-again if I have Professional Training 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T09:51:15-08:00","id":1529915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1529912#post1529912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Professional Training and Embeds/Exploits. If I use Merciless Gunmen, could I roll 9-again if I have Professional Training 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T19:28:59-08:00","id":1531861,"title":"","content":"Does destroying the contract for a soul pact called in to create a Cover that has ceased to exist (e.g. by going loud) still cause damage to the demon like the destruction of any other permanent pact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T10:24:53-08:00","id":1532171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1531861#post1531861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does destroying the contract for a soul pact called in to create a Cover that has ceased to exist (e.g. by going loud) still cause damage to the demon like the destruction of any other permanent pact?</div> </div> </div> </div>So Demon gets soul pact &amp; contract. Demon switches to Cover. Demon goes loud, destroying cover.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d ASSUME the contract loses its \u2018link\u2019 to the Demon. Since the only think that links the Demon to the contract would BE the Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T04:49:59-07:00","id":1540561,"title":"","content":"Can the Aura Sight Technology allows to see invisible beings?<br /> <br /> Does perception through the Blind Sense Technology suffice to use the Mind Reading or Teleportation Form Abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T17:12:53-07:00","id":1540597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1540561#post1540561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Aura Sight Technology allows to see invisible beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Take Blind Sense for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1540561#post1540561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does perception through the Blind Sense Technology suffice to use the Mind Reading or Teleportation Form Abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I would allow this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T09:15:00-07:00","id":1540629,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> I also wanted to know: What is the range of the Rivet Arm Modification? Can it be used in melee like a nail gun? Does it have the inaccurate or piercing tags?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T01:05:13-07:00","id":1540693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1540629#post1540629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wanted to know: What is the range of the Rivet Arm Modification? Can it be used in melee like a nail gun? Does it have the inaccurate or piercing tags?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not specified, and not written for the rules that were developed in Hurt Locker.<br /> If you're using Hurt Locker rules, off the top of my head, I would suggest the player's choice (when selecting the Modification) of either Short range and Piercing 1 or Medium range and no Piercing. Used in melee, treat it the same as a metal club, except add both the Brawl tag and the Inaccurate tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 08-19-2024, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T07:44:07-07:00","id":1540962,"title":"","content":"Do Form Abilities like Blade Hand or Aegis Protocol use Brawl or Weaponry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T08:35:22-07:00","id":1540963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1540962#post1540962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Form Abilities like Blade Hand or Aegis Protocol use Brawl or Weaponry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless stated otherwise, Brawl is used for attacks that act like extensions of a natural living body like claws, fangs, fists, etc, while Weaponry is used for attacks that involve weapons like swords, hammers, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-18T10:41:27-08:00","id":1547813,"title":"","content":"I would like to ask how can I create an Angel that is embodied. (In terms of the game rules.) If the Angel is an emphemeral entity, then I think it is clear - I assign Rank, Power, Finesse, Resistance, Influences, Numina, etc. However what if it has a physical form? When in cover, I would use the stats of a mortal. However what about the physical angelic form? Should I follow rules from Demon:The Descent about the Demonic Form, or are you doing it in a different way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-18T15:10:36-08:00","id":1547821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1547813#post1547813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to ask how can I create an Angel that is embodied. (In terms of the game rules.) If the Angel is an emphemeral entity, then I think it is clear - I assign Rank, Power, Finesse, Resistance, Influences, Numina, etc. However what if it has a physical form? When in cover, I would use the stats of a mortal. However what about the physical angelic form? Should I follow rules from Demon:The Descent about the Demonic Form, or are you doing it in a different way?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the Materialize Manifestation for angels to assume physical form temporarily.<br /> If you want an angel that's always in physical form, then I believe you're entering homebrew territory (though DtD isn't my strongest game so I might've missed something that someone else can point out). If so, then I would personally probably do a regular angel except make it Materialized by default instead of being in Twilight Form as default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T01:51:37-08:00","id":1547826,"title":"","content":"Angels, unlike demons, don't have a naturally physical form outside of their Cover identities. They're ephemeral entities that have to use Materialize (or whatever other Manifestations or Numina might do the job) to interact with physical matter. They don't use demonic form abilities; any powers they have are represented by their Influences and Numina.<br /> <br /> If the set of tools feels limited and you're having trouble writing your own, the Demon Storyteller's Guide adds a rule that the presence of supporting infrastructure gives their Numina either a +2 bonus or a 1 Essence cost reduction, provides a list of additional Numina written for angels, and adds Incepts that network with the God-Machine's occult knowledge for broader reality-shaping effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T13:27:07-08:00","id":1547836,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for the answers, I see that I made a wrong assumption. This makes things much more clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T09:32:40-08:00","id":1548707,"title":"","content":"I plan to prepare an Angel as an ephemeral being with influence over minds of people:<br /> <br /> Influence: Compliance (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Strengthen (1 Dot): Amplify a target\u2019s natural tendencies to obey or comply.<br /> Manipulate (2 Dots): Force or instill short-term obedience (e.g., cause a target to heed a false doctor\u2019s orders).<br /> Control (3 Dots): Enforce a much stronger, longer-lasting compliance\u2014someone might not question contradictory evidence for days.<br /> <br /> My question to you: How to roll to find out, whether the angel succeeded? How does he roll and how is it resisted?<br /> <br /> Is such influence legit or should this rather be Numina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T09:40:57-08:00","id":1548708,"title":"","content":"I found it in the rules: The entity pays the listed cost in Essence and rolls Power + Finesse, with success creating the desired effect. If the Influence is altering the thoughts or emotions of a sentient being, the roll is contested by Resolve or Composure (whichever is higher) + Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> Sorry for asking before searching throughly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T17:14:20-07:00","id":1552175,"title":"","content":"I'm finally reading the book, and I've found conflicting information about buying Primum: some parts of the book say it costs 3 XP, but at least one says it costs 5 XP. I'm prone to believe it's 5, but is that clarified somewhere else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T17:24:52-07:00","id":1552178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1552175#post1552175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm finally reading the book, and I've found conflicting information about buying Primum: some parts of the book say it costs 3 XP, but at least one says it costs 5 XP. I'm prone to believe it's 5, but is that clarified somewhere else?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can't find any instances of the former pricing, I do remember highlighting the error back in the day that Primum listed the cost in starting Merit dots as 3 instead of 5 in the same way as all of 1e's splats except Mummy allowed (which has since been fixed). The intention is definitely that a dot of Primum costs 5 Experiences as with every other purchased Supernatural Potency Trait in 2e.<br /> <br /> Are you looking at a current copy of the PDF?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T12:13:02-07:00","id":1553335,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know what happens if one tries to Precision Engineer a Form Power gadget? I know what most other forms of hardware provides, but I can't seem to find what a Form Power gadget might benefit from. (heck, I only recently found the line that states Form power gadgets can't be used in lambdas and it's just a single easily missed spot)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T12:49:41-07:00","id":1553338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1553335#post1553335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know what happens if one tries to Precision Engineer a Form Power gadget? I know what most other forms of hardware provides, but I can't seem to find what a Form Power gadget might benefit from. (heck, I only recently found the line that states Form power gadgets can't be used in lambdas and it's just a single easily missed spot)</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming it's not disallowed based on it not being included in the list of things that can't be precision engineered, it gets a permanent upgrade from the Overclocking list and 8-Again on rolls to use the hardware for its intended purpose, but given that form gadgets can't be overclocked and the process of Installation warps the hardware like an Exploited gadget it's entirely possible that it simply doesn't apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T13:08:17-07:00","id":1553342,"title":"","content":"A little disappointing, but that makes sense. I know that Precision Engineered Implanted Gadgets don't Overclock but instead don't suffer the Implanted condition, so I thought maybe Form Power gadgets had some other less typical bonus. Maybe if I were to comb through it I might find some mention, otherwise I'd presume it isn't something that is possible.<br /> <br /> I do wish that Flowers of Hell had a bit of a better time being edited since there are a number of inconsistencies within it (such as offering a penalty to reverse engineering One Shots, only to state on another page that one can't do that full stop), and being more cohesive on what info is where would have been nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T20:51:15-08:00","id":1557360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1531861#post1531861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does destroying the contract for a soul pact called in to create a Cover that has ceased to exist (e.g. by going loud) still cause damage to the demon like the destruction of any other permanent pact?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have thought about this one quite a bit. That former soul's identity has been utterly annihilated\u2014<i>twice</i>, really. The demon completely subsumed the identity, banishing the soul to a fate possibly worse than death, and then scoured the stolen identity from the universe in a blaze of glory. <br /> <br /> I'm inclined to say no. It's how I'd rule it, anyway, but it's one of the many, many, many weird edge cases with demons, and pacts in particular. <br /> <hr /><br /> For my own simple question, I put to you all: what questions do you have about how pacts work? Edge cases, general cases, anything, really. This thread (which I've finally read) has a bunch of good examples, but in the year of our God-Machine 2026, maybe the questions have changed. <br /> <br /> What would you have liked to see a book address, given the chance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T11:06:47-07:00","id":1563127,"title":"","content":"Does Cover Trading have any interaction with memory pacts, or can memory pacts only be made with non-demons?<br /> <br /> Relatedly, is the matter of retaining control of the pact document and/or memoir for a memory pact semantic or material, i.e. does a demon have to have the documents on hand to incorporate the memories (as distinct from renewing the Informed Condition, which expressly requires physical contact) or can the demon store them somewhere and still remember the described events as long as someone else hasn't changed the document from &quot;a document that [the undersigned demon] knows how to access without difficulty&quot; to &quot;a document that has been traded or stolen from [the undersigned demon]&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T03:26:31-07:00","id":1563139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1563127#post1563127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Cover Trading have any interaction with memory pacts, or can memory pacts only be made with non-demons?<br /> <br /> Relatedly, is the matter of retaining control of the pact document and/or memoir for a memory pact semantic or material, i.e. does a demon have to have the documents on hand to incorporate the memories (as distinct from renewing the Informed Condition, which expressly requires physical contact) or can the demon store them somewhere and still remember the described events as long as someone else hasn't changed the document from &quot;a document that [the undersigned demon] knows how to access without difficulty&quot; to &quot;a document that has been traded or stolen from [the undersigned demon]&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I m not familiar with memory pact.<br /> in wich book do they appear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T07:01:31-07:00","id":1563142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1563139#post1563139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m not familiar with memory pact.<br /> in wich book do they appear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Memory pacts are introduced in Empire of Gold and Dust, along with mechanics for sacrificial pacts, pactkeepers, and generational pacts (Dark Eras 2, pp173-176).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T10:41:25-07:00","id":1563146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/947973-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-demon-the-descent?p=1563127#post1563127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Cover Trading have any interaction with memory pacts, or can memory pacts only be made with non-demons?<br /> <br /> Relatedly, is the matter of retaining control of the pact document and/or memoir for a memory pact semantic or material, i.e. does a demon have to have the documents on hand to incorporate the memories (as distinct from renewing the Informed Condition, which expressly requires physical contact) or can the demon store them somewhere and still remember the described events as long as someone else hasn't changed the document from &quot;a document that [the undersigned demon] knows how to access without difficulty&quot; to &quot;a document that has been traded or stolen from [the undersigned demon]&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, i would say:<br /> -Memory contracts are still contracts, i would treat them as Cover bits(exp) not incorporated in a Cover<br /> <br /> -The book probably use control instead of possess to indicate that you could store them, also the touch required to renew the condition seems to indicate that the demon must return to a storage only to renew the condition, not the memory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}